{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","bridgeSessionId":"cse_01D7CJmXuD2ASqfBYm7Lk4WZ","lastSequenceNum":18951,"ownerAccountUuid":"138d593e-e185-4f72-89f2-82e1a501f134","ownerOrganizationUuid":"602db9b4-428d-49e6-a99c-64152cc62a79"}
{"parentUuid":"3a970d84-d8c9-4e61-b107-3cedb4d89841","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"881f8cb4-b128-427b-99c0-44ffab770da7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TbYQofPMLCbxcn11weTVkK","type":"tool_result","content":"main README mentions lazy/warmUp: []\n== fork README diff (head)\ndiff --git a/packages/storybook/README.md b/packages/storybook/README.md\nindex e147f80f..ad518ea0 100644\n--- a/packages/storybook/README.md\n+++ b/packages/storybook/README.md\n@@ -37,6 +37,9 @@ Before answering, the provider compares every source file's mtime and size with\n | `htmlAttributes` | `curated` | `curated` lists the notable HTML attributes, `full` all of them, `none` none. Wins over `skipHtmlProps`. |\n | `loadDependencies` | `true` | Read the type declarations your props reference from installed packages, so library-typed props resolve instead of degrading. `false` skips the work. |\n | `collapseInheritedProps` | `none` | `none` lists every inherited prop. `dependencies` or `all` list inherited sources of more than 30 props as one layer. |\n+| `lazy` | `true` | Resolve a component when a story asks for it. `false` resolves every component at start; the answers are the same. |\n+| `fillAfter` | `16` | With `lazy`, once this many distinct components were asked for, resolve the rest in the background in one parallel pass. `0` never does. |\n+| `warmUp` | `false` | With `lazy`, resolve a few components in the background after start. Off: it did not make the first story faster in measurement. |\n | `fallback` | `degraded` | `degraded`: a component whose extraction reported a warning or error goes to React's docgen. `never`: always answer. |\n \n A story whose component caliper-docgen can't find goes to React's docgen, which stays registered underneath. Each component handed on is logged once as a warning with the reason (the extraction diagnostics that affect it).\n\n== fork changeset\n---\ncargo/caliper-docgen-core: patch\ncargo/caliper-docgen-napi: patch\nnpm/caliper-docgen: patch\nnpm/caliper-docgen-storybook: patch\n---\n\n- **The Storybook addon resolves a component when a story asks for it:** the session indexes where components are from parsing alone and resolves one when a story names it, so the first story no longer waits for every component. Answers are the same as before (`lazy: false` restores the old session). Once 16 distinct components have been asked for, it resolves the rest in one parallel pass in the background (`fillAfter`, `0` to never), so a project read end to end costs about what the old session did. `warmUp: true` resolves a few components after start; it did not make the first story faster in measurement, so it is off.\n- **Core and binding:** `WatchSession::component_index()` lists where each component is declared without resolving any. The binding gains `sessionComponentAnswers` (a component's documentation and its own diagnostics in one call) and `sessionWarmUp`, and `initializeSessionIndex` honours `lazy`.\n\n== is pid 7405 alive: claude bg-spare --bg-spare /tmp/cc-daemon-501/342c42ed/spare/8642b0bf.claim.sock\nbackup: /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/worktree-backups/a482304b1a114609f.patch 20959 bytes of diff; 7 untracked files\nbackup: /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/worktree-backups/a95b63d52249414d6.patch 25417 bytes of diff; 0 untracked files\nbackup: /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/worktree-backups/ac253a6938dfbbec1.patch 1492 bytes of diff; 0 untracked files\nbackup: /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/worktree-backups/accb7ca7a9c75ecb5.patch 15264 bytes of diff; 1 untracked files","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"03f72cee-540b-4b3b-949b-570f09b24dbd","timestamp":"2026-10-25T16:34:02.123Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"main README mentions lazy/warmUp: []\n== fork README diff (head)\ndiff --git a/packages/storybook/README.md b/packages/storybook/README.md\nindex e147f80f..ad518ea0 100644\n--- a/packages/storybook/README.md\n+++ b/packages/storybook/README.md\n@@ -37,6 +37,9 @@ Before answering, the provider compares every source file's mtime and size with\n | `htmlAttributes` | `curated` | `curated` lists the notable HTML attributes, `full` all of them, `none` none. Wins over `skipHtmlProps`. |\n | `loadDependencies` | `true` | Read the type declarations your props reference from installed packages, so library-typed props resolve instead of degrading. `false` skips the work. |\n | `collapseInheritedProps` | `none` | `none` lists every inherited prop. `dependencies` or `all` list inherited sources of more than 30 props as one layer. |\n+| `lazy` | `true` | Resolve a component when a story asks for it. `false` resolves every component at start; the answers are the same. |\n+| `fillAfter` | `16` | With `lazy`, once this many distinct components were asked for, resolve the rest in the background in one parallel pass. `0` never does. |\n+| `warmUp` | `false` | With `lazy`, resolve a few components in the background after start. Off: it did not make the first story faster in measurement. |\n | `fallback` | `degraded` | `degraded`: a component whose extraction reported a warning or error goes to React's docgen. `never`: always answer. |\n \n A story whose component caliper-docgen can't find goes to React's docgen, which stays registered underneath. Each component handed on is logged once as a warning with the reason (the extraction diagnostics that affect it).\n\n== fork changeset\n---\ncargo/caliper-docgen-core: patch\ncargo/caliper-docgen-napi: patch\nnpm/caliper-docgen: patch\nnpm/caliper-docgen-storybook: patch\n---\n\n- **The Storybook addon resolves a component when a story asks for it:** the session indexes where components are from parsing alone and resolves one when a story names it, so the first story no longer waits for every component. Answers are the same as before (`lazy: false` restores the old session). Once 16 distinct components have been asked for, it resolves the rest in one parallel pass in the background (`fillAfter`, `0` to never), so a project read end to end costs about what the old session did. `warmUp: true` resolves a few components after start; it did not make the first story faster in measurement, so it is off.\n- **Core and binding:** `WatchSession::component_index()` lists where each component is declared without resolving any. The binding gains `sessionComponentAnswers` (a component's documentation and its own diagnostics in one call) and `sessionWarmUp`, and `initializeSessionIndex` honours `lazy`.\n\n== is pid 7405 alive: claude bg-spare --bg-spare /tmp/cc-daemon-501/342c42ed/spare/8642b0bf.claim.sock\nbackup: /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/worktree-backups/a482304b1a114609f.patch 20959 bytes of diff; 7 untracked files\nbackup: /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/worktree-backups/a95b63d52249414d6.patch 25417 bytes of diff; 0 untracked files\nbackup: /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/worktree-backups/ac253a6938dfbbec1.patch 1492 bytes of diff; 0 untracked files\nbackup: /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/worktree-backups/accb7ca7a9c75ecb5.patch 15264 bytes of diff; 1 untracked files","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"bcb489c2-6c0e-46be-915f-d61fbb7c87d8","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","branch":"chore/remove-lsp-scaffold","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/g