{"parentUuid":"10e35336-91ac-4420-8ef7-d7deebdb6f0f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPH6bLuxvN7CjsEPF2He","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good thing I kept the worktrees — the stopped `addonlazy` fork had uncommitted fixes missing from #172: `fillAfter` (fixes the slowdown when most stories are requested), `warmUp` defaulting to `false` (since enabling it didn't speed up the first story), README docs for these options, plus updated tests and a changeset. I've saved that work as a patch and am starting a new fork off current `main` to land it.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1534,"cache_read_input_tokens":602397,"output_tokens":2809,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1429},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1534,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2809,"cache_read_input_tokens":602397,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1534,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1534},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":1,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"99e084dd-969a-4790-b1fe-78948cc1cb2a","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgPH6awqwcyFGEwMVTxaD","requestRef":"3adf8973-2a32-478a-adae-b82cc943a2e8","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"1173731b-d585-42e6-8afb-7f965c4c1b89","timestamp":"2026-10-25T16:34:17.368Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"chore/remove-lsp-scaffold","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"1173731b-d585-42e6-8afb-7f965c4c1b89","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPH6bLuxvN7CjsEPF2He","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0153i1CdU3tnmiUgFu2hBUKJ","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Land the salvaged fillAfter and warmUp work","subagent_type":"fork","isolation":"worktree","name":"salvage-lazy","prompt":"Track Y: land the salvaged work of the stopped addon fork. Patch: /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/worktree-backups/accb7ca7a9c75ecb5.patch (tracked-file diff against its HEAD ed2497fc, plus its untracked `.changeset/addon-lazy-session.md` appended at the end of the file after a `# untracked:` marker). It adds to the Storybook addon (packages/storybook): `fillAfter` (default 16: with `lazy`, once this many distinct components were asked for, resolve the rest in the background in one parallel pass; 0 never), `warmUp` default false (the original fork measured the background warm-up did not make the first story faster), README documentation for `lazy`, `fillAfter`, `warmUp`, updated tests/preset/index/provider/session, and the harness script. PR #172 (merged) already put the addon on the lazy session with lazy default true and warmUp default TRUE, but WITHOUT fillAfter and WITHOUT README docs; its measured weakness: a project read end to end (Spectrum 50 real stories) takes 1.1-1.3 s lazy vs 0.4 s eager, which fillAfter fixes. Do: branch off origin/main (PR #196 removing the lsp scaffold is open and unrelated; PR base `main`); apply the patch (`git apply --3way` or by hand): main's packages/storybook/src differs from the fork's base: main has `lookups.ts` (lookup building moved out of session.ts to satisfy oxlint max-lines 300 and `documentation()` made synchronous, no `.catch`, a `warmUp` private method with try/await) plus the schema-version readers (assertSchemaVersion/expandDiagnostics from schema.ts); keep those and the 300-line limit (put new code in lookups.ts or a new small module, e.g. a `fill.ts`); and core/binding: check whether the patch touches crates (it should not; `sessionComponentAnswers`, `sessionWarmUp` exist on main; the fill-in pass may use existing binding calls such as sessionDocgenInfo/sessionComponentAnswers with all keys; if a binding addition is needed keep it minimal). Then verify with the harness (pnpm --filter caliper-docgen-napi build:napi; pnpm --filter caliper-docgen-storybook build; node packages/storybook/scripts/storybook-parity.mjs --corpora /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/bench-corpus --only spectrum,chakra --limit 50 --out <file>): first-story latency must stay low, and the end-to-end total on Spectrum real stories (all 50) should approach the eager session's; also report peak RSS; answers identical to eager (the harness checks). Gates: `just lint doc-check machete typos` and `pnpm --filter caliper-docgen-storybook test` and `cargo nextest run --workspace --exclude caliper-docgen-napi --locked` exit codes read directly (never pipe through tail); CI green; changeset (use the patch's, adjusted). Time-box ~60 tool calls. Commits end with Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED; PR body ends with https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED; never push main/force-push/merge; /usr/bin/git with sandbox off, one plain git command per call. Report the before/after table (first story, total, peak RSS) vs main's addon."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1534,"cache_read_input_tokens":602397,"output_tokens":2809,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1429},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1534,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2809,"cache_read_input_tokens":602397,"cache_creation_i