{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","id":"25bc835e-dd8f-44ed-8c27-fc386bb588fe","timestamp":"2026-10-25T16:34:25.167Z","version":"2.1.308","querySource":"repl_main_thread:outputStyle:Concise","shapeHash":"695ec5a8802936862d1cd8c71e730e293e4e9e400bcbffb95f0146470866b732","params":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"3adf8973-2a32-478a-adae-b82cc943a2e8","keep":753,"tail":["09014939a5e298936d8befb8b768f11ee7b15d87a028aad0a733787eda2cd8e3","8d7f940016a4f69ccc1f3f93e02f4847cc16a821f063e72ffc2933e9761ce8ee","adb0715fa12119618aa7ecbdaadb7fa398b46987bfcd10794b89a57c2a3539e0"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",755,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"501875a420834e850ca77268415889989667bbd24ec86698ae434d81e45281e4"}
{"parentUuid":"41911f38-5d31-43c1-b09f-88dcdd8ac14d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPH8JEZuDVjiB4mpSVZd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The cleanup mostly worked. Five worktrees were left, and I've saved patch backups of their uncommitted changes, so nothing is lost.\n\n**What the script did**\n- **Remote:** all six remote branches deleted (`bench/runners`, `scratch/bench-runners-run`, `fix/chakra-missing-props`, `fix/story-matching-and-controls`, `fix/storybook-accuracy`, `perf/chakra-floor`). The fetch also pruned about 50 branches that merging had already deleted.\n- **Worktrees:** 19 removed.\n- **Local branches:** every planned branch is gone except the four checked out by the five remaining worktrees (listed below). My script's `sed` label broke on branch names containing `/`, which only hid the confirmation output; git still deleted the branches, and the remaining-branch check confirms it. The `pr1xx` scratch branches and about 40 `worktree-agent-*` branches were deleted. One `worktree-agent-*` branch (a482304b) is still held by its worktree.\n\n**What's left, and what to do with it**\n\n| Worktree | Branch | Uncommitted | Recommendation |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `agent-accb7ca7a9c75ecb5` | `feat/addon-lazy-session` | the stopped addon fork's later work | **Salvaged**, see below. Safe to remove (backed up). |\n| `agent-ac253a6938dfbbec1` | `perf/addon-threads-and-durability` | one edit to `lazy_bench.rs` (`--fresh N`) | Dropped experiment. Safe to remove (backed up, 1.5 KB). |\n| `agent-a95b63d52249414d6` | `fix/story-matching-rebased` | `packages/napi/index.js` | A file the napi build regenerates. Safe to remove (backed up). |\n| `agent-a9f89c0bcfd31444e` | `fix/indexed-access-resolved-object` | none (clean) | Locked by a live `claude bg-spare` process (pid 7405), not a stuck agent. Unlock, then remove. |\n| `agent-a482304b1a114609f` | `worktree-agent-a482304b1a114609f` | 8 modified resolver files (`memo.rs`, `global.rs`, `chain.rs`, …) and 7 `.snap.new` files | Not from this part of the session and I don't know its origin. It looks like an old uncommitted resolver experiment. I saved a 21 KB patch. **Your call.** |\n\nThe patches are in `/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/worktree-backups/`. To finish:\n```\ncd /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper\ngit worktree unlock .claude/worktrees/agent-a9f89c0bcfd31444e\nfor id in a95b63d52249414d6 a9f89c0bcfd31444e ac253a6938dfbbec1 accb7ca7a9c75ecb5; do git worktree remove --force .claude/worktrees/agent-$id; done\ngit branch -D fix/story-matching-rebased fix/indexed-access-resolved-object perf/addon-threads-and-durability feat/addon-lazy-session\n```\nLeave `agent-a482304b1a114609f` until you've looked at its patch.\n\n**The salvage**\nThe stopped addon fork's uncommitted work was more than scratch. It fixes the weakness I flagged in #172: a lazy session read end to end (Spectrum, all 50 real stories) takes 1.1–1.3 s against 0.4 s eager. The work adds:\n- `fillAfter` (default 16): once 16 distinct components are asked for, the rest resolve in one background parallel pass.\n- `warmUp` defaulting to `false`. #172 merged with it `true`, but that fork measured that it did not make the first story faster, which matches my runs.\n- README documentation for `lazy`, `fillAfter` and `warmUp`. Main's addon README doesn't mention them.\n\nThe new `salvage-lazy` fork is applying it onto current `main` (it has to fit the refactors #172 landed). It will re-run the harness on Spectrum and Chakra and report first story, total and peak memory against what's on `main`. Cap is about 60 tool calls.\n\nOpen now: #196 (LSP removal) and #160 (release), plus the `salvage-lazy` PR when it lands. Issue #1 (presets) is still open for your decision."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6246,"cache_read_input_tokens":603931,"output_tokens":1496,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6246,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1496,"cache_read_input_tokens":603931,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6246,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6246},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"dbb553d1-a8a3-4737-a159-d8a9107c843b","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgPH8HpGvk2h19Etd5h3w","requestRef":"25bc835e-dd8f-44ed-8c27-fc386bb588fe","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"d3fb47d9-5bd1-4c71-bb3d-2720fdf70c5f","timestamp":"2026-10-25T16:34:36.126Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"chore/remove-lsp-scaffold","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
