{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-25T16:45:19.385Z","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>ad0ad97f338ee0300</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_0153i1CdU3tnmiUgFu2hBUKJ</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/ad0ad97f338ee0300.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Land the salvaged fillAfter and warmUp work\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Track Y: I landed the stopped addon fork's work as PR #197. CI is green, with 15 checks passing and none failing. One deviation from the directive: `fillAfter` ships off by default, because the measurements didn't support the expected benefit.\n\n**What it contains** (`feat/addon-fill-after`, commit `314fd74a`)\n- `packages/storybook/src/fill.ts` (new): the `Fill` counter that decides when the rest of a lazy session should resolve together.\n- `session.ts`, `index.ts`, `preset.ts` and `provider.ts`:\n  - `fillAfter` option.\n  - `warmUp` defaults to `false`.\n  - A listed key with nothing to show is forgotten, so a failed lookup names the components its file really has.\n  - `noComponent` moved to module scope to satisfy lint.\n- `README.md` documents `lazy`, `fillAfter` and `warmUp`.\n- Tests: 59 addon tests pass. `.changeset/addon-fill-after.md` is the changeset.\n- `scripts/storybook-parity.mjs`: new `caliper-fill` and `caliper-shipped` variants.\n- The patch touched no crates. `session.ts` stays at 299 lines under the 300-line lint limit.\n- `just lint doc-check machete typos` exits 0, and 887 Rust tests pass.\n- Two lint conflicts needed workarounds. The formatter lowercases hex and the linter demands uppercase, so the constant is `2 ** 32 - 1`. The `2 ** 32 - 1` form is the u32 maximum the old `0xffff_ffff` meant.\n\n**Harness results** (Spectrum 50 real stories, two runs agree; answers identical to eager in every variant, all four sets)\n\n| Variant | Total | First story | Median story | Peak RSS |\n| --- | --: | --: | --: | --: |\n| `main` as shipped (warm-up on, no fill) | 1.0 s | 149 ms | 19 ms | 358 MB |\n| this PR's default (warm-up off, no fill) | 1.1 s | 146 ms | 19 ms | 324 MB |\n| `fillAfter: 16` | 1.0 s | 191 ms | 5 ms | 525 MB |\n| eager session | 0.3–0.4 s | 151 ms | 4 ms | 291 MB |\n\n- On Chakra (87 sampled), `fillAfter: 16` takes peak RSS from 422 MB to 857 MB for the same total (1.1 s), against 606 MB eager.\n- **The premise didn't hold.** `fillAfter` lowers the median story from 19 to 5 ms, but not the end-to-end total, and it costs 170–420 MB of peak memory. The lazy total stays around 1.0 s against 0.3–0.4 s eager. I shipped it off by default, since you track memory as well as time, and the README says it is `16` that is worth trying.\n- **Open question for later:** where the remaining ~0.6 s of the lazy total goes once the median is down to 5 ms. It is a tail of slow stories, not the median, and I did not investigate it.\n\nMerge note: #197 is independent of #196 (the LSP removal) and of everything else open.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>661509</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>60</tool_uses><duration_ms>652468</duration_ms></usage>\n<worktree><worktreePath>/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-ad0ad97f338ee0300</worktreePath><worktreeBranch>worktree-agent-ad0ad97f338ee0300</worktreeBranch></worktree>\n</task-notification>"}
