{"parentUuid":"d4f3c8f5-fca9-4163-b184-37ec3e5ed826","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPLjtHH53yHCphVfRfLw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2309,"cache_read_input_tokens":620213,"output_tokens":1489,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":308},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2309,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1489,"cache_read_input_tokens":620213,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2309,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2309},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":2338,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"84870f86-e352-496f-bf9c-8eb425ed95f1","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgPLjsqytAkTKpN5QZtf1","requestRef":"6d151210-caa9-411f-ab6b-4b9e8322e536","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"a9d46499-133a-43c6-920d-c048e3c2a617","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:21:53.186Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"perf/lazy-session-whole-demand","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"a9d46499-133a-43c6-920d-c048e3c2a617","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPLjtHH53yHCphVfRfLw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"PR #198 is open with all 16 CI checks passing. It closes most of the lazy session's end-to-end gap, with one memory cost that you should decide on.\n\n**The cause: my hypothesis was only half right.**\n- Memos were not being thrown away: 98% of memo entries carry over each growth of the dependency layer.\n- The time went into rebuilding the resolution context on every growth. That rebuild clones the project's named-type index.\n- Fifty requests on Spectrum caused 33 rebuilds, which was 137 of the 300 ms, plus 33 small dependency loads.\n\n**The fix.** After the layer has grown three times, one background thread loads every name the project takes from a package. The first three answers still load only what they reach, so first-story latency is unchanged. A session that looks at a few components never loads more. ADR 0016 and `docs/architecture/pipeline-orchestration.md` are updated.\n\n**Core bench, 50 random components one at a time**\n\n| Corpus | Summed time | Peak memory |\n| --- | --: | --: |\n| Spectrum | 240 → 42 ms | 129 → 133 MB |\n| antd | 157 → 35 ms | 104 → 106 MB |\n| Mantine | 47 → 43 ms | 101 → 101 MB |\n| shadcn | 254 → 77 ms | **122 → 192 MB** |\n| Chakra | 368 → 233 ms | 142 → 139 MB |\n\n**Storybook harness** (before → after)\n- Spectrum 50 real stories: 1.1 → 0.4 s, median story 20 → 5 ms. The eager session takes 0.3 s.\n- Spectrum 90 sampled: 0.9 → 0.5 s.\n- Chakra 92 sampled: 1.1 → 0.8 s, which equals the eager session.\n- First story and peak memory are unchanged within noise. Answers equal the eager session's in all 18 variant sets.\n\n**Corrections to the fork's claims.** Its result line says \"up to 10×\". The numbers show 2.75× through the addon on Spectrum, and 3–6× in the core bench. Treat it as 3–6×, not 10×.\n\n**The memory cost.** shadcn's peak memory rises from 122 to 192 MB after 50 requests (450 declaration files loaded instead of 181). That is still below its eager session's 234 MB, but it breaks the \"no memory regression\" rule you set. There is no switch back to the minimal layer. The other corpora are within noise.\n\n**A cheaper alternative the fork didn't attempt.** Make the context rebuild cheap by sharing the named-type index (for example behind an `Arc` or a persistent structure) instead of cloning it on each growth. That should give the same speedup without loading more files, so no shadcn memory rise. It's a larger change to the resolution context. I'd do it as a follow-up, and merge #198 first only if you accept the shadcn memory cost for now.\n\n**Verified:** `lazy_parity` over the fixtures and all five corpora passes in both configurations and both ask orders. New tests cover a few requests loading only what they reach, eight components growing the layer four times rather than eight, and ten rounds of requests racing the background load all equal a batch run. Lint and 890 workspace tests exit 0. The harness ran on Spectrum and Chakra only. shadcn, antd and Mantine were core-bench only.\n\nOpen PRs: #196 (LSP removal), #197 (`fillAfter`, off by default), #198 (this), #160 (release). Want me to start the shared-index fork?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2309,"cache_read_input_tokens":620213,"output_tokens":1489,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":308},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2309,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1489,"cache_read_input_tokens":620213,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2309,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2309},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"84870f86-e352-496f-bf9c-8eb425ed95f1","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgPLjsqytAkTKpN5QZtf1","requestRef":"6d151210-caa9-411f-ab6b-4b9e8322e536","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"711d6b2f-0f95-4e30-8fb0-45aa38939507","timestamp":"2026-10-25T17:21:59.540Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"perf/lazy-session-whole-demand","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
