{"parentUuid":"1226ebc3-00e0-41f2-8a90-124de48478c8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPQoMujmmFHQ9EjuSDN7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4516,"cache_read_input_tokens":622522,"output_tokens":3314,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":770},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4516,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3314,"cache_read_input_tokens":622522,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4516,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4516},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":6289,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"80a38a31-dc7b-4da0-b91c-49945a51116a","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgPQoLPCvv6u1jEKNVvGW","requestRef":"b54b2387-fdd7-4bfa-a502-ea4f3a444413","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"90b4d705-ca70-4f89-b55f-7d612fe70e43","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:15:27.099Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"perf/lazy-session-whole-demand","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"90b4d705-ca70-4f89-b55f-7d612fe70e43","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPQoMujmmFHQ9EjuSDN7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"On speed and memory it means the gap to react-docgen-typescript (RDT) should be wider than the last time I measured it, but I can't state current numbers. My last full RDT comparison was early in this session, on `main` through #152.\n\n**What I last measured against RDT** (before most of the speed work)\n- 19–89× faster, and 3–6× less memory, on batch extraction with dependencies loaded.\n- Component recall (hooks, contexts and helpers excluded): Mantine 89%, Chakra 79%, shadcn 98%, antd 85%, Spectrum 98%.\n- Same Storybook control per prop: 86–100%.\n\n**What has changed since, and which way it moves the comparison**\n- **Speed:** the resolver work cut Chakra's cold resolve by roughly 35–40%, and the cold-start and exit changes took several more milliseconds off. The ratio to RDT should widen. The lazy session makes a Storybook's first story arrive in 55–150 ms and a whole project read end to end cost about the same as eager.\n- **Coverage and accuracy:** these should now be better than the old recall numbers. The fallback rate dropped from 27–92% to 0–10%, and Chakra now resolves props it was dropping. The oracle's wrong-prop rate is 0.0% on the corpora we checked.\n- **What I can't claim:** that every one of those improvements is a net gain against RDT's own output. A better fallback rate says nothing directly about agreement with RDT, and I have not re-run that comparison.\n\n**There are two comparisons, and they are different**\n1. **RDT**, the batch extractor: our ground truth for coverage and the one the README speed claims are about.\n2. **Storybook's own docgen** (react-component-meta): what the addon actually replaces. Against it, the addon was 1.2–5× faster per run, with Spectrum's real stories as the exception until #158. With #198, Spectrum's 50 stories take 0.4 s against Storybook's 1.2–1.3 s, and Chakra's equal the eager session.\n\nBecause the numbers I'd quote are mixed from different points in the session, I'd rather measure it once, cleanly. Nothing else is running now, so the machine is quiet. I'm starting a fork that builds `main` and the #198 branch, and measures all five corpora against RDT on time, peak memory and quality, plus the Storybook-level comparison."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4516,"cache_read_input_tokens":622522,"output_tokens":3314,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":770},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4516,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3314,"cache_read_input_tokens":622522,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4516,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4516},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"80a38a31-dc7b-4da0-b91c-49945a51116a","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgPQoLPCvv6u1jEKNVvGW","requestRef":"b54b2387-fdd7-4bfa-a502-ea4f3a444413","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"5e89ac07-452b-4a35-8970-b3ba61b0684e","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:15:33.112Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"perf/lazy-session-whole-demand","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"5e89ac07-452b-4a35-8970-b3ba61b0684e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPQoMujmmFHQ9EjuSDN7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015whGvwPPFux2BhCVaZxFfi","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Clean comparison against RDT and Storybook docgen","subagent_type":"fork","isolation":"worktree","name":"compare-rdt","prompt":"Track AA: one clean, honest comparison of caliper against react-docgen-typescript (RDT) and against Storybook's own docgen (react-component-meta), on current code. Measure only; do not change product code (you may add the numbers to docs/performance.md in a PR if everything is clean, see end). Machine: nothing else is running, keep it that way (do not start other heavy jobs); interleave runs and take best-of-N. Builds: (a) caliper at origin/main (release CLI + napi binding), (b) caliper at origin/perf/lazy-session-whole-demand (PR #198, lazy session whole-demand load), release CLI + napi. Corpora: /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/bench-corpus (mantine/packages/@mantine/core/src, chakra-ui/packages/react/src, shadcn-ui/apps/v4, ant-design/components, react-spectrum/packages) with their installed dependencies. Existing scripts from earlier in the session are in /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/bench (quality.py, real_recall.py, loss_patterns.py, mismatch_kinds.py, perf_vs_rdt.py, besttime.py, outsize.py, deps-caliper.sh, sem-caliper.sh, missing_components.py, chakra_missing.py): reuse and fix them (hyperfine 2 JSON schema differs from 1: `measurements[].time_wall_clock.value` and `memory_peak_resident`); RDT is run by apps/validate (see scripts/parity.py and docs/parity.md for how RDT is invoked and its baseline in scripts/parity-baseline.json). Report, per corpus: (1) SPEED: RDT wall time and peak RSS vs caliper CLI (default and --load-dependencies --html-attributes full as RDT-format output `--format rdt`) cold cache and warm cache; ratios; also caliper's lazy session first-component and 10/50-component latency (crates/core/examples/lazy_bench.rs) vs RDT; (2) QUALITY vs RDT with the project's agreed semantics (formatting differences like quotes, parentheses, Array<T> vs T[], trailing `;` are NOT meaningful): components found vs RDT's, with the plausible-component filter used earlier (hooks, contexts, helpers excluded: see real_recall.py), prop recall (share of RDT's props we report), same Storybook control kind per shared prop, meaningful type disagreements (count and classes: wrong, less precise, opaque, more precise), props we report that RDT does not, defaults, descriptions; plus the TS 7.1 oracle score (`python3 scripts/equivalence.py --oracle` or `scripts/parity.py oracle`, tsc available in apps/validate) for caliper main; (3) STORYBOOK LEVEL: node packages/storybook/scripts/storybook-parity.mjs --corpora ... --only <each> --limit 100 for caliper main and the #198 build (pnpm --filter caliper-docgen-napi build:napi; pnpm --filter caliper-docgen-storybook build for each checkout): fallback rate, answered counts, first story, total, median, peak RSS, extra/missing props, default and control-kind differences vs react-component-meta. Compare with the numbers from the start of this session where you can (mantine/chakra/shadcn/antd/spectrum: 19-89x faster than RDT, 3-6x less memory, same-Storybook-control 86-100%, exact text 19-78%, real recall Mantine 89%/Chakra 79%/shadcn 98%/antd 85%/Spectrum 98%, fallback rates 70/56-92/46/42/38%) and say what improved, what did not, and anything that regressed. Be explicit about caveats (sample sizes, machine, warm vs cold). Output: a markdown report at /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/compare-rdt.md plus a summary in your final message with the key tables. If all numbers are clean, open a non-draft PR (base main) updating docs/performance.md and the README speed/quality claims with the new measured numbers and the date, with a changeset only if shipped text requires one, `just lint doc-check machete typos` exit code read directly. Time-box ~70 tool calls. Commits end with Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED; PR body ends with https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED; never push main/force-push/merge; /usr/bin/git with sandbox off, one plain git command per call."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4516,"cache_read_input_tokens":622522,"output_tokens":3314,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":770},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4516,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3314,"cache_read_input_tokens":622522,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4516,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4516},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_015whGvwPPFux2BhCVaZxFfi":{"description":"Clean comparison against RDT and Storybook docgen","subagent_type":"fork","isolation":"worktree","name":"compare-rdt","prompt":"Track AA: one clean, honest comparison of caliper against react-docgen-typescript (RDT) and against Storybook's own docgen (react-component-meta), on current code. Measure only; do not change product code (you may add the numbers to docs/performance.md in a PR if everything is clean, see end). Machine: nothing else is running, keep it that way (do not start other heavy jobs); interleave runs and take best-of-N. Builds: (a) caliper at origin/main (release CLI + napi binding), (b) caliper at origin/perf/lazy-session-whole-demand (PR #198, lazy session whole-demand load), release CLI +