{"parentUuid":"57fcd379-46c1-479e-87a3-f69fdf29e3dd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPR6eoT5giEodLyXNQGR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015Hqi1yT525kL7hZhiAXb3d","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Make the lazy context rebuild cheap","subagent_type":"fork","isolation":"worktree","name":"cheap-context","prompt":"Track AB: make the lazy session's resolution-context rebuild cheap, so a dependency-layer growth no longer costs a clone of the project's index. Branch off origin/perf/lazy-session-whole-demand (PR #198, open, not merged: it makes a lazy session load the whole dependency demand set in the background after 3 growths; it fixed a 3x end-to-end gap but raised shadcn's peak RSS 122 -> 192 MB after 50 requests because 450 declaration files load instead of 181). Open your PR STACKED on it: base = perf/lazy-session-whole-demand (the repo deletes head branches on merge, so merging bottom-up retargets it to main), and say so in the body. Finding from #198's investigation: memos were NOT the loss (98% of memo entries carry over a growth); the time went into rebuilding the resolution context on every growth, once per new component: the rebuild clones the project's named-type index (and probably other per-layer tables); 50 requests on Spectrum caused 33 rebuilds = 137 of 300 ms, plus 33 small dependency loads. Goal: make a growth cheap (share the project index across context rebuilds with Arc / persistent or layered structure so only the dependency layer's additions are new; avoid cloning tables that did not change; look at ResolutionContext / Engine construction in crates/core/src/pipeline/revision/lazy.rs, NamedTypeIndex (named_type_index.rs), dependency_types::load/extend, `Revision::grow`), then REMOVE the need for loading the whole demand set eagerly: keep #198's background whole-demand load only if it is still a net win after rebuilds are cheap, otherwise make it opt-in or delete it, so shadcn's peak RSS returns to ~122 MB while Spectrum/antd/Chakra totals stay at #198's level. First measure with crates/core/examples/lazy_bench.rs (50 random components one at a time, loadDependencies + full HTML attributes; summed request time, peak RSS) on all five corpora (/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/bench-corpus): baseline = #198 and = main, then after. Gates: summed 50-request time at or below #198's (Spectrum 42 ms, antd 35, Mantine 43, shadcn 77, Chakra 233), peak RSS at or below main's (Spectrum ~129 MB, antd 104, Mantine 101, shadcn 122, Chakra 142) on every corpus; first-story latency not worse; answers identical to batch (lazy_parity over fixtures and all corpora, both ask orders; the Storybook harness for Spectrum/Chakra: node packages/storybook/scripts/storybook-parity.mjs --corpora ... --only spectrum,chakra --limit 50 after building binding and addon); batch extraction output byte-identical to main (`just equivalence`). Tests: exact-value test that many requests cause no per-growth index clone (a counter/Arc::strong_count or pointer-equality assertion), concurrency test racing requests. Update ADR 0016 and docs/architecture/pipeline-orchestration.md if the contract changes. `just lint doc-check machete typos` and `cargo nextest run --workspace --exclude caliper-docgen-napi --locked` exit codes read directly (never pipe through tail); CI green; changeset. Time-box ~80 tool calls. Commits end with Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED; PR body ends with https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED; never push main/force-push/merge; /usr/bin/git with sandbox off, one plain git command per call."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1409,"cache_read_input_tokens":644018,"output_tokens":3326,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":604},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"