{"parentUuid":"e45ece0a-8496-40f5-8a43-beda44ad23df","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ca44a88d-c011-41e7-928d-007d1864c82b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015Hqi1yT525kL7hZhiAXb3d","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Async agent launched successfully. (This tool result is internal metadata — never quote or paste any part of it, including the agentId below, into a user-facing reply.)\nagentId: a8b955cfb6063c0bc (internal ID - do not mention to user. Use SendMessage with to: 'a8b955cfb6063c0bc', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent.)\nThe agent is working in the background. You will be notified automatically when it completes. You know nothing about its results until that notification arrives — do not report, assume, or predict them; continue other work or respond to the user in the meantime.\nDo not duplicate this agent's work — avoid working with the same files or topics it is using.\noutput_file: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/a8b955cfb6063c0bc.output\nDo NOT Read or tail this file via the shell tool — it is the full subagent JSONL transcript and reading it will overflow your context. If the user asks for progress, say the agent is still running; you'll get a completion notification."}]}]},"uuid":"b40c251d-1a84-4a3d-b9d9-0d3b2b2b4925","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:19:24.215Z","toolUseResult":{"isAsync":true,"status":"async_launched","agentId":"a8b955cfb6063c0bc","description":"Make the lazy context rebuild cheap","resolvedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","prompt":"Track AB: make the lazy session's resolution-context rebuild cheap, so a dependency-layer growth no longer costs a clone of the project's index. Branch off origin/perf/lazy-session-whole-demand (PR #198, open, not merged: it makes a lazy session load the whole dependency demand set in the background after 3 growths; it fixed a 3x end-to-end gap but raised shadcn's peak RSS 122 -> 192 MB after 50 requests because 450 declaration files load instead of 181). Open your PR STACKED on it: base = perf/lazy-session-whole-demand (the repo deletes head branches on merge, so merging bottom-up retargets it to main), and say so in the body. Finding from #198's investigation: memos were NOT the loss (98% of memo entries carry over a growth); the time went into rebuilding the resolution context on every growth, once per new component: the rebuild clones the project's named-type index (and probably other per-layer tables); 50 requests on Spectrum caused 33 rebuilds = 137 of 300 ms, plus 33 small dependency loads. Goal: make a growth cheap (share the project index across context rebuilds with Arc / persistent or layered structure so only the dependency layer's additions are new; avoid cloning tables that did not change; look at ResolutionContext / Engine construction in crates/core/src/pipeline/revision/lazy.rs, NamedTypeIndex (named_type_index.rs), dependency_types::load/extend, `Revision::grow`), then REMOVE the need for loading the whole demand set eagerly: keep #198's background whole-demand load only if it is still a net win after rebuilds are cheap, otherwise make it opt-in or delete it, so shadcn's peak RSS returns to ~122 MB while Spectrum/antd/Chakra totals stay at #198's level. First measure with crates/core/examples/lazy_bench.rs (50 random components one at a time, loadDependencies + full HTML attributes; summed request time, peak RSS) on all five corpora (/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/bench-corpus): baseline = #198 and = main, then after. Gates: summed 50-request time at or below #198's (Spectrum 42 ms, antd 35, Mantine 43, shadcn 77, Chakra 233), peak RSS at or below main's (Spectrum ~129 MB, antd 104, Mantine 101, shadcn 122, Chakra 142) on every corpus; first-story latency not worse; answers identical to batch (lazy_parity over fixtures and all corpora, both ask orders; the Storybook harness for Spectrum/Chakra: node packages/storybook/scripts/storybook-parity.mjs --corpora ... --only spectrum,chakra --limit 50 after building binding and addon); batch extraction output byte-identical to main (`just equivalence`). Tests: exact-value test that many requests cause no per-growth index clone (a counter/Arc::strong_count or pointer-equality assertion), concurrency test racing requests. Update ADR 0016 and docs/architecture/pipeline-orchestration.md if the contract changes. `just lint doc-check machete typos` and `cargo nextest run --workspace --exclude caliper-docgen-napi --locked` exit codes read directly (never pipe through tail); CI green; changeset. Time-box ~80 tool calls. Commits end with Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED; PR body ends with https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED; never push main/force-push/merge; /usr/bin/git with sandbox off, one plain git command per call.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/a8b955cfb6063c0bc.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"9bd93712-b971-43e2-9a4e-bd87a1348967","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","branch":"chore/reset-equivalence-allow-list","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e45ece0a-8