{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","bridgeSessionId":"cse_01D7CJmXuD2ASqfBYm7Lk4WZ","lastSequenceNum":21749,"ownerAccountUuid":"138d593e-e185-4f72-89f2-82e1a501f134","ownerOrganizationUuid":"602db9b4-428d-49e6-a99c-64152cc62a79"}
{"parentUuid":"dca03a09-4053-471b-b1ff-2b9ea89d0770","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPR8dTeRqXYNgTDbsMSa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Two improvement forks are running now, and the RDT comparison is parked.\n\n**`cheap-context`** makes the lazy session's context rebuild cheap. It is stacked on #198, because it fixes #198's cost.\n- **What it fixes.** #198 found the time went into rebuilding the resolution context on every dependency-layer growth, which clones the project's named-type index (137 of 300 ms on Spectrum). That fork fixed it by loading the whole demand set, which cost shadcn 122 → 192 MB.\n- **The goal.** Share the index across rebuilds so a growth only adds the dependency layer's additions. Then drop #198's eager whole-demand load, or keep it only if it is still a net win.\n- **The gates.** Summed 50-request time at or below #198's on every corpus (Spectrum 42 ms, antd 35, Mantine 43, shadcn 77, Chakra 233). Peak memory back at `main`'s (shadcn ~122 MB). Answers identical to batch.\n- **Merge order.** #198, then its stacked PR.\n\n**`antd-gaps`** closes the remaining parity gaps. It branches off `main` and avoids the lazy-session files `cheap-context` owns.\n- antd props Storybook lists that we lack (`PurePanel` 33, `Col` breakpoints 7, `CheckableTagGroup` 5, `Progress` aria 2, `ref` on 3 components).\n- Spectrum `Avatar.alt`, where an empty-string default still differs from Storybook's.\n- The shadcn control-kind mismatches left after #188, with `z.infer` cases staying a documented gap that needs the checker.\n\nI've held two items until `cheap-context` has measured, so timings stay clean:\n- **Defaults-after-chain.** Apply component defaults after a chain resolves, so the shared bases like `JsxStyleProps` are resolved once. Estimated at up to 8–10% of Chakra's wall time.\n- **TS 7.1 fallback.** The optional fallback for degraded components, behind an ADR. It would handle cases like `z.infer`.\n\nOpen PRs now: #196 (LSP removal), #197 (`fillAfter`, off by default), #198 (lazy whole-demand load), #199 (empty allow-list) and #160 (release)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7512,"cache_read_input_tokens":645427,"output_tokens":767,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7512,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":767,"cache_read_input_tokens":645427,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7512,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7512},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"653ee919-d6e0-420c-9e50-d7281646d755","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgPR8csvPKQRvLMkJDL3d","requestRef":"1e338896-4fdd-4854-b796-b41e70c77007","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"4bab3fb2-03d5-4a61-9aef-554b0becea74","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:19:33.247Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"chore/reset-equivalence-allow-list","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
