{"parentUuid":"874029e3-5c68-4dfd-8f11-060ebc82bf14","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPRuP7hBbXQgM2pktj7k","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":870,"cache_read_input_tokens":652939,"output_tokens":2627,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1282},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":870,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2627,"cache_read_input_tokens":652939,"cache_creation_input_tokens":870,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":870},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":10001,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"d3b5e020-6e1f-4f12-9617-a0b27d77eeac","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgPRuNcSc3Y1c3gevNvSq","requestRef":"5e0fe442-bf06-44e9-a2cc-a0ae25ef0874","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"f1a460f1-07eb-4ced-b408-822e878fd9a4","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:29:43.299Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"perf/shared-index-on-growth","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"f1a460f1-07eb-4ced-b408-822e878fd9a4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPRuP7hBbXQgM2pktj7k","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"These are estimates, not measurements. I've extrapolated from the last full RDT comparison (early in the session) and the per-PR numbers since, and a clean run (the parked `compare-rdt` job) would replace them.\n\n**Speed against react-docgen-typescript (RDT), batch with dependencies**\n- **Then:** 19–89× faster, depending on the corpus.\n- **Since:** Chakra with dependencies went from about 343 ms to about 240 ms (#175 −21%, #177 −14%, #182 −4%, #192 −4%), roughly −30%. The others improved about 10% (Spectrum 107 → 93 ms, shadcn 121 → 110, antd 61 → 55, Mantine 69 → 61 on cold runs).\n- **My estimate now:** about 20–100×. Chakra's ratio is up roughly 1.4×, the others about 1.1×. Same order of magnitude as before, a bit wider.\n- **Confidence:** medium. RDT's own time is unchanged, so the ratio moves only with ours. I don't have a per-corpus breakdown of which corpus held the 19×.\n\n**Memory against RDT**\n- **Then:** 3–6× less.\n- **Since:** Chakra with dependencies fell about 11% (388 → 344 MB), Spectrum about 5%, and the others are flat.\n- **My estimate now:** about 3.3–6.5× less for batch. A lazy session holds far less than batch (Chakra about 140 MB after 50 components, against 530 MB batch earlier), but I can't turn that into an RDT ratio without a run.\n- **Caveat:** #198 raises shadcn's lazy peak by 70 MB, and `cheap-context` is meant to undo that.\n\n**Quality against RDT**\n- **Components found** (hooks and helpers excluded): Mantine 89%, Chakra 79%, shadcn 98%, antd 85%, Spectrum 98% earlier. I'd guess flat to a few points up on Chakra and Mantine (the wrapper and Ark/Radix fixes), flat elsewhere. Low confidence.\n- **Props reported:** up on Chakra (+676 props and 36 false circular diagnostics removed from the Ark intersection fix, plus the wrapper-call props), and up on shadcn (+175 defaults).\n- **Same Storybook control per prop:** 86–100% earlier. I'd say about 90–100% now. The nearby evidence is shadcn's mismatch with Storybook's docgen falling from 8.2% to 5.2% of shared props, and antd at about 6%.\n- **Wrong against the TS 7.1 oracle:** 0.0% on Mantine, shadcn and antd, down from 0.25–0.34% at the baseline, and \"less precise\" down on shadcn (14.5% → 10.8%) and Spectrum (30.2% → 14.9%).\n- **Exact type text:** about the same as before (19–78%), since the gap there is mostly formatting we agreed not to count.\n\n**Against Storybook's own docgen (what the addon replaces)**\n- **Then:** 1.2–5× faster per run, except Spectrum's real stories, which were slower. Fallback to Storybook's docgen on 38–92% of components.\n- **Now (harness, Spectrum 50 real stories):** about 0.4 s against 1.2–1.3 s, about 3× faster. Chakra with dependencies is about 420 MB against about 1,190 MB, about 2.8× less memory. The fallback rate is 0–10% on all five corpora.\n\n**What I'd bet on**\n- Speed and memory ratios: a modest improvement, roughly 10–45% depending on corpus.\n- Quality: clearly better on Chakra and shadcn, about equal elsewhere. No known regression.\n\n**What I don't know.** Whether the recall figures moved, how big RDT's own noise is, and the machine-load effects on these runs (several forks were running). A quiet run would settle it, so I'd put the clean comparison right after the current improvements."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":870,"cache_read_input_tokens":652939,"output_tokens":2627,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1282},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":870,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2627,"cache_read_input_tokens":652939,"cache_creation_input_tokens":870,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":870},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"d3b5e020-6e1f-4f12-9617-a0b27d77eeac","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgPRuNcSc3Y1c3gevNvSq","requestRef":"5e0fe442-bf06-44e9-a2cc-a0ae25ef0874","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"a285bda5-be8f-4c07-91ba-7917a03c40d3","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:29:53.119Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"perf/shared-index-on-growth","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
