{"parentUuid":"a5510716-cf50-4f51-9b10-00b455efc4ad","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPSSXbHow2SniEc2tyPB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"These come straight from the estimates in my last table, so they're rough. I use the \"deps on\" column because it compares like for like: with dependencies off, Chakra's RDT run does far more work than ours.\n\n**Speed against RDT, deps on (×faster)**\n\n| | Baseline (0.4.0) | Estimate now |\n| --- | --: | --: |\n| Median | 28× | 31× |\n| Geometric mean | 28× | ~36× |\n| Mean | 30× | ~43× |\n\n- The mean is pulled up by Chakra (about 45× → about 100×). The median is the honest headline.\n- Deps off: median about 35×, geometric mean about 56×, if you want the no-dependencies figure.\n\n**Memory against RDT, deps on (×less)**\n\n| | Baseline (0.4.0) | Estimate now |\n| --- | --: | --: |\n| Median | 4.2× | ~4.5× |\n| Mean | 4.7× | ~5.5× |\n\n- Deps off: median about 9× less.\n\n**Improvement since the baseline**\n- **Speed:** the median ratio is up about 11% and the geometric mean about 29%. Most of that is Chakra (caliper's own time down about 55%). The other corpora improved about 10%.\n- **Memory:** the median ratio is up about 7% and the mean about 17%, again mostly Chakra (1,461 MiB to about 345 MiB). The others are within a few percent.\n\n**Plain headline:** about 30× faster and about 4.5× less memory than RDT at the median with dependencies loaded, about 35× and 9× with them off. For react-docgen I have no per-library figures, so the only data point stays 1.15× on the shared Node harness."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2254,"cache_read_input_tokens":670434,"output_tokens":1176,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":616},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"eph