{"parentUuid":"7e100ad2-9fb8-465b-a22b-38335648864b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPSeShCmQPMvq5E6s454","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"It's a good position, but I'd phrase it more carefully, because two parts of that sentence are weaker than they sound.\n\n**Where \"accuracy of RDT\" holds (structural, deps loaded, baseline 0.4.0)**\n- **Mantine, Chakra, Spectrum:** 98.6–99.7% of RDT's props reported, and 93–100% the same Storybook control.\n- **antd:** about 80% of RDT's props, 95% the same control.\n- **shadcn:** the weak case, about 40% of RDT's props structurally (I'd guess 45–55% now), 87% the same control. The TS 7.1 opt-in gets it to about 96%, at 0.5–9 s.\n- **Exact type text** matches RDT only 19–78% of the time, mostly formatting we've agreed not to count. The true disagreement rate is far lower, but I haven't recounted it recently.\n\nSo the fair claim is \"RDT-level accuracy on most libraries, with a known gap on libraries like shadcn that lean on installed package types (closable with the opt-in)\". It isn't blanket parity.\n\n**Where \"at the speed of react-docgen\" is conservative.** My estimate is that we're faster than react-docgen, about 5–15× on compute, so \"at least as fast\" is safe. But the measured evidence is one data point: 1.15× on the site's Node harness. I'd back that with a measured run before publishing a multiple.\n\n**Why it matters**\n- RDT is accurate but slow (seconds, up to 27 s on Chakra). react-docgen is fast but shallow. Being close to the first on accuracy and at or past the second on speed is the whole pitch for Storybook.\n- The addon makes it concrete: 0–10% of components fall back to Storybook's default, against 38–92% earlier.\n\n**To make it publishable**\n1. The parked clean comparison (RDT, react-docgen and react-component-meta, same machine, same methodology as the site's 21-library harness), run after the current improvements land.\n2. Then update the site's stale lines (Storybook addon, TS 7.1 status, LSP, name and distribution) with measured numbers.\n\nRunning now: `cheap-context` and `antd-gaps`. The antd work should lift the antd row, and the shadcn row is the next biggest accuracy lever after them. Want me to queue a fork on that once `antd-gaps` reports?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1925,"cache_read_input_tokens":673956,"output_tokens":1094,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":311},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1925,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1094,"cache_read_input_tokens":673956,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1925,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1925},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"ee6401c0-fe33-46ea-93b7-22034731346f","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgPSeSHQ4RbJaZrkexEM4","requestRef":"92a2cac1-f26f-455e-aaca-288f6884b636","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"6eb9cc5d-88c3-4dfe-ad43-0717f9222ccf","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:39:25.424Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"perf/shared-index-on-growth","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
