{"parentUuid":"d52f5d49-0a64-4baf-8ba2-332974702e54","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPSwT3kVApd4hdNPPDsx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1310,"cache_read_input_tokens":678937,"output_tokens":2690,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":488},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1310,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2690,"cache_read_input_tokens":678937,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1310,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1310},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":4250,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"245438fb-525e-4daf-901d-880542e0264b","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgPSwSgvzsbe4m2ZMecmd","requestRef":"0a18a0cb-4d2d-4850-8597-9c9d25d5298d","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"24bde59b-64ec-4e25-9dd5-9b2e8a32f923","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:43:15.116Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"perf/shared-index-on-growth","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"24bde59b-64ec-4e25-9dd5-9b2e8a32f923","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPSwT3kVApd4hdNPPDsx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Agreed on flipping the default, with two caveats. Dependencies loaded no longer costs much in absolute terms, but my evidence that it's acceptable \"even compared to react-docgen\" is thin. I'm also not convinced we're close on on-demand TS 7.1.\n\n**Why flipping is justified**\n- The blocker in STATUS.md was Chakra at 1.3 GB and 0.5 s. It's now about 345 MB and 240 ms, in batch.\n- The other four corpora add 3–17 ms and 2–30 MB with dependencies on (Mantine 53 → 55 ms, antd 61 → 70 ms, Spectrum 116 → 121 ms at the last record).\n- In exchange Chakra goes from 0.1% to 98.6% of RDT's props, shadcn from 6% to 40%, and antd from 72% to 80%.\n- The addon already defaults it on, so the CLI, config and Vite plugin would just match it.\n\n**The caveat on react-docgen.** My only measurement against it is the site's Node harness (1.15×). Chakra at 240 ms is still tens of times faster than RDT, but whether it beats react-docgen in that mode is untested. It doesn't block the flip, but it means I wouldn't write \"faster than react-docgen with dependencies\" until the clean comparison runs.\n\n**On-demand TS 7.1: I'd say we're not close.** What exists is the whole-project opt-in (#154). The degraded-components-only fallback isn't started. It needs:\n- Detecting degraded components inside the lazy session and querying a warm `tsc` for just those.\n- A version range with a startup self-check, instead of the exact `7.1.0-beta` pin.\n- An ADR, since the current rule is \"experimental opt-in; `auto` needs oracle evidence\".\n- TS 7.1 stable, which the site says is expected 2026-11-24.\n\nTwo sensible steps: do the dependencies default now, then scope the fallback as a design fork.\n\nI'm starting the dependencies-default fork now. Other forks are still running, so it measures interleaved and the timings carry some noise."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1310,"cache_read_input_tokens":678937,"output_tokens":2690,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":488},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1310,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2690,"cache_read_input_tokens":678937,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1310,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1310},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"245438fb-525e-4daf-901d-880542e0264b","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgPSwSgvzsbe4m2ZMecmd","requestRef":"0a18a0cb-4d2d-4850-8597-9c9d25d5298d","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"33ac6795-b480-4826-aeeb-98f652408984","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:43:20.373Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"perf/shared-index-on-growth","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"33ac6795-b480-4826-aeeb-98f652408984","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPSwT3kVApd4hdNPPDsx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01P26HhZzCjaq3gXpUPv7ZbT","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Make --load-dependencies the default","subagent_type":"fork","isolation":"worktree","name":"deps-default","prompt":"Track AD: make dependency loading the default. Branch off origin/main (open PRs #196-#199, #160 and in-flight forks cheap-context (stacked on #198) and antd-gaps are unrelated; PR base `main`). Read docs/adr/0010-load-dependency-declarations-by-name.md and docs/adr/README.md rules and the adr skill (docs/adr/0000-template.md); STATUS.md says `--load-dependencies` was off by default and \"becomes the default in 0.5.0 once that cost is fixed\" (Chakra 1.3 GB / 0.5 s then; now ~345 MB / ~240 ms batch, measured). The Storybook addon already defaults `loadDependencies: true`. Do: (1) write ADR 0019 (succinct, no hard wrap, banned words per docs/adr/README.md, ground every claim in a number you measured) superseding 0010's 'off by default' clause: dependency loading is on by default; `--no-load-dependencies` / `loadDependencies: false` (CLI, docgen.config.ts, NAPI JsExtractOptions, Vite plugin, addon) turns it off; update the ADR index; (2) flip the defaults everywhere the default is set: PipelineOptions default (check how `load_dependencies` is declared; a Default change is a behavior change but not an API-shape change), CLI flag semantics (add `--no-load-dependencies`; keep `--load-dependencies` accepted as a no-op alias for compatibility), config schema (crates/cli/src/config.rs; docs; JSON schema), NAPI/packages/napi index.d.ts docs, Vite plugin option default and docs, README(s), docs/STATUS.md, docs/architecture/*, docs/parity.md, scripts (parity.py, equivalence.py, scorecard.py use `--load-dependencies` explicitly or rely on defaults: keep their meaning: baselines recorded with explicit modes must still compare like for like; update scripts/parity-baseline.json only if the tool says so), fixtures/snapshots that depended on the old default (expect snapshot changes only where deps affect output: the 7 corpus snapshots use fixtures without installed packages so they should not change; verify); (3) measure before/after for DEFAULT-mode runs on the five corpora at /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/bench-corpus (hyperfine best-of-N interleaved; machine is shared with other forks so repeat, report noise): wall time, peak RSS, props reported, unresolved warnings, vs the old default (deps off) and vs RDT's props; put the table in the ADR/PR; also measure a project WITHOUT node_modules installed (e.g. a fresh clone without install) to confirm graceful behavior: no crash, the same diagnostics as before (UNRESOLVABLE_IMPORT warnings), negligible time cost; and a monorepo layout (workspace packages) sanity check; (4) gates: `just equivalence` between old-default and new-default is EXPECTED to differ on corpora with installed deps: do not allow-list wholesale: instead compare new default with explicit `--load-dependencies` on the old build: must be byte-identical; `lazy_parity`; `just lint doc-check machete typos` and `cargo nextest run --workspace --exclude caliper-docgen-napi --locked` exit codes read directly (never pipe through tail); pnpm tests for touched packages; cargo semver-checks / SemVer CI job green (a changed Default is not an API break, but check); CI green; changeset (minor: default behavior changes). Time-box ~70 tool calls. Commits end with Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED; PR body ends with https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED; never push main/force-push/merge; /usr/bin/git with sandbox off, one plain git command per call."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1310,"cache_read_i