{"parentUuid":"95a29323-96aa-4ab3-b5b9-22cfd6061348","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPT9vzcAoBMQF9evJRrQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":795,"cache_read_input_tokens":686720,"output_tokens":2235,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1336},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":795,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2235,"cache_read_input_tokens":686720,"cache_creation_input_tokens":795,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":795},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":11858,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"58db554b-506a-4956-83af-76d6b872dc15","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgPT9vd2nzFoPQFBvhbVq","requestRef":"77412626-f3c9-4963-bac0-778b95df2384","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"a536fc92-52dc-47aa-8a65-dc4102b6fce5","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:46:09.336Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"perf/shared-index-on-growth","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"a536fc92-52dc-47aa-8a65-dc4102b6fce5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPT9vzcAoBMQF9evJRrQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, that makes sense, and it's the right shape for the on-demand TS 7.1 fallback. Most of the signals already exist.\n\n**What we already have to build the score from**\n- **Diagnostics with codes:** `UNRESOLVABLE_IMPORT`, `OPAQUE_TYPE`, `INDEXED_ACCESS_OPAQUE`, `TEMPLATE_LITERAL_OPAQUE`, `GENERIC_ARGUMENT_MISMATCH`, `CIRCULAR_REFERENCE`, max-depth, each with the list of components it affects. The addon's fallback rule already uses this: warning or error means hand the component on.\n- **How each type was found:** declaration-read, structurally evaluated, a hand-written shortcut (`known.rs`, like `VariantProps`), or left opaque.\n- **How the component was detected:** `DetectionRule` evidence, where name-based wrapper heuristics are the shakiest.\n\n**Shape I'd give it**\n- A small ordered level per prop, not a float: exact (read from a declaration or literal), evaluated (known operands), shortcut (a hand table), opaque or unresolved. A component's confidence is the lowest of its props, combined with how it was detected. A level is testable and explainable; a float adds false precision.\n- Policy: components below \"evaluated\" go to a warm `tsc` for that component only. A new `auto` mode would do this where TS 7.1 is installed, and the result records provenance (an Info diagnostic saying `tsc` answered).\n\n**The risk, and how to check it**\n- The score only helps if low-confidence props are where we're actually wrong. Some past bugs were confidently wrong with no diagnostic: the shadcn `VariantProps` lookup by bare name (a shortcut, so it would be caught) and antd's union-props branch (silent, so it wouldn't).\n- The TS 7.1 oracle gives per-prop verdicts, so we can measure it: of the props the oracle calls wrong or less precise, what share would have been routed to `tsc`, and how much of the routed set is unnecessary work? That decides the thresholds.\n\n**Cost**\n- Routing about the 0–10% of components that fall back today keeps `tsc` traffic small. The first query pays checker startup, so a Storybook story that can't wait should go to the next provider while the checker warms.\n\nI'd start with a measure-only fork before any design: inventory the signals, compute the levels offline on the five corpora, and report how well they predict oracle disagreement. That tells us whether the idea works on our data before we build the `tsc` path. Want me to start it? Running now: `cheap-context`, `antd-gaps`, `deps-default`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":795,"cache_read_input_tokens":686720,"output_tokens":2235,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1336},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":795,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2235,"cache_read_input_tokens":686720,"cache_creation_input_tokens":795,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":795},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"58db554b-506a-4956-83af-76d6b872dc15","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgPT9vd2nzFoPQFBvhbVq","requestRef":"77412626-f3c9-4963-bac0-778b95df2384","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"3ae6259a-d778-4ca7-9367-06163874cdf1","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:46:15.915Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"perf/shared-index-on-growth","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
