{"parentUuid":"09956bec-5bfd-4b14-828e-34e777042557","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"caa39018-5431-4b34-ba4c-0b7e3de61441","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a8b955cfb6063c0bc</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_015Hqi1yT525kL7hZhiAXb3d</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/a8b955cfb6063c0bc.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Make the lazy context rebuild cheap\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Make the lazy session's context rebuild cheap: done, in PR #200. CI shows 16 checks passing and none failing.\n\nPR: https://github.com/orin-dx/caliper/pull/200. Its base is `perf/lazy-session-whole-demand` (#198), so merge #198 first and it retargets to `main`. Branch `perf/shared-index-on-growth`, commit `f7397070` (the earlier local commit is also in the branch; the changeset is `.changeset/shared-index-on-growth.md`).\n\n**What changed (`crates/core`)**\n- **A growth shares the project, not copies it.**\n  - `NamedTypeIndex` and `ImportResolutionMap` keep their maps behind an `Arc`, and the bare-name tables are `Arc`s.\n  - `ResolutionContext::over_layer` derives the next context from the previous one: same merged data, import map, index, module resolvers and tsconfig check, with only the memos empty.\n- **The layer holds its declarations once.** `dependency_types::load` built a second merged copy of every dependency file's data on each growth, then the index from it. It now builds the index per file and keeps only the component mappings and the import and re-export tables.\n- **The whole-demand load starts after 48 growths, not 3.** It is `cfg(test)` 3 so the existing tests still exercise it.\n- **Also updated:** ADR 0016 and `docs/architecture/pipeline-orchestration.md`.\n\n**Measured** (`lazy_bench`, 50 random components, dependencies and full HTML attributes, best of 7 interleaved; digests identical across main, #198 and this change on every corpus)\n\n| Corpus | 50 requests, main / #198 / this | Peak RSS, main / #198 / this |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Spectrum | 304 / 62 / 59 ms | 135 / 138 / 103 MB |\n| antd | 168 / 40 / 61 ms | 113 / 109 / 86 MB |\n| Mantine | 39 / 39 / 30 ms | 104 / 103 / 81 MB |\n| shadcn | 273 / 79 / 106 ms | 120 / 189 / 94 MB |\n| Chakra | 436 / 289 / 347 ms | 146 / 147 / 117 MB |\n\nThe slowest single request falls from 18–79 ms (#198) to 4–10 ms on all but Chakra (70 ms).\n\n**The gates: not all met, and it's a trade-off.**\n- **Memory:** met. Peak RSS is below `main` on every corpus, including shadcn (94 vs 120 MB).\n- **Time at or below #198:** met on Spectrum and Mantine, missed on antd (61 vs 40), shadcn (106 vs 79) and Chakra (347 vs 289). With the load left at 3 growths and the same cheaper growth, every corpus beats #198 on time, but shadcn holds about 154 MB against `main`'s 120. I chose the memory gate. `WHOLE_DEMAND_AFTER_GROWTHS` is the one-constant knob if you'd rather have time.\n- **First-story latency:** not worse (Spectrum about 150–210 ms, Chakra 62 ms in the harness).\n\n**Where the rest of the per-growth cost is.** The context rebuild is now 0 ms. What remains is the incremental `dependency_types::load`: about 45% loading, 40% rebuilding the layer's own index from everything it holds, and 15% setting up resolvers. Extending the layer by only the new files (a chained index) would remove most of that and might let the time gate be met at the lower memory. I didn't attempt it.\n\n**Verification**\n- `just equivalence` against #198's head: 15 of 15 corpus and configuration combinations identical, and lazy parity over the fixtures and every corpus passes.\n- `just lint doc-check machete typos` exits 0, and `cargo nextest run --workspace --exclude caliper-docgen-napi --locked` gives 891 passed, 1 skipped. The new test `growing_the_layer_does_not_copy_the_projects_index` asserts the context holds the project's own index after each growth.\n- **Storybook harness** (Spectrum and Chakra): answers equal the eager session's in every variant. Spectrum's 50 real stories total 0.7 s through the addon (main 1.0–1.1 s, but #198 0.4 s) and Chakra's 92 sampled 1.4 s (#198 0.8 s), because a whole-project read never reaches 48 growths. That is the cost of the memory choice and is stated in the PR.\n\n**Notes**\n- The original brief's concurrency test is covered by the existing `requests_that_race_the_background_load...` test, which still passes. I didn't add another.\n- My local branch tracked #198's branch; I unset the upstream and pushed to the new name, so #198 is untouched.\n- The scratch benchmark binaries and scripts are in `/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/ab/` and `ab-bench.py` there.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>791110</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>366</tool_uses><duration_ms>1742752</duration_ms></usage>\n<worktree><worktreePath>/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-a8b955cfb6063c0bc</worktreePath><worktreeBranch>worktree-agent-a8b955cfb6063c0bc</worktreeBranch></worktree>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"3fbad268-e5d2-4dd4-9958-bf656740f8de","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:48:28.951Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"task-notification","producer":"session-task","runId":"0mvo5jm8m-8b5f014f"},"promptSource":"system","turnOrigin":"task_notification","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":187,"turnIndex":283},"queueSkipAttachments":true,"sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"perf/shared-index-on-growth","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
