{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","prNumber":201,"prUrl":"https://github.com/orin-dx/caliper/pull/201","prRepository":"orin-dx/caliper","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:48:29.155Z"}
{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","bridgeSessionId":"cse_01D7CJmXuD2ASqfBYm7Lk4WZ","lastSequenceNum":21749,"ownerAccountUuid":"138d593e-e185-4f72-89f2-82e1a501f134","ownerOrganizationUuid":"602db9b4-428d-49e6-a99c-64152cc62a79"}
{"parentUuid":"3fbad268-e5d2-4dd4-9958-bf656740f8de","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPTMEhmyU3xWb3J17WgU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"PR #200 is open with all 16 checks passing. It makes the context rebuild essentially free and cuts memory below `main`'s on every corpus. It misses the time gate on three corpora, which was a deliberate trade-off.\n\n**What it changed** (`crates/core`)\n- **A growth shares the project's data instead of copying it.** The named-type index and import map now sit behind `Arc`s, and the next context is derived from the previous one with only the memos empty. The rebuild now costs 0 ms.\n- **The layer holds its declarations once.** Before, every growth built a second merged copy of every dependency file's data. It now builds the index per file.\n- **The whole-demand load starts after 48 growths, not 3.** That is what keeps memory down.\n\n**Measured** (50 random components one at a time, dependencies loaded, best of 7)\n\n| Corpus | Time: main / #198 / #200 | Peak memory: main / #198 / #200 |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Spectrum | 304 / 62 / 59 ms | 135 / 138 / 103 MB |\n| antd | 168 / 40 / 61 ms | 113 / 109 / 86 MB |\n| Mantine | 39 / 39 / 30 ms | 104 / 103 / 81 MB |\n| shadcn | 273 / 79 / 106 ms | 120 / 189 / 94 MB |\n| Chakra | 436 / 289 / 347 ms | 146 / 147 / 117 MB |\n\n- Results are identical to batch on every corpus (15 of 15 combinations, plus lazy parity). Lint passes and 891 tests pass.\n- The slowest single request drops from 18–79 ms to 4–10 ms on all but Chakra (70 ms).\n\n**The trade-off, stated plainly**\n- **Memory:** met. Every corpus is below `main`, including shadcn at 94 MB against 120 MB, where #198 had raised it to 189.\n- **Time against #198:** met on Spectrum and Mantine, missed on antd (61 vs 40 ms), shadcn (106 vs 79) and Chakra (347 vs 289). Every corpus still beats `main`'s time by a lot.\n- **Whole-project reads cost more.** Because the whole-demand load now needs 48 growths, a whole-project read never reaches it. Through the addon that gives Spectrum's 50 stories 0.7 s (against #198's 0.4 s) and Chakra's 92 sampled 1.4 s (#198: 0.8 s). `main` is 1.0–1.1 s on Spectrum.\n- **The knob:** `WHOLE_DEMAND_AFTER_GROWTHS` is one constant. At 3 every corpus beats #198 on time, but shadcn holds about 154 MB against `main`'s 120.\n\n**The better fix is not done.** The remaining per-growth cost is the incremental dependency load: about 45% loading, 40% rebuilding the layer's own index from everything it holds, 15% setting up resolvers. Extending the index by only the new files would cut most of that and might meet both gates. That is the next step on this work, and I'd queue it.\n\n**Merge order:** #198, then #200. #198 raises shadcn's memory and #200 undoes it, so if you merge #198 alone, shadcn's lazy memory goes up in between.\n\nRunning now: `antd-gaps` and `deps-default`. Open PRs: #196, #197, #198, #199, #200 and #160. Still pending your call: the confidence-score measurement fork, and issue #1."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4542,"cache_read_input_tokens":687515,"output_tokens":1182,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4542,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1182,"cache_read_input_tokens":687515,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4542,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4542},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"dd2929b3-9542-42fd-8549-fc2167b37182","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgPTMENvNFWbXWsCw7h4p","requestRef":"7dc7f138-3e82-4e09-b4d3-c722a9ffd28d","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"eb69bb79-6b4f-40f8-90bc-841928a1da38","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:48:37.713Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"perf/shared-index-on-growth","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
