{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:52:04.813Z","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>abab292d8e2d758de</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01H7aXdyyRFqtUSo2dWgFMzj</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/abab292d8e2d758de.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Remaining antd gaps and empty-string default\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Task: closed the antd, Spectrum and shadcn Storybook-parity gaps from `origin/main`. PR #201 (base `main`) is open with all 15 CI checks passing.\n\n**Fixed (three general causes, none antd-specific)**\n- **`Record&lt;K, V&gt;` as a props base was a silent no-op.** It now gives one prop per literal key. A key alias of literals, or `(typeof ARRAY)[number]` over an `as const` array in another file, is followed. A `string`, `number` or `symbol` key names no prop. antd's `Col` gains `xs` to `xxxl`, and `ContextIsolator` gains `form` and `space`.\n- **`Pick&lt;React.Interface, K&gt;` lost its props when React's declarations weren't merged** (any `htmlAttributes` other than `full`). Each picked key is now read from React's interface, with optionality and docs. The walk follows React's own parents, so `onClick` on `HTMLAttributes` (declared in `DOMAttributes`) is found as `MouseEventHandler&lt;HTMLDivElement&gt;`. A missing key is reported. An alias like `ComponentProps&lt;typeof X&gt;` is not read as an interface. `Progress` gains `aria-label` and `aria-labelledby`, and `CheckableTagGroup` gains `className`, `id`, `role` and `style`.\n- **`React.PropsWithChildren` with no argument** is now `{ children?: ReactNode }`. This fixes `UniqueProvider` and Spectrum's `CalendarGrid`.\n\n**Harness counts**\n\n| | before | after |\n| --- | --: | --: |\n| antd: props Storybook lists that we lack | 51 in 8 stories | 37 in 5 stories |\n| antd: control kind differs | 65 | 64 |\n| shadcn: lack / defaults only Storybook lists / control kind | 0 / 0 / 18 | 0 / 0 / 18 |\n| Spectrum: lack / defaults only Storybook lists | 0 / 0 | 0 / 0 |\n\n**Not done**\n- antd's remaining missing props: `PurePanel` 33, `ref` on three forwardRef components, and `Dragger.capture`.\n  - The `PurePanel` in the story isn't an exported component, and I couldn't tie Storybook's Drawer props to it within budget.\n  - `ref` is omitted by design, as RDT does.\n- Spectrum `Avatar.alt`: no default differences remain on Spectrum in the harness, so there was nothing to fix. The corpus has two `Avatar`s, with `null` and `''`.\n- shadcn's 18 control-kind differences: no new finding beyond #188's classification (non-losses, plus `z.infer`, which needs the checker).\n\n**Gates**\n- Equivalence against `main` on all five corpora (default and dependencies): Chakra and shadcn identical; Mantine (2), antd (63) and Spectrum (6) differ, all allow-listed in `scripts/equivalence-allow.json`. They are new props, `composes` entries that became props, and two opaque reads that now resolve (`FloatButton.aria-label`, Mantine's `TextareaAutosize.style`). No false notes remain.\n- Oracle: wrong 0.00% on Mantine, Chakra, shadcn and antd, 0.01% on Spectrum (unchanged); less precise falls or holds.\n- Lazy parity over the fixtures passes. Lint exits 0. 896 tests pass (1 skipped). Nine new exact-value tests are in `crates/core/tests/utility_bases.rs`. The cache schema didn't change.\n\n**Commit:** `dfc84ff7` on `fix/antd-spectrum-gaps` — `crates/core/src/resolver/{alias,evaluate,substitute}.rs`, `crates/core/tests/utility_bases.rs`, `scripts/equivalence-allow.json` and `.changeset/utility-bases-record-pick-children.md`.\n\nOne caveat for the parent: `scripts/equivalence-allow.json` is non-empty in this PR, as the directive asked. If #199 (which empties it) merges first, this PR's allow-list entries need re-adding on rebase.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>798005</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>359</tool_uses><duration_ms>1930687</duration_ms></usage>\n<worktree><worktreePath>/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-abab292d8e2d758de</worktreePath><worktreeBranch>worktree-agent-abab292d8e2d758de</worktreeBranch></worktree>\n</task-notification>"}
