{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","id":"a0a3f8a4-dd6e-4b0d-b698-b77a3d4caaf7","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:52:04.903Z","version":"2.1.308","querySource":"repl_main_thread:outputStyle:Concise","shapeHash":"695ec5a8802936862d1cd8c71e730e293e4e9e400bcbffb95f0146470866b732","params":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"b3971c3a-4c07-4510-89f3-a60e882120c2","keep":863,"tail":["15be132bf16ca9c0152b91250bbadecde4a7365e2995011e695650baa42715ac","178cd26ea7d103ef7c48e92af011451c66d882e9261b1df11bdbba5bdd04589d"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",864,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"fd7be8ee45e2d05bea88441efdbb18bf61c59121d99ea2446c1d1db36c8e8b7e"}
{"parentUuid":"c4c95f08-edb5-4bdc-956c-58b52303f136","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPTd9h6ivBw9WKvbLpkv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"PR #201 is open with all 15 CI checks passing. It fixes three general type-resolution gaps found through antd, and leaves the others as designed or outside what we can do without the type checker.\n\n**Fixed** (none antd-specific)\n- **`Record<K, V>` as a props base was a silent no-op.** It now gives one prop per literal key. A key alias of literals, or `(typeof ARRAY)[number]` over an `as const` array in another file, is followed. A `string`, `number` or `symbol` key names no prop. antd's `Col` gains `xs` to `xxxl`, and `ContextIsolator` gains `form` and `space`.\n- **`Pick<React.Interface, K>` lost its props when React's declarations weren't merged**, which is any `htmlAttributes` setting other than `full`. Each picked key is now read from React's interface with its optionality and docs, following React's own parents. A missing key is reported. `Progress` gains `aria-label` and `aria-labelledby`, and `CheckableTagGroup` gains `className`, `id`, `role` and `style`.\n- **`React.PropsWithChildren` with no argument** is now `{ children?: ReactNode }`. That fixes `UniqueProvider` and Spectrum's `CalendarGrid`.\n\n**Harness counts, before → after**\n\n| Measure | Before | After |\n| --- | --: | --: |\n| antd: props Storybook lists that we lack | 51 in 8 stories | 37 in 5 stories |\n| antd: control kind differs | 65 | 64 |\n| shadcn: lack / defaults only Storybook lists / control kind | 0 / 0 / 18 | 0 / 0 / 18 |\n| Spectrum: lack / defaults only Storybook lists | 0 / 0 | 0 / 0 |\n\n**Not done, with reasons**\n- antd's remaining 37 props: `PurePanel` 33, `ref` on three forwardRef components and `Dragger.capture`. The story's `PurePanel` isn't an exported component and the fork couldn't tie Storybook's Drawer props to it in budget. `ref` is omitted by design, as RDT does.\n- Spectrum `Avatar.alt`: nothing left to fix. No default differences remain on Spectrum, and the corpus has two `Avatar`s, one with `null` and one with `''`.\n- shadcn's 18 control-kind differences: no new finding beyond #188's classification, which is non-losses plus `z.infer`, which needs the checker.\n\n**Gates**\n- `just equivalence` against `main`: Chakra and shadcn identical. Mantine (2), antd (63) and Spectrum (6) differ, all allow-listed and all new props, `composes` entries that became props, or two opaque reads that now resolve.\n- Oracle: wrong 0.00% on Mantine, Chakra, shadcn and antd, and 0.01% on Spectrum (unchanged).\n- Lazy parity over the fixtures passes. Lint exits 0, and 896 tests pass with nine new exact-value tests. The cache schema didn't change.\n\n**One merge note.** The PR's allow-list is non-empty on purpose. #199 empties that file, so if #199 merges first, #201 needs its entries re-added on rebase. Merge #201 first, then #199, and clear the entries after.\n\n**Merge order for everything open:** #198 then #200 (lazy), #201, #199 (after #201), #196, #197, #160 last. The dependencies-default fork (`deps-default`) is still running.\n\nI didn't hear back on the confidence-score measurement fork. Say yes and I'll start it with the risk-table method."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3648,"cache_read_input_tokens":696367,"output_tokens":1217,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3648,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1217,"cache_read_input_tokens":696367,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3648,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3648},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"d40b5f85-ab9c-4e5a-a1cc-95c24f85214d","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgPTd9G3Q43CjWw2AJrzt","requestRef":"a0a3f8a4-dd6e-4b0d-b698-b77a3d4caaf7","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"bc55e19c-86d0-4f0e-832b-82e31308df58","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:52:13.580Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"perf/shared-index-on-growth","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
