rybook-parity.mjs --corpora ... --only spectrum,chakra --limit 50; build binding+addon first); report a table; pick the smallest threshold meeting the memory ceiling with the best whole-project time; (2) then implement the CHAINED dependency index #200 identified as the remaining per-growth cost (incremental dependency_types::load: ~45% loading, 40% rebuilding the layer's own index from everything it holds, 15% setting up resolvers): extend the layer's index by only the new files (layered/persistent index with Arc'd parents; lookups walk the chain or a merged view built lazily) so a growth costs proportional to the new files, not the whole layer; then re-sweep: if growth is cheap enough, the threshold barely matters; set the final value; (3) correctness: results identical to batch (lazy_parity fixtures and corpora, both ask orders, the race test), `just equivalence` identical to #200's head, ADR 0016 + docs/architecture/pipeline-orchestration.md updated, changeset, tests (exact-value: a growth adds only the new files' entries; index lookups equal a from-scratch build over the same files, property-style over a few real dependency sets). Gates: `just lint doc-check machete typos` and `cargo nextest run --workspace --exclude caliper-docgen-napi --locked` exit codes read directly (never pipe through tail), CI green. The machine is shared with other forks: interleave, repeat, report noise. Time-box ~90 tool calls. Commits end with Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED; PR body ends with https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED; never push main/force-push/merge; /usr/bin/git with sandbox off, one plain git command per call."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1298,"cache_read_input_tokens":704327,"output_tokens":5542,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":792},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_