{"parentUuid":"2daa0f92-0db6-454a-8e01-0950155431cf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPTuANiD4MSd81XfVSo6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Gkp5zhWK3wFAefu2HgfPTe","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Measure how well signals predict oracle disagreement","subagent_type":"fork","isolation":"worktree","name":"confidence-score","prompt":"Track AF: measure a confidence score for type detection, using the TS 7.1 oracle for labels. Measure and prototype offline; do NOT build the tsc routing yet. Branch off origin/main (PR base `main`; open PRs #196-#201 are unrelated). Idea: every prop (and component) gets a confidence from signals we already have; low-confidence components would later be answered on demand by a warm tsc (TS 7.1) in an `auto` mode. Signals available per prop/component: how the type was produced (declaration read / structurally evaluated / hand shortcut in crates/core/src/known.rs e.g. VariantProps / opaque or unresolved named reference / composes), diagnostics with codes affecting the component (UNRESOLVABLE_IMPORT, OPAQUE_TYPE, INDEXED_ACCESS_OPAQUE, TEMPLATE_LITERAL_OPAQUE, GENERIC_ARGUMENT_MISMATCH, UNKNOWN, CIRCULAR_REFERENCE, max-depth), DetectionRule evidence of the component (crates/core/src/types/collected.rs; name-based wrapper heuristics are the shakiest), type shape (nesting depth, union size, generic arity, number of named refs), source (project vs dependency package), whether defaults/params involved. Labels: the oracle (apps/validate/src/oracle*.ts, `python3 scripts/parity.py oracle` / `scripts/equivalence.py --oracle`, baseline in scripts/oracle-baseline.json; per-prop verdicts: match, less precise, wrong, opaque; wrong is only 0.0-0.3% of props so use label = wrong OR less-precise as the soft label and report wrong alone too; know its blind spots: depth>3 and opaque treated alike, objects compared by field names). Do: (1) add a small offline exporter (an example in crates/core/examples/ or a script over `extract --json` + the oracle's per-prop output; keep it tiny and committed under scripts/ or apps/validate if useful; no shipped-code changes) producing one row per (corpus, component, prop) with the signals above and the oracle label, for the five corpora in /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/bench-corpus with --load-dependencies --html-attributes full; (2) analysis in python (-I): the empirical disagreement rate per signal and per signal combination (a smoothed risk table; Beta prior), then a simple logistic regression / small tree for comparison; evaluate by leave-one-corpus-out; weight corpora so Chakra's 470k props do not dominate; (3) the key chart: share of oracle disagreements (wrong; wrong+less-precise) caught vs share of COMPONENTS routed (a component is routed if any prop's risk exceeds a threshold), for (a) today's rule (any warning/error diagnostic affects the component = the addon's fallback rule), (b) the risk table, (c) the model; report at routed budgets 2%, 5%, 10%, 20%; (4) list the confidently-wrong cases (oracle wrong, no diagnostic, high confidence) and what signal would have caught them (examples from the session: union-props branch, VariantProps by bare name); (5) conclusion: does a score beat the existing diagnostic rule at <=10% routed? what thresholds? what extra signals should the resolver emit (e.g. a per-prop provenance field) to make the score better; propose the data model (small ordered enum levels + how component confidence aggregates) and the ADR outline, but do not implement it. Output: report at /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/confidence-score.md and a summary in your final message with the key table. If the exporter/script is clean and small open a PR (base main) with it plus docs/confidence-score.md findings; `just lint doc-check machete typos` exit code read directly. Time-box ~70 tool calls. Commits end with Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED; PR body ends with https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED; never push main/force-push/merge; /usr/bin/git with sandbox off, one plain git command per call."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1298,"cache_read_input_tokens":704327,"output_tokens":5542,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":792},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1298,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5542,"cache_read_input_tokens":704327,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1298,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1298},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Gkp5zhWK3wFAefu2HgfPTe":{"description":"Measure how well signals predict oracle disagreement","subagent_type":"fork","isolation":"worktree","name":"confidence-score","prompt":"Track AF: measure a confidence score for type detection, using the TS 7.1 oracle for labels. Measure and prototype offline; do NOT build the tsc routing yet. Branch off origin/main (PR base `main`; open PRs #196-#201 are unrelated). Idea: every prop (and component) gets a confidence from signals we already have; low-confidence components would later be answered on demand by a warm tsc (TS 7.1) in an `auto` mode. Signals available per prop/component: how the type was produced (declaration read / structurally evaluated / hand shortcut in crates/core/src/known.rs e.g. VariantProps / opaque or unresolved named reference / composes), diagnostics with codes affecting the component (UNRESOLVABLE_IMPORT, OPAQUE_TYPE, INDEXED_ACCESS_OPAQUE, TEMPLATE_LITERAL_OPAQUE, GENERIC_ARGUMENT_MISMATCH, UNKNOWN, CIRCULAR_REFERENCE, max-depth), DetectionRule evidence of the component (crates/core/src/types/collected.rs; name-based wrapper heuristics are the shakiest), type shape (nesting depth, union size, generic arity, number of named refs), source (project vs dependency package), whether defaults/params involved. Labels: the oracle (apps/validate/src/oracle*.ts, `python3 scripts/parity.py oracle` / `scripts/equivalence.py --oracle`, baseline in scripts/oracle-baseline.json; per-prop verdicts: match, less precise, wrong, opaque; wrong is only 0.0-0.3% of props so use label = wrong OR less-precise as the soft label and report wrong alone too; know its blind spots: depth>3 and opaque treated alike, objects compared by field names). Do: (1) add a small offline exporter (an example in crates/core/examples/ or a script over `extract --json` + the oracle's per-prop output; keep it tiny and committed under scripts/ or apps/validate if useful; no shipped-code changes) producing one row per (corpus, component, prop) with the signals above and the oracle label, for the five corpora in /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/bench-corpus with --load-dependencies --html-attributes full; (2) analysis in python (-I): the empirical disagreement rate per signal and per signal combination (a smoothed risk table; Beta prior), then a simple logistic regression / small tree for comparison; evaluate by leave-one-corpus-out; weight corpora so Chakra's 470k props do not dominate; (3) the key chart: share of oracle disagreements (wrong; wrong+less-precise) caught vs share of COMPONENTS routed (a component is routed if any prop's risk exceeds a threshold), for (a) today's rule (any warning/error diagnostic affects the component = the addon's fallback rule), (b) the risk table, (c) the model; report at routed budgets 2%, 5%, 10%, 20%; (4) list the confidently-wrong cases (oracle wrong, no diagnostic, high confidence) and what signal would have caught them (examples from the session: union-props branch, VariantProps by bare name); (5) conclusion: does a score beat the existing diagnostic rule at <=10% routed? what thresholds? what extra signals should the resolver emit (e.g. a per-prop provenance field) to make the score better; propose the data model (small ordered enum levels + how component confidence aggregates) and the ADR outline, but do not implement it. Output: report at /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/confidence-score.md and a summary in your final message with the key table. If the exporter/script is clean and small open a PR (base main) with it plus docs/confidence-score.md findings; `just lint doc-check machete typos` exit code read directly. Time-box ~70 tool calls. Commits end with Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED; PR body ends with https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED; never push main/force-push/merge; /usr/bin/git with sandbox off, one plain git command per call."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"2f6c890c-8e89-4a89-ad17-07091c794ed0","apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CgPTu9ze4f8EDNmoDh74z","requestRef":"7f5b53fe-dd7b-4d0e-9e6f-4589a58fe7ea","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"5ad2de46-2b55-4f13-ab86-2cd090c92d5e","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:56:12.374Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"feat/load-dependencies-by-default","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"5ad2de46-2b55-4f13-ab86-2cd090c92d5e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPTuANiD4MSd81XfVSo6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ND9Wmf1429wqVZ2e4PxDmE","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Structural cause of the shadcn and antd prop gap","subagent_type":"fork","isolation":"worktree","name":"prop-gap","prompt":"Track AG: explain and close the structural prop gap against RDT on shadcn and antd. Branch off origin/fix/antd-spectrum-gaps (PR #201, open, unmerged: Record<K,V> bases, Pick<React.X,K> keys, PropsWithChildren) and open your PR with base = fix/antd-spectrum-gaps (never `main` while it carries unmerged parent commits; the repo deletes head branches on merge so bottom-up merging retargets to main); say so in the body. Baseline numbers (scripts/parity-baseline.json, 0.4.0, deps on, `python3 scripts/parity.py run` for current): share of RDT's props that Caliper reports: shadcn 39.5% (5,134 of 12,994), antd 80.3% (2,395 of 2,983); Mantine/Spectrum/Chakra 98.6-99.7%. The TS 7.1 opt-in (--experimental-semantic-types) found ~96% on shadcn and ~97% on antd of component-specific props, so the missing props are real, but earlier I noted 'verify it is not RDT noise' (RDT lists every inherited HTML/aria/DOM prop of each wrapped element, and expands @types/react; Caliper's default html mode is curated). Do: (1) CLASSIFY the missing props on shadcn and antd with `--html-attributes full` AND with curated (so the HTML-attribute noise is separated): per missing prop: component, file, declaring package/type, kind (HTML/aria/DOM event from a wrapped element, inherited from a dependency component's props via ComponentProps<typeof X>/Pick/Omit, from a mapped/conditional/generic alias, forwardRef/ref/key, `as`/polymorphic, from a cva/variant helper, other); produce counts and top examples; (2) FIX the structural causes in crates/core that are fixable without a checker (follow TypeScript's model: one resolution path, then read; see docs/architecture/resolver-type-resolution.md, ADRs 0010/0014/0015, AGENTS.md non-negotiables incl. emit a Diagnostic when degrading): e.g. components whose props come from `React.ComponentProps<typeof Radix.Root>` where Radix's types are in dependencies (check they load: --load-dependencies is being made the default by another fork; measure with it on), `Omit<ComponentProps<'div'>, 'x'> & VariantProps<typeof v>` shapes, `asChild` polymorphism, generic components, re-exported primitives (`const X = Primitive.Root`), namespaces; leave genuinely checker-only cases (z.infer, conditional inference) classified as such with the reason; (3) re-measure the share of RDT's props reported, same-control %, and the oracle (`just equivalence --oracle`: no regression) for shadcn and antd and the other three corpora (must stay identical or improve); report before/after and the remaining gap by class, with the fraction attributable to RDT noise (props RDT lists that the TS oracle also says are absent/never a real prop, if the oracle can tell) vs real gaps the TS 7.1 opt-in fixes. Gates: exact-value tests per fix, `just equivalence` diffs explained (allow-list only intended ones), lazy parity, cache schema bump + golden test if SourceData changes, `just lint doc-check machete typos` and `cargo nextest run --workspace --exclude caliper-docgen-napi --locked` exit codes read directly (never pipe through tail), CI green, changeset. Do not touch crates/core/src/pipeline/revision/lazy.rs, named_type_index.rs or dependency_types.rs (fork knob-and-chain owns them). Time-box ~90 tool calls. Commits end with Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED; PR bodies end with https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED; never push main/force-push/merge; /usr/bin/git with sandbox off, one plain git command per call."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"ca