 bottom-up merging retargets it to main); say so in the body. Context from #200: WHOLE_DEMAND_AFTER_GROWTHS (crates/core, lazy session) was 3 in #198 and 48 in #200; at 3 every corpus beats #198's time but shadcn peak RSS ~154 MB vs main's 120; at 48 memory is below main everywhere but a whole-project read (Spectrum 50 real stories through the addon 0.7 s vs 0.4 s at 3; Chakra 92 sampled 1.4 s vs 0.8 s) is slower. The user's rule: speed matters more than a small memory cost at the edges; pick a threshold that keeps most of the speed with a reasonable memory ceiling (target: each corpus within +15% peak RSS of main, e.g. shadcn <= ~138 MB). Do: (1) SWEEP thresholds 3, 6, 12, 24, 48 (make it a runtime option for the bench only, no env switches on hot paths: a field on the session options or a test-only/cfg(feature) override; lazy_bench flag) on all five corpora (/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/bench-corpus) with loadDependencies + full HTML attributes: (a) 50 random components one at a time (summed request time, peak RSS, slowest request) and (b) a WHOLE-PROJECT read (every component in file order) total time and peak RSS, via lazy_bench and, for Spectrum and Chakra, the addon harness (node packages/storybook/scripts/storybook-parity.mjs --corpora ... --only spectrum,chakra --limit 50; build binding+addon first); report a table; pick the smallest threshold meeting the memory ceiling with the best whole-project time; (2) then implement the CHAINED dependency index #200 identified as the remaining per-growth cost (incremental dependency_types::load: ~45% loading, 40% rebuilding the layer's own index from everything it holds, 15% setting up resolvers): extend the layer's index by only the new files (layered/persistent index with Arc'd parents; lookups walk the chain or a merged view built lazily) so a growth costs proportional to the new files, not the whole layer; then re-sweep: if growth is cheap enough, the threshold barely matters; set the final value; (3) correctness: results identical to batch (lazy_parity fixtures and corpora, both ask orders, the race test), `just equivalence` identical to #200's head, ADR 0016 + docs/architecture/pipeline-orchestration.md updated, changeset, tests (exact-value: a growth adds only the new files' entries; index lookups equal a from-scratch build over the same files, property-style over a few real dependency sets). Gates: `just lint doc-check machete typos` and `cargo nextest run --workspace --exclude caliper-docgen-napi --locked` exit codes read directly (never pipe through tail), CI green. The machine is shared with other forks: interleave, repeat, report noise. Time-box ~90 tool calls. Commits end with Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED; PR body ends with https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED; never push main/force-push/merge; /usr/bin/git with sandbox off, one plain git command per call.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/acbb81e8b835c4e39.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"2f6c890c-8e89-4a89-ad17-07091c794ed0","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","branch":"chore/reset-equivalence-allow-list","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2daa0f92-0db6-454a-