{"parentUuid":"9feb8fb4-04f9-43af-9404-deb7b5858bcc","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"949a3d7a-7599-4ec3-98ed-4e5262379c20","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ND9Wmf1429wqVZ2e4PxDmE","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Async agent launched successfully. (This tool result is internal metadata — never quote or paste any part of it, including the agentId below, into a user-facing reply.)\nagentId: a8054f3772574ddd2 (internal ID - do not mention to user. Use SendMessage with to: 'a8054f3772574ddd2', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent.)\nThe agent is working in the background. You will be notified automatically when it completes. You know nothing about its results until that notification arrives — do not report, assume, or predict them; continue other work or respond to the user in the meantime.\nDo not duplicate this agent's work — avoid working with the same files or topics it is using.\noutput_file: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/a8054f3772574ddd2.output\nDo NOT Read or tail this file via the shell tool — it is the full subagent JSONL transcript and reading it will overflow your context. If the user asks for progress, say the agent is still running; you'll get a completion notification."}]}]},"uuid":"7989fe16-334f-4deb-ab14-17639f5f54fa","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:56:26.972Z","toolUseResult":{"isAsync":true,"status":"async_launched","agentId":"a8054f3772574ddd2","description":"Structural cause of the shadcn and antd prop gap","resolvedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","prompt":"Track AG: explain and close the structural prop gap against RDT on shadcn and antd. Branch off origin/fix/antd-spectrum-gaps (PR #201, open, unmerged: Record<K,V> bases, Pick<React.X,K> keys, PropsWithChildren) and open your PR with base = fix/antd-spectrum-gaps (never `main` while it carries unmerged parent commits; the repo deletes head branches on merge so bottom-up merging retargets to main); say so in the body. Baseline numbers (scripts/parity-baseline.json, 0.4.0, deps on, `python3 scripts/parity.py run` for current): share of RDT's props that Caliper reports: shadcn 39.5% (5,134 of 12,994), antd 80.3% (2,395 of 2,983); Mantine/Spectrum/Chakra 98.6-99.7%. The TS 7.1 opt-in (--experimental-semantic-types) found ~96% on shadcn and ~97% on antd of component-specific props, so the missing props are real, but earlier I noted 'verify it is not RDT noise' (RDT lists every inherited HTML/aria/DOM prop of each wrapped element, and expands @types/react; Caliper's default html mode is curated). Do: (1) CLASSIFY the missing props on shadcn and antd with `--html-attributes full` AND with curated (so the HTML-attribute noise is separated): per missing prop: component, file, declaring package/type, kind (HTML/aria/DOM event from a wrapped element, inherited from a dependency component's props via ComponentProps<typeof X>/Pick/Omit, from a mapped/conditional/generic alias, forwardRef/ref/key, `as`/polymorphic, from a cva/variant helper, other); produce counts and top examples; (2) FIX the structural causes in crates/core that are fixable without a checker (follow TypeScript's model: one resolution path, then read; see docs/architecture/resolver-type-resolution.md, ADRs 0010/0014/0015, AGENTS.md non-negotiables incl. emit a Diagnostic when degrading): e.g. components whose props come from `React.ComponentProps<typeof Radix.Root>` where Radix's types are in dependencies (check they load: --load-dependencies is being made the default by another fork; measure with it on), `Omit<ComponentProps<'div'>, 'x'> & VariantProps<typeof v>` shapes, `asChild` polymorphism, generic components, re-exported primitives (`const X = Primitive.Root`), namespaces; leave genuinely checker-only cases (z.infer, conditional inference) classified as such with the reason; (3) re-measure the share of RDT's props reported, same-control %, and the oracle (`just equivalence --oracle`: no regression) for shadcn and antd and the other three corpora (must stay identical or improve); report before/after and the remaining gap by class, with the fraction attributable to RDT noise (props RDT lists that the TS oracle also says are absent/never a real prop, if the oracle can tell) vs real gaps the TS 7.1 opt-in fixes. Gates: exact-value tests per fix, `just equivalence` diffs explained (allow-list only intended ones), lazy parity, cache schema bump + golden test if SourceData changes, `just lint doc-check machete typos` and `cargo nextest run --workspace --exclude caliper-docgen-napi --locked` exit codes read directly (never pipe through tail), CI green, changeset. Do not touch crates/core/src/pipeline/revision/lazy.rs, named_type_index.rs or dependency_types.rs (fork knob-and-chain owns them). Time-box ~90 tool calls. Commits end with Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED; PR bodies end with https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED; never push main/force-push/merge; /usr/bin/git with sandbox off, one plain git command per call.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/a8054f3772574ddd2.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"2f6c890c-8e89-4a89-ad17-07091c794ed0","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","branch":"chore/reset-equivalence-allow-list","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":