{"parentUuid":"c7b85888-dc60-4c9b-bcf0-87f7a50c6289","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPTxV3hxGkjJ9fjeodTL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Three forks are running, each opening its PR stacked on its parent branch. The dependencies-default fork (`deps-default`) is also still running.\n\n**`knob-and-chain`** is stacked on #200. It finds the good spot for the whole-demand threshold, then removes the cost behind it.\n- **The sweep.** Thresholds 3, 6, 12, 24 and 48 on all five corpora, with two workloads: 50 random components one at a time, and a whole-project read in file order. For each it records time, peak memory and the slowest request, and reports the table.\n- **The choice.** The smallest threshold that keeps each corpus within +15% peak memory of `main` (shadcn at most about 138 MB), with the best whole-project time. That follows your rule that speed beats a small memory cost at the edges.\n- **The real fix.** A chained dependency index that extends the layer by only the new files, so a growth costs in proportion to what's new. After that it re-sweeps, and the threshold should barely matter.\n- **Correctness.** Results identical to batch (lazy parity, both ask orders, the race test), and a test that index lookups equal a from-scratch build.\n\n**`confidence-score`** is measure-only, no shipped-code changes. It builds one row per prop with our signals (how the type was found, diagnostics, detection evidence, type shape) and the oracle's verdict, then compares routing rules by the share of oracle disagreements caught against the share of components routed (2%, 5%, 10%, 20%):\n- today's rule (any warning or error), the risk table, and a small model, evaluated leaving one corpus out and weighted so Chakra doesn't dominate.\n- It also lists the confidently-wrong cases and the extra signal the resolver should emit, and proposes a data model and an ADR outline. This tells us whether a score beats today's rule at about 10% routed before we build the `tsc` path.\n\n**`prop-gap`** is stacked on #201. It classifies why shadcn reports about 40% of RDT's props and antd about 80%, separating RDT's inherited-HTML noise from real gaps. It fixes the structural causes without a checker (`ComponentProps<typeof X>` from dependencies, `Omit<…> & VariantProps<…>`, `asChild`, re-exported primitives, namespaces), and labels what only the checker can do. It reports the remaining gap by class, with how much the TS 7.1 opt-in closes.\n\nBetween them the three tell us how much of the gap is closable structurally, how much needs TS 7.1, and how to decide which components get routed.\n\nOpen PRs: #196, #197, #198, #199, #200, #201, #160. Merge bottom-up: #198 → #200, then #201, then the independent ones."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10221,"cache_read_input_tokens":705625,"output_tokens":898,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10221,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":898,"cache_read_input_tokens":705625,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10221,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10221},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"26b63dd7-f44b-4d42-a5e6-3285625fcfc3","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgPTxURVqyaTk186hxMP4","requestRef":"4ee214e0-5173-4928-9834-f9032da29949","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"56071edd-e32c-4d81-9b7e-9d41fe0b2eb7","timestamp":"2026-10-25T18:56:42.769Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id"