ch is now gone with it. The release CLI built in 1m26s, also gone.\n- Wrote the classifier at `/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/ag_classify.py`, which survives. It reuses `scripts/parity.py`'s own definition of \"missing\" and groups the missing props by declaring package, component and DOM-likeness.\n\n**What I learned about the measure, which matters for the diagnosis**\n- `parity.py measure()` counts only RDT's non-React props (those not declared in `@types/react`) on components that both tools report. The 39.5% on shadcn and 80.3% on antd therefore exclude React's HTML attributes, and the gap is not React-attribute noise.\n- Components RDT reports that Caliper doesn't match (shadcn 1,519 of 1,594, antd 162 of 258) are not counted in that denominator at all, so the real gap against RDT is larger than those percentages say.\n\n**Blocker met before the deletion.** `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` fails in a fresh worktree with `ERR_PNPM_LOCKFILE_CONFIG_MISMATCH` (\"ignoredOptionalDependencies\" does not match the lockfile). RDT's dump needs `apps/validate`'s dependencies, so the next attempt needs `pnpm install --no-frozen-lockfile`, with `pnpm-lock.yaml` restored afterwards. I had not yet run that.\n\n**For the parent:** relaunch this track in a fresh worktree. The classifier script is reusable as is: `python3 -I /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/ag_classify.py BIN CORPUS [deps] [html] [out.json]`, run from the repo root after `scripts/parity.py setup --corpus shadcn --corpus antd` and the pnpm install above.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>741906</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>20</tool_uses><duration_ms>305152</duration_ms></usage>\n<worktree><worktreePath>/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-a8054f3772574ddd2</worktreePath><worktreeBranch>worktree-agent-a8054f3772574ddd2</worktreeBranch></worktree>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"eadc2801-69bd-410f-8b49-5fd22ed9a76e","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:01:33.671Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":