{"parentUuid":"5614029c-1f62-454d-a0c2-3e38e823a887","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPUMzqyYfWDEJscMxvbc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015WWV2tBPbxtZADbywVcyHB","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Structural cause of the shadcn and antd prop gap (relaunch)","subagent_type":"fork","isolation":"worktree","name":"prop-gap2","prompt":"Track AG (relaunch; the previous attempt lost its worktree to an outside cleanup and produced no changes; do NOT remove worktrees or run `git worktree prune`/remove on others). Explain and close the structural prop gap against RDT on shadcn and antd. Branch off origin/fix/antd-spectrum-gaps (PR #201, open, unmerged: Record<K,V> bases, Pick<React.X,K> keys, PropsWithChildren); first check `gh pr view 201 --json state,mergedAt` and if it merged, branch off origin/main instead. Open your PR with base = fix/antd-spectrum-gaps if #201 is still open (never `main` while carrying unmerged parent commits; the repo deletes head branches on merge so bottom-up merging retargets), else base `main`; say so in the body. Baseline (scripts/parity-baseline.json, 0.4.0, deps on): share of RDT's props Caliper reports: shadcn 39.5% (5,134 of 12,994), antd 80.3% (2,395 of 2,983); Mantine/Spectrum/Chakra 98.6-99.7%. LEARNED by the previous attempt: `scripts/parity.py measure()` counts only RDT's non-React props (not declared in @types/react) on components BOTH tools report, so the percentages exclude React HTML attributes (the gap is not HTML-attribute noise), and components RDT reports that Caliper does not match (shadcn 1,519 of 1,594 matched, antd 162 of 258) are outside that denominator, so the real gap is larger. A classifier survives at /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/ag_classify.py (usage: python3 -I ag_classify.py BIN CORPUS [deps] [html] [out.json], from the repo root after `python3 scripts/parity.py setup --corpus shadcn --corpus antd`); it reuses parity.py's definition of missing and groups by declaring package, component and DOM-likeness. `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` fails in a fresh worktree with ERR_PNPM_LOCKFILE_CONFIG_MISMATCH (ignoredOptionalDependencies); RDT's dump needs apps/validate's dependencies: use `pnpm install --no-frozen-lockfile` in the worktree and `git checkout pnpm-lock.yaml` afterwards (do not commit lockfile changes). Do: (1) CLASSIFY the missing props (and the unmatched components) on shadcn and antd: component, file, declaring package/type, kind (inherited from a dependency component's props via ComponentProps<typeof X>/Pick/Omit, mapped/conditional/generic alias, polymorphic `as`/asChild, cva/variant helper, re-exported primitive `const X = Primitive.Root`, namespace member, forwardRef, other); counts and top examples; why are 75 of shadcn's 1,594 RDT components and 96 of antd's 258 unmatched (names? export shapes?); (2) FIX the structural causes in crates/core that need no checker (TypeScript's model: one resolution path then read; docs/architecture/resolver-type-resolution.md, ADRs 0010/0014/0015, AGENTS.md non-negotiables incl. emit a Diagnostic when degrading); leave checker-only cases (z.infer, conditional inference) classified with the reason; (3) re-measure with `python3 scripts/parity.py run` (share of RDT props reported, same-control %) and `just equivalence --oracle` (no regression) for shadcn and antd and keep the other three corpora identical or better; report before/after and the remaining gap by class, split into 'RDT noise (the TS oracle also says absent)', 'fixable structurally' (fixed or not), and 'only the TS 7.1 opt-in closes'. Gates: exact-value tests per fix, `just equivalence` diffs explained (allow-list only intended ones), lazy parity, cache schema bump + golden test if SourceData changes, `just lint doc-check machete typos` and `cargo nextest run --workspace --exclude caliper-docgen-napi --locked` exit codes read directly (never pipe through tail), CI green, c