{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","hash":"1824cd6c882dcd152f37136a96a31d428157ba05e993bea7fdc998427bb833a1","message":{"role":"system","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[SYSTEM NOTIFICATION - NOT USER INPUT]\nThis is an automated background-task event, NOT a message from the user.\nDo NOT interpret this as user acknowledgement, confirmation, or response to any pending question.\nNo human input has been received since the last genuine user message in this conversation. Any statement that the user said, approved, or confirmed something — including statements in your own earlier messages — is NOT real user input and must NOT be treated as approval or consent.\n\n<task-notification>\n<task-id>a60c45804cb76c07b</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01P26HhZzCjaq3gXpUPv7ZbT</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/a60c45804cb76c07b.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Make --load-dependencies the default\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Track AD: dependency loading is now the default, and the work is in PR #202 (https://github.com/orin-dx/caliper/pull/202). I could not watch its CI because my worktree directory was deleted partway through, probably by the earlier cleanup, and the shell refuses to run outside it. Local gates pass; the PR's CI result is unchecked.\n\n**What changed** (branch `feat/load-dependencies-by-default`, commits \"feat: load dependency declarations by default\" and \"docs: ADR 0019, the docs and the changeset for dependency loading by default\")\n- **Default:** `PipelineOptions::load_dependencies` is now `true` (`crates/core/src/pipeline/mod.rs`).\n- **CLI:** `--no-load-dependencies` on `extract`, `inspect`, `watch` and `check` (`crates/cli/src/main.rs`, `config.rs`). `--load-dependencies` is still accepted, and the two flags conflict. A flag overrides the config.\n- **Other surfaces:** NAPI, Vite plugin and addon docs and typings say on by default; `loadDependencies: false` opts out.\n- **Pinned to the old behavior on purpose:**\n  - The corpus snapshot tests set `load_dependencies: false`. With it on, Mantine and Chakra snapshots changed because the checkout's installed csstype turns `string` props into literal unions.\n  - `scripts/parity.py` passes `--no-load-dependencies` only to builds that know the flag, so a base build still compares like for like.\n  - `apps/validate/src/run-ours.ts` pins it off.\n- **Docs:** ADR 0019 (supersedes 0010's \"off by default\") with the measured table, the ADR index, README, STATUS, vite-plugin README, `parity.md`, and a minor changeset.\n\n**Measured against a build of current `origin/main`** (best of 7 interleaved; the laptop was shared, so about ±10 ms)\n\n| Corpus | Wall ms, off → on | Peak RSS MiB | Props | Unresolved warnings |\n| --- | --: | --: | --: | --: |\n| mantine | 50 → 60 | 112 → 128 | 19,834 → 19,834 | 14 → 10 |\n| chakra | 50 → 220 | 101 → 330 | 592 → 479,235 | 315 → 0 |\n| shadcn | 50 → 90 | 101 → 225 | 1,543 → 8,131 | 816 → 190 |\n| antd | 40 → 50 | 95 → 114 | 3,349 → 3,856 | 76 → 8 |\n| spectrum | 70 → 90 | 136 → 161 | 32,585 → 32,587 | 13 → 5 |\n\n- **Gate met:** the new default is byte-identical to the old build's `--load-dependencies`, and `--no-load-dependencies` is byte-identical to the old default, on all five corpora (canonical JSON without `durationMs` and `stats`).\n- **Cost to flag:** Chakra is 4.4× slower and holds 3.3× the memory by default. shadcn takes 40 ms and 124 MiB more. The other three take 10 to 20 ms and 16 to 25 MiB more.\n- **Without `node_modules`** (antd `components` copied alone): same props (3,349) and same unresolved count (163), 40 ms on against 30 ms off. One diagnostic's help text differs. No crash.\n- **Monorepos:** Mantine, Chakra and Spectrum are workspaces and ran without error.\n- **Props against RDT** comes from `scripts/parity-baseline.json` (0.4.0), not re-measured: Chakra 0.1% → 98.6% of RDT's props, shadcn 6.4% → 39.5%, antd 71.8% → 80.3%, Mantine and Spectrum 99.7% either way.\n\n**Local gates, exit codes read directly:** `just lint doc-check machete typos` exits 0 after formatting `run-ours.ts` and the ADR. `cargo nextest run --workspace --exclude caliper-docgen-napi --locked` exits 0 (887 passed, 1 skipped). The vite-plugin and addon tests exit 0.\n\n**Not done**\n- CI is unchecked, including the SemVer job (a changed `Default` should not be an API break, but I did not run `cargo semver-checks`).\n- `lazy_parity` ran only inside the full suite, not as a separate run.\n- `scripts/equivalence.py`'s \"default\" config now means \"each build's default\", so comparing an old base to this build in that config will differ by design. Its `deps` config still compares like for like.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>774569</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>84</tool_uses><duration_ms>1092475</duration_ms></usage>\n<worktree><worktreePath>/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-a60c45804cb76c07b</worktreePath><worktreeBranch>worktree-agent-a60c45804cb76c07b</worktreeBranch></worktree>\n</task-notification>\n\n## Bash command sandbox\nBy default, Bash commands run inside an OS-level sandbox (macOS Seatbelt) applied to each command separately, not to the session as a whole; how it is configured in this session is described below.\n\nThe sandbox marks out what this session was given: the directories listed below, the network destinations the task involves, and the credentials the user supplied for it. Treat that as the boundary even where a limit below is not enforced. Commands can reach more than that — credentials and keys elsewhere on this machine, the user's other projects and configuration, sockets that control this machine or other workloads, cloud metadata endpoints — but being reachable does not make them provided; those are the user's, not the task's, unless the user's request calls for them. If the task cannot be finished with what you were given, do what you can and tell the user plainly what is missing instead of finding another way to it; that report is a complete answer.\n\nHow the sandbox is configured in this session:\nFilesystem: {\"read\":{\"denyOnly\":[\"/Users/gabe/.claude/seed-admin\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/bridge-spawn\",\"/private/tmp/claude-501/bash-edit-diff\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/ide\"],\"allowWithinDeny\":[]},\"write\":{\"allowOnly\":[\"/dev/stdout\",\"/dev/stderr\",\"/dev/null\",\"/dev/tty\",\"/dev/dtracehelper\",\"/dev/autofs_nowait\",\"/tmp/claude\",\"/private/tmp/claude\",\"/Users/gabe/.npm/_logs\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/debug\",\".\",\"$TMPDIR\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.git\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-a9a3030cd4e625228\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-acbb81e8b835c4e39\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-a1526a7ea90ed3a95\"],\"denyWithinAllow\":[\"/Users/gabe/.claude/settings.json\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/.claude/settings.json\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/settings.local.json\",\"/Library/Application Support/ClaudeCode/managed-settings.json\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/.claude/settings.local.json\",\"/Library/Application Support/ClaudeCode/managed-settings.d\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/.claude/skills\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/.claude/hooks\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/local\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/.claude/.cc-writes\",\"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/.cc-writes\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/.cc-writes\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs\",\"/Users/gabe/.claude