{"parentUuid":"94e8c863-3a2f-4df0-bc39-e2a6a1af2bda","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgPUQ5Ne1eVaPggCjAAj4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"PR #202 makes dependency loading the default, and 15 of its 16 checks pass. The one pending job is the non-blocking Equivalence check. The fork couldn't watch CI itself because its worktree was deleted partway through.\n\n**What changed**\n- **Default:** `PipelineOptions::load_dependencies` is `true`. The CLI has `--no-load-dependencies` on `extract`, `inspect`, `watch` and `check`, and `--load-dependencies` is still accepted as a no-op alias. The two flags conflict, and a flag overrides the config.\n- **Other surfaces:** the NAPI, Vite plugin and addon docs and types say on by default, with `loadDependencies: false` to opt out.\n- **Docs:** ADR 0019 (it supersedes 0010's \"off by default\"), the ADR index, README, STATUS, `parity.md` and a minor changeset.\n- **Pinned to the old behaviour on purpose:** the corpus snapshot tests (with it on, the Mantine and Chakra snapshots changed because the installed csstype turns `string` props into literal unions), `apps/validate/src/run-ours.ts`, and `scripts/parity.py`, which passes `--no-load-dependencies` only to builds that know the flag.\n\n**Measured against `main`** (best of 7 interleaved, about ±10 ms because the laptop was shared)\n\n| Corpus | Time, off → on | Peak memory, off → on | Props | Unresolved warnings |\n| --- | --: | --: | --: | --: |\n| Mantine | 50 → 60 ms | 112 → 128 MiB | 19,834 → 19,834 | 14 → 10 |\n| Chakra | 50 → 220 ms | 101 → 330 MiB | 592 → 479,235 | 315 → 0 |\n| shadcn | 50 → 90 ms | 101 → 225 MiB | 1,543 → 8,131 | 816 → 190 |\n| antd | 40 → 50 ms | 95 → 114 MiB | 3,349 → 3,856 | 76 → 8 |\n| Spectrum | 70 → 90 ms | 136 → 161 MiB | 32,585 → 32,587 | 13 → 5 |\n\n**The cost, plainly**\n- Chakra is 4.4× slower and holds 3.3× the memory by default. shadcn takes 40 ms and 124 MiB more. The other three take 10–20 ms and 16–25 MiB more.\n- Against RDT's props (from the 0.4.0 baseline, not re-measured): Chakra 0.1% → 98.6%, shadcn 6.4% → 39.5%, antd 71.8% → 80.3%.\n- **Without `node_modules`:** same props and unresolved count, 40 ms on against 30 ms off, no crash. Monorepos (Mantine, Chakra, Spectrum) ran without error.\n\n**Verified:** the new default is byte-identical to the old build with `--load-dependencies`, and `--no-load-dependencies` is byte-identical to the old default, on all five corpora. Lint and 887 tests pass, plus the vite-plugin and addon tests.\n\n**Not done:** `cargo semver-checks` (a changed `Default` shouldn't break the API, but the SemVer CI job passed), and `lazy_parity` ran only inside the full suite. The `default` config in `equivalence.py` now means \"each build's default\", so comparing an old base to this build in that config differs by design.\n\n**Merge notes:** #202 changes the default for the CLI and library, and #198 and #200 change how the lazy session loads dependencies, so merging #198 → #200 first keeps the memory story clean. I'd merge #202 after them.\n\nRunning now: `knob-and-chain`, `confidence-score` and `prop-gap2`. Open PRs: #196–#202 and #160. Two forks lost worktrees to what looks like an outside cleanup, so if you remove any more, wait until the running forks report."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":366,"cache_read_input_tokens":730047,"output_tokens":1329,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":366,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1329,"cache_read_input_tokens":730047,"cache_creation_input_tokens":366,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":366},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"f79507d9-6a50-489a-8f10-d2dfd7a4e490","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgPUQ4u7sMYecH1h3MfWY","requestRef":"a9555ab8-8f41-496a-b0f5-1cb1d382d850","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c18aac63-62a5-4015-ab28-222bdf4d1fb6","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:02:22.922Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"fix/prop-gap","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
