:"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"chore/reset-equivalence-allow-list","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"1a9aa2c7-1922-4e16-9d0c-e57f9466f0e6","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"bc5176d7-6e57-4f44-a79c-14dc9371404a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019TMJ16cfV61Knx63LkN9PJ","type":"tool_result","content":"## Summary\n\nAdd offline labels for checker-only and summarized props to the TypeScript oracle, then evaluate Caliper-only confidence signals against both missing props and shared-prop type disagreements. This PR adds research tooling and a no-go report; it does not route production extraction through the checker.\n\nIndependent of the prop-gap PR stack. The recorded measurements use the binary at `3f20f965` with #204–#207 applied.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Re-ran the pinned five corpora and fixtures against TypeScript 7.1 beta from one binary. The oracle produced 518,268 labelled shared props after skipping three ambiguous export matches and matching export names by case.\n- The missing-prop metric excludes `ref` and `key`, which Caliper deliberately omits. Case-sensitive matching removes eight false Spectrum missing labels from lowercase style helpers. At a 10% component budget, five-corpus missing-prop recall is 23% for the warning rule, 3% for the smoothed table, and 6% for the logistic model.\n- At the same budget, the model catches 25% of soft shared-prop disagreements and the table catches 27%.\n- The sole `wrong` oracle label is `RouterProvider.navigate`, whose source uses aliases that the checker instantiates under an unaugmented `RouterConfig`. None of the tested scores catches that label at a 20% component budget.\n- `scripts/confidence.py` ran end-to-end on the fresh oracle output; all eight validation tests and the full lint recipe passed locally.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"35dd287f-fbd2-4053-885e-f2c9d90372ec","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:28:22.420Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## Summary\n\nAdd offline labels for checker-only and summarized props to the TypeScript oracle, then evaluate Caliper-only confidence signals against both missing props and shared-prop type disagreements. This PR adds research tooling and a no-go report; it does not route production extraction through the checker.\n\nIndependent of the prop-gap PR stack. The recorded measurements use the binary at `3f20f965` with #204–#207 applied.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Re-ran the pinned five corpora and fixtures against TypeScript 7.1 beta from one binary. The oracle produced 518,268 labelled shared props after skipping three ambiguous export matches and matching export names by case.\n- The missing-prop metric excludes `ref` and `key`, which Caliper deliberately omits. Case-sensitive matching removes eight false Spectrum missing labels from lowercase style helpers. At a 10% component budget, five-corpus missing-prop recall is 23% for the warning rule, 3% for the smoothed table, and 6% for the logistic model.\n- At the same budget, the model catches 25% of soft shared-prop disagreements and the table catches 27%.\n- The sole `wrong` oracle label is `RouterProvider.navigate`, whose source uses aliases that the checker instantiates under an unaugmented `RouterConfig`. None of the tested scores catches that label at a 20% component budget.\n- `scripts/confidence.py` ran end-to-end on the fresh oracle output; all eight validation tests and the full lint recipe passed locally.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"dangerouslyDisableSandbox":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"be9084fe-9b17-4ede-9ebb-d63dd584a42e","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","branch":"chore/reset-equivalence-allow-list","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1a9aa2c7-1922-4e16-9d0c-e57f9466f0e6","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"chore/reset-equivalence-allow-list","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
