{"parentUuid":"cd952d11-ab34-432a-8e1e-aa63ca42ceb3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgQvpo1s4wWBNtBLH68pP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1778,"cache_read_input_tokens":747850,"output_tokens":2607,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1286},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1778,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2607,"cache_read_input_tokens":747850,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1778,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1778},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":15560,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"709929bd-93f6-4332-a6cc-79d17ac95f72","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgQvpna5867cPp7hpkQPS","requestRef":"16999ab1-9002-4999-a209-d5ebd752dd6d","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c06099fb-27af-4bbb-b004-b5d0039405eb","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:29:39.679Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"chore/reset-equivalence-allow-list","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"c06099fb-27af-4bbb-b004-b5d0039405eb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgQvpo1s4wWBNtBLH68pP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Codex merged a lot while the forks were rate-limited. Everything I had in flight is merged except the release PR (#217), and `main` has two failing gates that need attention.\n\n**What merged (#196–#222)**\n- **My open PRs:** #196 (LSP removal), #197 (`fillAfter`), #198 and #200 (lazy dependency loading), #199 (empty allow-list), #201 (`Record`/`Pick` bases), and #202 (dependencies loaded by default).\n- **Codex's work that replaced my failed forks:**\n  - #203 chains the lazy dependency layers. A growth stays in a bounded chain that flattens after eight links, and the whole-demand load starts after three growths. The PR says whole-project time improved on all five corpora, and shadcn's 50-request peak went from 94 to 144 MB compared with a 48-growth threshold. That is the speed-over-memory choice you asked for.\n  - #204–#207, #209–#214, #218–#220 are the structural prop-gap fixes: static and namespace component members, generic namespace members, polymorphic factory results, Chakra recipe props, asserted props on exported aliases, discriminated `Extract` over dependency arrays, and callable and imported component members. I haven't measured their combined effect on the shadcn and antd recall.\n  - #208 is the confidence-score measurement, with a result below.\n  - #221 and #222 are release tooling.\n\n**#208 changes my proposal: it is a no-go for a Caliper-only score.** Over 518,268 oracle-labelled props, at a 10% component budget:\n\n| Rule | Missing-prop recall | Soft type disagreements caught |\n| --- | --: | --: |\n| Today's warning rule | 23% | not reported |\n| Smoothed risk table | 3% | 27% |\n| Logistic model | 6% | 25% |\n\n- The oracle has exactly one `wrong` label across all of it (`RouterProvider.navigate`), and none of the scores catches it at 20%.\n- So signals we can compute without the checker don't reliably predict where we're wrong, and the existing warning rule is the best of them. The routing idea needs a different trigger. A cheaper variant would be to run the checker over a sample to find the real disagreements, not to predict them. I'd drop the risk-table plan.\n\n**Two failures on `main`, not yet diagnosed**\n1. **Scorecard: speed gate failed.** Mantine 109.9 ms against main's 79.9 ms, and Chakra 75.0 ms against 51.1 ms, both over the 1.1× limit. The scorecard corpora have no dependencies installed, so the likely cause is #202 flipping the default: dependency loading with nothing to load still adds 10 ms or so. The fix is probably to pin the scorecard to `--no-load-dependencies`, as `parity.py` was. The other possibility is the added structural work in #204–#220. I haven't confirmed either.\n2. **Parity: Mantine and Spectrum installs failed** with `Dynamic require of \"util\" is not supported`. That's the Yarn crash under Node 26 that #189 was meant to fix, and it still fails in CI, so that fix didn't work.\n\n**My failed forks:** `prop-gap2`, `knob-and-chain` and `confidence-score` all hit the weekly limit. Their work is superseded by Codex's PRs, so I won't resume them. Their worktrees still hold uncommitted changes; I'll leave them for you to remove.\n\n**Next steps, if you want them**\n1. Diagnose and fix the Scorecard regression, with a bisect between #201 and `main` to separate the default flip from the resolver work. This matters most, since it's the speed gate.\n2. Make the Parity installs work (a real Yarn-under-Node fix).\n3. A clean combined measurement of the whole merged state.\n\nI'll hold on launching forks if the weekly limit hasn't reset (5am PT). Tell me to go ahead and I'll try."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1778,"cache_read_input_tokens":747850,"output_tokens":2607,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1286},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1778,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2607,"cache_read_input_tokens":747850,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1778,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1778},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"709929bd-93f6-4332-a6cc-79d17ac95f72","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgQvpna5867cPp7hpkQPS","requestRef":"16999ab1-9002-4999-a209-d5ebd752dd6d","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"d962145a-1212-4e55-a2a0-056e271c5800","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:29:43.813Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"chore/reset-equivalence-allow-list","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
