{"parentUuid":"23f2495f-2494-48ba-a55c-e190c63f86b8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgQwJ9zg9yHvYSrmnkddT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":421,"cache_read_input_tokens":779992,"output_tokens":2702,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1051},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":421,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2702,"cache_read_input_tokens":779992,"cache_creation_input_tokens":421,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":421},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":12545,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"badf95ba-7e93-42f5-afcd-352beb4f3ee4","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgQwJ9cMjH8aHgLvxhzuq","requestRef":"f2e754b8-fb69-44b3-a8e5-52a892d139f6","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"85a52862-fb11-4d21-ac96-f31537f3fcc9","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:35:48.515Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"85a52862-fb11-4d21-ac96-f31537f3fcc9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgQwJ9zg9yHvYSrmnkddT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Cleanup is mostly done, and the adversarial pass on the Codex work found real problems.\n\n**Cleanup**\n- **Removed my worktrees:** the three failed forks' (all clean; their branches are the ones Codex used for #203, #204–#208 and #212, so nothing was lost), plus four older leftovers (the matching fork, the dropped thread-cap experiment, the stopped addon fork that #197 replaced, and the earlier clean ones). Everything uncommitted was backed up first to `/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/worktree-backups/`.\n- **Deleted 12 stale local branches** (the merged PR heads and the failed forks' branches). My own worktree is now detached at `origin/main`.\n- **Left alone:**\n  - `agent-a482304b1a114609f`, the old unattributed resolver patch (backed up, still your call).\n  - Codex's 20 named worktrees (`ambient-callable-components`, `antd-getprops`, `reconcile-201`/`202`, and so on). Every one of their branch tips is in `main`, so they are stale by content, but I can't tell whether Codex is running. When you know it isn't, `git worktree remove` each one.\n\n**Adversarial analysis of the Codex work (#203–#222)**\n\n*What holds up*\n- Every merged PR had all required checks green, and every file the PRs added exists on `main`, so nothing was stranded despite twelve merging in the same second.\n- No added `.unwrap()`, `.expect()`, `std::HashMap` or `println!` in non-test code, and the cache schema was bumped to 24 with a golden test.\n- #208 reports an honest negative: the confidence score is a no-go (above).\n\n*Problems, most serious first*\n1. **The equivalence allow-list is full again.** I emptied it in #199 because it should be empty on `main`. It now has 85 entries, including blanket patterns: `antd/* prop-added *`, `shadcn/deps* prop-added *`, `shadcn/deps* notable-added *`, `shadcn/deps* diagnostic-added info OPAQUE_TYPE *`, `shadcn/deps* stat-changed componentsExtracted`. On those corpora the safety net now allows any added prop or diagnostic. It also whitelists new warnings: a Mantine `OPAQUE_TYPE … cannot be used as a component's props base` and a shadcn `UNRESOLVABLE_IMPORT … 'TrustedHTML'`. New warnings send components to Storybook's docgen, and nobody has quantified that. It also allows new `CIRCULAR_REFERENCE` infos on shadcn, after we removed false ones earlier.\n2. **A speed regression merged because no gate ran.** Scorecard failed on `main` after the merges: Mantine 109.9 ms against 79.9 ms (+38%), Chakra 75.0 against 51.1 (+47%). The scorecard and parity gates only run after merge or weekly, not on PRs, and twenty PRs went in together, so the culprit can't be named without a bisect. The likeliest cause is #202's default flip, but I haven't confirmed it.\n3. **The accuracy gate is broken too.** Parity can't install Mantine and Spectrum (the Yarn error), so those two corpora haven't been measured on `main`. My #189 fix didn't work in CI.\n4. **Thin verification in the PR bodies.** They cite \"core unit tests (639–649)\" rather than the full workspace run (about 890 tests), and dismiss snapshot differences as path-only. I saw the same path noise myself, so that's plausible, but it could mask a real change. Several say the allow-list \"covers all measured differences\", which is circular, since the same PRs widened the list.\n5. **Name-based special-casing.** `extractor/interface.rs` matches callee names `cva`, `tv`, `defineRecipe`, `recipe`, `defineSlotRecipe` and `chakra`. This is the library-name hardcoding we agreed to avoid, and it breaks under import aliasing.\n6. **Unmeasured effect.** Nobody has re-run the oracle, the Storybook harness or the RDT parity on merged `main`, so the claimed shadcn and antd gains are unverified.\n\n**What I'd do, in order**\n1. A PR that empties the allow-list again and adds a check that fails if it is non-empty on `main`.\n2. Make the speed gate run on PRs that touch the resolver, as Equivalence does, and bisect the +38%/+47% regression.\n3. A real fix for the Yarn install in Parity.\n4. A combined measurement of the merged `main`: oracle, harness, RDT parity.\n5. Replace the callee-name list with shape detection, or document it as a known limit.\n\nI'll start with items 1 and 2 if you want them. A bisect needs a fork and a quiet machine, and the weekly limit may still block forks."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":421,"cache_read_input_tokens":779992,"output_tokens":2702,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1051},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":421,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2702,"cache_read_input_tokens":779992,"cache_creation_input_tokens":421,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":421},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"badf95ba-7e93-42f5-afcd-352beb4f3ee4","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgQwJ9cMjH8aHgLvxhzuq","requestRef":"f2e754b8-fb69-44b3-a8e5-52a892d139f6","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"8f6667aa-d05b-4d2e-b897-82930f738ac1","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:35:54.187Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"purring-snuggling-