{"parentUuid":"060631b8-d129-4697-a7b4-e1bdf3977c9f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgR361fjgqgTbCBQoDs3w","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012BDgm5xP1AsH8rCs4qXBFS","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Allow-list guard, PR speed gate, Parity install fix","subagent_type":"fork","isolation":"worktree","name":"gates","prompt":"Track AH: repair the safety gates. Branch off origin/main (fetch first); PR base `main`; one PR per item is fine (item 1 and 2 may share one). Do NOT remove any worktrees (others, including Codex, are using the repo; `git worktree remove/prune` only your own at the end is not needed). Context: after Codex's 20-PR batch (#203-#222) three gates are broken. ITEM 1 allow-list: scripts/equivalence-allow.json on main has 85 entries, many blanket (`antd/* prop-added *`, `shadcn/deps* prop-added *`, `shadcn/deps* notable-added *`, `shadcn/deps* diagnostic-added info OPAQUE_TYPE *`, `shadcn/deps* stat-changed componentsExtracted`, `mantine/deps* diagnostic-added warning OPAQUE_TYPE 'Payload* ...`, new CIRCULAR_REFERENCE infos); it must be empty on main (design: a PR lists only its own intended differences, and a stacked PR compares with its own base). Do: empty it; add enforcement: (a) scripts/equivalence.py validates entries (reject a bare category wildcard: every entry must name a specific component, prop or diagnostic code/text, not a lone `*`; unit tests in scripts/test_equivalence.py) and (b) a check that FAILS CI on pushes to main (and in the weekly parity workflow) when the allow-list is non-empty (a small step or workflow `allow-list-empty`, documented in docs/parity.md); while on PRs it may be non-empty. Also, since the emptied list will make the Equivalence job report real differences vs main for any open PR that relied on it: just note that in the PR body. ITEM 2 speed gate on PRs: `.github/workflows/scorecard.yml` / scripts/scorecard.py gate (10% regression vs base build timed in the same job, RDT ratio >= 10x, scaling) currently runs only after merge/manually, so a +38% (Mantine 109.9 vs 79.9 ms) and +47% (Chakra 75.0 vs 51.1 ms) regression merged ungated. Add a pull_request trigger with the same path filter as equivalence.yml (resolver/extractor/types/pipeline, plus scorecard files), comparing against the PR's own base ref (`github.base_ref`, passed via env, not interpolated into the shell), restricted to mantine and chakra (shallow corpora, keep the job under ~8 minutes), `continue-on-error: true` initially with the result in the job summary, and document the promotion criterion (make it blocking after 10 consecutive green runs on main-targeting PRs) in docs/performance.md. Another fork (`scorecard-bisect`) is separately bisecting the current regression and may change scripts/scorecard.py's modes: coordinate by keeping your edits to the workflow file and a small flag; rebase if needed. ITEM 3 Parity install: the weekly Parity workflow fails to install Mantine and react-spectrum (`Error: Dynamic require of \"util\" is not supported` in .parity/logs/install-mantine.log; the failing run is 40320804312: `gh run view 40320804312 --log` for the exact step/log); PR #189 (merged) pinned Node 24 for corpus installs but it still fails in CI. Find the real cause (which node/yarn actually ran? yarn 4.x bundled with a corepack shim vs the repo's setup-node; `packageManager` field; `YARN_IGNORE_PATH`; ESM/CJS loader flag `--experimental-require-module`), reproduce locally if possible, fix scripts/parity.py setup and/or .github/workflows/parity.yml so the install works, and verify with `gh workflow run parity.yml --ref <your branch>` then `gh run watch` (run the smallest corpus set that includes mantine and spectrum). Report the cause. Gates: `python3 scripts/test_equivalence.py` and any python tests, `just lint doc-check machete typos` exit code read directly (never pipe through tail), CI green, changeset only if shipped text changes (CI/tooling usually none). Time-box ~80 tool calls. Commits end with Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED; PR bodies end with https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED; never push main/force-push/merge; /usr/bin/git with sandbox off, one plain git command per call."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":507,"cache_read_input_tokens":786908,"output_tokens":6293,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1804},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":507,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6293,"cache_read_input_tokens":786908,"cache_creation_input_tokens":507,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":507},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_012BDgm5xP1AsH8rCs4qXBFS":{"description":"Allow-list guard, PR speed gate, Parity install fix","subagent_type":"fork","isolation":"worktree","name":"gates","prompt":"Track AH: repair the safety gates. Branch off origin/main (fetch first); PR base `main`; one PR per item is fine (item 1 and 2 may share one). Do NOT remove any worktrees (others, including Codex, are using the repo; `git worktree remove/prune` only your own at the end is not needed). Context: after Codex's 20-PR batch (#203-#222) three gates are broken. ITEM 1 allow-list: scripts/equivalence-allow.json on main has 85 entries, many blanket (`antd/* prop-added *`, `shadcn/deps* prop-added *`, `shadcn/deps* notable-added *`, `shadcn/deps* diagnostic-added info OPAQUE_TYPE *`, `shadcn/deps* stat-changed componentsExtracted`, `mantine/deps* diagnostic-added warning OPAQUE_TYPE 'Payload* ...`, new CIRCULAR_REFERENCE in