{"parentUuid":"a8d60810-2b2a-45f5-b069-38832ef5a6b7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgR361fjgqgTbCBQoDs3w","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01U6o1inMuycK4VmebpjsACf","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Bisect the Scorecard speed regression and fix it","subagent_type":"fork","isolation":"worktree","name":"scorecard-bisect","prompt":"Track AI: find and fix the Scorecard speed regression on main. Do NOT remove worktrees (others are using the repo). Branch off origin/main (fetch first); PR base `main`. Facts: the Scorecard run after Codex's merges failed: mantine 109.9 ms vs main's 79.9 ms (+38%), chakra 75.0 ms vs 51.1 ms (+47%) (run 40310917278; `gh run view 40310917278 --log`; the scorecard corpora are sparse fetches WITHOUT dependencies installed; `scripts/scorecard.py` times `extract --json` with a warm parse cache, process start to exit; gates in docs/performance.md). Candidates: (a) #202 (dependency loading by default) added work even with no node_modules (ADR 0019 measured 40 ms on vs 30 ms off for antd without node_modules); (b) Codex's resolver/extractor additions #203-#220 (static/namespace members, generic factory results, polymorphic factories, Chakra recipe props in extractor/interface.rs, callable component members, discriminated Extract over dependency arrays, scoped module augmentations, etc.); (c) cache schema 24 invalidating warm caches in the scorecard. Do: BISECT with real builds: merge commits on origin/main from the merge of #201 (5519cddb) to HEAD (`git log --first-parent`): build release CLI for ~8-10 commits chosen by bisection (build into separate target dirs under /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/bisect/, `cargo build --release -p caliper-docgen`), time `extract --json` on the mantine and chakra scorecard corpora (python3 scripts/scorecard.py setup or its corpus cache `.scorecard/corpora`; use hyperfine 2 (JSON: measurements[].time_wall_clock.value) best-of-15 interleaved, warm cache, `--no-load-dependencies` AND default), report a table commit -> time; the machine may be shared with other forks: interleave and repeat. Classify: if the jump is #202's default flip, the scorecard's meaning is 'no dependencies installed', so pin the scorecard to explicit `--no-load-dependencies` (record dependency-loading cost separately as its own row/gate with a fair threshold) instead of calling it a regression; if it is resolver work, profile (macOS `sample`) the culprit PR's hot path and fix or narrow it (e.g. a lookup per component that should be memoized or a scan of all files per type) with byte-identical output (`just equivalence`, lazy_parity). Report which PR(s) cost how many ms on each corpus. Gates: scorecard `--check` passes locally for mantine and chakra vs a build of the pre-regression commit (`python3 scripts/scorecard.py --bin NEW --base-bin OLD --rdt --check`), `just lint doc-check machete typos` and `cargo nextest run --workspace --exclude caliper-docgen-napi --locked` exit codes read directly (never pipe through tail), CI green, changeset if shipped behavior changes. Time-box ~90 tool calls. Commits end with Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED; PR bodies end with https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED; never push main/force-push/merge; /usr/bin/git with sandbox off, one plain git command per call."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":507,"cache_read_input_tokens":786908,"output_tokens":6293,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1804},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":507,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6293,"cache_read_input_tokens":786908,"cache_creation_input_tokens":507,"cache_creation":{"ephe