{"parentUuid":"d5b0b8ca-53b0-44ff-b312-aba99370af93","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgR361fjgqgTbCBQoDs3w","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JTPH8BJf1kRdfiavGHaC2n","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Replace callee-name lists with shape detection","subagent_type":"fork","isolation":"worktree","name":"callee-shape","prompt":"Track AJ: remove library-name special-casing from the extractor. Do NOT remove worktrees (others are using the repo). Branch off origin/main (fetch first); PR base `main`. Finding from an adversarial review: crates/core/src/extractor/interface.rs (added by Codex's #213 'Recover inferred Chakra recipe props' and earlier cva code) matches callee NAMES: `matches!(callee_name, \"cva\" | \"tv\" | \"defineRecipe\" | \"recipe\" | \"defineSlotRecipe\" | \"chakra\")` and `usize::from(matches!(callee_name, \"cva\" | \"chakra\"))` for the config argument position. That is library-name hardcoding (the project rule since the research report: detect by shape, not by library names; see AGENTS.md, docs/architecture/extractor*.md, ADR 0006/0014 and crates/core/src/known.rs for the existing, measured shortcut tables) and breaks under import aliasing (`import { cva as c }`). Do: (1) read the code and its tests; list every place where a callee name decides behavior in crates/core/src/extractor and resolver (grep for string-literal callee/function names: cva, tv, recipe, defineRecipe, defineSlotRecipe, chakra, styled, forwardRef, memo, lazy, etc.; forwardRef/memo/lazy are React API and an accepted, documented exception if they go through the import-source check; report the rest); (2) replace the variant-recipe name list with shape detection: a call is a variant bag when one of its object-literal arguments (any position) has a `variants` property whose value is an object of objects (and optionally `defaultVariants`/`slots`/`compoundVariants`); the `chakra(...)`-style config position falls out of that shape rule; keep behavior identical for the real libraries (cva, tailwind-variants tv, Chakra defineRecipe/defineSlotRecipe/recipe, Panda cva/sva) and make it work under import aliasing and for unknown libraries with the same shape; (3) guard against false positives: require the `variants` object's values to be objects of string/array/object-literal class values, and emit nothing (no new diagnostics) when the shape does not match; (4) tests: exact-value tests for aliased imports (`import { cva as c }`, `import { tv as t }`), an unknown library `makeVariants({ variants: { size: { sm: 'x' } } })`, a negative case (an object with `variants` that is not a map of maps, e.g. a plain React prop), and the existing recipe tests unchanged; (5) gates: `just equivalence` against origin/main must be byte-identical on all five corpora in the default and deps configurations (the allow-list is being emptied by another fork: do not rely on it; any difference must be explained and justified in the PR, e.g. aliased imports now found), lazy parity, cache schema bump + golden test only if SourceData changes, `just lint doc-check machete typos` and `cargo nextest run --workspace --exclude caliper-docgen-napi --locked` exit codes read directly (never pipe through tail), CI green, changeset. If shape detection cannot cover some case without the name, keep that one name behind the import-source check (resolved package specifier, not the identifier) and document it in docs/architecture. Time-box ~70 tool calls. Commits end with Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED; PR body ends with https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED; never push main/force-push/merge; /usr/bin/git with sandbox off, one plain git command per call."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":507,"cache_read_input_tokens":786908,"output_tokens":6293,"output_tokens_details":