0917278 --log`; the scorecard corpora are sparse fetches WITHOUT dependencies installed; `scripts/scorecard.py` times `extract --json` with a warm parse cache, process start to exit; gates in docs/performance.md). Candidates: (a) #202 (dependency loading by default) added work even with no node_modules (ADR 0019 measured 40 ms on vs 30 ms off for antd without node_modules); (b) Codex's resolver/extractor additions #203-#220 (static/namespace members, generic factory results, polymorphic factories, Chakra recipe props in extractor/interface.rs, callable component members, discriminated Extract over dependency arrays, scoped module augmentations, etc.); (c) cache schema 24 invalidating warm caches in the scorecard. Do: BISECT with real builds: merge commits on origin/main from the merge of #201 (5519cddb) to HEAD (`git log --first-parent`): build release CLI for ~8-10 commits chosen by bisection (build into separate target dirs under /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/bisect/, `cargo build --release -p caliper-docgen`), time `extract --json` on the mantine and chakra scorecard corpora (python3 scripts/scorecard.py setup or its corpus cache `.scorecard/corpora`; use hyperfine 2 (JSON: measurements[].time_wall_clock.value) best-of-15 interleaved, warm cache, `--no-load-dependencies` AND default), report a table commit -> time; the machine may be shared with other forks: interleave and repeat. Classify: if the jump is #202's default flip, the scorecard's meaning is 'no dependencies installed', so pin the scorecard to explicit `--no-load-dependencies` (record dependency-loading cost separately as its own row/gate with a fair threshold) instead of calling it a regression; if it is resolver work, profile (macOS `sample`) the culprit PR's hot path and fix or narrow it (e.g. a lookup per component that should be memoized or a scan of all files per type) with byte-identical output (`just equivalence`, lazy_parity). Report which PR(s) cost how many ms on each corpus. Gates: scorecard `--check` passes locally for mantine and chakra vs a build of the pre-regression commit (`python3 scripts/scorecard.py --bin NEW --base-bin OLD --rdt --check`), `just lint doc-check machete typos` and `cargo nextest run --workspace --exclude caliper-docgen-napi --locked` exit codes read directly (never pipe through tail), CI green, changeset if shipped behavior changes. Time-box ~90 tool calls. Commits end with Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED; PR bodies end with https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED; never push main/force-push/merge; /usr/bin/git with sandbox off, one plain git command per call.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/a9720545efb857791.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"114f1a40-35b6-4807-9161-3488d8c115ad","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","branch":"HEAD","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d5b0b8ca-53b0-44ff-b312-aba99370af93","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId"