{"parentUuid":"bc926b27-e0d9-4ce9-865c-6869470eeab3","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"4e409928-47b1-4b10-b20a-0a330bbb5a06","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JTPH8BJf1kRdfiavGHaC2n","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Async agent launched successfully. (This tool result is internal metadata — never quote or paste any part of it, including the agentId below, into a user-facing reply.)\nagentId: a05d452585cdfc10a (internal ID - do not mention to user. Use SendMessage with to: 'a05d452585cdfc10a', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent.)\nThe agent is working in the background. You will be notified automatically when it completes. You know nothing about its results until that notification arrives — do not report, assume, or predict them; continue other work or respond to the user in the meantime.\nDo not duplicate this agent's work — avoid working with the same files or topics it is using.\noutput_file: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/a05d452585cdfc10a.output\nDo NOT Read or tail this file via the shell tool — it is the full subagent JSONL transcript and reading it will overflow your context. If the user asks for progress, say the agent is still running; you'll get a completion notification."}]}]},"uuid":"532fa53f-88c5-4aee-8ec6-1fc6dbd584a5","timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:52:21.606Z","toolUseResult":{"isAsync":true,"status":"async_launched","agentId":"a05d452585cdfc10a","description":"Replace callee-name lists with shape detection","resolvedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","prompt":"Track AJ: remove library-name special-casing from the extractor. Do NOT remove worktrees (others are using the repo). Branch off origin/main (fetch first); PR base `main`. Finding from an adversarial review: crates/core/src/extractor/interface.rs (added by Codex's #213 'Recover inferred Chakra recipe props' and earlier cva code) matches callee NAMES: `matches!(callee_name, \"cva\" | \"tv\" | \"defineRecipe\" | \"recipe\" | \"defineSlotRecipe\" | \"chakra\")` and `usize::from(matches!(callee_name, \"cva\" | \"chakra\"))` for the config argument position. That is library-name hardcoding (the project rule since the research report: detect by shape, not by library names; see AGENTS.md, docs/architecture/extractor*.md, ADR 0006/0014 and crates/core/src/known.rs for the existing, measured shortcut tables) and breaks under import aliasing (`import { cva as c }`). Do: (1) read the code and its tests; list every place where a callee name decides behavior in crates/core/src/extractor and resolver (grep for string-literal callee/function names: cva, tv, recipe, defineRecipe, defineSlotRecipe, chakra, styled, forwardRef, memo, lazy, etc.; forwardRef/memo/lazy are React API and an accepted, documented exception if they go through the import-source check; report the rest); (2) replace the variant-recipe name list with shape detection: a call is a variant bag when one of its object-literal arguments (any position) has a `variants` property whose value is an object of objects (and optionally `defaultVariants`/`slots`/`compoundVariants`); the `chakra(...)`-style config position falls out of that shape rule; keep behavior identical for the real libraries (cva, tailwind-variants tv, Chakra defineRecipe/defineSlotRecipe/recipe, Panda cva/sva) and make it work under import aliasing and for unknown libraries with the same shape; (3) guard against false positives: require the `variants` object's values to be objects of string/array/object-literal class values, and emit nothing (no new diagnostics) when the shape does not match; (4) tests: exact-value tests for aliased imports (`import { cva as c }`, `import { tv as t }`), an unknown library `makeVariants({ variants: { size: { sm: 'x' } } })`, a negative case (an object with `variants` that is not a map of maps, e.g. a plain React prop), and the existing recipe tests unchanged; (5) gates: `just equivalence` against origin/main must be byte-identical on all five corpora in the default and deps configurations (the allow-list is being emptied by another fork: do not rely on it; any difference must be explained and justified in the PR, e.g. aliased imports now found), lazy parity, cache schema bump + golden test only if SourceData changes, `just lint doc-check machete typos` and `cargo nextest run --workspace --exclude caliper-docgen-napi --locked` exit codes read directly (never pipe through tail), CI green, changeset. If shape detection cannot cover some case without the name, keep that one name behind the import-source check (resolved package specifier, not the identifier) and document it in docs/architecture. Time-box ~70 tool calls. Commits end with Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED; PR body ends with https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED; never push main/force-push/merge; /usr/bin/git with sandbox off, one plain git command per call.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/a05d452585cdfc10a.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"114f1a40-35b6-4807-9161-3488d8c115ad","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","branch":"HEAD","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"orin-dx/caliper","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0