orecard.py, scripts/equivalence*.py, .github/workflows, crates/core/src/extractor/interface.rs). Evidence: scripts/parity-baseline.json (0.4.0, deps on) lists, per corpus, the 'loss' categories (how many shared props where Caliper's type is worse than RDT's): Mantine (19,595 shared props): member read left as X[\"k\"] 6,542; template literal left 469; rest parameter lost 355; conditional left as source 226; utility type left as written 29; RefObject shown as Ref 10; typeof left in output 11; unbound type parameter 6. The other corpora are in the same file (read it: python3 -I -c json). These are real losses (a prop whose type text says `MantineSize[\"xs\"]` or leaves a conditional unevaluated tells a consumer nothing). Many fixes landed since 0.4.0 (indexed-access via resolved props #184, const-array spreads, Record/Pick bases, callable members, etc.), so FIRST re-measure on current main: build release; use `python3 scripts/parity.py setup/run` for the corpora that install in this environment, or the earlier scripts in /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/bench (loss_patterns.py, mismatch_kinds.py, quality.py, real_recall.py) against the installed corpora in /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/bench-corpus (mantine/packages/@mantine/core/src, chakra-ui/packages/react/src, shadcn-ui/apps/v4, ant-design/components, react-spectrum/packages) with RDT dumps (apps/validate; pnpm install --no-frozen-lockfile in the worktree and `git checkout pnpm-lock.yaml` afterwards, do not commit lockfile changes); get the current loss table per corpus. Then take the TOP categories by count and fix the structural causes in crates/core, one PR per category (stacked only if they depend on each other; base `main` otherwise): e.g. (1) 'member read left as X[\"k\"]': find the 3-5 dominant shapes by sampling 30 examples (T[K] over a generic parameter, over an imported const object, over a dependency interface, over a mapped type, over `typeof obj`) and implement the missing evaluation following TypeScript's model (one resolution path, then read; docs/architecture/resolver-type-resolution.md, ADRs 0010/0014/0015; AGENTS.md non-negotiables: emit a Diagnostic when degrading, no name-based special cases, pure/deterministic memo contract incl. `past_max_depth`); (2) template literal types left as source (expand when the parts are literal unions, up to the existing 4,096 cap; otherwise a clear opaque reason); (3) rest parameter lost in function types (keep `...args: T[]` in the printed signature: needs the output type to carry rest/optional: check PropType::Function and docs/adr for the output-contract constraints; a PropType change needs a schema version bump per ADR 0017 and an ADR note: if it does, implement it as its own PR and flag it); (4) conditional left as source (evaluate when operands are known; infer-based stay opaque). For each fix: exact-value tests, `just equivalence` showing only intended differences (put intended differences in the allow-list ONLY for your PR and as narrowly as possible: a fork is emptying the list on main and adding a validator that rejects bare `*` entries), lazy parity, oracle (`just equivalence --oracle`) no regression (wrong must stay ~0.0%), cache schema bump + golden test if SourceData changes, changeset, `just lint doc-check machete typos` and `cargo nextest run --workspace --exclude caliper-docgen-napi --locked` exit codes read directly (never pipe through tail), CI green. Report the loss table before/after per corpus. Time-box ~100 tool calls. Commits end with Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED; PR bodies end with https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED; never push main/force-push/merge; /usr/bin/git with sandbox off, one plain git command per call.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/aabbfc817ff6b5c71.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"8da6c8