{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","bridgeSessionId":"cse_01D7CJmXuD2ASqfBYm7Lk4WZ","lastSequenceNum":21749,"ownerAccountUuid":"138d593e-e185-4f72-89f2-82e1a501f134","ownerOrganizationUuid":"602db9b4-428d-49e6-a99c-64152cc62a79"}
{"parentUuid":"11ffdf53-fb90-4a2e-aadb-765b46e89d10","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgR3CvZrq8BHipTKwfPz3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Five forks are running, covering all five review items plus the two accuracy gaps. Each opens its PR against `main`, and I told every one not to remove worktrees, since Codex is also using the repo.\n\n**The five review items**\n1. **`gates`:**\n   - Empties the equivalence allow-list again and adds a validator that rejects bare category wildcards (`antd/* prop-added *`).\n   - Adds a check that fails CI on `main` when the list is non-empty.\n   - Adds a pull-request trigger for the speed gate, restricted to Mantine and Chakra, comparing against the PR's own base. It is non-blocking at first, and promoted after 10 consecutive green runs.\n   - Finds the real cause of the Yarn crash in Parity's Mantine and Spectrum installs (the #189 fix didn't hold) and fixes it. It will verify by dispatching the workflow on its branch.\n2. **`scorecard-bisect`:**\n   - Builds about 8–10 commits between #201 and `main` and times Mantine and Chakra on each, with dependencies on and off.\n   - If the jump is #202's default flip, the scorecard should be pinned to `--no-load-dependencies`, with dependency loading tracked as its own row. If it is resolver work, it profiles the culprit and fixes it with byte-identical output.\n3. **`callee-shape`:** replaces the `cva | tv | defineRecipe | recipe | defineSlotRecipe | chakra` name list with detection by shape (an object argument whose `variants` is a map of maps). This works under import aliasing and for unknown libraries, with a negative test for false positives, and output byte-identical on the corpora.\n4. **Measurement of merged `main`** (oracle, harness, RDT and react-docgen): held until `scorecard-bisect` finishes, because it needs a quiet machine.\n\n**The remaining gaps**\n- **`type-losses`:**\n  - It starts by re-measuring the 0.4.0 loss table (Mantine alone had 6,542 props left as `X[\"k\"]`, 469 template literals, 355 lost rest parameters and 226 unevaluated conditionals), since many fixes landed since.\n  - It then fixes the top categories by count, one PR each. A rest-parameter fix would change the output type, so it needs a schema version bump and an ADR note, and would be its own flagged PR.\n- **`unmatched-components`:**\n  - It lists every plausible RDT component we don't report, by declaration shape, and separates RDT false positives from real misses.\n  - It fixes the top real shapes in detection (by shape, not library name, with precision checks).\n  - It also checks which story-referenced components the addon fails to find, with counts by reason.\n\n**Not started:** the TS 7.1 on-demand work. The confidence-score result (#208) means prediction-based routing doesn't work: even at a 10% routed budget it caught only 23% of missing props. The honest alternative is to query a warm `tsc` for each component a story asks for, not to predict. Its feasibility depends on per-component latency, which is a timing measurement, so it waits with item 4.\n\nBetween merged PRs and the five open forks, the machine will be busy. The bisect interleaves and repeats its runs, so its numbers will carry some noise. Say if you want me to hold any fork."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9112,"cache_read_input_tokens":798165,"output_tokens":1094,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9112,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1094,"cache_read_input_tokens":798165,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9112,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9112},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"2570d50f-ab71-4457-9832-7905303bbc96","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgR3Cv8KMjnW3BUkDDruu","requestRef":"1c0c507d-987d-4adc-9349-3d15bd289c26","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"cfe8d556-564e-49e6-bc27-f9905d5310dd","timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:53:12.898Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"feat/component-recall","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
