{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","hash":"2f12327d63084b1faf22d0407bcd0151c2f9ef2036e692d08797104e6a8af7ef","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Found that all my earlier changesets violated AGENTS.md by starting with `- **…**` instead of a plain paragraph, since Callisto adds the changelog bullet itself. I'll send the corrected rule, with an example, to all six running forks along with the stacking rule.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012uPYae5M3Rqr1VQWERxqxc","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"gates","message":"House rules for commits, PRs and changesets (from AGENTS.md; apply before you commit and open PRs). Changesets: one short, consumer-facing paragraph per changeset, written for a user reading the release notes: friendly, plain, scannable. Start with the OUTCOME in the user's terms (what they now get or what stopped hurting), then, only when needed, the upgrade action or cost (a flag, a default, a number). No heading and no list marker at the start (Callisto adds the changelog bullet itself; the old '- **Bold:** ...' style is wrong now), no bold lead-in, no internal names (PR numbers, crate internals, 'memo', 'rebuild') unless the user must act on them, no hard wrapping (one line per paragraph), same front matter package list as before. Example: 'Props that come from a wrapped Radix or Base UI primitive now show their real unions, so Storybook renders them as selects. No action needed.' CI/tooling-only changes need no changeset. Commits: imperative subject, at most one or two sentences of why, no list of what changed, no 'This commit...'. PR bodies: succinct, no hard wrap, bullets/tables ok, end with the Claude-Session URL. Stacking: if your PR depends on an unmerged PR (yours or another fork's), set its base to that PR's HEAD BRANCH (never to main while it carries the parent's commits), say what it stacks on in the body, and give the bottom-up merge order in your final report; independent PRs have base main. The repo deletes head branches on merge, so merging bottom-up retargets children to main automatically. Commit your work in small logical commits as you go and push before you finish; do not leave anything uncommitted.","summary":"Send changeset, commit and stacking rules to gates"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Mfg4skiscXnBRWWo3wDTav","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"scorecard-bisect","message":"House rules for commits, PRs and changesets (from AGENTS.md; apply before you commit and open PRs). Changesets: one short, consumer-facing paragraph per changeset, written for a user reading the release notes: friendly, plain, scannable. Start with the OUTCOME in the user's terms (what they now get or what stopped hurting), then, only when needed, the upgrade action or cost (a flag, a default, a number). No heading and no list marker at the start (Callisto adds the changelog bullet itself; the old '- **Bold:** ...' style is wrong now), no bold lead-in, no internal names (PR numbers, crate internals, 'memo', 'rebuild') unless the user must act on them, no hard wrapping (one line per paragraph), same front matter package list as before. Example: 'Props that come from a wrapped Radix or Base UI primitive now show their real unions, so Storybook renders them as selects. No action needed.' CI/tooling-only changes need no changeset. Commits: imperative subject, at most one or two sentences of why, no list of what changed, no 'This commit...'. PR bodies: succinct, no hard wrap, bullets/tables ok, end with the Claude-Session URL. Stacking: if your PR depends on an unmerged PR (yours or another fork's), set its base to that PR's HEAD BRANCH (never to main while it carries the parent's commits), say what it stacks on in the body, and give the bottom-up merge order in your final report; independent PRs have base main. The repo deletes head branches on merge, so merging bottom-up retargets children to main automatically. Commit your work in small logical commits as you go and push before you finish; do not leave anything uncommitted.","summary":"Send changeset, commit and stacking rules to scorecard-bisect"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LvtmQmoSYuYthSs1dzYW7c","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"callee-shape","message":"House rules for commits, PRs and changesets (from AGENTS.md; apply before you commit and open PRs). Changesets: one short, consumer-facing paragraph per changeset, written for a user reading the release notes: friendly, plain, scannable. Start with the OUTCOME in the user's terms (what they now get or what stopped hurting), then, only when needed, the upgrade action or cost (a flag, a default, a number). No heading and no list marker at the start (Callisto adds the changelog bullet itself; the old '- **Bold:** ...' style is wrong now), no bold lead-in, no internal names (PR numbers, crate internals, 'memo', 'rebuild') unless the user must act on them, no hard wrapping (one line per paragraph), same front matter package list as before. Example: 'Props that come from a wrapped Radix or Base UI primitive now show their real unions, so Storybook renders them as selects. No action needed.' CI/tooling-only changes need no changeset. Commits: imperative subject, at most one or two sentences of why, no list of what changed, no 'This commit...'. PR bodies: succinct, no hard wrap, bullets/tables ok, end with the Claude-Session URL. Stacking: if your PR depends on an unmerged PR (yours or another fork's), set its base to that PR's HEAD BRANCH (never to main while it carries the parent's commits), say what it stacks on in the body, and give the bottom-up merge order in your final report; independent PRs have base main. The repo deletes head branches on merge, so merging bottom-up retargets children to main automatically. Commit your work in small logical commits as you go and push before you finish; do not leave anything uncommitted.","summary":"Send changeset, commit and stacking rules to callee-shape"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018MwVCrqcmqdQ7eHeJbJpmJ","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"type-losses","message":"House rules for commits, PRs and changesets (from AGENTS.md; apply before you commit and open PRs). Changesets: one short, consumer-facing paragraph per changeset, written for a user reading the release notes: friendly, plain, scannable. Start with the OUTCOME in the user's terms (what they now get or what stopped hurting), then, only when needed, the upgrade action or cost (a flag, a default, a number). No heading and no list marker at the start (Callisto adds the changelog bullet itself; the old '- **Bold:** ...' style is wrong now), no bold lead-in, no internal names (PR numbers, crate internals, 'memo', 'rebuild') unless the user must act on them, no hard wrapping (one line per paragraph), same front matter package list as before. Example: 'Props that come from a wrapped Radix or Base UI primitive now show their real unions, so Storybook renders them as selects. No action needed.' CI/tooling-only changes need no changeset. Commits: imperative subject, at most one or two sentences of why, no list of what changed, no 'This commit...'. PR bodies: succinct, no hard wrap, bullets/tables ok, end with the Claude-Session URL. Stacking: if your PR depends on an unmerged PR (yours or another fork's), set its base to that PR's HEAD BRANCH (never to main while it carries the parent's commits), say what it stacks on in the body, and give the bottom-up merge order in your final report; independent PRs have base main. The repo deletes head branches on merge, so merging bottom-up retargets children to main automatically. Commit your work in small logical commits as you go and push before you finish; do not leave anything uncommitted.","summary":"Send changeset, commit and stacking rules to type-losses"},"calle