{"parentUuid":"9c8e3309-3622-4a9a-b621-c17d049c9507","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgR3d6qAZNPb2zDAKjyBR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I checked the repo's rules and sent them to all six forks. I have nothing of my own to commit: this session's worktree is clean and detached at `origin/main`, and the work in flight lives in the forks, which commit and open their own PRs.\n\n**Changesets (AGENTS.md)**\n- One short, consumer-facing paragraph that starts with the outcome and adds an upgrade action or cost only when needed.\n- No heading and no list marker at the start, because Callisto adds the changelog bullet itself.\n- No bold lead-ins, internal names, or hard wrapping.\n- The `- **Bold:** …` style I wrote for earlier changesets is wrong under this rule. #222 already rewrote the pending ones.\n\nExample the forks got: *\"Props that come from a wrapped Radix or Base UI primitive now show their real unions, so Storybook renders them as selects. No action needed.\"*\n\n**Commits and PRs**\n- Commits: imperative subject, at most one or two sentences of why, no list of what changed.\n- PR bodies: short, no hard wrapping, ending with the session link.\n- Tooling-only and CI-only changes need no changeset.\n\n**Stacking.** A PR that depends on an unmerged PR (its own or another fork's) uses that PR's head branch as its base, and says so in the body. It never uses `main` while carrying a parent's commits, since that is what broke the Equivalence job before. Each fork gives the bottom-up merge order in its final report. The repo deletes branches on merge, so merging bottom-up retargets children automatically.\n\n**Checkpoints.** Each fork commits small logical commits as it goes and pushes before finishing, so nothing is left uncommitted if one is cut off by a limit again.\n\nForks running: `gates`, `scorecard-bisect`, `callee-shape`, `type-losses`, `unmatched-components` and `ts-on-demand`. I'll collect their PRs and give you one combined merge order when they report."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5862,"cache_read_input_tokens":818420,"output_tokens":644,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5862,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":644,"cache_read_input_tokens":818420,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5862,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5862},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"2cf16b06-c0f7-459e-aac0-6d1aed6d301c","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgR3d6S6PWvHSapHArTRW","requestRef":"ca6467cb-ee2c-4799-8caf-673c04ecc062","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"63e6c2b2-9f9a-4bb4-a505-e1fac769d4ea","timestamp":"2026-10-26T14:58:37.540Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"fix/type-losses","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
