{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:09:32.038Z","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a9720545efb857791</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01U6o1inMuycK4VmebpjsACf</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/a9720545efb857791.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Bisect the Scorecard speed regression and fix it\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>I fixed the speed-gate failure in PR #226, base `main`. The cause is #202 (dependency loading on by default), not Codex's resolver work. CI has 15 checks passing and none failing.\n\n**Bisect.** I built eight commits from the merge of #201 to `main` and timed them interleaved, best of 15, in median ms:\n\n| Build | Mantine default | Mantine `--no-load-dependencies` | Chakra default | Chakra `--no-load-dependencies` |\n| --- | --: | --: | --: | --: |\n| #201 | 61.0 | 57.2 | 57.1 | 57.6 |\n| #214 | 61.0 | 58.0 | 57.7 | 58.4 |\n| **#202** | **71.4** | 58.4 | **66.6** | 57.7 |\n| `main` | 72.2 | 58.2 | 63.4 | 58.7 |\n\n- Default mode jumps at #202 alone: +10 ms on Mantine and +9 ms on Chakra.\n- With dependencies off, the resolver and extractor PRs (#204–#220) cost 0–1 ms. They are not the regression.\n- The Scorecard corpora have no `node_modules`. The dependency index only stores answers found inside a package, so each run redoes every failed import's directory walk, about 10 ms.\n\n**The fix** (`scripts/scorecard.py`, `docs/performance.md`; commit `56d3cedb`)\n- The scorecard runs with `--no-load-dependencies` when the build has the flag, so a base build with a different default compares like for like.\n- A new \"With dependencies loading\" column times the default mode, with its own gate at 1.7× the loading-off time. Measured 1.16–1.21× here.\n- The scorecard check against `main` and the #214 build passes every gate (0.91–0.98× of base). The same two builds fail the old gate at 1.17×. I did not run the RDT-ratio gate (`--rdt`), which is unchanged.\n- `just lint doc-check machete typos` exits 0. No Rust changes, so no nextest run and no changeset.\n\n**Not done:** caching failed resolutions for a project with no `node_modules` would remove the 10 ms. It touches the index format and PnP and `paths` resolution, so I left it. Real projects, which have `node_modules`, don't pay it.\n\n**Merge order:** #226 is independent, with base `main`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>848865</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>45</tool_uses><duration_ms>1029777</duration_ms></usage>\n<worktree><worktreePath>/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-a9720545efb857791</worktreePath><worktreeBranch>worktree-agent-a9720545efb857791</worktreeBranch></worktree>\n</task-notification>"}
