{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:13:04.880Z","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a05d452585cdfc10a</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01JTPH8BJf1kRdfiavGHaC2n</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/a05d452585cdfc10a.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Replace callee-name lists with shape detection\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Task: replace the library-name callee lists in the extractor with shape detection. It's done: PR #225, base `main` (independent), with all 16 CI checks passing and none failing.\n\n**The change**\n- **Shape rule.** `try_collect_variant_bag` (renamed from `try_collect_cva_call`, in `crates/core/src/extractor/interface.rs`) takes any object-literal argument, at any position, with a `variants` map of maps whose leaves are styling (strings, templates, arrays, objects or references). That covers `cva`, `tv`, Chakra's recipes and `chakra(element, config)`, Panda's, aliased imports and libraries nobody listed. The per-name config position is gone.\n- **Guards.**\n  - A plain-literal group (`size: \"sm\"`, a list, a number) or a number, boolean or function leaf means no bag and nothing is recorded.\n  - Groups written as references or calls (`size: inputRecipe.variants!.size`) are skipped as before, and the literal groups still count.\n- **The first run caught a real difference.** Three Chakra recipe enums (`inputAddonRecipe`, `numberInputSlotRecipe`, `pinInputSlotRecipe`) changed, because those recipes mix literal and reference groups and my stricter rule rejected the whole bag. After the fix they are identical, and a test covers the case.\n\n**Where callee names still decide behaviour** (documented in `docs/architecture/extractor-ast-visiting.md`)\n- React's own API, matched by identifier rather than by import source: `forwardRef`, `React.forwardRef` and `memo` in `component.rs`, and `createContext` in `wrapper.rs`. An aliased `forwardRef` import isn't recognized.\n- `known.rs` holds the measured `VariantProps` shortcut table (ADR 0014), including the `function_name: \"cva\"` label in its diagnostics. That's a shortcut table, not detection, so I left it.\n\n**Verification**\n- `scripts/equivalence.py` against `origin/main` with an empty allow-list: 20 of 20 combinations identical (five corpora × default, deps, html-full, deps+html-full). Lazy parity on the fixtures passes.\n- `just lint doc-check machete typos` exits 0, and `cargo nextest run --workspace --exclude caliper-docgen-napi --locked` gives 905 passed, 1 skipped.\n- New tests: aliased `cva as c`, aliased `tv as t` (config first), an unknown `makeVariants(\"x\", 1, {…})`, the mixed-group case, and six negative shapes. With the leaf guard switched off, the negative test fails.\n- The existing Chakra recipe test is unchanged. No cache schema change, because `SourceData` is untouched.\n\n**Commits** (branch `fix/variant-bag-by-shape`):\n- `e65bbb17`: the extractor change and tests, in `crates/core/src/extractor/interface.rs`, `crates/core/src/extractor/visit.rs` and `crates/core/src/pipeline/tests.rs`.\n- `fcdb5d68`: the docs note and the changeset, in `docs/architecture/extractor-ast-visiting.md` and `.changeset/variant-bags-by-shape.md`.\n\nNo stacking, so merge it any time; it has no dependency on another open PR.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>850382</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>41</tool_uses><duration_ms>1242664</duration_ms></usage>\n<worktree><worktreePath>/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-a05d452585cdfc10a</worktreePath><worktreeBranch>worktree-agent-a05d452585cdfc10a</worktreeBranch></worktree>\n</task-notification>"}
{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","prNumber":231,"prUrl":"https://github.com/orin-dx/caliper/pull/231","prRepository":"orin-dx/caliper","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:13:23.703Z"}
{"parentUuid":"b0de55ae-660f-4abd-a5f8-ad818e26b310","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgR4j3Hd42KKk6rXo9kq4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Three of the original forks are done. PRs #226 and #230 are open, and the rest-parameter fix has started as its own fork, `fn-params`.\n\n**Where things stand**\n- **#226, speed gate:** `scorecard-bisect` is finished. The regression was #202, not Codex's resolver work.\n- **#230, type losses:** `type-losses` finished and fixed one loss. Member reads on intersections now work, which cut Chakra's `Tokens[\"…\"]` leftovers from 148,646 occurrences (161 distinct) to 20,831 (27 distinct). It checked output equivalence on all five corpora and the oracle's wrong-prop rate stays at 0.00–0.01%. Its CI had only just started when I checked, so I haven't confirmed it's green.\n- **`fn-params`, new:** it keeps rest and optional parameters in function types. A signature like `(...args: any[]) => void` currently prints as `() => void`, which is a wrong call signature for Storybook and for agents. It is 140 hits on antd, 380 on Mantine and 15,182 on Chakra. This changes the output format (a schema version bump under ADR 0017, plus the RDT, TOON and JSON Schema output). So it is its own PR, with a short ADR and a friendly changeset that says readers must update together. It also looks at `readonly` (lost on 540 distinct Chakra types) and `RefObject` shown as `Ref`.\n\n**One caveat on #230:** the oracle gate printed four \"components matched fell\" failures (for example Mantine 89.73 → 89.46). Those compare against a stale baseline and equivalence shows no component added or removed, so I believe they aren't caused by #230. The fork didn't run the oracle on `main` to prove it, so the stale oracle baseline should be refreshed.\n\n**Forks still running:** `gates`, `callee-shape`, `unmatched-components`, `ts-on-demand` and `fn-params`. I'll give you one merge order when the rest report."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5695,"cache_read_input_tokens":833818,"output_tokens":662,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5695,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":662,"cache_read_input_tokens":833818,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5695,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5695},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"36d54937-d0d8-4eaa-86be-ab4f19f656db","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgR4j2mcwWwuZgGoL2wUQ","requestRef":"ac0c4776-b70d-4fd0-93d1-c100290bc45d","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"3150d71f-66e0-4657-8755-b63721a1f0d8","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:13:28.026Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"feat/semantic-on-demand","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
