{"parentUuid":"02d78d97-420d-4cb3-aa7a-142b07950a28","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"c490e18d-933a-4116-8345-7d9a8bc8f0e8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>accbf15a5e0d1dd07</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_012BDgm5xP1AsH8rCs4qXBFS</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/accbf15a5e0d1dd07.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Allow-list guard, PR speed gate, Parity install fix\" is waiting on its own background work</summary>\n<note>This agent stopped with background work of its own still running. It may resume on its own when that work completes or reports, and the same task-id notifies again if it does; the result below may be interim.</note>\n<result>Track AH is done: all three gates are repaired in PR #224 (base `main`, independent), and all 17 CI checks on it pass.\n\n**Item 3, Parity install.** I found the cause, and it is not what #189 assumed.\n- `Dynamic require of \"util\" is not supported` was not Yarn 4.18 on Node 26. On the failing run Node 24 ran Yarn from `.parity/caches/corepack/v1/yarn/4.18.0/yarn.js`.\n- `parity.py` puts `COREPACK_HOME` inside the repo, and the repo's root `package.json` says `\"type\": \"module\"`. Node therefore loaded Yarn's CommonJS bundle as an ES module, where `require` doesn't exist.\n- I reproduced it with a two-line probe: the same file prints `esm` under the repo and `cjs` with a `{\"type\": \"commonjs\"}` manifest beside it.\n- `parity.py setup` now writes that manifest into the corepack home.\n- Verified on a real runner with `gh workflow run parity.yml --ref ci/repair-gates` (run 40344431531). Setup is green and all five corpora install.\n\n**Item 1, allow-list.**\n- `scripts/equivalence-allow.json` is empty again (it had 85 entries).\n- `equivalence.py` now refuses an entry that names no corpus, kind, or component/prop/diagnostic, such as `antd/* prop-added *`. Four new tests in `test_equivalence.py`; the 9 Python tests pass.\n- `--require-empty-allow` exits 1 on any entry. The new `Allow-list empty` workflow runs it on pushes to `main`, and the weekly Parity workflow runs it first. I checked the exit codes: 0 on an empty list, 1 with an entry. Pull requests can still carry entries.\n- Open PRs that relied on the old entries will now show real differences in the Equivalence job. The PR body says so.\n\n**Item 2, speed gate on PRs.**\n- `scorecard.yml` now runs on pull requests touching resolver, extractor, types, pipeline or dependency_types, plus the scorecard files.\n- It compares against the PR's own base (`github.base_ref` through an env var, not interpolated into the shell) on Mantine and Chakra only, via a new `scorecard.py --corpus` flag.\n- It is `continue-on-error` with the result in the job summary. `docs/performance.md` documents promotion to blocking after ten consecutive green runs on `main`-targeting PRs.\n- The workflow itself has only run through the 17 passing checks on #224; its first real exercise will be a resolver PR. I did not bisect the current regression (the other fork owns that).\n\n**Commits** on `ci/repair-gates`: `1d67ce6c` (Parity install), `e937b2d0` (allow-list), `2e5ad9fc` (scorecard gate), `eaa16081` (docs: `docs/parity.md`, `docs/performance.md`). Lint exits 0. No changeset, since it is CI and tooling only.\n\n**What the fixed install revealed.** The Parity run now measures all five corpora, and its two later gates fail. They fail on the stored 0.4.0 baseline, not on anything in this PR:\n- **Measure and gate.** Real or stale-baseline accuracy drops:\n  - Chakra with dependencies: \"utility type left as written\" grew from 1 to 1,127 props, and \"unreduced &amp; string\" from 0 to 40.\n  - Spectrum: props reported fell 99.69% to 98.75%, same text 67.43% to 63.04%, components matched 77.20% to 76.19%.\n  - Mantine: \"unbound type parameter\" 6 to 31.\n  - Smaller growths on shadcn and antd.\n- **Compare prop types with TypeScript's checker.** Components matched fell on fixtures (82.5% to 77.5%), Mantine, antd, and most on Spectrum (41.13% to 37.51%).\n- The Chakra jump is the most likely real regression. Some of the rest is probably the baseline being stale, since it predates #202 and #203–#222. Someone needs to triage the failures and then refresh `scripts/parity-baseline.json` and `scripts/oracle-baseline.json`.\n\n**Merge order:** #224 is independent, so it can go in at any point.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>864179</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>60</tool_uses><duration_ms>1608300</duration_ms></usage>\n<worktree><worktreePath>/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-accbf15a5e0d1dd07</worktreePath><worktreeBranch>worktree-agent-accbf15a5e0d1dd07</worktreeBranch></worktree>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"477a56da-0a4a-4ddf-9cf9-ecde9f38a053","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:19:10.356Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"task-notification","producer":"session-task","runId":"0mvpdl7h7-e4a8697b"},"promptSource":"system","turnOrigin":"task_notification","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":196,"turnIndex":299},"queueSkipAttachments":true,"sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"feat/semantic-on-demand","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
