{"parentUuid":"c61be461-1799-4c80-91ff-af627c4753d8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgR5CRhkwzp9GzKtbTY2o","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"PR #224 is open with all 17 checks passing, and all three gates are repaired. The fixed Parity install also showed that accuracy has slipped in places, and I'm starting a triage fork for that now.\n\n**What `gates` fixed** (CI and tooling only, so no changeset)\n- **Parity install, real cause found.** It wasn't Yarn on Node 26. `parity.py` puts `COREPACK_HOME` inside the repo, whose root `package.json` says `\"type\": \"module\"`, so Node loaded Yarn's CommonJS bundle as an ES module. `setup` now writes a CommonJS manifest into the corepack home. The fork reproduced it with a two-line probe and verified it on a real runner (run 40344431531): all five corpora install.\n- **Allow-list.** It's empty again. `equivalence.py` now rejects entries that name no corpus, kind, or component, such as `antd/* prop-added *`, and a new `Allow-list empty` workflow fails pushes to `main` if the list isn't empty. PRs can still carry entries. Open PRs that relied on the old entries will now show real differences in Equivalence, and the PR body says so.\n- **Speed gate on PRs.** `scorecard.yml` now runs on resolver, extractor, types, pipeline and dependency PRs, comparing Mantine and Chakra against the PR's own base. It's non-blocking at first, with a documented path to blocking after 10 consecutive green runs on `main`-targeting PRs. Its first real test will be a resolver PR.\n\n**What the repaired Parity run revealed.** Two later gates fail, against the stored 0.4.0 baseline:\n- **Chakra with dependencies:** \"utility type left as written\" grew from 1 to 1,127 props, and \"unreduced `& string`\" from 0 to 40. This is the likeliest real regression.\n- **Spectrum:** props reported fell from 99.69% to 98.75%, same text from 67.43% to 63.04%, and components matched from 77.20% to 76.19%.\n- **Mantine:** \"unbound type parameter\" went from 6 to 31, with smaller growth on shadcn and antd.\n- **Oracle gate:** components matched fell on the fixtures (82.5% to 77.5%), Mantine, antd, and most on Spectrum (41.13% to 37.51%).\n- Some of this is a stale baseline (it predates #202 and #203–#222), but the Chakra jump looks real.\n\nI'm starting a triage fork stacked on #224's branch. It will:\n- Bisect each growth to a PR.\n- Fix the real regressions with tests.\n- Refresh `scripts/parity-baseline.json` and `scripts/oracle-baseline.json` only for the stale parts, with reasoning in the PR."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3044,"cache_read_input_tokens":841898,"output_tokens":3018,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":340},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3044,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":3018,"cache_read_input_tokens":841898,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3044,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3044},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"c3978940-b4c2-4e3e-b800-26e7d46eafe0","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgR5CR8Ha8xZCMAM9672r","requestRef":"2db4c30d-f6d4-4802-a731-76ce9b15e067","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"ae996f56-b25f-4bd6-90d6-e6130f182023","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:19:23.632Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"feat/semantic-on-demand","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"ae996f56-b25f-4bd6-90d6-e6130f182023","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgR5CRhkwzp9GzKtbTY2o","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011H4Y5Cntqhmpvu76iDjp5Z","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Triage the Parity and oracle regressions on main","subagent_type":"fork","isolation":"worktree","name":"parity-triage","prompt":"Track AO: triage the Parity and oracle failures that PR #224 (branch ci/repair-gates, open, unmerged: fixes the Parity install so all five corpora install, empties the allow-list) exposed on current main. Do NOT remove worktrees (others, including Codex, use the repo). Branch off origin/ci/repair-gates; open your PR(s) with base = ci/repair-gates (never main while carrying that parent's commits; the repo deletes head branches on merge so merging bottom-up retargets to main) and say so in the body. If #224 has merged by the time you start (`gh pr view 224 --json state`), branch off origin/main and use base main. Facts from the repaired run (scripts/parity.py run vs the stored 0.4.0 scripts/parity-baseline.json and scripts/oracle-baseline.json): Chakra with dependencies: 'utility type left as written' 1 -> 1,127 props and 'unreduced & string' 0 -> 40; Spectrum: props reported 99.69% -> 98.75%, same text 67.43% -> 63.04%, components matched 77.20% -> 76.19%; Mantine 'unbound type parameter' 6 -> 31; smaller growths on shadcn and antd; oracle gate 'components matched' fell: fixtures 82.5 -> 77.5, Mantine 89.73 -> 89.46, antd 59.68 -> 59.35, Spectrum 41.13 -> 37.51. The baselines predate PRs #202 (dependency loading by default) and #203-#230 (Codex's structural batch and ours). Do: (1) reproduce on current main (build release; `python3 scripts/parity.py setup && python3 scripts/parity.py run` and `python3 scripts/equivalence.py --oracle` or parity.py oracle; needs `pnpm install --no-frozen-lockfile` in your worktree for apps/validate and `git checkout pnpm-lock.yaml` afterwards; do not commit lockfile changes); (2) for EACH regressed metric find the introducing change: bisect over the merge commits from #201 (5519cddb) to main, e.g. build a handful and re-run just the affected corpus (Chakra for the utility-type growth, Spectrum for props reported/same text/components matched, Mantine for unbound type parameter), and list the specific props/components that changed (before/after type text) with 5 examples each; (3) classify each: REAL REGRESSION (we now say something worse or lose a prop/component), IMPROVEMENT scored as loss by a stale/naive pattern (e.g. a unioned alias printed differently, 'unbound type parameter' regex matching Spectrum's breakpoint keys S/M/L as noted before, RDT printing an alias name), or ACCEPTABLE DIFFERENCE; (4) fix the real regressions in crates/core (exact-value tests, `just equivalence` for intended differences with NARROW allow-list entries only in your PR since main's list must stay empty and bare `*` entries are rejected, lazy parity, oracle no regression) and tighten naive parity.py patterns when they misclassify (with a test); (5) then refresh scripts/parity-baseline.json and scripts/oracle-baseline.json from a clean run of the repaired gates on the final code, in its own commit with the numbers and reasoning in the PR body, ONLY for metrics you classified as improvement/acceptable. Gates: `python3 scripts/test_equivalence.py` and parity python tests, `just lint doc-check machete typos` and `cargo nextest run --workspace --exclude caliper-docgen-napi --locked` exit codes read directly (never pipe through tail), CI green incl. the Parity workflow dispatched on your branch (`gh workflow run parity.yml --ref <branch>`; watch it). HOUSE RULES: changeset (only when shipped behavior changes) = one short, consumer-facing paragraph, friendly and scannable, starting with the OUTCOME in the user's terms then any action/cost, no heading, no list marker, no bold lead-in, no internal names, one line per paragraph; commits: imperative subject, at most 1-2 sentences of why, no list of what changed; PR body succinct, no hard wrap, ending with https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED; commits end with Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED; commit small logical commits as you go and push before finishing; never push main/force-push/merge; /usr/bin/git with sandbox off, one plain git command per call. Time-box ~100 tool calls. Report a table: metric, before, now, introducing PR, class, action."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3044,"cache_read_input_tokens":841898,"output_tokens":3018,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":340},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3044,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":3018,"cache_read_input_tokens":841898,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3044,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3044},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_011H4Y5Cntqhmpvu76iDjp5Z":{"description":"Triage the Parity and oracle regressions on main","subagent_type":"fork","isolation":"worktree","name":"parity-triage","prompt":"Track AO: triage the Parity and oracle failures that PR #224 (branch ci/repair-gates, open, unmerged: fixes the Parity install so all five corpora install, empties the allow-list) exposed on current main. Do NOT remove worktrees (others, including Codex, use the repo). Branch off origin/ci/repair-gates; open your PR(s) with base = ci/repair-gates (never main while carrying that parent's commits