as name), or ACCEPTABLE DIFFERENCE; (4) fix the real regressions in crates/core (exact-value tests, `just equivalence` for intended differences with NARROW allow-list entries only in your PR since main's list must stay empty and bare `*` entries are rejected, lazy parity, oracle no regression) and tighten naive parity.py patterns when they misclassify (with a test); (5) then refresh scripts/parity-baseline.json and scripts/oracle-baseline.json from a clean run of the repaired gates on the final code, in its own commit with the numbers and reasoning in the PR body, ONLY for metrics you classified as improvement/acceptable. Gates: `python3 scripts/test_equivalence.py` and parity python tests, `just lint doc-check machete typos` and `cargo nextest run --workspace --exclude caliper-docgen-napi --locked` exit codes read directly (never pipe through tail), CI green incl. the Parity workflow dispatched on your branch (`gh workflow run parity.yml --ref <branch>`; watch it). HOUSE RULES: changeset (only when shipped behavior changes) = one short, consumer-facing paragraph, friendly and scannable, starting with the OUTCOME in the user's terms then any action/cost, no heading, no list marker, no bold lead-in, no internal names, one line per paragraph; commits: imperative subject, at most 1-2 sentences of why, no list of what changed; PR body succinct, no hard wrap, ending with https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED; commits end with Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED; commit small logical commits as you go and push before finishing; never push main/force-push/merge; /usr/bin/git with sandbox off, one plain git command per call. Time-box ~100 tool calls. Report a table: metric, before, now, introducing PR, class, action.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/a77265bdad974924a.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request"