{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","bridgeSessionId":"cse_01D7CJmXuD2ASqfBYm7Lk4WZ","lastSequenceNum":21749,"ownerAccountUuid":"138d593e-e185-4f72-89f2-82e1a501f134","ownerOrganizationUuid":"602db9b4-428d-49e6-a99c-64152cc62a79"}
{"parentUuid":"ffbfe53a-36c8-4468-ad9e-1a46b735a40f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgR5ETt2qFL7Se8EQTjgC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The `parity-triage` fork is running with a cap of about 100 tool calls. It is stacked on #224's branch.\n\nWhat it does:\n1. **Reproduces** the failures on current `main` with the repaired gates, and **bisects** each regressed metric to the PR that introduced it: Chakra's utility types (1 → 1,127) and `& string` (0 → 40), Spectrum's props reported, same text and components matched, and Mantine's unbound type parameter.\n2. **Classifies** each metric as a real regression, an improvement scored as a loss by a naive pattern (the single-capital-letter regex that catches Spectrum's `S`/`M`/`L` breakpoints is already a known example), or an acceptable difference.\n3. **Fixes** the real regressions with exact-value tests, and tightens naive patterns in `parity.py` with a test.\n4. **Refreshes** the stale `parity-baseline.json` and `oracle-baseline.json` in a separate commit, only for metrics it classified as improvement or acceptable, with the reasoning in the PR body.\n\nIt will dispatch the Parity workflow on its branch to confirm the gates pass, and report a table of metric, before, now, introducing PR, class and action.\n\nOpen PRs for you to merge, as they report:\n\n| PR | What | Base |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| #224 | Allow-list guard, PR speed gate, Parity install fix | `main` |\n| #225 | Variant bags by shape | `main` |\n| #226 | Scorecard pinned to loading-off, with its own loading gate | `main` |\n| #230 | Member reads on intersections | `main` |\n\nAll four are independent. #224 first is worth it, because it empties the allow-list and makes Parity install, which the triage fork stacks on.\n\nRunning: `unmatched-components`, `ts-on-demand`, `fn-params` and `parity-triage`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6565,"cache_read_input_tokens":844942,"output_tokens":624,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6565,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":624,"cache_read_input_tokens":844942,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6565,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6565},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"8a8a2ddc-8bc8-49c6-99f1-e2b099cff4ba","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgR5ETWD1xStmphxeeuiA","requestRef":"cf55fcea-0b39-4db3-9520-1d8d1f196a3d","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"67d883a6-a37f-4912-b7e9-126b3439856d","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:19:45.081Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"feat/semantic-on-demand","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
