{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:22:59.264Z","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a67a67ece3aaa85b9</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_014vuEnRMC9fwSrEJmKBYt3d</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/a67a67ece3aaa85b9.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Why RDT components are not matched\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Track AL: re-measure plausible-component recall against RDT on current main, fix the top real misses, and fix the Storybook matching gap. I opened four PRs. #227 and #228 are fully green, #231 has one check pending, and #229 has Test / Rust, Coverage and the Equivalence re-run pending after the allow-list commit.\n\n**Recall (plausible components, versus RDT)**\n\n| Corpus | Before | After | New components |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| mantine | 89% | 90% | +3 |\n| chakra | 79% | 80% | +11 |\n| shadcn | 98% | 98% | 0 |\n| antd | 85% | 85% | +3 |\n| spectrum | 98% | 98% | 0 |\n\nNo component was removed or changed on any corpus. Most remaining \"misses\" are naming artifacts (displayName assignments, namespace-member assignments, re-export sites) or RDT noise (hooks, contexts, helpers). The real misses are the shapes listed below.\n\n**PRs**\n\nAll four are independent with base `main`, so any merge order works.\n\n| PR | Branch | Shape fixed | Commits |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| #227 | `fix/parenthesized-factory-argument` | Factory render function wrapped in parentheses or `as` (Mantine `RadioGroup`, `CheckboxGroup`, `SwitchGroup`) | 73f6c148, 1cf85138 |\n| #228 | `fix/fc-annotation-intersection` | `FC&lt;P&gt; &amp; {…}` annotation (antd `Drawer`, `ConfigProvider`, `Tour`) | 6e93aaa0 (fix; I did not re-check the hash on the PR branch), f76e1ec8 |\n| #229 | `feat/tagged-factory-components` | New `taggedFactory` rule: `chakra(\"div\", {…})` with a `{Name}Props` type beside it (11 Chakra components). Cache schema 24→25, golden snapshot updated, minor changeset, 22 narrow allow-list entries in `scripts/equivalence-allow.json` | 5075bacb, ae2504b1, 576f49f2 |\n| #231 | `fix/story-export-of-renamed-component` | Addon `resolveExport` returns the file's only component when the source declares the export but its displayName differs (Mantine `Thumb`) | one `fix:` commit |\n\nEach Rust fix has exact-value tests and negative guards. #231 has two unit tests (61 addon tests pass; oxlint, oxfmt and tsc clean). Changesets are included. `packages/napi/index.js` was modified by the napi build and was not committed.\n\n**CI**\n- #227 and #228: all checks pass (16 each).\n- #231: 15 pass, with no failures and one pending.\n- #229: the Equivalence failure is the expected one for new components. The allow-list commit addresses it, and the re-run is pending.\n\n**Storybook side**\n- The harness found no unmatched stories on the default addon variant.\n- The only real story sets are Chakra (1) and Spectrum (100), and all were answered. The generated stories for mantine, shadcn and antd also matched.\n- The displayName≠export case is fixed (#231) but is not exercised by the harness, so it is covered by unit tests only.\n- Not fixed: `component: Ns.Member` where `Ns.Member = Local` is assigned (Mantine `Combobox.Target`). It needs `keyOfMember` to read the namespace module's source.\n\n**Real shapes not fixed**\n- Non-generic project functions returning components (`createEdgeComponent` ×4 Mantine, `createIconLoader` ×5 shadcn, `createImageGroup`, `createIcon`). They need cross-file resolution of the callee's result.\n- Project-alias annotations (`Bars: MantineLoaderComponent`, ×3 Mantine).\n- Class aliases from a dependency (shadcn `const ChartLegend = RechartsPrimitive.Legend`).\n- `React.lazy(() =&gt; import(...))` (Spectrum docs).\n- Six Chakra `chakra(...)` components whose props type is not a same-file `{Name}Props` (`CheckboxGroup`, `FocusTrap`, `Presence`, `Span`, `Toaster`, `VisuallyHidden`).\n\n**Gates not run locally (budget)**\n- Not run: the precision sampling script, a separate lazy parity run, `just equivalence --oracle`, and the full `just lint doc-check machete typos` and `cargo nextest run --workspace` on each branch.\n- What I have instead is CI results, the before/after output diff (additions of real components only), fmt, and the targeted tests.\n- Running `clippy --all-targets` ad hoc showed `unwrap` errors in `crates/core/tests/no_cache.rs`. I did not check whether `main` has them too.\n\nresult: Four independent PRs (#227, #228, #229, #231) add 17 real components (Mantine +3, Chakra +11, antd +3) with none removed or changed, and fix Storybook export matching for renamed components. #227 and #228 are green, and #231 and #229 have CI still pending.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>88705</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>127</tool_uses><duration_ms>1794679</duration_ms></usage>\n<worktree><worktreePath>/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-a67a67ece3aaa85b9</worktreePath><worktreeBranch>worktree-agent-a67a67ece3aaa85b9</worktreeBranch></worktree>\n</task-notification>"}
