{"parentUuid":"c38d780f-5c00-4db3-859e-7e3ce7f3fb94","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgR5VHDkJy9Zc8759ZBzk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Four independent PRs are open that add 17 real components, with none removed or changed. #227 and #228 are green, #231 has one check pending, and #229's re-run is still pending.\n\n**Recall against RDT** (plausible components, hooks and helpers excluded)\n\n| Corpus | Before | After | New components |\n| --- | --: | --: | --: |\n| Mantine | 89% | 90% | +3 |\n| Chakra | 79% | 80% | +11 |\n| shadcn | 98% | 98% | 0 |\n| antd | 85% | 85% | +3 |\n| Spectrum | 98% | 98% | 0 |\n\nMost of the remaining \"misses\" are naming artifacts (displayName assignments, namespace-member assignments, re-export sites) or RDT noise, so recall is close to its ceiling for these shapes.\n\n**The PRs** (all base `main`, any order)\n\n| PR | Fixes | CI |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| #227 | Factory render function wrapped in parentheses or `as` (Mantine `RadioGroup`, `CheckboxGroup`, `SwitchGroup`) | green |\n| #228 | `FC<P> & {…}` annotations (antd `Drawer`, `ConfigProvider`, `Tour`) | green |\n| #229 | New `taggedFactory` rule for `chakra(\"div\", {…})` with a `{Name}Props` type beside it (11 Chakra components); cache schema 24 → 25, minor changeset | Equivalence re-run pending |\n| #231 | Storybook addon finds the file's only component when the export name differs from the displayName (Mantine `Thumb`) | one check pending |\n\nEach Rust fix has exact-value tests and negative guards, plus a changeset.\n\n**Storybook side.** The harness found no unmatched stories on the default addon variant. The real story sets are Chakra (1) and Spectrum (100), and all were answered. What's not fixed: `component: Ns.Member` where `Ns.Member = Local` is assigned (Mantine's `Combobox.Target`), which needs the namespace module's source read.\n\n**Real shapes still missed**\n- Non-generic project functions returning components (`createEdgeComponent` ×4 Mantine, `createIconLoader` ×5 shadcn, `createImageGroup`, `createIcon`). These need cross-file resolution of the callee's result.\n- Project-alias annotations (`Bars: MantineLoaderComponent`, ×3 Mantine).\n- Class aliases from a dependency (shadcn `const ChartLegend = RechartsPrimitive.Legend`).\n- `React.lazy(() => import(...))` (Spectrum docs).\n- Six Chakra `chakra(...)` components whose props type isn't a same-file `{Name}Props`.\n\n**Two things to know before merging**\n1. **Verification was thinner than I asked for.** The fork skipped the precision sampling, a separate lazy parity run, the oracle, and the full lint and workspace test run on each branch, because of budget. CI is the gate. Its fmt checks and before/after diffs show only real components added. It also saw `unwrap` errors from `clippy --all-targets` in `crates/core/tests/no_cache.rs` and didn't check whether `main` has them too.\n2. **Allow-list collision.** #229 carries 22 narrow allow-list entries, and #230 carries entries for 241 props. #224 adds a check that fails a push to `main` when the list isn't empty. So once #224 merges, merging #229 or #230 will turn that check red on `main` until a follow-up empties the list. Options: merge them before #224, or have each PR drop its entries in a final commit once its Equivalence run is green. I'd do the second, and I can send that instruction to the forks and clean up the two PRs.\n\nRunning: `ts-on-demand`, `fn-params` and `parity-triage`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2506,"cache_read_input_tokens":852848,"output_tokens":1894,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":600},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2506,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1894,"cache_read_input_tokens":852848,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2506,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2506},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"fc81a403-f024-423d-bb69-78691651d47f","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgR5VGkDzuNd3SC5CUcwF","requestRef":"cfe88ad2-084d-4261-9945-9c1d92038def","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"3270e6ee-4764-4886-ab87-bf57890049cf","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:23:15.674Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"feat/function-param-flags","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
