{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:31:18.756Z","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>ab8a57f3074b60627</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01DWRiykF7L3JHH36CxB6h3u</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/ab8a57f3074b60627.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"On-demand TS 7.1 resolution per requested component\" is waiting on its own background work</summary>\n<note>This agent stopped with background work of its own still running. It may resume on its own when that work completes or reports, and the same task-id notifies again if it does; the result below may be interim.</note>\n<result>PR #232 is open and CI is running; I'm waiting on it before the final report.\n\nDone so far:\n- **End-to-end harness:** on shadcn and antd, on-demand adds props. antd's missing props drop from 37 to 5, shadcn goes from 0 to 3, and median story time rises from about 2–10 ms to about 30–65 ms.\n- **Mode off:** `scripts/equivalence.py` is identical on all five corpora, and lazy parity on the fixtures is ok.\n- **Fix found by the harness:** the checker omitted `children`, `aria-*` and DOM handlers, so a story lost them. They now stay structural, in the on-demand hook only (the whole-project merge is unchanged).\n- **Real-tsc test:** passes when `CALIPER_TEST_TSC` names the beta binary.\n- **Lint:** `just lint doc-check machete typos` exits 0.\n- **Workspace nextest:** the earlier run passed all 908 tests, before the inherited-props change, this commit's last edits and the real-tsc test. It has not been rerun since. The tests for the changed pieces (core `semantic_hook`, `semantic` lib, semantic `on_demand`) pass.\n\nRemaining: the CI result, then the final report with merge order (this PR is independent, base `main`).</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>133282