{"parentUuid":"748a742b-0f01-46d2-8666-edaab64b7c12","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgR687tCSFfDj6JZUe1g9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The `ts-on-demand` fork has a PR open (#232) and is waiting on CI. This is an interim result, and the final report with its measurements and the ADR will follow.\n\n**What the end-to-end harness shows** (on-demand mode against structural, through the addon)\n- **antd:** props Storybook lists that we lack fall from 37 to 5.\n- **shadcn:** 3 props added where there were none.\n- **Cost:** the median story goes from about 2–10 ms to about 30–65 ms. That's inside the 5–20 ms budget I set for later stories only on the low end, so it's the price of the accuracy and the reason the mode stays opt-in.\n- **Bug the harness found:** the checker omitted `children`, `aria-*` and DOM handlers, so a story lost them. Those now stay structural, but only in the on-demand hook, leaving the whole-project merge unchanged.\n\n**Safety**\n- **Mode off is unchanged:** `scripts/equivalence.py` is identical on all five corpora, and lazy parity on the fixtures passes.\n- **Real `tsc`:** the integration test passes when `CALIPER_TEST_TSC` points at the beta binary.\n- **Lint exits 0.**\n- **Gap:** the full workspace test run (908 tests) last passed before the inherited-props change and the final edits. It has not been rerun since. The tests for the changed pieces pass (core `semantic_hook`, the `semantic` library, `on_demand`), but I'd want the full run green in CI before merging.\n\n**Also open for you:** #224, #225, #226 and #230 (independent), #227, #228, #229 and #231 (independent), and #232 (independent, base `main`).\n\nThe allow-list collision I raised stands: #229 and #230 carry allow-list entries, and #224's new check fails a push to `main` while the list is non-empty. I'll hold off on asking the forks to drop their entries until you say how you want to order the merges.\n\nStill running: `ts-on-demand` (CI wait), `fn-params` and `parity-triage`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2949,"cache_read_input_tokens":855354,"output_tokens":870,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":190},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2949,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":870,"cache_read_input_tokens":855354,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2949,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2949},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"d489149b-dfb3-4377-bde6-0cca9cd3fe39","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgR6877pdCoYnesPxRtwf","requestRef":"3ed39fe8-3635-4cc7-882a-799f37bcfd2f","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"87b6c173-8138-46f7-b5f4-bea29a797833","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:31:34.201Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"feat/function-param-flags","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
