{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:38:26.190Z","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>ab8a57f3074b60627</task-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/ab8a57f3074b60627.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"On-demand TS 7.1 resolution per requested component\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Track AM: on-demand TS 7.1 resolution for the component a Storybook story asks for. PR #232 is open (base `main`) and all CI checks pass, including Equivalence, SemVer, Test/Rust, Lint and Coverage.\n\nresult: Track AM shipped as PR #232 (https://github.com/orin-dx/caliper/pull/232), an opt-in `semanticTypes: 'on-demand'` mode for Storybook. CI is green. In the harness the checker cuts antd's missing props from 37 to 5, but median story time rises from about 2–10 ms to about 30–65 ms.\n\n**Go/no-go: go as opt-in.** The first answer takes 82–137 ms on Mantine, shadcn, antd and Spectrum, and 703 ms on Chakra. That fits the ~150 ms first-story budget except on Chakra. Later uncached stories cost 21–41 ms each (Chakra 534 ms), above the 5–20 ms budget.\n\n**Design (ADR 0022).**\n- **Request flow:** the structural answer comes first, then a bounded wait of `semanticWaitMs` (default 150). A late answer is cached for the next request.\n- **Failure handling:** a missing `tsc`, a crash or a timeout falls back to the structural answer with one warning per session.\n- **Process limits:** the checker process is replaced after 64 programs and after a crash; three crashes keep it down for the session.\n- **Not built yet:** prefetch, the on-disk cache, a semver range and `--version` check in place of the exact pin to `7.1.0-beta`, and an RSS-based memory cap.\n\n**Harness results** (shadcn 95 and antd 83 stories, two runs each, shared machine, so noisy):\n\n| Corpus | Variant | First story | Median story | Props Storybook lists that we lack |\n| --- | --- | --: | --: | --: |\n| shadcn | structural | 75–144 ms | 2–10 ms | 0 |\n| shadcn | on-demand | 101–335 ms | 29–66 ms | 3 |\n| antd | structural | 59–102 ms | 2–4 ms | 37 |\n| antd | on-demand | 96–147 ms | 39–53 ms | 5 |\n\nPeak RSS was about the same (shadcn 314–328 MiB, antd 222–230 MiB). That figure leaves out the `tsc` process, which peaked at 157–612 MiB when asked for one component at a time; antd is the high end.\n\nOn Mantine, Chakra and Spectrum the checker finds the same props as the structural pass, so the mode only adds a process there.\n\n**Fix made along the way:** the checker leaves out props that `@types/react` declares (`children`, `aria-*`, DOM handlers), so the first run lost 6 props on shadcn. The on-demand hook now keeps inherited structural props. The 3 shadcn and 5 antd props still missing are `children`/`ref`-style props with no `parent` that the checker omits; I left that rule alone.\n\n**Gates:**\n- **Equivalence:** with the mode off it is identical on all five corpora (run against the bench corpora, lazy parity on fixtures only).\n- **Lint:** `just lint doc-check machete typos` exits 0.\n- **Tests:** workspace nextest passed 908 earlier, before the last commits, and I did not rerun it; CI's Test/Rust run covers the final code.\n- **Real-tsc test:** it passes when `CALIPER_TEST_TSC` names a `typescript@beta` binary, and otherwise skips. CI skips it because the variable is unset.\n- **Addon tests:** 60 pass.\n- **Changeset:** minor, covering core, semantic, napi and the Storybook addon.\n\n**Commits** on `feat/semantic-on-demand` (all pushed):\n- `7964d581` core hook and tests\n- `0c7f9afb` warm tsc worker and bench example\n- `1a5d4093` binding option\n- `4939013d` addon options\n- `c6adbac9` semantic on-demand tests\n- `1a08aed8` docs, ADR and changeset\n- `36b0ffb5` format\n- Two later commits: the inherited-props fix, the real-tsc test and the ADR table\n\nI didn't capture their hashes.\n\n**Merge order:** PR #232 is independent, so it can merge on its own.\n\n**Caveats:** the harness numbers are noisy because other forks share the machine, and I did not re-measure antd's checker memory with the 64-program recycle.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>150399</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>144</tool_uses><duration_ms>2473960</duration_ms></usage>\n<worktree><worktreePath>/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-ab8a57f3074b60627</worktreePath><worktreeBranch>worktree-agent-ab8a57f3074b60627</worktreeBranch></worktree>\n</task-notification>"}
