ies cost 21–41 ms each (Chakra 534 ms), above the 5–20 ms budget.\n\n**Design (ADR 0022).**\n- **Request flow:** the structural answer comes first, then a bounded wait of `semanticWaitMs` (default 150). A late answer is cached for the next request.\n- **Failure handling:** a missing `tsc`, a crash or a timeout falls back to the structural answer with one warning per session.\n- **Process limits:** the checker process is replaced after 64 programs and after a crash; three crashes keep it down for the session.\n- **Not built yet:** prefetch, the on-disk cache, a semver range and `--version` check in place of the exact pin to `7.1.0-beta`, and an RSS-based memory cap.\n\n**Harness results** (shadcn 95 and antd 83 stories, two runs each, shared machine, so noisy):\n\n| Corpus | Variant | First story | Median story | Props Storybook lists that we lack |\n| --- | --- | --: | --: | --: |\n| shadcn | structural | 75–144 ms | 2–10 ms | 0 |\n| shadcn | on-demand | 101–335 ms | 29–66 ms | 3 |\n| antd | structural | 59–102 ms | 2–4 ms | 37 |\n| antd | on-demand | 96–147 ms | 39–53 ms | 5 |\n\nPeak RSS was about the same (shadcn 314–328 MiB, antd 222–230 MiB). That figure leaves out the `tsc` process, which peaked at 157–612 MiB when asked for one component at a time; antd is the high end.\n\nOn Mantine, Chakra and Spectrum the checker finds the same props as the structural pass, so the mode only adds a process there.\n\n**Fix made along the way:** the checker leaves out props that `@types/react` declares (`children`, `aria-*`, DOM handlers), so the first run lost 6 props on shadcn. The on-demand hook now keeps inherited structural props. The 3 shadcn and 5 antd props still missing are `children`/`ref`-style props with no `parent` that the checker omits; I left that rule alone.\n\n**Gates:**\n- **Equivalence:** with the mode off it is identical on all five corpora (run against the bench corpora, lazy parity on fixtures only).\n- **Lint:** `just lint doc-check machete typos` exits 0.\n- **Tests:** workspace nextest passed 908 earlier, before the last commits, and I did not rerun it; CI's Test/Rust run covers the final code.\n- **Real-tsc test:** it passes when `CALIPER_TEST_TSC` names a `typescript@beta` binary, and otherwise skips. CI skips it because the variable is unset.\n- **Addon tests:** 60 pass.\n- **Changeset:** minor, covering core, semantic, napi and the Storybook addon.\n\n**Commits** on `feat/semantic-on-demand` (all pushed):\n- `7964d581` core hook and tests\n- `0c7f9afb` warm tsc worker and bench example\n- `1a5d4093` binding option\n- `4939013d` addon options\n- `c6adbac9` semantic on-demand tests\n- `1a08aed8` docs, ADR and changeset\n- `36b0ffb5` format\n- Two later commits: the inherited-props fix, the real-tsc test and the ADR table\n\nI didn't capture their hashes.\n\n**Merge order:** PR #232 is independent, so it can merge on its own.\n\n**Caveats:** the harness numbers are noisy because other forks share the machine, and I did not re-measure antd's checker memory with the 64-program recycle.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>150399</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>144</tool_uses><duration_ms>2473960</duration_ms></usage>\n<worktree><worktreePath>/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-ab8a57f3074b60627</worktreePath><worktreeBranch>worktree-agent-ab8a57f3074b60627</worktreeBranch></worktree>\n</task-notification>\n</system-reminder>"}]}}
{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","id":"f7992e32-c58d-42b8-b7e7-34ddb1e4250a","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:38:26.283Z","version":"2.1.308","querySource":"repl_main_thread:outputStyle:Concise","shapeHash":"695ec5a8802936862d1cd8c71e730e293e4e9e400bcbffb95f0146470866b732","params":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"65967831-b298-46b2-a811-fe7cc43d8190","keep":1027,"tail":["ef13ba9b53e55fe123d286115a8a3d14fad1a427cdc95985db7cf66ebca72087","2f401832392edeb22812974cb2a9ad5a5cfe79163a99a690242328f708aff89e"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",1028,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"0bb70610668301cf4a2e9ec6749caf98aed305a4e35889dc456928f76eb81cf8"}
{"parentUuid":"b376af95-e3b6-42be-8f42-793398acd877","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgR6fcFP4yPYeQE8M8zdd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2222,"cache_read_input_tokens":859874,"output_tokens":1612,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":363},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2222,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1612,"cache_read_input_tokens":859874,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2222,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2222},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":3148,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"702ea681-5e74-4e4f-8a39-26c56bffc665","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgR6fbs4fiV5jc94vjYAo","requestRef":"f7992e32-c58d-42b8-b7e7-34ddb1e4250a","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"2d60283d-72ac-4515-bef8-3a9dcde5c6df","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:38:31.594Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"feat/function-param-flags","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"2d60283d-72ac-4515-bef8-3a9dcde5c6df","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgR6fcFP4yPYeQE8M8zdd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"PR #232 is open and all its CI checks pass. It adds an opt-in `semanticTypes: 'on-demand'` mode for the Storybook addon. It works and the accuracy gain is real, but it helps only two of the five corpora and costs time and memory per story.\n\n**What it does (ADR 0022)**\n- The structural answer comes first, then the addon waits up to `semanticWaitMs` (default 150 ms) for a warm `tsc` to answer. A late answer is cached for the next request.\n- A missing `tsc`, a crash or a timeout falls back to the structural answer with one warning per session. The checker process is replaced after 64 programs and after a crash, and three crashes keep it down for the session.\n\n**Measured** (shadcn 95 and antd 83 stories, two runs each, on a shared machine so noisy)\n\n| Corpus | Variant | First story | Median story | Props Storybook lists that we lack |\n| --- | --- | --: | --: | --: |\n| shadcn | structural | 75–144 ms | 2–10 ms | 0 |\n| shadcn | on-demand | 101–335 ms | 29–66 ms | 3 |\n| antd | structural | 59–102 ms | 2–4 ms | 37 |\n| antd | on-demand | 96–147 ms | 39–53 ms | 5 |\n\n- **Where it pays off:** antd's missing props fall from 37 to 5. On Mantine, Chakra and Spectrum the checker finds the same props the structural pass does, so there the mode only adds a process.\n- **Latency:** the first answer takes 82–137 ms on four corpora (703 ms on Chakra), inside the 150 ms budget except on Chakra. Later uncached stories cost 21–41 ms each (Chakra 534 ms), above the 5–20 ms budget.\n- **Memory:** addon peak is about the same (shadcn 314–328 MiB, antd 222–230 MiB). The `tsc` process adds 157–612 MiB on top, with antd at the high end.\n- **A bug the harness caught:** the checker omits props that `@types/react` declares (`children`, `aria-*`, DOM handlers), so the first run lost 6 props on shadcn. The on-demand hook now keeps those structural props.\n- **Still missing:** the 3 shadcn and 5 antd props left are `children` and `ref`-style props with no parent, which the checker omits. The fork left that rule alone.\n\n**Safety.** With the mode off, equivalence is identical on all five corpora, and lazy parity passes on the fixtures. Lint exits 0 and the addon tests pass (60). The workspace run (908 tests) passed before the last commits and wasn't rerun, so CI's Test / Rust is the check on the final code.\n\n**What's not built, which blocks making it default**\n- **The version pin is still exact `7.1.0-beta`.** No semver range or `--version` self-check yet.\n- No prefetch, no on-disk cache, and no resident-memory cap on the `tsc` process.\n- **CI doesn't exercise the real `tsc` path.** The real-`tsc` test skips unless `CALIPER_TEST_TSC` is set, and CI doesn't set it, so end-to-end behavior is only covered by the fork's local run.\n\n**My read:** keep it opt-in. It is a clean answer for libraries like antd and shadcn that lean on installed package types, at a cost people should choose deliberately. The next steps that would bring the per-story cost toward the budget are the on-disk cache and prefetch, plus the version-range check. Want those queued?\n\nIndependent open PRs for you to merge: #224, #225, #226, #227, #228, #229, #230, #231 and #232. Running: `fn-params` and `parity-triage`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2222,"cache_read_input_tokens":859874,"output_tokens":1612,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":363},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2222,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1612,"cache_read_input_tokens":859874,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2222,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2222},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"702ea681-5e74-4e4f-8a39-26c56bffc665","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgR6fbs4fiV5jc94vjYAo","requestRef":"f7992e32-c58d-42b8-b7e7-34ddb1e4250a","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"92df6563-1393-44c3-8d18-d0aa56b4313a","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:38:39.198Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"feat/function-param-flags","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
