{"parentUuid":"03a1cedc-7b18-4b98-a03e-6761f6c360a9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgR77nQ3dUCqXqjEbxBon","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5000,"cache_read_input_tokens":862096,"output_tokens":3273,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1740},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5000,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3273,"cache_read_input_tokens":862096,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5000,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5000},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":14974,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"d24cb62c-b46e-4594-9a83-f79b4f362cd5","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgR77mnM4nVn28X8QH9r3","requestRef":"69e597a4-cb9d-4ffd-992a-47f791128e4c","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"dd75f10d-1698-4c7e-898a-e9547e5a3b71","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:44:38.055Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"feat/function-param-flags","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"dd75f10d-1698-4c7e-898a-e9547e5a3b71","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgR77nQ3dUCqXqjEbxBon","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, they matter: `children`, `aria-*` and the DOM event handlers are what people actually use. The checker pass was dropping them, and the fix is to apply one policy to both engines instead of letting the checker decide.\n\n**What happened.** In #232 the checker's answer left out every prop that `@types/react` declares. The fork patched that by keeping the structural pass's inherited props. It still loses 3 on shadcn and 5 on antd, which are own props that reach the component through `PropsWithChildren`, `children` for example. Those have no inheritance parent, so the patch didn't catch them.\n\n**The fix I'd make.**\n1. **Merge by name, not by parent.** After the checker answers, keep every structural prop the checker didn't return, with its structural type. Where both have a prop, the checker's type wins. That covers `children`, `className`, ARIA and handlers whichever way they were declared.\n2. **Stop the checker side from filtering React declarations at all.** The `htmlAttributes` setting (`curated`, `full`, `none`) should be the only thing deciding which DOM attributes show up, applied after the merge. Then both engines follow the same rule and a user's setting means the same thing in either mode.\n3. **Test it** with a component using `PropsWithChildren`, one with `HTMLAttributes` and one with an own `children`, in on-demand and structural modes, expecting identical sets under `full`.\n\n**A decision for you: `ref` and `key`.** Today we leave out both, and RDT lists them (they were 24 of the props the site said we miss). `key` is never a real prop at runtime, but in React 19 `ref` is a normal prop on function components. I'd include `ref` for function components and keep omitting `key`. Say if you'd rather match RDT on both.\n\nI'll resume the `ts-on-demand` fork for this, since it has the context. It will also check whether the default structural `curated` mode drops any React-declared props that a story needs."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5000,"cache_read_input_tokens":862096,"output_tokens":3273,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1740},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5000,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3273,"cache_read_input_tokens":862096,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5000,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5000},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"d24cb62c-b46e-4594-9a83-f79b4f362cd5","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgR77mnM4nVn28X8QH9r3","requestRef":"69e597a4-cb9d-4ffd-992a-47f791128e4c","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"10af77c8-acaa-442e-9e81-fbc2fbcad675","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:44:43.649Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"feat/function-param-flags","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"10af77c8-acaa-442e-9e81-fbc2fbcad675","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgR77nQ3dUCqXqjEbxBon","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CojPS78b7vrjsqHYxb8qao","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"ts-on-demand","message":"Follow-up from the user: we must not omit @types/react-declared props at all in the on-demand mode (children, aria-*, DOM handlers, className, style, id, etc.). Your inherited-props patch still loses 3 shadcn and 5 antd props (own props reaching the component via PropsWithChildren etc., with no parent). Fix generally, as a new commit on PR #232's branch (feat/semantic-on-demand; it is open, unmerged; stacked work stays on that branch): (1) merge by NAME not by parent: after the checker answers, keep every structural prop the checker did not return (structural type, provenance noted); where both have a prop the checker's type wins; (2) remove any filtering of @types/react-declared props on the semantic side (crates/semantic): the `htmlAttributes` setting (curated / full / none, the same policy and curated list the structural path uses in crates/core/src/react_types.rs and resolver/html.rs) is applied AFTER the merge, once, for both engines, so a user's setting means the same thing in either mode; (3) tests: a component with PropsWithChildren<P>, one extending React.HTMLAttributes<HTMLDivElement>, and one with an own `children?: ReactNode`, in structural and on-demand modes with htmlAttributes full: identical prop NAME sets (the checker only improves types/optionality); curated and none behave per their definition in both modes; (4) re-run the shadcn/antd harness (node packages/storybook/scripts/storybook-parity.mjs --corpora /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/bench-corpus --only shadcn,antd --limit 60 --out <file>; build binding+addon first) and report 'props Storybook lists that we lack' (target 0 on both) plus first/median story; also check whether the DEFAULT structural curated mode drops any React-declared props a story needs (children/aria/handlers) and report. `ref`/`key`: the user's call is pending; do not change them yet but make the policy a single named place so it is a one-line change (propose: include `ref` for function components in React 19 semantics, omit `key`). Same house rules as before (consumer-facing friendly changeset, small commits, push before finishing, lint and tests with exit codes read directly, CI green). Update the PR body and the ADR 0022 text if the contract changes.","summary":"Ask ts-on-demand to keep all React props by name merge","type":"message","recipient":"ts-on-demand","recipient_kind":"name","content":"Follow-up from the user: we must not omit @types/…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5000,"cache_read_input_tokens":862096,"output_tokens":3273,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1740},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5000,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3273,"cache_read_input_tokens":862096,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5000,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5000},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01CojPS78b7vrjsqHYxb8qao":{"to":"ts-on-demand","message":"Follow-up from the user: we must not omit @types/react-declared props at all in the on-demand mode (children, aria-*, DOM handlers, className, style, id, etc.). Your inherited-props patch still loses 3 shadcn and 5 antd props (own props reaching the component via PropsWithChildren etc., with no parent). Fix generally, as a new commit on PR #232's branch (feat/semantic-on-demand; it is open, unmerged; stacked work stays on that branch): (1) merge by NAME not by parent: after the checker answers, keep every structural prop the checker did not return (structural type, provenance noted); where both have a prop the checker's type wins; (2) remove any filtering of @types/react-declared props on the semantic side (crates/semantic): the `htmlAttributes` setting (curated / full / none, the same policy and curated list the structural path uses in crates/core/src/react_types.rs and resolver/html.rs) is applied AFTER the merge, once, for both engines, so a user's setting means the same thing in either mode; (3) tests: a component with PropsWithChildren<P>, one extending React.HTMLAttributes<HTMLDivElement>, and one with an own `children?: ReactNode`, in structural and on-demand modes with htmlAttributes full: identical prop NAME sets (the checker only improves types/optionality); curated and none behave per their definition in both modes; (4) re-run the shadcn/antd harness (node packages/storybook/scripts/storybook-parity.mjs --corpora /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/bench-corpus --only shadcn,antd --limit 60 --out <file>; build binding+addon first) and report 'props Storybook lists that we lack' (target 0 on both) plus first/median story; also check whether the DEFAULT structural curated mode drops any React-declared props a story needs (children/aria/handlers) and report. `ref`/`key`: the user's call is pending; do not change them yet but make the policy a single named place so it is a one-line change (propose: include `ref` for function components in React 19 semantics, omit `key`). Same house rules as before (consumer-facing friendly changeset, small commits, push before finishing, lint and tests with exit codes read directly, CI green). Update the PR body and the ADR 0022 text if the contract changes.","summary":"Ask ts-on-demand to keep all React props by name merge"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"d24cb62c-b46e-4594-9a83-f79b4f362cd5","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgR77mnM4nVn28X8QH9r3","requestRef":"69e597a4-cb9d-4ffd-992a-47f791128e4c","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"ddcfd658-a94f-4b26-9f45-90bb02ba39ef","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:44:50.108Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"feat/function-param-flags","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
