{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","bridgeSessionId":"cse_01D7CJmXuD2ASqfBYm7Lk4WZ","lastSequenceNum":21749,"ownerAccountUuid":"138d593e-e185-4f72-89f2-82e1a501f134","ownerOrganizationUuid":"602db9b4-428d-49e6-a99c-64152cc62a79"}
{"parentUuid":"d31cfb67-9eab-418f-b865-8fb03614cf1c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgR7AHGfzMoKyiCqQNzUH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The `ts-on-demand` fork is resumed on this fix, as a new commit on PR #232's branch.\n\n**What it will do**\n1. **Merge by name.** Every structural prop the checker didn't return is kept with its structural type. Where both have a prop, the checker's type wins. That covers `children`, `className`, ARIA and handlers however they were declared.\n2. **One policy for both engines.** It removes any filtering of `@types/react` props on the checker side. The `htmlAttributes` setting (`curated`, `full`, `none`) then applies once, after the merge, for both engines.\n3. **Tests** for three shapes in both modes: `PropsWithChildren<P>`, `React.HTMLAttributes<HTMLDivElement>`, and an own `children?: ReactNode`. Under `full` the prop-name sets must be identical, and `curated` and `none` must behave per their definitions.\n4. **Re-run the harness** on shadcn and antd, targeting 0 missing props on both. It will also report whether the default structural `curated` mode drops any React props a story needs, which would be a bug in its own right.\n5. **`ref` and `key`:** the policy goes in one named place so your decision is a one-line change. My suggestion remains to include `ref` for function components (React 19) and keep omitting `key`.\n\nIf that check finds the default `curated` mode is dropping React props that stories use, we'll want to widen the curated list or reconsider the default. I'll report what it finds before proposing anything.\n\nRunning: `ts-on-demand` (this fix), `fn-params` and `parity-triage`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6484,"cache_read_input_tokens":867096,"output_tokens":524,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6484,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":524,"cache_read_input_tokens":867096,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6484,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6484},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"3e6335c4-c12d-4594-a86d-c7145a6ef559","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgR7AGoeTsBKgb3A2zkBj","requestRef":"b3c4f79c-974a-4e5b-9cfb-17e92443a92e","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"088f5862-e04a-4a20-86e9-b8070c078836","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:45:00.922Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"feat/function-param-flags","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
