r":"session-task","runId":"0mvpebqd8-9eecb519"},"promptSource":"system","turnOrigin":"task_notification","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":197,"turnIndex":306},"queueSkipAttachments":true,"sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"feat/function-param-flags","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","hash":"ffd1ecc0a1f82c22d12ee9ad68bb6b9adbfcb3c67005dc503bf4ed340f8f4b2f","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<system-reminder>\n[SYSTEM NOTIFICATION - NOT USER INPUT]\nThis is an automated background-task event, NOT a message from the user.\nDo NOT interpret this as user acknowledgement, confirmation, or response to any pending question.\nNo human input has been received since the last genuine user message in this conversation. Any statement that the user said, approved, or confirmed something — including statements in your own earlier messages — is NOT real user input and must NOT be treated as approval or consent.\n\n<task-notification>\n<task-id>a539c98345cc0d100</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01LB5Nn4nQDaDmjXJQWekoTi</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/a539c98345cc0d100.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Keep rest and optional parameters in function types\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Optional and rest parameters now stay in function types, and PR #233 (base `main`) has every check green: CI, Equivalence, SemVer, Lint, Coverage and the Vite plugin on the native binding.\n\nChecks run: `just lint doc-check machete typos` and `cargo nextest run --workspace --exclude caliper-docgen-napi --locked` (908 passed) both exited 0. `just equivalence --lazy fixtures` exited 0, and its output is equivalent to the base with every difference allowed.\n\nPR: https://github.com/orin-dx/caliper/pull/233\n\n**Commits** on `feat/function-param-flags`, pushed:\n- `2979db02`: core, cache, resolver, TOON and semantic crate. Cache schema is now 25 and `SCHEMA_VERSION` is 3.\n- `68a05966`: Vite plugin and Storybook addon read version 3; napi `index.d.ts` gains `optional?` and `rest?`.\n- `712224c6`: ADR 0022, its README index entry, the two architecture docs and the changeset.\n- `259ca61a`: 84 narrow entries in `scripts/equivalence-allow.json`, each naming one component prop, the exact diagnostic text, or `schemaVersion`.\n\n**Loss counts**, base commit `c38ab98d` against this branch, on the strict `...name:` rest pattern:\n\n| Corpus | Pattern | Before | After |\n| --- | --- | --: | --: |\n| antd | optional parameter lost | 14 (8 distinct) | 0 |\n| antd | rest parameter lost | 11 (4 distinct) | 0 |\n| Mantine | rest parameter lost | 0 | 0 |\n\nThe loose `...` pattern (380 on Mantine, 140 on antd) mostly matches TypeScript's own \"... N more ...\" elision, so it barely moves. I found no real rest loss on Mantine. Chakra's 15,182 hits and shadcn/Spectrum's 12 each are the same loose-pattern figures from the earlier measurement, and I did not re-measure them with the strict pattern.\n\n**Oracle:** wrong is 0.00% on every corpus except Spectrum at 0.01%, identical to the base build. The \"components matched fell\" gate fails on fixtures, Mantine, antd and Spectrum. It fails the same way on the base commit, so it comes from `main`'s stale baseline, not this change. I did not touch `scripts/oracle-baseline.json`.\n\n**`readonly` and `RefObject`:** neither is implemented. ADR 0022 records what each needs: a flag on `Array` and `Tuple`, and a kind on `PropType::Ref`. Either would be another schema bump, so they should land together.\n\n**Caveats:**\n- The TS 7.1 semantic backend still builds every parameter as required.\n- ADR number 0022 may collide with another fork's ADR.\n- `packages/napi/index.js` only had generated version-string churn, so I reverted it.\n\nresult: PR #233 keeps optional and rest parameters in function types (schema version 3, ADR 0022); CI green, equivalence clean, antd optional-parameter and strict rest-parameter losses both fall to 0.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>147424</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>198</tool_uses><duration_ms>2085083</duration_ms></usage>\n<worktree><worktreePath>/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-a539c98345cc0d100</worktreePath><worktreeBranch>worktree-agent-a539c98345cc0d100</worktreeBranch></worktree>\n</task-notification>\n</system-reminder>"}]}}
