{"parentUuid":"6b370e8a-3cba-447f-a108-2c85667caaea","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgR7NoedK7ecswUMXurRW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2199,"cache_read_input_tokens":873580,"output_tokens":1475,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":424},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2199,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1475,"cache_read_input_tokens":873580,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2199,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2199},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":3153,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"4d8d0d4a-963a-4dd8-ad95-fc79569a2258","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgR7No97XJzpA6LoaBWb4","requestRef":"965346b0-b3fb-473c-a00a-5b43fd1f9b24","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"05855827-5560-4dbb-9f5f-cc8e8cc8007c","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:47:51.473Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"feat/function-param-flags","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"05855827-5560-4dbb-9f5f-cc8e8cc8007c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgR7NoedK7ecswUMXurRW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"PR #233 is open with all checks green, and it works. Its payoff is smaller than I told you earlier, and it collides with two other open PRs.\n\n**What it does**\n- **Optional and rest parameters stay in function types.** `(a?: string, ...rest: number[]) => void` prints as itself instead of as `()` or `(a: string)`. This reaches the RDT output, TOON, the canonical JSON, the cache and the napi types. The Vite plugin and addon read version 3.\n- **Contract:** `SCHEMA_VERSION` is 3, the cache schema is 25, and ADR 0022 records it. Readers must update together, which the changeset says.\n- **Checks:** 908 tests and lint pass, equivalence is clean with every difference allowed, and the oracle's wrong rate is 0.00% on every corpus (0.01% on Spectrum), identical to the base build.\n\n**The benefit is smaller than I said.** I quoted 15,182 hits on Chakra and 380 on Mantine. Those came from a loose pattern that mostly matches TypeScript's own \"… N more …\" elision. On the strict pattern:\n\n| Corpus | Pattern | Before | After |\n| --- | --- | --: | --: |\n| antd | optional parameter lost | 14 (8 distinct) | 0 |\n| antd | rest parameter lost | 11 (4 distinct) | 0 |\n| Mantine | rest parameter lost | 0 | 0 |\n\nThe strict pattern was not re-measured on Chakra, shadcn or Spectrum, so the real remaining count there is unknown. It is a correctness fix, but not the broad signature problem I described.\n\n**Not done**\n- **`readonly` and `RefObject`:** ADR 0022 records what each needs (a flag on `Array` and `Tuple`, a kind on `PropType::Ref`). Either is another schema bump, so they should land together.\n- **The TS 7.1 backend still builds every parameter as required**, so on-demand answers lose the flags.\n- **The oracle gate still fails on \"components matched fell\"** in the same way on the base commit, so it is the stale baseline and `parity-triage` owns it.\n\n**Collisions to resolve when merging**\n1. **ADR 0022:** #232 (on-demand TS) and #233 both claim it. One needs renumbering.\n2. **Cache schema 25:** #229 (tagged factories) and #233 both bump 24 → 25. Whichever merges second must move to 26 and update its golden snapshot.\n3. **Allow-list entries:** #233 carries 84 entries, on top of #229's 22 and #230's 241. #224's new check fails a push to `main` while the list is non-empty.\n\nI'd suggest merging in this order, with each of the three colliding PRs reconciled right after its predecessor: #224, #225, #226, then #227, #228, #230, #231, then #229, #233, #232. Once you've merged a few, I can have a fork do the renumbering and empty the allow-list in one cleanup PR. Say if you want me to start it earlier against open branches instead.\n\nRunning: `ts-on-demand` (the React-props merge fix) and `parity-triage`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2199,"cache_read_input_tokens":873580,"output_tokens":1475,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":424},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2199,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1475,"cache_read_input_tokens":873580,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2199,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2199},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"4d8d0d4a-963a-4dd8-ad95-fc79569a2258","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgR7No97XJzpA6LoaBWb4","requestRef":"965346b0-b3fb-473c-a00a-5b43fd1f9b24","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"d0d2e1de-5475-4530-b4e7-5483b9c490f5","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:47:58.042Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"feat/function-param-flags","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
