{"parentUuid":"0e194f07-3298-41b1-a2c7-79e234741982","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgR7mPm5dMTk4UHbNo1Yw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3059,"cache_read_input_tokens":895669,"output_tokens":3979,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2325},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3059,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3979,"cache_read_input_tokens":895669,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3059,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3059},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":23369,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"48b86e13-1c3d-4fb9-b6d4-080323a9f7d4","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgR7mPCqdhn6QkcCaMFYb","requestRef":"32e242ee-c0c1-4c0c-a7e0-b971c315ea3a","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"601d1426-6f18-415e-844a-60d4c057448e","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:53:19.442Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"feat/function-param-flags","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"601d1426-6f18-415e-844a-60d4c057448e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgR7mPm5dMTk4UHbNo1Yw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"There are two answers here: the Homebrew tap, and the special-casing review of the open PRs. I assumed \"this PR\" means the set of open fix PRs (#224–#233) and reviewed those.\n\n## Homebrew tap auto-update\n\nThe tap side is ready and the caliper side isn't wired up. The notifier action is in an open PR that hasn't merged.\n\n**What exists**\n- **Tap (`orin-dx/homebrew-tap`):** `update-formula.yml` listens for a `repository_dispatch` event `tool_released` with `client_payload.tool` and `client_payload.tag`. It also runs a daily check at 08:17 UTC, so a missed notification is caught within a day.\n- **Caliper's manifest** (`tools/caliper.json`) says the tap follows the npm platform packages (`caliper-docgen-darwin-arm64`, `-darwin-x64`, `-linux-arm64-gnu`, `-linux-x64-gnu`) with tag prefix `npm/caliper-docgen@`. It verifies each archive's digest, opens a formula PR, runs Homebrew CI, and a maintainer approves.\n- **The new action** is **PR #2 on `orin-dx/actions`** (\"Add a shared Homebrew release notifier\"), open. It's a composite action `notify-homebrew-tap` with inputs `client-id`, `private-key`, `tap-repository`, `tool` and `release-tag`. It mints a token scoped to the tap with `contents: write` and sends `tool_released`.\n\n**What's needed**\n1. **Merge `actions#2`**, then pin it by commit in caliper's workflow. Its own description says the App credentials and the calls from release workflows \"will be configured separately after this action is merged.\"\n2. **A GitHub App** installed on `orin-dx/homebrew-tap`, with its client ID and private key stored as secrets in the caliper repo. I can't create these.\n3. **A step in `release.yml`'s `execute` job**, after `callisto release execute` succeeds, that calls the action with `tap-repository: orin-dx/homebrew-tap`, `tool: caliper` and `release-tag: npm/caliper-docgen@<version>`. The version should come from the release receipt, and the step should run only when this run actually released the CLI. It should not fail the release, since the daily check is the backstop.\n4. **A completed release.** #222 notes that the 0.6.0 release is incomplete (`caliper-docgen@0.6.0` isn't on crates.io), and the tap needs the platform packages to exist at that version to verify them.\n\nI can write step 3 as a PR once `actions#2` is merged. I haven't verified that `main` has no Homebrew mentions beyond a plain text search, and I didn't read the tap's `docs/automation.md`.\n\n## Special-casing review of the open PRs\n\nI scanned the added non-test source in #224–#233.\n\n**Consistent, no new special-casing found**\n- No `matches!` or `==` comparisons on library or component names in any of them. The only library names are in doc comments.\n- No new `unwrap`/`expect` in non-test source. The two `expect` hits are in a test module.\n- #225 (variant bags), #230 (intersections), #233 (parameter flags) and #227 (parenthesized factories) fix general shapes.\n\n**Concerns before calling these done**\n1. **#229 `taggedFactory` leans on a naming convention.** It pairs `chakra(\"div\", {…})` with a `{Name}Props` type beside it. Six Chakra components miss out because their props type is named differently. It needs a shape rule (the declared type that the call's props flow into) instead of a name pattern, plus an ADR for the new detection rule.\n2. **React API is still matched by identifier** (`forwardRef`, `memo`, `createContext`, `FC<P>` in #228). An aliased import isn't recognized. One fix for all of them: resolve through the import source (`react`). This is the same class of problem #225 fixed for `cva`.\n3. **#232 still special-cases `@types/react`** by filtering its declarations out of the checker's answer. The fix I started (merge by name, one `htmlAttributes` policy for both engines) is in progress.\n4. **Collisions:** ADR 0022 (#232 and #233), cache schema 25 (#229 and #233), and allow-list entries (#229: 22, #230: 241, #233: 84) against #224's new check.\n5. **Verification gaps:** #227–#231 skipped the precision sampling, a separate lazy parity run and the oracle, and #232's full workspace run predates its last commits. The real-`tsc` test doesn't run in CI.\n6. **Not checked:** whether the new tests assert exact values or use `contains` and `is_some`, which AGENTS.md discourages. I'd scan for that next.\n\nI'd start with a fork for concern 2, since it's the one place we still special-case by name across several PRs. Want that, and the notifier step once `actions#2` merges?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3059,"cache_read_input_tokens":895669,"output_tokens":3979,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2325},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3059,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3979,"cache_read_input_tokens":895669,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3059,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3059},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"48b86e13-1c3d-4fb9-b6d4-080323a9f7d4","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgR7mPCqdhn6QkcCaMFYb","requestRef":"32e242ee-c0c1-4c0c-a7e0-b971c315ea3a","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"d1c55983-a1b1-462a-97a4-08cf2808226e","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:53:25.003Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"feat/function-param-flags","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"d1c55983-a1b1-462a-97a4-08cf2808226e","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"Stop","toolUseID":"637add1b-e540-4bf1-9893-22dc9faccd0f","hookEvent":"Stop","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"stop\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"release-0.2.0\\\",\\\"query\\\":\\\"Are we staying consistent with addressing patterns, not special casing everything? Are there concerns we should address before we consider this PR done? Let's not be lazy\\\",\\\"response\\\":\\\"There are two answers here: the Homebrew tap, and the special-casing review of the open PRs. I assumed \\\\\\\"this PR\\\\\\\" means the set of open fix PRs (#224–#233) and reviewed those.\\\\n\\\\n## Homebrew tap auto-...\\\",\\\"transcript_path\\\":\\\"/Users/gabe/.claude/projects/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675.jsonl\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/gabe/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.1.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-stop.sh","durationMs":1870},"type":"attachment","uuid":"c9a4b1c8-63b7-4ca5-933b-8327bb75418f","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:53:26.903Z","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"feat/function-param-flags","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
