** missing on Dragger, because it isn't in the curated list.\n- **PurePanel:** 32 props missing, including handlers and attributes (`onClick`, `onFocus`, `onKeyDown`, `onMouseEnter`, `id`, `autoFocus`, and others) alongside its own Drawer props such as `open` and `width`. I didn't separate the DOM attributes from the own props.\n\nShadcn loses none in the sample.\n\n**Docs**\nI updated ADR 0022, `docs/type-checker-integration.md`, the changeset and the PR body.\n\n**Merge order:** PR #232 is independent, base `main`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>224892</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>40</tool_uses><duration_ms>1076969</duration_ms></usage>\n<worktree><worktreePath>/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-ab8a57f3074b60627</worktreePath><worktreeBranch>worktree-agent-ab8a57f3074b60627</worktreeBranch></worktree>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"ab80e5c2-8dd8-4df3-ba2e-04f2efa861e7","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:02:53.115Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"task-notification","producer":"session-task","runId":"0mvpfgswy-cd34dc06"},"promptSource":"system","turnOrigin":"task_notification","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":199,"turnIndex":309},"queueSkipAttachments":true,"sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"feat/function-param-flags","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","hash":"2dd12cf1177923b182b8c7c735307d2323fd18f460c38d70849e95d31e7874a5","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<system-reminder>\n[SYSTEM NOTIFICATION - NOT USER INPUT]\nThis is an automated background-task event, NOT a message from the user.\nDo NOT interpret this as user acknowledgement, confirmation, or response to any pending question.\nNo human input has been received since the last genuine user message in this conversation. Any statement that the user said, approved, or confirmed something — including statements in your own earlier messages — is NOT real user input and must NOT be treated as approval or consent.\n\n<task-notification>\n<task-id>ab8a57f3074b60627</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01CojPS78b7vrjsqHYxb8qao</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/ab8a57f3074b60627.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"On-demand TS 7.1 resolution per requested component\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>`@types/react` props are no longer omitted in on-demand mode. The shadcn harness now reports 0 props Storybook lists that we lack, and antd reports 2. Both are pushed to PR #232 (`feat/semantic-on-demand`), and CI is green on all checks, including Equivalence and SemVer.\n\n**What changed**\n- **Merge by name:** where both engines have a prop, the checker's type, optionality and description win. Every structural prop the checker doesn't return stays with its structural type. The provenance `Info` diagnostic counts those kept props.\n- **No filtering in `crates/semantic`:** the checker reports `@types/react` props flagged `react_declared`. The request carries `react_wanted`, and the session sets it from `htmlAttributes`; without it a component would convert hundreds of DOM attributes it then drops. The whole-project merge still drops them, so its behaviour is unchanged.\n- **`htmlAttributes` applied once after the merge:** the policy lives in `checker_prop_used` in `crates/core/src/react_types.rs`.\n  - `full` takes every `@types/react` prop the checker reports.\n  - `curated` and `none` take only those the structural pass already lists among the component's props, such as `children` through `PropsWithChildren` or an own `children`.\n  - The curated attributes and `none`'s absence stay the structural pass's.\n- **`key` and `ref`:** both are omitted in every mode, and the user's call is still pending. The whole policy is the constant `REACT_SPECIAL_PROPS` in `react_types.rs`, so showing `ref` for function components is a one-line change there.\n\n**Tests**\n- Core: a fake checker that reports `@types/react` props runs against `PropsWithChildren&lt;P&gt;`, an own `children?: ReactNode`, and `extends HTMLAttributes&lt;HTMLDivElement&gt;`.\n  - Under `curated` and `none` the prop names equal the structural ones and the checker's type wins on `children`.\n  - Under `full` every reported prop is taken except `key` and `ref`.\n  - The request asks only for the names the mode can use.\n- Real tsc with the repo's real `@types/react`: prop names and `notable_inherited` keys are identical to the structural pass for all three components in `full`, `curated` and `none`. This test is gated on `CALIPER_TEST_TSC` and skips when it's unset, so CI skips it. I ran it locally.\n- Workspace nextest passes 914 tests, with 1 skipped. Lint exits 0, and equivalence with the mode off is identical on the five corpora.\n\n**Harness, two runs, shared machine**\n\n| Corpus | Variant | Props Storybook lists that we lack | First story | Median story |\n| --- | --- | --: | --: | --: |\n| shadcn | structural | 0 | 81–82 ms | 2 ms |\n| shadcn | on-demand | 0 | 110 ms | 32–35 ms |\n| antd | structural | 37 | 62–63 ms | 2 ms |\n| antd | on-demand | 2 | 116–128 ms | 44–49 ms |\n\nThe 2 antd props still missing are `ref` on `CheckableTagGroup` (omitted by policy) and `capture` on `Dragger`. `capture` is an `&lt;input&gt;` attribute that isn't in the curated set, so it's missing by the `curated` definition.\n\n**Does default structural curated mode drop props a story needs?** Yes, on antd:\n- **`ref`:** missing on Breadcrumb, CheckableTagGroup and Transfer.\n- **`capture`:** missing on Dragger, because it isn't in the curated list.\n- **PurePanel:** 32 props missing, including handlers and attributes (`onClick`, `onFocus`, `onKeyDown`, `onMouseEnter`, `id`, `autoFocus`, and others) alongside its own Drawer props such as `open` and `width`. I didn't separate the DOM attributes from the own props.\n\nShadcn loses none in the sample.\n\n**Docs**\nI updated ADR 0022, `docs/type-checker-integration.md`, the changeset and the PR body.\n\n**Merge order:** PR #232 is independent, base `main`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>224892</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>40</tool_uses><duration_ms>1076969</duration_ms></usage>\n<worktree><worktreePath>/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-ab8a57f3074b60627</worktreePath><worktreeBranch>worktree-agent-ab8a57f3074b60627</worktreeBranch></worktree>\n</task-notification>\n</system-reminder>"}]}}
