{"parentUuid":"ab80e5c2-8dd8-4df3-ba2e-04f2efa861e7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgR8XnkfjpwKPCYLjip7K","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2026,"cache_read_input_tokens":902707,"output_tokens":1988,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":786},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2026,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1988,"cache_read_input_tokens":902707,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2026,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2026},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":6815,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"cfb7f60f-83f3-4e1f-ba1b-bb836d8b8b6d","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgR8XkKZxNjGszeGPUs3C","requestRef":"40ee8077-f2f2-49c4-90a2-22232d3f029e","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"aa589d3e-3f7a-4327-8fa3-47e3aca01f30","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:03:02.453Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"feat/function-param-flags","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"aa589d3e-3f7a-4327-8fa3-47e3aca01f30","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgR8XnkfjpwKPCYLjip7K","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The on-demand mode no longer drops `@types/react` props. PR #232 is green on every check, including Equivalence and SemVer.\n\n**What changed in #232**\n- **Merge by name.** Where both engines have a prop, the checker's type, optionality and description win. Every structural prop the checker doesn't return stays, and the provenance note counts the kept props.\n- **No filtering in `crates/semantic`.** The checker reports `@types/react` props flagged `react_declared`, and the session's `htmlAttributes` setting decides what's used. A request asks only for the names the mode can use, so a component doesn't convert hundreds of DOM attributes it will drop. The whole-project merge is unchanged.\n- **One policy, applied once** after the merge (`checker_prop_used` in `crates/core/src/react_types.rs`):\n  - `full` takes every `@types/react` prop the checker reports.\n  - `curated` and `none` take only what the structural pass already lists, such as `children`.\n- **`key` and `ref` are still omitted in every mode.** That's your call. It is the single constant `REACT_SPECIAL_PROPS`, so showing `ref` for function components is a one-line change.\n\n**Result** (harness, two runs, shared machine)\n\n| Corpus | Variant | Props Storybook lists that we lack | First story | Median story |\n| --- | --- | --: | --: | --: |\n| shadcn | structural | 0 | 81–82 ms | 2 ms |\n| shadcn | on-demand | 0 | 110 ms | 32–35 ms |\n| antd | structural | 37 | 62–63 ms | 2 ms |\n| antd | on-demand | 2 | 116–128 ms | 44–49 ms |\n\nThe two antd props left are `ref` on `CheckableTagGroup` (policy) and `capture` on `Dragger`, an `<input>` attribute outside the curated list. Tests cover all three declaration shapes against a fake checker, and against the real `@types/react` with a real `tsc` locally. CI skips the real-`tsc` test because `CALIPER_TEST_TSC` is unset. 914 workspace tests pass.\n\n**The larger finding: the default structural `curated` mode drops props stories need.** On antd:\n- `ref` is missing on Breadcrumb, CheckableTagGroup and Transfer.\n- `capture` is missing on Dragger.\n- `PurePanel` loses 32 props, including `onClick`, `onFocus`, `onKeyDown`, `onMouseEnter`, `id` and `autoFocus`, next to its own Drawer props. The fork didn't separate DOM attributes from own props. shadcn loses none in the sample.\n\nThat conflicts with your rule that we shouldn't omit `@types/react` props.\n\n**What I'd do.** Make the data complete and let the display decide what to show:\n- Include all `@types/react` props in the output, with provenance, and let the addon's `collapseInheritedProps` and Storybook's UI hide them. The `none` and `curated` modes drop data, not just display.\n- **Cost looks small.** The React attributes are one shared prop set after schema v2, so they cost almost nothing in size. Earlier Chakra runs showed HTML attributes weren't the time cost either (320 ms with and without). I haven't measured the default flip.\n- So I'd measure `full` as the default on all five corpora, covering time, memory and output size, and flip it if it holds.\n\n**Merge note.** ADR 0022 is still claimed by #232 and #233; one needs renumbering when you merge. Want me to start the `full`-by-default measurement as a fork?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2026,"cache_read_input_tokens":902707,"output_tokens":1988,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":786},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2026,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1988,"cache_read_input_tokens":902707,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2026,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2026},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"cfb7f60f-83f3-4e1f-ba1b-bb836d8b8b6d","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgR8XkKZxNjGszeGPUs3C","requestRef":"40ee8077-f2f2-49c4-90a2-22232d3f029e","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"00c56f89-e431-43c3-aaf7-9c1aa847c477","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:03:09.546Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"feat/function-param-flags","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
