{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:04:09.162Z","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a77265bdad974924a</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_011H4Y5Cntqhmpvu76iDjp5Z</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/a77265bdad974924a.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Triage the Parity and oracle regressions on main\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Track AO is only partly done. I fixed one real regression and tightened one pattern. The `MenuTrigger` regression is not fixed, the baselines are not refreshed, and the dispatched Parity workflow fails. PR #234 is a draft with base `ci/repair-gates`, because #224 is still open.\n\nLocal gates all exit 0: `cargo nextest` (900 passed), `just lint doc-check machete typos`, `scripts/test_equivalence.py`, `scripts/test_parity.py`, and `just equivalence` (which includes lazy parity). I did not re-run the oracle on the final code or refresh the baselines.\n\n**Committed on `ci/triage-parity-regressions`, pushed:**\n- `34259693` — drops a call signature's own type parameter from a polymorphic union. Mantine's `component` prop now prints `ElementType` instead of `C | ElementType`. The pipeline test now asserts the exact value.\n- `455c51fd` — `scripts/parity.py` `type_params` now ignores string literals, with `scripts/test_parity.py`.\n- `ba524a5e` — one narrow allow-list entry, `mantine/* prop-type-changed *.component`, plus `.changeset/polymorphic-component-prop-text.md`. The entry must be removed after merge.\n\n**Why the Parity workflow failed.** The dispatch (run 40355403892) failed three ways:\n1. `Allow-list is empty` fails because of my one allow-list entry. That is intended while the PR is open.\n2. The oracle step fails with `FileNotFoundError` on `apps/validate/node_modules/typescript-beta/package.json`. That dependency isn't installed in the dispatch run.\n3. The equivalence step fails because it is given `$RUNNER_TEMP/caliper-base`, a path, where `git rev-parse` needs a commit.\n\nI believe 2 and 3 are workflow defects from #224 that show up only on dispatch, not caused by my code, but I haven't confirmed that.\n\n| metric | before | now | introducing PR | class | action |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Mantine `component` prop text (25 props) | `C \\| ElementType` | `ElementType` | unknown, not bisected | real regression | fixed in `34259693`, narrow allow-list entry |\n| Spectrum \"unbound type parameter\" | counted `\"S\" \\| \"M\" \\| \"L\"` breakpoint keys | not counted | none, the pattern was naive | improvement scored as loss | pattern tightened in `455c51fd` |\n| base-ui `MenuTrigger` detection | detected | lost | #209 (`e0b7054f`) | real regression | not fixed, see below |\n| Chakra utility-type growth | n/a | n/a | predates the range I bisected | acceptable difference | none, refresh later |\n| Spectrum, antd, Mantine oracle numbers | baseline values | not reproducible, even with the baseline commit's own build | none, stale baseline | stale baseline | refresh later |\n\nI have no numbers for the Chakra, Spectrum, antd and Mantine-oracle rows beyond this classification.\n\n`MenuTrigger` returns `renderByProp(...)`, a same-file helper annotated `React.ReactElement`, and #209's narrower call evidence no longer counts it. The fix is to treat calls to same-file element-returning helpers as element evidence in `extractor/evidence.rs`. I ran out of time-box before doing it.\n\n**Next:**\n- Fix the two #224 workflow dispatch bugs, or run the oracle locally with antd and shadcn set up.\n- Refresh the baselines in their own commit from a clean run.\n- Fix `MenuTrigger`.\n- Remove the allow-list entry once this PR merges.\n\nPR: https://github.com/orin-dx/caliper/pull/234\n\nresult: PR #234 (draft, base `ci/repair-gates`) fixes the Mantine `component` prop text and a naive Spectrum parity pattern; the `MenuTrigger` regression, baseline refresh and Parity workflow dispatch are still open.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>95290</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>117</tool_uses><duration_ms>2669791</duration_ms></usage>\n<worktree><worktreePath>/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-a77265bdad974924a</worktreePath><worktreeBranch>worktree-agent-a77265bdad974924a</worktreeBranch></worktree>\n</task-notification>"}
