{"parentUuid":"171ed373-0088-422e-93c4-1dc18303aba8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgR8dMBgzBHEk4zYLjQp9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VULr9eacBqZPxjxTHqBDAB","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"gates","message":"Follow-up on your PR #224 (branch ci/repair-gates; keep committing to it). The triage fork dispatched the weekly Parity workflow on its branch (run 40355403892) and two steps fail for reasons that look like defects in your workflow changes that only show on dispatch: (1) the oracle step fails with FileNotFoundError on apps/validate/node_modules/typescript-beta/package.json: the dispatch run does not install apps/validate's dependencies including the typescript-beta alias (check parity.yml's install steps vs what the oracle needs: `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` at the root, the alias dependency in apps/validate/package.json, and whether the corepack/COREPACK_HOME manifest change or a missing step skips it); (2) the equivalence step is given `$RUNNER_TEMP/caliper-base` (a path) where `git rev-parse` needs a commit: scripts/equivalence.py takes a git ref OR an executable; make the argument handling accept an existing executable path first (os.path.isfile + executable) before trying `rev-parse`, with a unit test in scripts/test_equivalence.py, or fix what parity.yml passes. Fix both, dispatch it yourself (`gh workflow run parity.yml --ref ci/repair-gates`, watch with `gh run watch`) and confirm the Install, Allow-list-empty, Measure/gate, Equivalence and Oracle steps reach their real pass/fail verdicts (the accuracy gate may still fail on baseline drift: that is the triage fork's job; report exactly which steps pass). Same house rules (friendly consumer-facing changeset only if shipped text changes; CI/tooling needs none; small commits; push before finishing; lint with exit codes read directly).","summary":"Ask gates fork to fix the two Parity dispatch defects","type":"message","recipient":"gates","recipient_kind":"name","content":"Follow-up on your PR #224 (branch ci/repair-gates…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3960,"cache_read_input_tokens":904733,"output_tokens":2716,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":356},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3960,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":2716,"cache_read_input_tokens":904733,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3960,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3960},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01VULr9eacBqZPxjxTHqBDAB":{"to":"gates","message":"Follow-up on your PR #224 (branch ci/repair-gates; keep committing to it). The triage fork dispatched the weekly Parity workflow on its branch (run 40355403892) and two steps fail for reasons that look like defects in your workflow changes that only show on dispatch: (1) the oracle step fails with FileNotFoundError on apps/validate/node_modules/typescript-beta/package.json: the dispatch run does not install apps/validate's dependencies including the typescript-beta alias (check parity.yml's install steps vs what the oracle needs: `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` at the root, the alias dependency in apps/validate/package.json, and whether the corepack/COREPACK_HOME manifest change or a missing step skips it); (2) the equivalence step is given `$RUNNER_TEMP/caliper-base` (a path) where `git rev-parse` needs a commit: scripts/equivalence.py takes a git ref OR an executable; make the argument handling accept an existing executable path first (os.path.isfile + executable) before trying `rev-parse`, with a unit test in scripts/test_equivalence.py, or fix what parity.yml passes. Fix both, dispatch it yourself (`gh workflow run parity.yml --ref ci/repair-gates`, watch with `gh run watch`) and confirm the Install, Allow-list-empty, Measure/gate, Equivalence and Oracle steps reach their real pass/fail verdicts (the accuracy gate may still fail on baseline drift: that is the triage fork's job; report exactly which steps pass). Same house rules (friendly consumer-facing changeset only if shipped text changes; CI/tooling needs none; small commits; push before finishing; lint with exit codes read directly).","summary":"Ask gates fork to fix the two Parity dispatch defects"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"606513ce-c8f3-4b25-a7b1-2adb6e7790e8","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgR8dLehQmVkKJA6Hrxgr","requestRef":"f73b2b8e-7e38-4d6a-a394-0c934924503d","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"de81ab44-5942-4107-aad0-b01c39e4d0f8","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:04:24.157Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"ci/triage-parity-regressions","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"de81ab44-5942-4107-aad0-b01c39e4d0f8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgR8dMBgzBHEk4zYLjQp9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01X7EBRNAnvUvpBXVXGhgvxS","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"parity-triage","message":"Follow-up on PR #234 (branch ci/triage-parity-regressions, base ci/repair-gates). Do next, in order: (1) fix the MenuTrigger regression introduced by #209 (e0b7054f): MenuTrigger returns `renderByProp(...)`, a same-file helper annotated `React.ReactElement`, and #209's narrower call evidence stopped counting it. Fix by shape, not by name, in crates/core/src/extractor/evidence.rs: a call to a same-file function whose declared return type is a React element type (ReactElement / JSX.Element / ReactNode subtype via the existing React-type recognition) counts as element evidence; keep #209's intent (JSX passed to response constructors like `new Response(<div/>)` is NOT render evidence: its constructor-jsx tests must stay green); add exact tests for: the helper-returning-element case, an aliased return type, a helper returning a non-element (negative), and the constructor case. Check base-ui across the other corpora with equivalence for other lost components (list any). (2) The `gates` fork is fixing the two Parity workflow dispatch defects in #224 (oracle needs typescript-beta installed; equivalence given a path instead of a commit): once that lands on ci/repair-gates, merge origin/ci/repair-gates into your branch and re-dispatch `gh workflow run parity.yml --ref ci/triage-parity-regressions`. (3) Then refresh scripts/parity-baseline.json and scripts/oracle-baseline.json in their OWN commit from a clean run of the repaired gates, only for metrics you classified improvement/acceptable, with before/after numbers per corpus in the PR body. (4) Mark #234 ready for review when the Parity workflow reaches real verdicts and passes, or say exactly which gate still fails and why. Remove the allow-list entry only after the PR merges (note it in the PR). House rules as before; commit small, push before finishing.","summary":"Ask parity-triage to fix MenuTrigger and refresh baselines","type":"message","recipient":"parity-triage","recipient_kind":"name","content":"Follow-up on PR #234 (branch ci/triage-parity-reg…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3960,"cache_read_input_tokens":904733,"output_tokens":2716,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":356},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3960,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":2716,"cache_read_input_tokens":904733,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3960,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3960},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01X7EBRNAnvUvpBXVXGhgvxS":{"to":"parity-triage","message":"Follow-up on PR #234 (branch ci/triage-parity-regressions, base ci/repair-gates). Do next, in order: (1) fix the MenuTrigger regression introduced by #209 (e0b7054f): MenuTrigger returns `renderByProp(...)`, a same-file helper annotated `React.ReactElement`, and #209's narrower call evidence stopped counting it. Fix by shape, not by name, in crates/core/src/extractor/evidence.rs: a call to a same-file function whose declared return type is a React element type (ReactElement / JSX.Element / ReactNode subtype via the existing React-type recognition) counts as element evidence; keep #209's intent (JSX passed to response constructors like `new Response(<div/>)` is NOT render evidence: its constructor-jsx tests must stay green); add exact tests for: the helper-returning-element case, an aliased return type, a helper returning a non-element (negative), and the constructor case. Check base-ui across the other corpora with equivalence for other lost components (list any). (2) The `gates` fork is fixing the two Parity workflow dispatch defects in #224 (oracle needs typescript-beta installed; equivalence given a path instead of a commit): once that lands on ci/repair-gates, merge origin/ci/repair-gates into your branch and re-dispatch `gh workflow run parity.yml --ref ci/triage-parity-regressions`. (3) Then refresh scripts/parity-baseline.json and scripts/oracle-baseline.json in their OWN commit from a clean run of the repaired gates, only for metrics you classified improvement/acceptable, with before/after numbers per corpus in the PR body. (4) Mark #234 ready for review when the Parity workflow reaches real verdicts and passes, or say exactly which gate still fails and why. Remove the allow-list entry only after the PR merges (note it in the PR). House rules as before; commit small, push before finishing.","summary":"Ask parity-triage to fix MenuTrigger and refresh baselines"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"606513ce-c8f3-4b25-a7b1-2adb6e7790e8","apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CgR8dLehQmVkKJA6Hrxgr","requestRef":"f73b2b8e-7e38-4d6a-a394-0c934924503d","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"740edb1e-1aa7-458a-80e3-855eb41e6f97","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:04:28.967Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"ci/triage-parity-regressions","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
