{"parentUuid":"dfeefc62-1d50-450c-848b-032a5240eeeb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgR8ewBNmNfdJ2dYcDX3G","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both forks are resumed.\n\n- **`gates`** is fixing the two workflow defects in #224's branch. It will make the equivalence step accept an executable path before trying a commit, with a unit test. It will also make sure the oracle step has `apps/validate`'s dependencies, including `typescript-beta`. It will then dispatch the Parity workflow itself and report which steps now reach a real pass or fail verdict.\n- **`parity-triage`** is fixing `MenuTrigger` by shape in `extractor/evidence.rs`. A call to a same-file function whose declared return type is a React element type counts as element evidence. #209's rule that JSX passed to response constructors like `new Response(<div/>)` is not render evidence must keep holding, so the exact tests cover the helper case, an aliased return type, a non-element helper (negative), and the constructor case. It will also check the other corpora for lost components. After `gates` lands, it merges that branch in, re-dispatches Parity, and refreshes the two baselines in their own commit, only for metrics it classified as improvement or acceptable.\n\n**Open for you, by what I know right now**\n\n| Group | PRs | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Independent, green | #225, #226, #227, #228, #230, #231, #232, #233 | #232 now also has the React-props fix |\n| CI and tooling | #224 | install fix and allow-list guard good; weekly Parity steps being fixed |\n| Draft, stacked on #224 | #234 | not ready yet |\n| Pending decisions | `ref` and `key` policy, `full` HTML attributes as the default, which PR number \"this PR\" meant | |\n\nCollisions to resolve at merge: ADR 0022 (#232 and #233), cache schema 25 (#229 and #233), and allow-list entries (#229, #230, #233, #234) against #224's empty-list check."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6020,"cache_read_input_tokens":908693,"output_tokens":620,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6020,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":620,"cache_read_input_tokens":908693,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6020,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6020},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"ce054ff4-f7a5-4634-9aaf-5e936e76c8d8","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgR8eve8YubeesbjJBBi3","requestRef":"64f41001-9072-4a08-866f-3321c3147e9f","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"305ef021-45a6-40c1-b51e-a624b95f24c4","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:04:37.597Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"ci/triage-parity-regressions","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
