{"parentUuid":"92c2b79e-575d-4531-b003-e03c57f5ca7d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRA5E9cyEHi6FnRG3sXZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"They are slow, but not stuck. Three Parity runs are in flight right now:\n\n| Run | Branch | Started (UTC) | Status |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 40356079429 | `ci/repair-gates` | 16:07 | in progress |\n| 40356147683 | `scratch/parity-allow-probe` | 16:08 | in progress |\n| 40356517818 | `ci/triage-parity-regressions` | 16:10 | in progress, last update 16:21 |\n\nIt is 16:23 now. A full Parity run takes 12–16 minutes: the earlier `main` run took 12 and the first `ci/repair-gates` run took 16. So the oldest of these is within the normal range.\n\n**Why it feels long**\n- **Each fix needs a full dispatch.** The weekly Parity workflow can't be run locally, so every attempt installs five large corpora and runs the gates on a runner. The `gates` fork found two defects, so that's two or three rounds at about 15 minutes each, and `parity-triage` then waits on `gates` and runs its own.\n- **They overlap.** `gates` also started a scratch probe for the allow-list step, so three runs share the runner pool.\n\n**What I'd do**\n1. Let this round finish. If all three are green or fail on a known baseline-drift step, no more rounds are needed.\n2. If a fork starts a fourth round for a small fix, make the workflow's dispatch take a `corpora` input (for example Chakra only), so a check takes 3–4 minutes instead of 15. I'd add that to #224.\n\nI can also cancel the scratch probe run if you want fewer concurrent runs. Say if you'd like me to add the input, or wait for this round first."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":618,"cache_read_input_tokens":915684,"output_tokens":1010,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":444},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":618,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1010,"cache_read_input_tokens":915684,"cache_creation_input_tokens":618,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":618},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"e4982ef3-bbd7-4832-abe5-6b65ddb9e845","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgRA5DjpKj9uUYSii9mzj","requestRef":"c2123291-f041-483a-8293-ead727fcf72e","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"15df5ec5-8d89-42dd-8200-4e7454b0ccf6","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:23:18.182Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"scratch/parity-allow-probe","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
