{"parentUuid":"ef3aa55b-6174-4961-8d52-742cbf5c11de","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"1f3f1241-c01d-4ff5-86e4-90e900015437","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>accbf15a5e0d1dd07</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01VULr9eacBqZPxjxTHqBDAB</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/accbf15a5e0d1dd07.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Allow-list guard, PR speed gate, Parity install fix\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Both defects are fixed on `ci/repair-gates` (PR #224), pushed, and verified by dispatching Parity myself. The causes were not the ones the coordinator guessed.\n\n**What actually happened in the triage run (40355403892)**\n- The triage branch carries allow-list entries on purpose. My `Allow-list is empty` step failed the whole job there, so every step after it was skipped: pnpm install, build, corpus install.\n- The `always()` steps then ran against nothing. The oracle step hit `FileNotFoundError` on `typescript-beta` because `apps/validate` was never installed, and the equivalence step got a `caliper-base` path that was never built.\n- `resolve_base` already tried an existing executable first. The path \"failed\" only because the build was skipped. So the workflow was the defect, not the argument handling.\n\n**Fixes**\n- `parity.yml`: the allow-list step is `continue-on-error` unless the run is scheduled or on `main`. A run dispatched on a branch now reports its entries, and everything after it still runs.\n- `equivalence.py`: a base that is neither an executable nor a commit now exits with \"not an executable and not a commit; if it is a path, the step that builds it did not run\". Before, `git rev-parse` died with its own error. Two new tests in `test_equivalence.py` cover an executable path and a missing path. All 11 Python tests pass, and `just lint doc-check machete typos` exits 0.\n- `docs/parity.md` says a branch run only reports entries.\n- Commits: `195637e9` (workflow and doc) and `74cd0aeb` (`equivalence.py` and tests). Both are pushed. No changeset, since it is CI and tooling only.\n\n**Verified by two dispatches**\n- 40356079429 on `ci/repair-gates`, empty list.\n- 40356147683 on `scratch/parity-allow-probe`, one entry, reproducing the triage condition.\n\n| Step | Both runs |\n| --- | --- |\n| Allow-list is empty | passes; on the probe it logs `has 1 entries; it must be empty on main` and the job continues |\n| Install (pnpm, build, corpora) | passes, Mantine and Spectrum included |\n| Measure and gate | fails with a real verdict: for example shadcn and Spectrum components matched fell (95.29% to 95.23%, 77.20% to 76.19%) |\n| Compare prop types with TypeScript's checker (oracle) | fails with a real verdict, no `FileNotFoundError` |\n| Compare output with the base (equivalence) | passes |\n\nThe two failing accuracy gates are baseline drift and regressions, which is the triage fork's job. No `FileNotFoundError` remains.\n\n**Cleanup for you:** I created the remote branch `scratch/parity-allow-probe` for the probe. Remote deletion is blocked here, so run `git push origin --delete scratch/parity-allow-probe`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>898518</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>32</tool_uses><duration_ms>1210962</duration_ms></usage>\n<worktree><worktreePath>/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-accbf15a5e0d1dd07</worktreePath><worktreeBranch>worktree-agent-accbf15a5e0d1dd07</worktreeBranch></worktree>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"0a7fa9a1-562a-4143-8085-0934756ccc01","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:24:42.214Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"task-notification","producer":"session-task","runId":"0