{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","bridgeSessionId":"cse_01D7CJmXuD2ASqfBYm7Lk4WZ","lastSequenceNum":21749,"ownerAccountUuid":"138d593e-e185-4f72-89f2-82e1a501f134","ownerOrganizationUuid":"602db9b4-428d-49e6-a99c-64152cc62a79"}
{"parentUuid":"0a7fa9a1-562a-4143-8085-0934756ccc01","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRACF4t5ASYperraP1gb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The `gates` fork is done, and my guess about the cause was wrong. The workflow was the defect, not the argument handling. Both fixes are pushed to #224 and verified by two real dispatches.\n\n**What actually happened.** The triage branch carries an allow-list entry on purpose, and my `Allow-list is empty` step failed the whole job there. Every step after it was skipped, including install and build. The `always()` steps then ran against nothing: the oracle hit `FileNotFoundError` on `typescript-beta` because `apps/validate` was never installed, and the equivalence step got a base path that was never built. `resolve_base` already tried an executable path first.\n\n**Fixes**\n- **`parity.yml`:** the allow-list step is `continue-on-error` unless the run is scheduled or on `main`. A branch run reports its entries and the rest still runs.\n- **`equivalence.py`:** a base that is neither an executable nor a commit now exits with a clear message that the step that builds it did not run, instead of a raw `git rev-parse` error. Two new tests cover an executable path and a missing path. All 11 Python tests pass and lint exits 0.\n- `docs/parity.md` says a branch run only reports entries. No changeset, since it is CI and tooling.\n\n**Verified** by two dispatches (40356079429 on `ci/repair-gates`, and 40356147683 on a scratch probe with one entry):\n\n| Step | Both runs |\n| --- | --- |\n| Allow-list is empty | passes; on the probe it logs the entry and the job continues |\n| Install (pnpm, build, corpora) | passes, Mantine and Spectrum included |\n| Measure and gate | fails with a real verdict (for example shadcn components matched 95.29% → 95.23%, Spectrum 77.20% → 76.19%) |\n| Oracle | fails with a real verdict, no `FileNotFoundError` |\n| Equivalence | passes |\n\nSo the two failing gates are now genuine accuracy findings against the stored baselines, which `parity-triage` owns.\n\n**Cleanup for you:** delete the probe branch with `git push origin --delete scratch/parity-allow-probe`.\n\n`parity-triage` can now merge `ci/repair-gates` and re-dispatch, then fix `MenuTrigger` and refresh the baselines. Running: `parity-triage`. Waiting on you: #224–#233 as listed before."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1590,"cache_read_input_tokens":917312,"output_tokens":798,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1590,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":798,"cache_read_input_tokens":917312,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1590,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1590},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"1284220f-97e9-4c8d-a5ae-7b29192a1e87","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgRACEXtLqA3RTFAxQ4jm","requestRef":"cfb403d9-aeae-4a86-adeb-9c899eaef5ec","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"184589fd-af46-44d1-bc06-4dac9a2d6f3f","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:24:50.887Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"scratch/parity-allow-probe","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
