{"parentUuid":"367dc226-79ac-4efd-8a86-017b6515ce85","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRAF5i9BAwpi6eXVWJ1p","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Agreed on both. I'll make `ref` part of the fix, and `key` stays omitted until you say otherwise (it isn't a runtime prop). I'm starting a fork to find out why PurePanel lost `onClick`, `onFocus` and the rest, since losing core handlers is a bug whatever the `curated` list says."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3881,"cache_read_input_tokens":918902,"output_tokens":3253,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":692},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3881,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3253,"cache_read_input_tokens":918902,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3881,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3881},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"94706a82-5787-4c69-801f-48e1e357dd30","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgRAF55wWNZGd2bhhJvs1","requestRef":"cb4e671f-544d-42a5-a2cb-1159124ef59a","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"89030a76-e530-467a-a63e-36f14fcfed02","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:25:47.116Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"scratch/parity-allow-probe","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"89030a76-e530-467a-a63e-36f14fcfed02","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRAF5i9BAwpi6eXVWJ1p","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SH7KQbUqfzqT6yvi76cbYo","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Why React handlers are lost, and include ref","subagent_type":"fork","isolation":"worktree","name":"react-props","prompt":"Track AP: React-declared props must never go missing (user: 'we should not exclude ref, and we should dig into why we lost onClick, onFocus, etc. Those are crucial'). Do NOT remove worktrees (others, including Codex, use the repo). Branch off origin/feat/semantic-on-demand (PR #232, open, unmerged; it introduced the `REACT_SPECIAL_PROPS` constant and `checker_prop_used` in crates/core/src/react_types.rs and the merge-by-name logic); open your PR with base = feat/semantic-on-demand (never main while carrying that parent; the repo deletes head branches on merge so merging bottom-up retargets to main) and say so in the body; if #232 has merged (`gh pr view 232 --json state`), branch off origin/main with base main. Part 1 DIG: on antd (installed corpus /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/bench-corpus/ant-design/components, Storybook harness: node packages/storybook/scripts/storybook-parity.mjs --corpora /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/bench-corpus --only antd --limit 100 --out <file> after `pnpm --filter caliper-docgen-napi build:napi` and `pnpm --filter caliper-docgen-storybook build`), the default structural `curated` mode lost 32 props on `PurePanel` (drawer) including onClick, onFocus, onKeyDown, onMouseEnter, id, autoFocus beside its own Drawer props, and `ref` on Breadcrumb, CheckableTagGroup, Transfer, and `capture` on Dragger. Find the ROOT CAUSE for PurePanel: run `caliper-docgen extract --src <antd components> --format rdt|--json` in curated, full and none modes and look at the PurePanel entry: does the props type reach `React.HTMLAttributes<HTMLDivElement>` through `Omit<>`/`Pick<>`/`ComponentProps<'div'>`/an interface extends in a dependency (rc-component/drawer)? Is the component's props type unresolved (a diagnostic) so only own props show? Is the curated list simply too small (react_types.rs notable HTML attrs: which names does it contain, is onClick etc. in it?) or does the curated filter run before the Omit so everything is dropped? Is there a difference between PurePanel's entry and the RDT/Storybook expectation (Storybook's react-docgen-typescript lists them? they come from node_modules @types/react: Storybook's DEFAULT propFilter in many setups EXCLUDES node_modules props, so compare to what the harness's baseline (react-component-meta) lists, which is what the parity count is measured against)? Report the cause with evidence (the exact diagnostics/lists) before fixing. Fix the root cause generally (no per-component or per-library special case), with exact-value tests: a component whose props = `Omit<React.HTMLAttributes<HTMLDivElement>, 'title'> & {open?: boolean}`, `Pick<React.HTMLAttributes<...>, 'onClick' | 'id'>`, `ComponentProps<'div'>`, `PropsWithoutRef<...>`, and an interface from a dependency, each must list the handlers per mode. Part 2 POLICY: the user's rule is that React-declared props (children, ref, className, style, id, aria-*, all DOM event handlers like onClick/onFocus/onKeyDown/onMouseEnter, `capture`/`autoFocus`) are never silently omitted. Decide with numbers what `curated` should contain: ideally the curated mode lists every handler (`on*` event handlers), `aria-*`, `data-*` is open-ended so skip, `id`, `className`, `style`, `children`, `ref`, `autoFocus`, `tabIndex`, `role`, `title`, `hidden` etc. Measure the cost of making `full` the DEFAULT instead (time, peak RSS, JSON size with schema v2 interned prop sets, on all five corpora with --load-dependencies; the React attribute set is one shared interned prop set, so it should be cheap; earlier Chakra run showed HTML attrs were not a time cost) and propose/implement the better default: if `full` costs <5% time and <10% memory, make it the default with the addon's collapseInheritedProps keeping the Storybook UI tidy (check how collapse presents them: packages/storybook/src/arg-types.ts and the harness counts); otherwise widen `curated` to the list above. `ref`: include it (React 19: ref is an ordinary prop on function components; for forwardRef components it is `Ref<T>`) in every mode where the component's props accept it; `key` stays omitted (not a runtime prop); make REACT_SPECIAL_PROPS the single place, update ADR 0022 text / docs/type-checker-integration.md where it says ref is omitted, and the structural path too (not only the checker path) so both engines agree. Gates: exact-value tests; `just equivalence` showing only intended differences (NARROW allow-list entries only in your PR; bare `*` entries are rejected; main's list must stay empty); lazy parity; oracle (`just equivalence --oracle`) no regression (wrong ~0.0%); harness: 'props Storybook lists that we lack' on antd/shadcn/Spectrum before/after (target 0 on all, incl. ref); cache schema bump + golden test if SourceData changes (note PR #229 and #233 also bump to 25: pick the next free number against open PRs and say so); `just lint doc-check machete typos` and `cargo nextest run --workspace --exclude caliper-docgen-napi --locked` exit codes read directly (never pipe through tail); CI green. HOUSE RULES: changeset = one short, consumer-facing paragraph, friendly and scannable, starting with the OUTCOME in the user's terms then any action/cost (e.g. 'Event handlers like onClick and onFocus, and ref, now always appear in your props table. No action needed.'), no heading, no list marker, no bold lead-in, no internal names, one line per paragraph; commits: imperative subject, at most 1-2 sentences of why, no list of what changed; PR body succinct, no hard wrap, ending with https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED; commits end with Claude-S