{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","bridgeSessionId":"cse_01D7CJmXuD2ASqfBYm7Lk4WZ","lastSequenceNum":21749,"ownerAccountUuid":"138d593e-e185-4f72-89f2-82e1a501f134","ownerOrganizationUuid":"602db9b4-428d-49e6-a99c-64152cc62a79"}
{"parentUuid":"61f3e341-4a1b-446f-be2c-d6f82f8de8af","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRAJPqtYA9zz4m7BRFwH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The `react-props` fork is running. It's stacked on #232's branch, because that PR introduced the policy constant, and it has a cap of about 100 tool calls.\n\n**Part 1: find out why PurePanel lost its handlers.**\n- **Where it looks.** It extracts antd's `PurePanel` in curated, full and none modes and traces how its props reach `React.HTMLAttributes<HTMLDivElement>`. That means through `Omit`, `Pick`, `ComponentProps<'div'>`, an interface `extends` in a dependency, or an unresolved props type that leaves only the Drawer's own props.\n- **The three possible causes.** A curated list that's too small, a curated filter that runs before the `Omit`, or an unresolved type.\n- **A comparison to settle.** It compares against what the parity baseline (react-component-meta) actually lists. Storybook's own docgen filters node_modules props by default in many setups, so the fork checks whether the 32 props are a real loss or a baseline-definition gap. The report names the evidence before it changes anything.\n- **The fix.** A general fix with exact tests for the shapes `Omit<HTMLAttributes, 'title'> & {…}`, `Pick<HTMLAttributes, 'onClick' | 'id'>`, `ComponentProps<'div'>`, `PropsWithoutRef<…>` and an interface from a dependency.\n\n**Part 2: the policy.**\n- **What it covers.** `children`, `ref`, `className`, `style`, `id`, `aria-*`, every DOM event handler, `autoFocus` and `capture` are never silently omitted.\n- **`ref` and `key`.** `ref` is included (an ordinary prop on function components in React 19, `Ref<T>` for `forwardRef`). `key` stays omitted. `REACT_SPECIAL_PROPS` stays the single place for this, applied in the structural path too, so both engines agree.\n- **Measuring the default.** It measures making `full` the default (time, peak memory and JSON size on all five corpora). If it costs under 5% time and 10% memory, `full` becomes the default and the addon's collapse keeps the UI tidy. Otherwise `curated` is widened to every handler, `aria-*` and the common attributes.\n\n**Gates.** Exact tests, narrow allow-list entries only, the oracle at about 0.0% wrong, and a harness target of 0 missing props on antd, shadcn and Spectrum, including `ref`. If it bumps the cache schema it picks the next free number, since #229 and #233 both claim 25.\n\nRunning: `react-props` and `parity-triage`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6732,"cache_read_input_tokens":922783,"output_tokens":876,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6732,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":876,"cache_read_input_tokens":922783,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6732,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6732},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"85378a53-f7a7-4f6b-920b-e7f13e9bd163","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgRAJPGuh2cAYz8g13sKc","requestRef":"0bb36f0b-9a1c-4388-b9ef-683bdc1540fb","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"dd2454b8-0d79-410e-a86d-103a6c81b5c5","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:26:14.818Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"scratch/parity-al