{"parentUuid":"e2ee8c28-839a-4551-994b-894fb3fc1b0b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"34190470-98f4-4d3f-9ba9-3b3dcf447d1f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a77265bdad974924a</task-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/a77265bdad974924a.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Triage the Parity and oracle regressions on main\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Step 1 is done: `MenuTrigger` is detected again. The rest of the follow-up is blocked. The Parity workflow now reaches real verdicts but fails the Parity gate and the oracle gate, so I did not refresh the baselines or mark #234 ready.\n\n**1. MenuTrigger (pushed).** `68c62e1f` makes a call to a same-file function whose declared return type is a React element count as render evidence. It is judged by shape, not name.\n- It covers the `ReactElement`, `JSX.Element` and `ReactNode` types, aliases of them, and `const f = (): T =&gt;` arrows.\n- It does not count `Promise&lt;…&gt;` returns, untyped helpers, or element types imported from non-React modules.\n- `new Response(&lt;div/&gt;)`-style JSX stays non-evidence.\n- Five exact-value tests were added in `extractor/tests.rs`: helper returns an element, aliased return type, non-element helpers, element type imported from elsewhere, and the constructor case with a helper beside it.\n- `cargo nextest` for core passes (714 tests), and lint, doc-check, machete, typos and `just equivalence` all exit 0.\n- Equivalence shows no other lost or gained components on any corpus. The only differences are the 25 allowed Mantine `component` props. Base-ui is not one of those corpora, so I checked it directly: it extracts `MenuRoot` and `MenuTrigger`.\n- A changeset is included.\n\n**2. Merge and re-dispatch.** I merged the gates fork's `ci/repair-gates` commits (`195637e9`, `74cd0aeb`) into the branch as `85e3db67` and re-dispatched. The workflow no longer stops at the allow-list step or the base-path crash. It ran every measurement, so these are real verdicts (run 40356517818).\n\n**3. Baselines not refreshed.** The run fails two gates.\n- **Parity gate:**\n  - Chakra: \"utility type left as written\" grew from 1 to 1,127, and \"unreduced &amp; string\" from 0 to 40.\n  - Chakra, Mantine and shadcn: \"rest parameter lost\" and \"readonly lost\" grew.\n  - Mantine: \"member read left as X[\"k\"]\" grew from 6,542 to 6,614.\n  - Spectrum: components matched fell from 77.20% to 76.19%, and same text from 67.42% to 63.03%.\n  - shadcn: components matched fell from 95.29% to 95.23%.\n  - antd: \"typeof left in output\" grew from 7 to 8.\n\n  I only classified some of these earlier (Chakra utility types as a naive pattern, Spectrum's string-literal pattern, Mantine `component`). The rest are unclassified, so I can't refresh them as improvements or acceptable differences. A baseline refresh would also hide possible regressions.\n- **Oracle gate:** components matched fell for fixtures (82.50% to 80.00%, 32/40 against a baseline of 33/40), Mantine, antd and Spectrum.\n  - I reproduced the fixtures number locally with the fixed build, with `MenuTrigger` present, so one more fixture component is missing. I did not identify which one. The oracle output doesn't list the 40 checker components, so I couldn't name it without building the baseline binary.\n\n**Next steps.**\n- Name the second lost fixture component, probably by extracting the fixtures with the baseline-commit binary and diffing the component lists.\n- Bisect and classify the remaining Parity-gate movements, starting with the Spectrum component and prop drops and the Chakra/Mantine/shadcn rest-parameter and readonly growth. Fix real regressions.\n- Refresh both baselines in their own commit only for the improvement/acceptable rows.\n- Remove the Mantine allow-list entry after #234 merges. I'll note it in the PR body.\n\nPR: https://github.com/orin-dx/caliper/pull/234 (draft, base `ci/repair-gates`)\n\nneeds input: Say whether to keep triaging in this task. The remaining Parity and oracle regressions are unclassified, and doing them properly is a new bisect round past the original time-box.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>170380</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>182</tool_uses><duration_ms>4783315</duration_ms></usage>\n<worktree><worktreePath>/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-a77265bdad974924a</worktreePath><worktreeBranch>worktree-agent-a77265bdad974924a</worktreeBranch></worktree>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"833ef650-4ccf-4c92-a2d4-113caa083f86","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:39:22.495Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"task-notification","producer":"session-task","runId":"0mvphcb85-419ddaad"},"promptSource":"system","turnOrigin":"task_notification","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":201,"turnIndex":315},"queueSkipAttachments":true,"sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"fix/react-props-never-omitted","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
