d build, with `MenuTrigger` present, so one more fixture component is missing. I did not identify which one. The oracle output doesn't list the 40 checker components, so I couldn't name it without building the baseline binary.\n\n**Next steps.**\n- Name the second lost fixture component, probably by extracting the fixtures with the baseline-commit binary and diffing the component lists.\n- Bisect and classify the remaining Parity-gate movements, starting with the Spectrum component and prop drops and the Chakra/Mantine/shadcn rest-parameter and readonly growth. Fix real regressions.\n- Refresh both baselines in their own commit only for the improvement/acceptable rows.\n- Remove the Mantine allow-list entry after #234 merges. I'll note it in the PR body.\n\nPR: https://github.com/orin-dx/caliper/pull/234 (draft, base `ci/repair-gates`)\n\nneeds input: Say whether to keep triaging in this task. The remaining Parity and oracle regressions are unclassified, and doing them properly is a new bisect round past the original time-box.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>170380</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>182</tool_uses><duration_ms>4783315</duration_ms></usage>\n<worktree><worktreePath>/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-a77265bdad974924a</worktreePath><worktreeBranch>worktree-agent-a77265bdad974924a</worktreeBranch></worktree>\n</task-notification>\n</system-reminder>"}]}}
