peof left' 7 -> 8. Fix real regressions by shape with exact-value tests, narrow allow-list entries only in your PR. (4) Refresh scripts/parity-baseline.json and scripts/oracle-baseline.json in their own commit ONLY for rows classified improvement/acceptable/known-gap, with a per-row table in the PR body; leave rows that are real unfixed regressions failing and list them. (5) Mark #234 ready only if the Parity workflow passes on the final tip; otherwise say exactly which gate fails and why. House rules as before (consumer-facing friendly changeset only for shipped behavior; small commits; push before finishing).","summary":"Tell parity-triage to continue and classify remaining rows","type":"message","recipient":"parity-triage","recipient_kind":"name","content":"Yes: keep triaging in this task; extended time-bo…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2058,"cache_read_input_tokens":931018,"output_tokens":1646,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":581},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2058,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1646,"cache_read_input_tokens":931018,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2058,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2058},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01TcTtKquY5hxfeHiKaVZaaF":{"to":"parity-triage","message":"Yes: keep triaging in this task; extended time-box of ~100 more tool calls. Plan, in order: (1) The dispatched run's verdicts may predate your MenuTrigger fix (68c62e1f): first re-dispatch on the CURRENT branch tip and use only that run's numbers. Add a `corpora` input to the parity workflow_dispatch (e.g. 'chakra,spectrum') in your PR only if it saves you rounds (gates owns parity.yml on ci/repair-gates; merge it first; keep the edit small). (2) Name the second lost fixture component: build the baseline-commit binary (the commit where scripts/oracle-baseline.json was last updated: `git log -- scripts/oracle-baseline.json`) in a scratch dir, extract the fixtures with both builds (`--format rdt`/json, the same flags the oracle uses), diff component lists; bisect the introducing PR (#209 narrowed evidence is the prime suspect for Spectrum's component drops too: check the Spectrum 77.20 -> 76.19 'components matched' list against it with the fixed build; the MenuTrigger fix may already recover some). (3) Classify EVERY remaining Parity-gate movement with before/after examples: Chakra 'utility type left as written' 1 -> 1,127 and 'unreduced & string' 0 -> 40; 'rest parameter lost' (the loose `...` pattern also matches TypeScript's own '... N more ...' elision: tighten the pattern in scripts/parity.py to a strict `...name:` match with a test, as the type-loss fork found); 'readonly lost' (a known unimplemented follow-up of PR #233/ADR 0022: classify as known-gap, not a regression, unless it grew because of a change); Mantine 'member read left as X[k]' 6,542 -> 6,614 (find the 72 new props); Spectrum same text 67.42 -> 63.03; shadcn matched 95.29 -> 95.23; antd 'typeof left' 7 -> 8. Fix real regressions by shape with exact-value tests, narrow allow-list entries only in your PR. (4) Refresh scripts/parity-baseline.json and scripts/oracle-baseline.json in their own commit ONLY for rows classified improvement/acceptable/known-gap, with a per-row table in the PR body; leave rows that are real unfixed regressions failing and list them. (5) Mark #234 ready only if the Parity workflow passes on the final tip; otherwise say exactly which gate fails and why. House 