{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:52:17.598Z","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>ad5269bcad04ba5a7</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01SH7KQbUqfzqT6yvi76cbYo</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/ad5269bcad04ba5a7.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Why React handlers are lost, and include ref\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Task: stop React-declared props (handlers, `aria-*`, `ref`) from going missing. I fixed the main causes and opened PR #235, but several required gates have not run, so it isn't ready to merge.\n\n**Root cause**\n1. `--format rdt` and the addon's `docgenInfo` never emitted `notableInherited`. Default curated mode therefore dropped every curated attribute. The float-button `PurePanel` showed 25 props and no `onClick`, `onFocus` or `id`, while `full` showed 195.\n2. The curated table was small and hand-written. It lacked `onMouseEnter`, `autoFocus` and similar props, and had no `ref`.\n3. Some ways of reaching React's attributes never produced an element layer: `Omit&lt;HTMLAttributes&lt;…&gt;&gt;` in every mode, and `ComponentProps&lt;'div'&gt;`, `PropsWithoutRef&lt;…&gt;` and `Omit` in `full`. Before the fix, `Omit&lt;HTMLAttributes&lt;HTMLDivElement&gt;, 'title'&gt; &amp; {open}` listed only `open`, and `ComponentProps&lt;'div'&gt;` listed 0 props.\n4. Eight of nine antd `PurePanel`s don't extend HTML attributes at all, so I don't count those as omissions. The harness's 33 missing `PurePanel` props look like Drawer-level props paired to a different `PurePanel`. I couldn't confirm that, because the generated story file was already cleaned up.\n\n**Policy, with numbers**\n- Full as default costs +5% CPU on antd and +12–13% peak RSS on antd and Spectrum, so I widened curated instead.\n- Curated now keeps `ref`, `aria-*`, every handler except the `*Capture` twins, the global attributes and each element's notable ones. It reads these from React's own declarations. `key` stays omitted, and `REACT_SPECIAL_PROPS` is now `[\"key\"]`.\n- Widened curated costs more than the old curated: CPU +4% (Spectrum) to +26% (shadcn), RSS +6% to +30%. Canonical JSON is larger too, and on shadcn it is bigger than `full` (17.0 vs 12.2 MB).\n- `forwardRef` components list `ref` as `Ref&lt;unknown&gt;`. I didn't touch `SourceData`, so there is no cache schema bump.\n\n**Counts**\n- Harness \"before\" (props Storybook lists that we lack):\n\n  | Corpus | Before |\n  |---|---|\n  | antd | 37 |\n  | shadcn | 0 |\n  | Spectrum | 1 (`TreeView` `ref`) |\n\n  The antd 37 are the 33 `PurePanel` props, `ref` on Breadcrumb, CheckableTagGroup and Transfer, and `capture` on Dragger.\n- Fixture, handlers per mode:\n\n  | Props type | Curated | Full | None |\n  |---|---|---|---|\n  | `ComponentProps&lt;'div'&gt;` | 85 | 168 | 0 |\n  | `Omit&lt;HTMLAttributes, 'title'&gt; &amp; {open}` | 85 | 168 | 0 |\n  | interface from a dependency | 85 | 168 | 0 |\n  | `PropsWithoutRef&lt;…&gt;` | 85 | 168 | 0 |\n  | `Pick&lt;…, 'onClick' \\| 'id'&gt;` | `{id, onClick}` | 0 | 0 |\n\n  The first two now list `open`, `id`, `className`, `style`, `aria-label` and `onClick`; the `Omit` case drops `title`. `ref` appears for `ComponentProps&lt;'div'&gt;` and `forwardRef` only, never for plain `HTMLAttributes`, and `key` never appears.\n\n**Not done**\n- The harness \"after\" run, `just equivalence`, `--oracle`, lazy parity and CI. I didn't confirm that the antd `ref` and `capture` gaps are closed.\n- `Pick&lt;HTMLAttributes&lt;…&gt;&gt;` lists nothing in `full` and `none`. That was already the case. The exact-value test covers curated only.\n- `cargo nextest` run on the core crate with `--no-fail-fast` passed once I fixed the failures my change caused. I haven't re-run it after the last commits. Watch tests in the CLI crate fail under this sandbox, and I didn't check them against the base commit.\n- `just lint doc-check machete typos` exit 0. I added `Seeked` to `.typos.toml` because `onSeeked` is React's own name.\n- The eight snapshots grew by about 82k lines, which is expected since each HTML-based component now lists about 160 props. Please review.\n\n**Where it lives**\n- Branch `fix/react-props-never-omitted`, with base `feat/semantic-on-demand` (#232 was still open), and a new test file `crates/core/tests/react_declared_props.rs`.\n- Commits: `a6495e8f` (code, tests, snapshots) and `ce2b3a26` (docs and changeset).\n- PR: https://github.com/orin-dx/caliper/pull/235\n- Next command: `just equivalence` and `just equivalence --oracle`. To see the antd gaps, run `node packages/storybook/scripts/storybook-parity.mjs --corpora &lt;dir&gt; --only antd,shadcn,spectrum --limit 100`.\n\nneeds input: the CPU/RSS hit from widened curated (shadcn +26% CPU, +30% RSS) is bigger than the thresholds you set. Decide whether to accept it, or have me trim curated further (for example, handlers only for elements that take them).</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>218330</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>147</tool_uses><duration_ms>1571140</duration_ms></usage>\n<worktree><worktreePath>/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-ad5269bcad04ba5a7</worktreePath><worktreeBranch>worktree-agent-ad5269bcad04ba5a7</worktreeBranch></worktree>\n</task-notification>"}
