{"parentUuid":"fa9775cb-b460-4a69-843f-983a7d28b50e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRCJHjm5wd7FJTRxbSUC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3428,"cache_read_input_tokens":938158,"output_tokens":1933,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":681},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3428,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1933,"cache_read_input_tokens":938158,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3428,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3428},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":5351,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"93260f98-1cb7-481d-912d-7ce6823eba65","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgRCJGzNAk4667e1vvH7o","requestRef":"9ce87d8f-9f8e-45e9-a750-044e2270cbbd","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"14d71944-67fe-4728-8444-b3cf08f608d2","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:52:26.065Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"fix/react-props-never-omitted","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"14d71944-67fe-4728-8444-b3cf08f608d2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRCJHjm5wd7FJTRxbSUC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"PR #235 is open, but it isn't ready to merge, and it needs one decision from you. The investigation found a real bug.\n\n**Root cause: the Storybook path never emitted the curated attributes.**\n1. **`--format rdt` and the addon's `docgenInfo` never emitted `notableInherited`.** So default curated mode dropped every curated attribute for Storybook. The float-button `PurePanel` showed 25 props and no `onClick`, `onFocus` or `id`, while `full` showed 195.\n2. **The curated table was small and hand-written.** It lacked `onMouseEnter`, `autoFocus` and `ref`.\n3. **Some ways of reaching React's attributes produced no element layer at all.** `Omit<HTMLAttributes<…>>` in every mode, and `ComponentProps<'div'>` and `PropsWithoutRef<…>` in `full`. Before the fix, `Omit<HTMLAttributes<HTMLDivElement>, 'title'> & {open}` listed only `open`, and `ComponentProps<'div'>` listed 0 props.\n4. **Eight of nine antd `PurePanel`s don't extend HTML attributes at all.** The harness's 33 missing `PurePanel` props look like Drawer props paired to a different `PurePanel`, but the fork couldn't confirm that because the generated story file was already cleaned up.\n\n**What changed.** Curated now keeps `ref`, `aria-*`, every handler except the `*Capture` twins, the global attributes and each element's notable ones, read from React's own declarations. `key` stays omitted. `forwardRef` components list `ref` as `Ref<unknown>`. There is no cache schema bump.\n\n**The decision.** I asked for a default that costs under 5% time and 10% memory. Neither option meets it, so you choose:\n\n| | CPU | Peak memory | JSON size |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Widened curated (what the fork built) | +4% (Spectrum) to +26% (shadcn) | +6% to +30% | shadcn 17.0 MB |\n| `full` as default | +5% on antd | +12–13% on antd and Spectrum | shadcn 12.2 MB |\n\nOn shadcn, widened curated is bigger than `full` and costs more CPU, because `full` shares one interned React attribute set across components and curated writes its list per component. So `full` is cheaper than what the fork built on some measures, and it is the mode that matches your rule of never omitting. **My recommendation is to make `full` the default**, keep `curated` as a compact option, and accept the memory cost. Say yes and I'll send the fork back to flip it. If you'd prefer to keep curated as the default, the fork offers to trim it further (for example, handlers only for elements that take them).\n\n**Why it isn't mergeable yet**\n- **Gates not run:** the harness \"after\" run (so the antd `ref` and `capture` gaps are unconfirmed), `just equivalence`, the oracle, lazy parity, and CI.\n- The core test run passed once, but wasn't re-run after the last commits. The CLI watch tests fail under this sandbox, and the fork didn't check them against the base commit.\n- **Snapshots grew by about 82,000 lines across eight files**, because each HTML-based component now lists about 160 props. That needs your review. If `full` becomes the default through the shared interned set, the snapshot growth may shrink.\n- `Pick<HTMLAttributes<…>>` lists nothing in `full` and `none`; that was already so, and the exact-value test only covers curated.\n\nThe PR is stacked on #232 (`fix/react-props-never-omitted`), so merge #232 first.\n\nRunning: `parity-triage`. Which way do you want to go on the default?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3428,"cache_read_input_tokens":938158,"output_tokens":1933,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":681},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3428,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1933,"cache_read_input_tokens":938158,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3428,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3428},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"93260f98-1cb7-481d-912d-7ce6823eba65","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgRCJGzNAk4667e1vvH7o","requestRef":"9ce87d8f-9f8e-45e9-a750-044e2270cbbd","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"3b2a5c4f-52e6-44b6-a64d-98b43d29ca47","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:52:33.337Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"fix/react-props-never-omitted","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
