{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","hash":"cc1e1342734b174c16c77b7ee36b95716202e2d34f144970571ff81505a2a57c","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Decision made: `full` becomes the default. I'm sending that to the `react-props` fork, then finishing the tap step."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Sezu69uFvBupA79irpkypv","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"react-props","message":"Decision from the user: make `full` the DEFAULT htmlAttributes ('it's faster and has a smaller JSON'). Accepted costs: +12-13% peak RSS on antd/Spectrum. Do: (1) flip the default to full everywhere it is defined: PipelineOptions default, CLI (`--html-attributes` default, help text), docgen.config.ts schema + docs, NAPI JsExtractOptions docs/typings, Vite plugin and Storybook addon options/docs/README (the addon's `skipHtmlProps` still means none), scripts that rely on the default (parity.py, equivalence.py, scorecard.py: keep their meaning by passing explicit modes where baselines were recorded with curated; update `default` config semantics notes), docs/STATUS, ADR (new ADR at the next free number after checking open PRs #232/#233/#229 for numbers they claimed; supersede the 'curated by default' decision, cite your measured numbers); keep `curated` as an opt-in compact mode but you do NOT need to keep investing in widening it beyond what already works (keep your fixes that make curated correct: notableInherited emitted in rdt/docgenInfo, ref/aria/handlers). (2) Re-measure with full as the default vs the old default on all five corpora with --load-dependencies: wall time, peak RSS, canonical JSON size, and the Storybook harness 'props Storybook lists that we lack' (target 0 on antd/shadcn/Spectrum incl. ref and the PurePanel question: confirm or refute the Drawer/PurePanel pairing now that the harness story file is regenerated) plus first/median story. (3) Run the gates you skipped: `just equivalence` (NARROW allow-list entries only in this PR; the intended differences are the HTML-attribute layers on html-based components), `just equivalence --oracle` (wrong ~0.0%), lazy parity, `cargo nextest run --workspace --exclude caliper-docgen-napi --locked` and `just lint doc-check machete typos` exit codes read directly, the vite-plugin/addon/napi pnpm tests, and CI green. Regenerate the corpus snapshots and report the size of the snapshot diff after the flip (the interned full set should be smaller than the widened curated one). (4) Changeset: consumer-facing, friendly, outcome first, e.g. 'Event handlers such as onClick and onFocus, and ref, now always appear in your props table; use htmlAttributes: curated to keep the old compact list. No action needed.' no list marker, no bold lead-in. House rules as before; small commits; push before finishing.","summary":"Tell react-props to make full the default"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
