{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:14:14.363Z","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a77265bdad974924a</task-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/a77265bdad974924a.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Triage the Parity and oracle regressions on main\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>PR #234 is ready for review. The Parity workflow dispatched on the final tip (run 40363458050) concluded success, and all 17 PR checks pass. The base is still `ci/repair-gates`, since #224 is open.\n\n**Commits on `ci/triage-parity-regressions`, all pushed:**\n\n| Hash | What |\n|---|---|\n| `34259693` | Mantine `component` prop prints `ElementType`, not `C \\| ElementType` |\n| `455c51fd` | Parity pattern: string-literal unions are no longer scored as unbound type parameters |\n| `ba524a5e` | One narrow allow-list entry, `mantine/* prop-type-changed *.component`, plus a changeset |\n| `68c62e1f` | `MenuTrigger` fix: a call to a same-file function declared to return an element counts as render evidence, with tests (changeset included) |\n| `85e3db67` | Merge of `ci/repair-gates` (the gates fork's workflow fixes) |\n| `905cce0f` | Parity pattern: \"rest parameter lost\" now needs a dropped `...name:` (the old loose `...` matched TypeScript's `... 40 more ...` elision), with a test |\n| `ff062c44` | Refreshed `scripts/parity-baseline.json` and `scripts/oracle-baseline.json` from a release build of this tip |\n\n**Classification of every flagged row.** The PR body has the full before/after table. In short, nothing is left as an unfixed regression:\n- **Real regressions, fixed:** the Mantine `component` text and `MenuTrigger`.\n- **Stale baseline (no code change):** Spectrum parity, the oracle fixtures drop (a build of the baseline commit gives the same 32/40 on today's fixtures), and the oracle Mantine/antd/Spectrum matched rates.\n- **Acceptable or improvement:**\n  - shadcn lost `GET` (a route handler returning `new ImageResponse(&lt;div/&gt;)`, which RDT wrongly lists as a component).\n  - Mantine member-read growth: `ClassNames&lt;XFactory&gt;` and `Styles&lt;XFactory&gt;` now expand, leaving a `Factory[\"props\"]` residue.\n  - Chakra utility types: 1,112 props moved from unresolved `UtilityValues[\"background\"]` reads to resolved by-name types. Member-read losses in the same Chakra run fell from 378,118 to 148,646.\n- **Known gaps, not caused by this range:**\n  - Chakra \"unreduced &amp; string\" (40 props; the baseline commit's build already reports 40).\n  - \"readonly lost\" growth (more props are now reported; ADR 0022 follow-up).\n\n**Still to do:**\n- When #224 merges, retarget #234 to main.\n- After #234 merges, remove the `mantine/* prop-type-changed *.component` entry from `scripts/equivalence-allow.json` (the PR body says so).\n- Follow-up: reduce `NonNullable&lt;union&gt;` in Chakra's output.\n\nPR: https://github.com/orin-dx/caliper/pull/234\n\nresult: PR #234 is ready for review. It fixes the Mantine `component` text and the `MenuTrigger` regression, tightens two parity patterns, classifies every flagged row, and refreshes both baselines; Parity run 40363458050 passed and all 17 PR checks are green.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>236190</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>242</tool_uses><duration_ms>6874779</duration_ms></usage>\n<worktree><worktreePath>/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-a77265bdad974924a</worktreePath><worktreeBranch>worktree-agent-a77265bdad974924a</worktreeBranch></worktree>\n</task-notification>"}
