{"parentUuid":null,"logicalParentUuid":"2e1702ee-f5cc-4f2b-9ac2-b87d7b15d000","isSidechain":false,"type":"system","subtype":"compact_boundary","content":"Conversation compacted","level":"info","compactMetadata":{"trigger":"auto","preTokens":967453,"postTokens":32606,"cumulativeDroppedTokens":6301534,"durationMs":64354,"preCompactDiscoveredTools":["ExitWorktree","SendMessage","TaskCreate","TaskList","TaskStop","TaskUpdate","WebFetch","WebSearch"],"preservedSegment":{"headUuid":"6ca58afa-8f3d-46cd-81c0-4ecae285686f","anchorUuid":"44008b67-0943-49d9-a0da-8a306139db68","tailUuid":"2e1702ee-f5cc-4f2b-9ac2-b87d7b15d000"},"preservedMessages":{"anchorUuid":"44008b67-0943-49d9-a0da-8a306139db68","uuids":["6ca58afa-8f3d-46cd-81c0-4ecae285686f","0777b914-c119-4a42-be05-d67bd5d499d9","bf9341fa-4248-4c58-898b-78dc3f2bccf7","39b70ed3-1835-40bc-97be-921737cfc544","2460389e-5e16-4529-9658-ce92d65c67d6","01e051a9-50c7-477b-80b0-8ef986984231","2e1702ee-f5cc-4f2b-9ac2-b87d7b15d000"],"allUuids":["6ca58afa-8f3d-46cd-81c0-4ecae285686f","0777b914-c119-4a42-be05-d67bd5d499d9","bf9341fa-4248-4c58-898b-78dc3f2bccf7","730c1237-cb70-40e3-9ccf-aff33eb609be","39b70ed3-1835-40bc-97be-921737cfc544","2460389e-5e16-4529-9658-ce92d65c67d6","01e051a9-50c7-477b-80b0-8ef986984231","2e1702ee-f5cc-4f2b-9ac2-b87d7b15d000"]}},"uuid":"5d39e1a4-3daf-4790-9576-51ea37f4a217","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:15:16.221Z","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"ci/notify-homebrew-tap","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"5d39e1a4-3daf-4790-9576-51ea37f4a217","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"instructions","files":[{"path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/CLAUDE.md","type":"User","content":"@RTK.md"},{"path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/RTK.md","type":"User","content":"# RTK - Rust Token Killer\n\n**Usage**: Token-optimized CLI proxy (60-90% savings on dev operations)\n\n## Meta Commands (always use rtk directly)\n\n```bash\nrtk gain              # Show token savings analytics\nrtk gain --history    # Show command usage history with savings\nrtk discover          # Analyze Claude Code history for missed opportunities\nrtk proxy <cmd>       # Execute raw command without filtering (for debugging)\n```\n\n## Installation Verification\n\n```bash\nrtk --version         # Should show: rtk X.Y.Z\nrtk gain              # Should work (not \"command not found\")\nwhich rtk             # Verify correct binary\n```\n\n⚠️ **Name collision**: If `rtk gain` fails, you may have reachingforthejack/rtk (Rust Type Kit) installed instead.\n\n## Hook-Based Usage\n\nAll other commands are automatically rewritten by the Claude Code hook.\nExample: `git status` → `rtk git status` (transparent, 0 tokens overhead)\n\nRefer to CLAUDE.md for full command reference."},{"path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/AGENTS.md","type":"Project","content":"# caliper-docgen\n\n10-100x faster than react-docgen-typescript. OXC parses TypeScript/TSX; we extract React component props and emit RDT-compatible JSON via `--format rdt`. See `docs/STATUS.md` for current state and known gaps.\n\n## Commands\n\n```bash\ncargo test -p caliper-docgen-core          # unit + snapshot tests\ncargo clippy -p caliper-docgen-core -- -D warnings\ncargo build --release                         # full build including CLI\n```\n\nOr use `/check` and `/snapshot` for the common workflows.\n\n## Non-negotiables\n\n1. No `unwrap()` outside `#[cfg(test)]` — use `?`\n2. `FxHashMap` for internal maps; `BTreeMap` for JSON-output maps\n3. `CompactString` for type/prop names in hot paths\n4. No AST refs escape `parse_file()` — allocator is local per call\n5. No terminal/display code in `crates/core`\n6. Always emit `Diagnostic` when degrading — never fail silently\n\n## Architecture\n\n```\nOXC parse → SourceData (extractor/) → GlobalSourceData (pipeline/) → ComponentEntry (resolver/) → ExtractionOutput\n```\n\nNo reverse dependencies. `pub(crate)` for implementation modules; `pub` only for consumer-facing API (`pipeline/`, `types/`, `react_types`).\n\nSee `ARCHITECTURE.md` for the full pipeline/crate-graph overview, and `docs/architecture/` for per-subsystem invariants and known gaps (pipeline orchestration, extractor, resolver, types, serialization, CLI, NAPI binding) — start at `docs/architecture/README.md`.\n\n## Decisions\n\nRead `docs/adr/README.md` before changing the parser choice, `PropType` serialization, the DTS cache format, panic containment or the semantic backend. Reversing an ADR needs a new ADR.\n\n## Testing discipline\n\nTwo habits that repeatedly caught real bugs during the 2026-08-12 spec-validation pass (a stale-by-one-edit watch mode, always-zero watch stats — both had zero test coverage despite extensive existing suites):\n\n1. **Sibling-path parity.** When a function parallels an already-tested one (e.g. `WatchSession::update_file` mirrors `extract()`'s resolve/panic-containment logic; `create_session`'s guard boundary mirrors `initialize_session`/`extract_file_incremental`'s), the new path needs a test asserting the _same_ contract, not just \"it runs without error.\" A sibling path is exactly where coverage silently lapses.\n2. **Assert content, not presence.** Prefer `assert_eq!` against an exact expected value over `contains(...)`/`is_some()`/liveness checks wherever the cost is comparable. A test asserting \"component X exists\" survives X's props resolving to stale or wrong data; a test asserting X's exact prop set does not.\n\n## Crate guide\n\n- `crates/core` — pure extraction logic; @crates/core/AGENTS.md\n- `crates/cli` — clap CLI, no logic; @crates/cli/AGENTS.md\n- `crates/binding` — thin NAPI wrapper, delegates to core\n\n## Writing and commits\n\n- Succinct: short sentences, bullets, tables. No backstory, hedging or filler. Banned words are in `docs/adr/README.md`.\n- Never hard-wrap Markdown, commit messages or PR descriptions: one line per paragraph.\n- Comments: only the non-obvious why, no history (the commit records it). Fill to 120 columns (`.rustfmt.toml`). Rewriting a comment block counts as writing it: re-fill and cut it, don't inherit the old wrapping.\n- Commits: imperative subject, at most one or two sentences of why, no list of what changed, no \"This commit...\". Skip the body when the subject says it all."},{"path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/crates/core/AGENTS.md","type":"Project","content":"# crates/core\n\nPure extraction logic — no terminal, no NAPI, no async. Everything here must be `Send + Sync` for rayon.\n\n## Module layout\n\n```\ntypes/          — shared data types (the contract between phases)\nextractor/      — OXC AST visitor → SourceData\nresolver/       — SourceData + GlobalSourceData → ComponentEntry\npipeline/       — orchestration: discover → parse → merge → resolve\ncache.rs        — DTS parse cache (mtime+size invalidation, msgpack)\nimport_map.rs   — import resolution map\nknown.rs        — library-specific type shortcuts (SxProps, VariantProps…)\nreact_types.rs  — React builtin recognition + notable HTML attrs\n```\n\n## Types discipline\n\nWhen adding a public type, run through the checklist in the `rust-types` skill. Canonical reference: `src/types/diagnostic.rs`.\n\n## Resolver\n\n`resolve_component()` is called in parallel via rayon. All inputs must be owned or `Arc`-wrapped — no borrowed data crosses thread boundaries. `ResolveState` accumulates diagnostics and visited-type tracking for a single resolution call; it is not shared.\n\n## Panic containment\n\nAnything reachable from a rayon `.map()` or a `DocgenPlugin` impl must go through `panic_guard::contain_panic` — see `pipeline/mod.rs` and `plugin.rs` for the call sites, and `docs/adr/0005-panic-containment-boundary.md` for why.\n\n## Snapshot tests\n\nSeven fixtures in `crates/core/tests/snapshots/`. If a change affects output, regenerate with `/snapshot` before committing."},{"path":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/crates/cli/AGENTS.md","type":"Project","content":"# crates/cli\n\nThin command layer — no extraction logic. Each command parses args and delegates to `caliper-docgen-core::pipeline`.\n\n## Layout\n\n```\nmain.rs              — Cli struct, Command enum, *Args structs, main(), init_tracing()\ncommands/            — one file per subcommand (extract, watch, inspect, check, completions)\nconfig.rs            — docgen.config.ts loading, maps to PipelineOptions\noutput.rs            — comfy-table formatting helpers\n```\n\n## Rules\n\nCommand payloads go to stdout with `println!`; diagnostics, progress and everything on stderr go through `output.rs` or the tracing subscriber — never `eprintln!`. Error display uses `miette`. Progress uses `indicatif`.\n\nConfig loading (`config.rs`) runs the user's `docgen.config.ts` via node+tsx. The config file path is passed via env var, not embedded in a shell string — command injection risk otherwise."},{"path":"/Users/gabe/.claude/projects/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper/memory/MEMORY.md","type":"AutoMem","content":"- [Stacked PR retargeting](stacked-pr-retargeting.md) — retarget children to main when a parent merges, or GitHub closes them\n- [Sandbox, git and gh](sandbox-git-and-gh.md) — gh and git commits need the sandbox off; one plain git command per call\n- [Storybook is the goal](storybook-is-the-goal.md) — Storybook integration is the product's purpose; roadmap's \"out of scope\" is stale\n- [TS 7.1 backend is experimental opt-in](ts71-backend-experimental-opt-in.md) — off by default; `auto` later needs oracle evidence and a new ADR\n- [Measure memory and time](measure-memory-and-time.md) — check Chakra+deps peak RSS, not only wall time, for resolver changes"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"5fc200fc-8661-4945-8af4-1b5619428062","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:15:16.220Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCodebase and user instructions are shown below. Be sure to adhere to these instructions. IMPORTANT: These instructions OVERRIDE any default behavior and you MUST follow them exactly as written.\n\nContents of /Users/gabe/.claude/CLAUDE.md (user's private global instructions for all projects):\n\n@RTK.md\n\nContents of /Users/gabe/.claude/RTK.md (user's private global instructions for all projects):\n\n# RTK - Rust Token Killer\n\n**Usage**: Token-optimized CLI proxy (60-90% savings on dev operations)\n\n## Meta Commands (always use rtk directly)\n\n```bash\nrtk gain              # Show token savings analytics\nrtk gain --history    # Show command usage history with savings\nrtk discover          # Analyze Claude Code history for missed opportunities\nrtk proxy <cmd>       # Execute raw command without filtering (for debugging)\n```\n\n## Installation Verification\n\n```bash\nrtk --version         # Should show: rtk X.Y.Z\nrtk gain              # Should work (not \"command not found\")\nwhich rtk             # Verify correct binary\n```\n\n⚠️ **Name collision**: If `rtk gain` fails, you may have reachingforthejack/rtk (Rust Type Kit) installed instead.\n\n## Hook-Based Usage\n\nAll other commands are automatically rewritten by the Claude Code hook.\nExample: `git status` → `rtk git status` (transparent, 0 tokens overhead)\n\nRefer to CLAUDE.md for full command reference.\n\nContents of /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/AGENTS.md (project instructions, checked into the codebase):\n\n# caliper-docgen\n\n10-100x faster than react-docgen-typescript. OXC parses TypeScript/TSX; we extract React component props and emit RDT-compatible JSON via `--format rdt`. See `docs/STATUS.md` for current state and known gaps.\n\n## Commands\n\n```bash\ncargo test -p caliper-docgen-core          # unit + snapshot tests\ncargo clippy -p caliper-docgen-core -- -D warnings\ncargo build --release                         # full build including CLI\n```\n\nOr use `/check` and `/snapshot` for the common workflows.\n\n## Non-negotiables\n\n1. No `unwrap()` outside `#[cfg(test)]` — use `?`\n2. `FxHashMap` for internal maps; `BTreeMap` for JSON-output maps\n3. `CompactString` for type/prop names in hot paths\n4. No AST refs escape `parse_file()` — allocator is local per call\n5. No terminal/display code in `crates/core`\n6. Always emit `Diagnostic` when degrading — never fail silently\n\n## Architecture\n\n```\nOXC parse → SourceData (extractor/) → GlobalSourceData (pipeline/) → ComponentEntry (resolver/) → ExtractionOutput\n```\n\nNo reverse dependencies. `pub(crate)` for implementation modules; `pub` only for consumer-facing API (`pipeline/`, `types/`, `react_types`).\n\nSee `ARCHITECTURE.md` for the full pipeline/crate-graph overview, and `docs/architecture/` for per-subsystem invariants and known gaps (pipeline orchestration, extractor, resolver, types, serialization, CLI, NAPI binding) — start at `docs/architecture/README.md`.\n\n## Decisions\n\nRead `docs/adr/README.md` before changing the parser choice, `PropType` serialization, the DTS cache format, panic containment or the semantic backend. Reversing an ADR needs a new ADR.\n\n## Testing discipline\n\nTwo habits that repeatedly caught real bugs during the 2026-08-12 spec-validation pass (a stale-by-one-edit watch mode, always-zero watch stats — both had zero test coverage despite extensive existing suites):\n\n1. **Sibling-path parity.** When a function parallels an already-tested one (e.g. `WatchSession::update_file` mirrors `extract()`'s resolve/panic-containment logic; `create_session`'s guard boundary mirrors `initialize_session`/`extract_file_incremental`'s), the new path needs a test asserting the _same_ contract, not just \"it runs without error.\" A sibling path is exactly where coverage silently lapses.\n2. **Assert content, not presence.** Prefer `assert_eq!` against an exact expected value over `contains(...)`/`is_some()`/liveness checks wherever the cost is comparable. A test asserting \"component X exists\" survives X's props resolving to stale or wrong data; a test asserting X's exact prop set does not.\n\n## Crate guide\n\n- `crates/core` — pure extraction logic; @crates/core/AGENTS.md\n- `crates/cli` — clap CLI, no logic; @crates/cli/AGENTS.md\n- `crates/binding` — thin NAPI wrapper, delegates to core\n\n## Writing and commits\n\n- Succinct: short sentences, bullets, tables. No backstory, hedging or filler. Banned words are in `docs/adr/README.md`.\n- Never hard-wrap Markdown, commit messages or PR descriptions: one line per paragraph.\n- Comments: only the non-obvious why, no history (the commit records it). Fill to 120 columns (`.rustfmt.toml`). Rewriting a comment block counts as writing it: re-fill and cut it, don't inherit the old wrapping.\n- Commits: imperative subject, at most one or two sentences of why, no list of what changed, no \"This commit...\". Skip the body when the subject says it all.\n\nContents of /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/crates/core/AGENTS.md (project instructions, checked into the codebase):\n\n# crates/core\n\nPure extraction logic — no terminal, no NAPI, no async. Everything here must be `Send + Sync` for rayon.\n\n## Module layout\n\n```\ntypes/          — shared data types (the contract between phases)\nextractor/      — OXC AST visitor → SourceData\nresolver/       — SourceData + GlobalSourceData → ComponentEntry\npipeline/       — orchestration: discover → parse → merge → resolve\ncache.rs        — DTS parse cache (mtime+size invalidation, msgpack)\nimport_map.rs   — import resolution map\nknown.rs        — library-specific type shortcuts (SxProps, VariantProps…)\nreact_types.rs  — React builtin recognition + notable HTML attrs\n```\n\n## Types discipline\n\nWhen adding a public type, run through the checklist in the `rust-types` skill. Canonical reference: `src/types/diagnostic.rs`.\n\n## Resolver\n\n`resolve_component()` is called in parallel via rayon. All inputs must be owned or `Arc`-wrapped — no borrowed data crosses thread boundaries. `ResolveState` accumulates diagnostics and visited-type tracking for a single resolution call; it is not shared.\n\n## Panic containment\n\nAnything reachable from a rayon `.map()` or a `DocgenPlugin` impl must go through `panic_guard::contain_panic` — see `pipeline/mod.rs` and `plugin.rs` for the call sites, and `docs/adr/0005-panic-containment-boundary.md` for why.\n\n## Snapshot tests\n\nSeven fixtures in `crates/core/tests/snapshots/`. If a change affects output, regenerate with `/snapshot` before committing.\n\nContents of /Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/crates/cli/AGENTS.md (project instructions, checked into the codebase):\n\n# crates/cli\n\nThin command layer — no extraction logic. Each command parses args and delegates to `caliper-docgen-core::pipeline`.\n\n## Layout\n\n```\nmain.rs              — Cli struct, Command enum, *Args structs, main(), init_tracing()\ncommands/            — one file per subcommand (extract, watch, inspect, check, completions)\nconfig.rs            — docgen.config.ts loading, maps to PipelineOptions\noutput.rs            — comfy-table formatting helpers\n```\n\n## Rules\n\nCommand payloads go to stdout with `println!`; diagnostics, progress and everything on stderr go through `output.rs` or the tracing subscriber — never `eprintln!`. Error display uses `miette`. Progress uses `indicatif`.\n\nConfig loading (`config.rs`) runs the user's `docgen.config.ts` via node+tsx. The config file path is passed via env var, not embedded in a shell string — command injection risk otherwise.\n\nContents of /Users/gabe/.claude/projects/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper/memory/MEMORY.md (user's auto-memory, persists across conversations):\n\n- [Stacked PR retargeting](stacked-pr-retargeting.md) — retarget children to main when a parent merges, or GitHub closes them\n- [Sandbox, git and gh](sandbox-git-and-gh.md) — gh and git commits need the sandbox off; one plain git command per call\n- [Storybook is the goal](storybook-is-the-goal.md) — Storybook integration is the product's purpose; roadmap's \"out of scope\" is stale\n- [TS 7.1 backend is experimental opt-in](ts71-backend-experimental-opt-in.md) — off by default; `auto` later needs oracle evidence and a new ADR\n- [Measure memory and time](measure-memory-and-time.md) — check Chakra+deps peak RSS, not only wall time, for resolver changes\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"user","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"ci/notify-homebrew-tap","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
