{"parentUuid":"1a4e427b-a9b9-4563-91ab-dce89301382c","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_012uCFvfgyYGBugsPBiiyu9e","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"PreToolUse\",\"permissionDecisionReason\":\"RTK auto-rewrite\",\"updatedInput\":{\"command\":\"rtk gh pr create --base main --head ci/notify-homebrew-tap --title \\\"ci: notify the Homebrew tap after a CLI release\\\" --body \\\"A CLI release now tells \\\\`orin-dx/homebrew-tap\\\\` right away, so \\\\`brew upgrade\\\\` follows npm without waiting for the tap's daily check.\\n\\n- After the release step, the workflow finds the \\\\`npm/caliper-docgen@*\\\\` tag on the release commit and calls \\\\`orin-dx/actions/notify-homebrew-tap\\\\` (pinned to a SHA).\\n- No CLI tag in the run means no notification.\\n- The step is \\\\`continue-on-error\\\\`: the tap's daily cron is the backstop, so a failed notification never fails a release.\\n- The tap verifies the npm platform archives and opens a formula PR; a maintainer approves it.\\n\\nNeeds \\\\`vars.TAP_APP_CLIENT_ID\\\\` and \\\\`secrets.TAP_APP_PRIVATE_KEY\\\\` (set) and the notify action from orin-dx/actions#2 (merged).\\n\\nCI-only, no changeset. \\\\`actionlint\\\\` passes. The first real test is the next CLI release.\\n\\nhttps://claude.ai/code/REDACTED\\\"\",\"description\":\"Open the tap notifier PR\",\"dangerouslyDisableSandbox\":true}}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"rtk hook claude","durationMs":21},"type":"attachment","uuid":"c965beb0-6208-44f7-abdf-48df40e5bbdd","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:15:37.243Z","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"ci/notify-homebrew-tap","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
