{"parentUuid":"0f081b77-3fe3-4e09-812d-4c272c6b5e7a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRE8KjmqfYu5vyU7b7ra","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"PR #236 (Homebrew tap notifier) is open against `main`, and all 16 of its checks pass. Of the 14 open PRs, 12 are fully green. #235 and #229 each fail only Equivalence, and I haven't changed either. For #229 I only saw the summary lines, not the diffs.\n\n- **#235 (React props, `full` default):** the failure is the intended change. Chakra gains about 166k `prop-added` rows and shadcn gets handler and `aria-*` changes. It needs a reviewer's call, not a code fix. Per the repo's rule, allow-list entries for it would have to go away once it lands.\n- **#229 (tagged-factory components):** Chakra shows 592 `diagnostic-added` and 605 `diagnostic-removed`, and component count goes from 618 to 629. It looks like the 11 newly found components changing which components each existing diagnostic lists as affected. That would be harmless, but I haven't confirmed it, and it still needs a narrow allow-list entry or a diff-normalizing fix.\n- **#234 (parity triage):** now ready, with all 17 checks green and Parity passing. It targets `ci/repair-gates`, so retarget it to `main` once #224 merges.\n- **Merge order (bottom-up):**\n  1. #224\n  2. #234\n  3. #225–#228, #230, #231, #226\n  4. #232\n  5. #235\n  6. #233\n  7. #229\n  8. #236 anytime\n  9. #217 last (release PR)\n- **Collisions to fix when their turn comes:**\n  - ADR 0022 is claimed by both #232 and #233.\n  - Cache schema 25 is claimed by both #229 and #233.\n  - Allow-list entries in #229, #230, #233 and #234 must be dropped after merge, because #224 enforces an empty list on `main`.\n- **Remote cleanup (I can't delete remote branches):** `git push origin --delete scratch/parity-allow-probe`, plus the earlier list.\n\nI can start a fork to handle #229's Equivalence failure and the ADR and schema renumbering now. Say if you want that.\n\nresult: Homebrew tap notifier PR #236 is open and green. A merge order and the collisions to fix are listed above. Equivalence still fails on #235, which is the intended output change and needs your call, and on #229, which needs an allow-list entry or a fix."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":741,"cache_read_input_tokens":101770,"output_tokens":1050,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":258},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":741,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1050,"cache_read_input_tokens":101770,"cache_creation_input_tokens":741,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":741},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"faa7989c-cf6b-4e39-801e-bef7209a75d6","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgRE8KSuu1RD2Lewf4TjE","requestRef":"2a5f7a16-de49-4504-9a35-6e4ba1395dcc","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"44c683f3-14bc-488a-9c2b-44893895c779","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:16:25.712Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"ci/notify-homebrew-tap","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
