{"parentUuid":"29e79498-4b3d-4905-87f9-7eb168c81d32","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgREB7W9WDjabd4cBbERL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Mostly yes. The base branches look right, but I only checked commit counts, not whether each PR's commits are its own.\n\n- **Stacked correctly:**\n  - #235 is based on `feat/semantic-on-demand` (#232) and adds 2 commits of its own.\n  - #234 is based on `ci/repair-gates` (#224) and adds 7 commits, one of which is a merge of that branch.\n- **Based on `main`, small and independent:** #225–#231, #226 and #236, with 1–4 commits each. The ones I counted (#229, #230, #233) have 3, 1 and 4.\n- **Larger:** #232 has 11 commits, which is plausible for the TS on-demand feature.\n\nI haven't confirmed that no `main`-based PR carries an unmerged parent's commits. Two PRs could, and I suspect #233 depends on #232: both claim ADR 0022 and cache schema 25. If #233 does depend on #232, it should be stacked on `feat/semantic-on-demand` instead of `main`. I can check #233's diff against #232 and retarget it if needed. Say if you want that."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":790,"cache_read_input_tokens":106009,"output_tokens":369,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":790,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":369,"cache_read_input_tokens":106009,"cache_creation_input_tokens":790,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":790},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"b26b2abe-56f7-4db4-8cd8-96060a34e42d","