{"parentUuid":"3575210a-f9bc-4568-bde4-133b1b68941b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgREUZ716xkxxdtouyc24","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KioV2trebTccwzUF9TQYMd","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Reconcile open PRs after merges","subagent_type":"fork","name":"reconcile-open-prs","prompt":"Main now has #217, #224–#227 merged (allow-list is enforced empty on main). Fix the open PRs, sequentially, each in its own worktree (git worktree add under .claude/worktrees; use python/subprocess only for read-only inspection of others). For each PR in this order: #228 (CONFLICTING), #234 (now base main), #230, #231, #229, #232, #233, #235, #236: (1) `git merge origin/main` (or its parent branch for stacked ones) — never force-push, never rebase-push; (2) resolve conflicts keeping both sides' intent; (3) run `just lint`/relevant cargo tests reading exit codes directly; (4) drop that PR's entries from scripts/equivalence-allow.json that #224's check rejects, or replace with the narrowest justified entry only if the diff is a genuine intended change (explain in PR body) — no blanket wildcards; (5) push and wait for CI, fix failures. Stacking decisions: if a PR depends on an unmerged one (check by diffing: #233 vs #232 for ADR 0022 / cache schema 25 collision; #229 vs #233 for schema 25), set its base to the parent head branch via `gh pr edit --base`, and renumber ADR/cache-schema/SCHEMA_VERSION so each is unique in merge order (#232 gets 0022 and its schema first). #235 stays on feat/semantic-on-demand; its Equivalence diff is the intended `full` default — handle via the PR body and the minimal allow policy, but flag to the user if the gate cannot pass without a blanket entry. Commits end with `Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED`. gh and git need the sandbox off; one plain git command per call. Never merge. Finish with a table: PR, base, merge state, CI state, what changed."}