{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:37:08.899Z","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>ad5269bcad04ba5a7</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01Sezu69uFvBupA79irpkypv</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/ad5269bcad04ba5a7.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Why React handlers are lost, and include ref\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>The default is now `full` and pushed to PR #235 (base `feat/semantic-on-demand`), but the equivalence and oracle gates still fail, so it isn't ready to merge. CI had not finished when I stopped.\n\n**What's in the PR**\n- `PipelineOptions` defaults to `full`. The CLI, config file, NAPI binding, Vite plugin and addon follow it, and `skipHtmlProps` still means `none`.\n- `curated` stays as an opt-in compact mode, with my earlier fixes (`notableInherited` emitted, `ref`, `aria-*`, handlers).\n- The missing-`@types/react` notice is now one info diagnostic per component that needed attributes, instead of a run-wide warning.\n- `Pick&lt;React.AriaAttributes, …&gt;` lists nothing in `full` (now the default). I fixed that by letting `full` read React interfaces for `Pick`.\n- `ref` on `forwardRef` components now has no parent, so the addon's `collapseInheritedProps` keeps showing it.\n- `scripts/equivalence.py` pins `default` and `deps` to `--html-attributes curated`. `parity.py` already passed `full` explicitly. `scorecard.py` passes no mode, so it follows the new default.\n- ADR 0023 supersedes 0013's default; the README, `MIGRATING.md`, `docs/STATUS.md`, `docs/rdt-coverage.md` and package READMEs are updated. The ADR number is free: #232 and #233 both claim 0022 and nothing claims 0023. The changeset uses your wording.\n- Commits are `739dfbf6`, `426a6fdf` and `ad027bb5`.\n\n**Your premise doesn't hold against the old default.** Full is slower and larger than the old curated default, not faster and smaller. It beats my widened curated only on Chakra and shadcn.\n\n| Corpus | Wall ms | Peak RSS MiB | Canonical JSON MB |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| antd | 56 → 62 | 130 → 151 | 3.6 → 6.3 |\n| chakra | 424 → 470 | 514 → 577 | 11.1 → 16.7 |\n| mantine | 149 → 164 | 175 → 229 | 8.4 → 14.2 |\n| spectrum | 90 → 98 | 171 → 191 | 8.3 → 11.7 |\n| shadcn | 144 → 188 | 220 → 301 | 5.9 → 12.2 |\n\nWall time is +9% to +31%, peak RSS +12% to +37%, and JSON +42% to +105%. Measurements used `--load-dependencies`, canonical JSON and no cache. The RDT corpus snapshots total 0.35 MB at the old default, 2.9 MB widened curated and 6.4 MB full, so interning does not make them smaller. I did not record first/median story time per variant. The harness table has those columns, but I only pulled the `caliper` rows (83 ms for antd, 183 ms for Spectrum real stories, medians 2 and 6 ms).\n\n**Storybook harness, \"props Storybook lists that we lack\"**\n- antd 37 → 34, shadcn 0 → 0, Spectrum 1 → 1.\n- `Dragger`'s `capture`, `Transfer`'s `ref` and `CheckableTagGroup`'s `ref` are now listed.\n- Still missing: `ref` on antd `Breadcrumb` and Spectrum `TreeView`, because they aren't detected as `forwardRef` and fixing that needs an extractor change.\n- Still missing: 33 `PurePanel` props. They are Drawer-level props (`open`, `resizable`, `panelRef`). The declared Drawer `PurePanel` type extends none of them, so this is almost certainly a pairing mismatch, but I could not confirm it because the generated story file is deleted after the run.\n\n**Gates**\n\n| Gate | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `cargo nextest run --workspace --exclude caliper-docgen-napi --locked` | exit 0, 921 passed |\n| `just lint doc-check machete typos` | exit 0 |\n| Lazy parity | ok |\n| `caliper-docgen-napi` Rust tests | 23 passed |\n| storybook and vite-plugin vitest | 60 and 58 passed |\n| `just equivalence` | fails |\n| `just equivalence --oracle` | fails |\n| CI | pending |\n\n- The `packages/napi` package has no test script.\n- Equivalence runs against `origin/feat/semantic-on-demand` on my existing corpus copies, not a fresh `parity.py setup`. I added narrow entries for the intended HTML-layer differences: `notable-*` and `prop-added` per config, plus `inheritance` fields. Still unexplained and not allowed:\n  - 516 `notable-removed`, including shadcn button attributes.\n  - 95 `prop-type-changed`, mostly `children` or `onClick` turning into `X &amp; X` intersections.\n  - 384 `prop-field-changed`.\n  - Some diagnostic churn.\n- The oracle's wrong rate improved to about 0.00%. The \"components matched\" gate fell, by 5 points on fixtures (82.5 → 77.5%) and by 0.3 points on mantine, antd and spectrum.\n\nneeds input: decide whether I should chase the equivalence leftovers (the `notable-removed` and the `X &amp; X` type intersections look like real regressions in my layer changes) before this merges, or whether you want to accept them in the allow-list.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>329915</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>83</tool_uses><duration_ms>1404039</duration_ms></usage>\n<worktree><worktreePath>/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/agent-ad5269bcad04ba5a7</worktreePath><worktreeBranch>worktree-agent-ad5269bcad04ba5a7</worktreeBranch></worktree>\n</task-notification>"}
