d Spectrum `TreeView`, because they aren't detected as `forwardRef` and fixing that needs an extractor change.\n- Still missing: 33 `PurePanel` props. They are Drawer-level props (`open`, `resizable`, `panelRef`). The declared Drawer `PurePanel` type extends none of them, so this is almost certainly a pairing mismatch, but I could not confirm it because the generated story file is deleted after the run.\n\n**Gates**\n\n| Gate | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `cargo nextest run --workspace --exclude caliper-docgen-napi --locked` | exit 0, 921 passed |\n| `just lint doc-check machete typos` | exit 0 |\n| Lazy parity | ok |\n| `caliper-docgen-napi` Rust tests | 23 passed |\n| storybook and vite-plugin vitest | 60 and 58 passed |\n| `just equivalence` | fails |\n| `just equivalence --oracle` | fails |\n| CI | pending |\n\n- The `packages/napi` package has no test script.\n- Equivalence runs against `origin/feat/semantic-on-demand` on my existing corpus copies, not a fresh `parity.py setup`. I added narrow entries for the intended HTML-layer differences: `notable-*` and `prop-added` per config, plus `inheritance` fields. Still unexplained and not allowed:\n  - 516 `notable-removed`, including shadcn button attributes.\n  - 95 `prop-type-changed`, mostly `children` or `onClick` turning into `X &amp; X` intersections.\n  - 384 `prop-field-changed`.\n  - Some diagnostic churn.\n- The oracle's wrong rate improved to about 0.00%. The \"components matched\" gate fell, by 5 points on fixtures (82.5 → 77.5%) and by 0.3 points on mantine, antd and spectrum.\n\nneeds input: decide whether I should chase the equivalence leftovers (the `notable-removed` and the `X &amp; X` type intersections look like real regressions in my layer changes) before this merges, or whether you want to accept them in the allow-list.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>329915</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>83</tool_uses><duration_ms>1404039</duration_ms></usage>\n<worktree><worktreePath>/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.c