{"parentUuid":"a3afaa52-3b5a-468c-87a3-b55f463ca547","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRFjS9L2KyQKmFDyNtaJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The `react-props` fork finished #235 with `full` as the default, but its equivalence and oracle gates still fail, so I've sent it back to fix them.\n\n- **Implemented:** `full` is the default across the CLI, config, NAPI binding and addon. ADR 0023 supersedes 0013 on the default, and the docs are updated.\n- **Cost against the old curated default:**\n\n  | Measure | Change |\n  |---|---|\n  | Wall time | +9% to +31% |\n  | Peak RSS | +12% to +37% |\n  | JSON size | +42% to +105% |\n\n  It beats the widened curated mode only on Chakra and shadcn. So `full` is not faster or smaller than the old default, which was your reason for choosing it.\n- **Still failing:** equivalence and oracle. The leftovers look like real regressions in its changes: 516 attributes dropped on shadcn, 95 `X & X` type intersections, and 384 prop field changes. The oracle matched rate fell 5 points on fixtures.\n- **Next:** I told the fork to fix those at the source and allow-list only genuinely intended differences, narrowly. The `reconcile-open-prs` fork picks up #235 last.\n\nI'll report when they finish. Do you still want `full` as the default, given it costs more than the old default?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4021,"cache_read_input_tokens":114800,"output_tokens":429,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4021,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":429,"cache_read_input_tokens":114800,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4021,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input