{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:12:10.462Z","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>ab68e81f3acc582fe</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01KioV2trebTccwzUF9TQYMd</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/ab68e81f3acc582fe.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Reconcile open PRs after merges\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>All the open PRs are merged up with main and pushed. #228–#232, #234 and #236 are mergeable with passing CI, and #233 and #235 are still waiting on their last runs. One decision is yours: the Scorecard speed gate fails on #235. I never force-pushed, and I merged nothing.\n\n| PR | Base | State | What I changed |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| #228 | main | clean, green | Merged main and kept both tests in `extractor/tests.rs`. |\n| #234 | main | clean, green | Merged main with no conflicts. Its single `mantine … .component` allow-list entry is kept for now. |\n| #230 | main | clean, green | Merged main and kept its own allow-list entries. |\n| #231 | main | clean, green | Merged main with no conflicts. |\n| #229 | main | clean, green (17/17) | Merged main and kept both tests. Rewrote the allow-list to 51 narrow entries covering the 11 new Chakra components and the diagnostics that shift around them. It stays on cache schema 25. |\n| #232 | main | clean, green | Merged main and resolved the `Cargo.toml` version conflicts (core 0.7.0, tsc-client 0.1.1). Keeps ADR 0022. |\n| #233 | **#229's branch** | 1 run pending | Retargeted onto #229 so the numbers line up. Cache schema is now 26, the ADR moved from 0022 to 0023, and the PR body is updated. Its 170-entry allow-list had bare wildcards the gate rejects, so I replaced it with 7 entries (the schema version plus `Command.filter`, `FormField.control`, `InputOTP.onComplete`, `Markdown.rehypePlugins`, `Markdown.remarkPlugins`). |\n| #235 | #232's branch | 5 runs pending | Merged the #232 branch. Its ADR moved from 0023 to 0024. The allow-list is now 2,084 entries naming each prop the `full` default adds, such as `*.onClick`. |\n| #236 | main | clean, green | Merged main. |\n\n- **How I checked:** I reproduced each Equivalence diff locally on the bench corpora and confirmed the new lists pass. Core tests pass on every branch I touched. Two CLI watch tests fail inside the sandbox and pass outside it.\n- **Matching change:** To keep matching fast with 2,000+ entries, `allowed()` in `scripts/equivalence.py` now indexes `*.prop` entries in a set. A test checks it matches the same items as plain `fnmatch`.\n- **Merge order:** #228, #234, #230, #231, #229, #233 (retargets to main), #232, #235, then #236.\n- **Allow-list cleanup:** `main` must have an empty allow-list. After #229, #230, #233, #234 and #235 land, each needs a follow-up that empties it, or the \"Allow-list empty\" check on `main` fails.\n- **Scorecard on #235:** The speed gate fails because the `full` default makes the no-dependency run slower than main. Mantine takes 240 ms against main's 153 ms, and Chakra 210 ms against 103 ms, versus the 1.1× limit. That is the cost of listing every attribute by default. Either accept it and relax or override the gate for this PR, or reconsider the default.\n- **Install job:** The Install check on #235 failed with a 404 because the 0.7.0 npm platform packages weren't published yet. A rerun after the release finishes should clear it.\n- **ADR numbers:** 0022 is #232, 0023 is #233, and 0024 is #235. The README lines for 0022 and 0023 will collide trivially in `docs/adr/README.md` when #232 and #233 merge.\n- **Possible regression to check:** On #229, the \"skipped candidate\" diagnostics for `StyledGroup` and `VisuallyHidden` disappear, but neither shows up as a new component. I didn't investigate.\n- **Not mine:** #239 is open and looks like another release PR.\n\nI did the work on local branches `rc-228`, `rc-229`, `rc-230`, `rc-231`, `rc-232`, `rc-233`, `rc-234` and `rc-235`, each pushed to its PR's head branch. The scratch scripts are `derive_allow.py` and `empty-allow.json` in `$CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp`.\n\nresult: Open PRs merged up with main and pushed with no force-pushes. #228–#232, #234 and #236 are mergeable with green CI, #233 is restacked on #229, and #233 and #235 are awaiting their last runs. #235's Scorecard speed gate fails by design from the `full` default and needs your decision.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>232842</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>168</tool_uses><duration_ms>3055911</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
