{"parentUuid":"bc0382cf-73e8-4284-ad0a-f8af0d3036a4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRQGWPMivTrHhZsrzdzp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Our lead over react-docgen is probably small end to end, and I have no measurement of it. It was never measured properly.\n\n- **Only data point:** the site's Node harness, which gave caliper 2.96 s, react-docgen 3.39 s and RDT 10.37 s. That is about 1.15× over react-docgen, against about 3.5× over RDT. Node startup and the NAPI load dominate that run.\n- **With `full`:** at +10% wall, caliper would be about 3.3 s, which is roughly even with react-docgen at 3.39 s. In that harness we could lose the lead entirely.\n- **My earlier 5–15× compute figure:** that is an unmeasured guess about native parsing against JS parsing. Treat it as unsupported. The real gap depends on corpus size and how much of the run is fixed startup cost.\n- **What we get for the money:** react-docgen is fast because it is shallow. It doesn't resolve imported types or `@types/react`, so it misses most inherited props. Our case against it is accuracy at similar speed, not a big speed multiple.\n- **Where we'd actually win on speed:** the lazy Storybook session. A story costs 21–140 ms for a single component, because we resolve one component on demand and react-docgen parses the whole file. I haven't compared that to react-docgen per story either.\n\nSo the claim I can defend is RDT-level accuracy at about react-docgen's speed, which matches what you said earlier. \"5–15× faster than react-docgen\" is not defensible without a measurement.\n\nI can measure react-docgen against caliper (old default and `full`) on the five corpora with a fork: one-shot extract and per-story latency, time and peak RSS. Should I start it?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":77,"cache_read_input_tokens":130237,"output_tokens":687,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":126},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":77,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":687,"cache_read_input_tokens":130237,"cache_creation_input_tokens":77,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":77},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"5be215be-ad30-4f8f-9cbd-636b966db457","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgRQGW6kCSJE7dFPrDktF","requestRef":"c42d14f6-f33e-4805-9d93-d7365b886a98","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"4cc30e33-6c1f-4c34-a4f8-bb45be420df0","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:29:24.481Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"rc-233","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
