{"parentUuid":"135655e8-e878-4400-b83e-393619af9524","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRQPpBsiJhk5DUjNwDQz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HJzkHJjFXswPYVJyrnzgVB","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Measure Storybook full cost, share element layer","subagent_type":"fork","name":"full-element-layer","prompt":"Work in a new worktree off branch fix/react-props-never-omitted (PR #235; stacked on feat/semantic-on-demand). Goal: make `htmlAttributes: full` (now default) cheap, with evidence. Step 1 (measure first, report before building): (a) Storybook path per-story cost — first-story and later-story latency, peak RSS, for old default (curated, prior to #235 — use the parent branch build) vs full, on the five corpora in /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/bench-corpus via packages/storybook/scripts/storybook-parity.mjs (pnpm --filter caliper-docgen-napi build:napi, then storybook build); (b) profile where the eager one-shot extract cost of full goes (resolve vs merge vs interning vs serialization/canonical JSON) with a real profiler (samply/cargo flamegraph/perf-like) on shadcn and antd; (c) react-docgen (Storybook's built-in) and RDT one-shot and per-file timings on the same corpora for an honest speed/RSS/recall comparison against old default and full — measured, not estimated. Step 2: prototype sharing the element attribute layer — resolve the attribute set once per element type and let components reference it (build on ADR 0018 interned prop sets; keep canonical JSON output byte-identical or bump SCHEMA_VERSION with an ADR at the next free number, check open PRs for numbers), and re-measure. Keep only changes that cut time/RSS/JSON with identical output; equivalence must stay green with no new allow-list entries. Rules: never force-push, never merge, push commits to a new branch stacked on #235's branch with a non-draft PR whose base is fix/react-props-never-omitted, friendly scannable changeset per AGENTS.md, commits end with `Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED`, PR body ends with the session URL, read exit codes directly, sandbox off for git/gh, one plain git command per call, scratch in $CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp. Final report: measured tables (old default vs full vs full+shared layer vs react-docgen vs RDT: time, RSS, JSON size, recall), what the prototype saved, and a recommendation on `full` as default."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":68,"cache_read_input_tokens":132273,"output_tokens":924,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":68,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":924,"cache_read_input_tokens":132273,"cache_creation_input_tokens":68,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":68},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01HJzkHJjFXswPYVJyrnzgVB":{"description":"Measure Storybook full cost, share element layer","subagent_type":"fork","name":"full-element-layer","prompt":"Work in a new worktree off branch fix/react-props-never-omitted (PR #235; stacked on feat/semantic-on-demand). Goal: make `htmlAttributes: full` (now default) cheap, with evidence. Step 1 (measure first, report before building): (a) Storybook path per-story cost — first-story and later-story latency, peak RSS, for old default (curated, prior to #235 — use the parent branch build) vs full, on the five corpora in /Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/bench-corpus via packages/storybook/scripts/storybook-parity.mjs (pnpm --filter caliper-docgen-napi build:napi, then