{"parentUuid":"2d94a3de-fecb-4827-b1b5-7546f22914b7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRRcY9wrR4SyEEDWceTK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01W4eGcHefriaUaRYghwDkZN","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Cleanup docs, ADRs, confidence script","subagent_type":"fork","name":"cleanup-docs-adrs","prompt":"New worktree off origin/main. One non-draft PR, base main. Tasks: (1) Delete scripts/confidence.py, scripts/precision-sample.py if only it uses, and docs/confidence-experiment.md's tooling references; keep a short findings paragraph (warning rule beats Caliper-only signals) in docs/archive or docs/STATUS.md; remove any justfile/CI references. (2) Audit docs/*.md (edge-cases, rdt-coverage, root-cause-analysis, type-checker-integration, benchmarks, performance, parity, storybook-parity, precision, projects/, archive/): for each, verify against code/STATUS whether it is current; delete or move to docs/archive what is stale or duplicated, fold what's useful into docs/STATUS.md or docs/architecture/, fix links. Don't invent facts; verify claims you keep. (3) ADRs: re-read docs/adr/README.md. For each ADR 0001–0021 decide: keep (architectural, expensive to reverse, not obvious from code) vs demote (tweak/behavior detail -> move its rationale into the relevant docs/architecture/ page or a code comment, delete the ADR file, leave a one-line tombstone in the README index so numbers stay stable). Be conservative: keep 0001, 0005, 0006, 0007, 0016, 0017, 0019 unless clearly wrong; justify each demotion in the PR body table. Tighten the README's inclusion rule with a short 'not an ADR' list. Also write, in the PR body, recommendations (do not edit their branches) on whether open-PR ADRs 0022 (#232 on-demand TS), 0023 (#233) and 0024 (#235) deserve to be ADRs. Do not touch scripts/equivalence*, parity*, scorecard* or workflows (a separate redesign is in flight and open PRs edit them). Rules: never force-push/merge, changeset only if consumer-visible (likely none), commits end `Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED`, PR body ends with the session URL, no hard-wrapping, read exit codes directly (just lint, doc-check, typos), sandbox off for git/gh, one plain git command per call, scratch in $CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp. Report: PR link, what was deleted/demoted, anything uncertain."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1183,"cache_read_input_tokens":136267,"output_tokens":2151,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":376},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1183,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2151,"cache_read_input_tokens":136267,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1183,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1183},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01W4eGcHefriaUaRYghwDkZN":{"description":"Cleanup docs, ADRs, confidence script","subagent_type":"fork","name":"cleanup-docs-adrs","prompt":"New worktree off origin/main. One non-draft PR, base main. Tasks: (1) Delete scripts/confidence.py, scripts/precision-sample.py if only it uses, and docs/confidence-experiment.md's tooling references; keep a short findings paragraph (warning rule beats Caliper-only signals) in docs/archive or docs/STATUS.md; remove any justfile/CI references. (2) Audit docs/*.md (edge-cases, rdt-coverage, root-cause-analysis, type-checker-integration, benchmarks, performance, parity, storybook-parity, precision, projects/, archive/): for each, verify against code/STATUS whether it is current; delete or move to docs/archive what is stal