{"parentUuid":"cd5b29cc-c9b0-426b-9162-e785b05ff87d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRRcY9wrR4SyEEDWceTK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019gWKxmWoQV9REnAi5GUHVi","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Design simpler measurement gates","subagent_type":"fork","name":"measurement-redesign","prompt":"Design only, no code changes and no PRs yet (open PRs #228–#236 edit the current scripts/workflows; implementation waits until they merge). Read scripts/{equivalence,parity,scorecard,confidence}.py, scripts/*baseline*.json, scripts/equivalence-allow.json, .github/workflows/{ci,equivalence,parity,scorecard,allow-list-empty,release}.yml, justfile, docs/{parity,benchmarks,performance,storybook-parity}.md and the history of why each exists (git log, PR #224 body). Goal from the user: good and reliable benchmarks, not complex. Produce a proposal (write to $CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp/measurement-proposal.md and summarize in your final message): (a) what each current gate protects, its real catch record (which real regressions did it catch vs how many false alarms/baseline-drift triages — use git/gh history), (b) the minimal set that keeps that value: e.g. one speed+RSS gate on a fixed corpus with a noise-robust method (repeat, median, compare base vs head on the same runner, same-job A/B), one 'output changed' diff vs the PR's base that prints a human-readable summary instead of an allow-list (decide: informational comment vs failing gate; how intended changes get acknowledged without a growing file), and accuracy tracked as a recorded number (recall vs RDT / react-docgen on pinned corpora at a pinned commit) rather than a baseline-diff gate, (c) what to delete, (d) CI time/cost, flakiness risks, (e) migration steps and an implementation order that avoids conflicts with the open stack, (f) estimated line count before/after. Be concrete and skeptical; if a gate has never caught a real regression, say so. Include react-docgen as a comparison target in the accuracy/speed record. Final message: the proposal summary with a clear recommendation."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1183,"cache_read_input_tokens":136267,"output_tokens":2151,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":376},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1183,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2151,"cache_read_input_tokens":136267,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1183,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1183},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_019gWKxmWoQV9REnAi5GUHVi":{"description":"Design simpler measurement gates","subagent_type":"fork","name":"measurement-redesign","prompt":"Design only, no code changes and no PRs yet (open PRs #228–#236 edit the current scripts/workflows; implementation waits until they merge). Read scripts/{equivalence,parity,scorecard,confidence}.py, scripts/*baseline*.json, scripts/equivalence-allow.json, .github/workflows/{ci,equivalence,parity,scorecard,allow-list-empty,release}.yml, justfile, docs/{parity,benchmarks,performance,storybook-parity}.md and the history of why each exists (git log, PR #224 body). Goal from the user: good and reliable benchmarks, not complex. Produce a proposal (write to $CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp/measurement-proposal.md and summarize in your final message): (a) what each current gate protects, its real catch record (which real regressions did it catch vs how many false alarms/baseline-drift triages — use git/gh history), (b) the minimal set that keeps that value: e.g. one speed+RSS gate on a