s/{parity,benchmarks,performance,storybook-parity}.md and the history of why each exists (git log, PR #224 body). Goal from the user: good and reliable benchmarks, not complex. Produce a proposal (write to $CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp/measurement-proposal.md and summarize in your final message): (a) what each current gate protects, its real catch record (which real regressions did it catch vs how many false alarms/baseline-drift triages — use git/gh history), (b) the minimal set that keeps that value: e.g. one speed+RSS gate on a fixed corpus with a noise-robust method (repeat, median, compare base vs head on the same runner, same-job A/B), one 'output changed' diff vs the PR's base that prints a human-readable summary instead of an allow-list (decide: informational comment vs failing gate; how intended changes get acknowledged without a growing file), and accuracy tracked as a recorded number (recall vs RDT / react-docgen on pinned corpora at a pinned commit) rather than a baseline-diff gate, (c) what to delete, (d) CI time/cost, flakiness risks, (e) migration steps and an implementation order that avoids conflicts with the open stack, (f) estimated line count before/after. Be concrete and skeptical; if a gate has never caught a real regression, say so. Include react-docgen as a comparison target in the accuracy/speed record. Final message: the proposal summary with a clear recommendation.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/a47522a479758c32d.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"c60e959b-87b6-472c-bd3e-0e6235d0773f","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","root":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","branch":"perf/shared-element-layer","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":3,"untracked":null,"un