{"parentUuid":"8a896f13-efbb-4d74-9491-3aae5f269510","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRRduiGVkagAFDae9LWo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Two forks are running.\n\n- **`cleanup-docs-adrs`** opens one PR against `main`.\n  - It deletes `confidence.py` and keeps a short note of the finding.\n  - It checks every stale doc against the code, then deletes it, archives it or folds it into `STATUS.md`.\n  - It demotes ADRs that are only tweaks, with a table justifying each. It keeps 0001, 0005, 0006, 0007, 0016, 0017 and 0019 unless they're clearly wrong.\n  - It adds a \"not an ADR\" rule to the README.\n  - It gives its view on whether 0022–0024 deserve to be ADRs, without touching those branches.\n- **`measurement-redesign`** writes a proposal only, with no PR or code yet.\n  - It reviews each gate's real catch record against its false alarms.\n  - It proposes the smallest set that keeps the value: one speed and memory gate, an output diff against the PR's base without an allow-list, and recorded accuracy against RDT and react-docgen.\n  - It covers deletions, CI cost, flakiness risks, and an implementation order that avoids the open stack.\n\nImplementation waits until the stack merges, because #228–#236 edit the same scripts. A third fork (`full-element-layer`) is still measuring `full`. I'll report as each one finishes."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3043,"cache_read_input_tokens":137450,"output_tokens":442,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3043,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":442,"cache_read_input_tokens":137450,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3043,"cache_creatio