{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:49:31.953Z","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a47522a479758c32d</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_019gWKxmWoQV9REnAi5GUHVi</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/a47522a479758c32d.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Design simpler measurement gates\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Task: design a simpler measurement setup (design only). The proposal is at `/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/measurement-proposal.md`; I changed no code and opened no PRs.\n\n**Recommendation: three jobs, no committed baselines and no allow-list.**\n1. **PR speed and memory gate, blocking.**\n   - Keep the existing method: head and the PR's own base, built and timed interleaved in one job.\n   - Use 15 runs, median wall and peak RSS, and fail above 1.10× wall or 1.15× RSS on any corpus. Re-run only the failing corpus once before failing.\n   - Intended costs, such as `full`, get a `perf-accepted` label and the numbers printed in the PR.\n   - First run base-against-base 20 times to measure the noise before choosing thresholds.\n   - Delete the side gates (RDT ratio, dependency-loading, scaling).\n2. **PR output diff, informational.**\n   - Post a summary of what changed against the PR's base. It becomes a failure only when the PR carries a `no-output-change` label, which fits refactors and perf PRs.\n   - Delete the allow-list, its validator, and the `allow-list-empty` workflow.\n   - Lazy-versus-batch parity becomes a plain cargo test.\n3. **Weekly accuracy and speed record.**\n   - Caliper, RDT and react-docgen on the installed pinned corpora.\n   - It records recall and agreement, the oracle's wrong rate, in-process and cold-start time, peak RSS, and per-story latency.\n   - It is compared to the last green main record kept as an artifact, so there is no baseline file and no refresh PRs. It opens an issue on a drop of more than 2 recall points.\n   - The record is what lets us put a real number on react-docgen.\n\n**Catch record (a week of data, so \"never caught\" means I found no evidence):**\n- **Scorecard:**\n  - It caught one real regression, Mantine +38% and Chakra +47%. That ran only weekly and merged unseen.\n  - Its PR job is `continue-on-error`, so it has never blocked anything.\n  - Its three side gates caught nothing.\n- **Parity:**\n  - Triage found 2 real regressions among about 10 flagged rows.\n  - 6 of 7 runs on 10-26 failed, from the install bug, the allow-list step and baseline drift.\n- **Oracle:**\n  - It found real extraction bugs on 10-23/24.\n  - Its committed baseline is stale.\n  - The beta TS checker should inform the record, never gate.\n- **Equivalence:**\n  - It caught one real class, the 95 `X &amp; X` intersections in #235.\n  - Its job is `continue-on-error` too: 55 of 60 runs show success whatever the diff.\n  - The allow-list grew to 85 blanket entries and silenced it. #235 now carries about 2,000.\n- **Confidence experiment:** `confidence.py` found nothing and nothing consumes it. Delete it.\n\n**Size:** Python goes from about 2,360 lines to about 1,000, committed baselines and allow-lists from about 650 lines to 0, and docs from about 60 KB to about 15 KB. Four docs merge into one `docs/measurement.md`. No ADR is needed.\n\n**Order:**\n- Wait for the open stack to merge, since it edits the same scripts.\n- Run the base-against-base calibration, then three mostly-deletion PRs: speed gate, output diff, weekly record.\n- Docs consolidation follows.\n- Making the new speed job required in branch protection is a maintainer step.\n\n**Open items:**\n- `apps/validate` is about 1,990 lines and needs a separate audit of what the weekly record keeps.\n- antd's install has no lockfile, so its weekly numbers drift.\n\nresult: The measurement proposal is written at `/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/measurement-proposal.md`. It recommends a blocking speed and memory gate, an informational output diff, and a weekly accuracy record that includes react-docgen. It also lists what to delete and the order to do it in. No code was changed.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>178784</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>15</tool_uses><duration_ms>137495</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
