thing consumes it. Delete it.\n\n**Size:** Python goes from about 2,360 lines to about 1,000, committed baselines and allow-lists from about 650 lines to 0, and docs from about 60 KB to about 15 KB. Four docs merge into one `docs/measurement.md`. No ADR is needed.\n\n**Order:**\n- Wait for the open stack to merge, since it edits the same scripts.\n- Run the base-against-base calibration, then three mostly-deletion PRs: speed gate, output diff, weekly record.\n- Docs consolidation follows.\n- Making the new speed job required in branch protection is a maintainer step.\n\n**Open items:**\n- `apps/validate` is about 1,990 lines and needs a separate audit of what the weekly record keeps.\n- antd's install has no lockfile, so its weekly numbers drift.\n\nresult: The measurement proposal is written at `/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/measurement-proposal.md`. It recommends a blocking speed and memory gate, an informational output diff, and a weekly accuracy record that includes react-docgen. It also lists what to delete and the order to do it in. No code was changed.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>178784</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>15</tool_uses><duration_ms>137495</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>\n</system-reminder>"}]}}
{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","id":"1fc7303e-9919-43e2-a152-7d73f6694b76","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:49:32.028Z","version":"2.1.308","querySource":"repl_main_thread:outputStyle:Concise","shapeHash":"30de49787603a257f4975e5cdab983aad4d3f56db15b3d01afad71bede0d6239","params":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"8c22795b-aaab-46e8-a8e9-08f022753864","keep":95,"tail":["0ce518b1b77391c26edee5505bfd986ae94f3e708376903d41b01dc49d3a19a2","bb86d21b1919964222948d44ad38f165c4a20e27a5d4ace72e0308b054edd4ef"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",96,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"f35ca9f8fd1c2db9a30db46c835766acd5cc99199e59189fcb8191d573ff98d0"}
{"parentUuid":"794e2ff1-d3db-4c1c-a87e-9cf94554d908","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRRpAb1LHU3c9JzAgFDZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The measurement fork recommends three jobs and no committed baselines or allow-list. Full proposal: `/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/measurement-proposal.md`.\n\n**The three jobs:**\n1. **PR speed and memory gate, blocking.**\n   - It builds the PR's head and its own base and times them interleaved in one job.\n   - It takes the median of 15 runs and fails above 1.10× wall time or 1.15× peak memory on any corpus, after one re-run of the failing corpus.\n   - Intended costs, such as `full`, get a `perf-accepted` label with the numbers printed in the PR.\n   - Thresholds come from 20 base-against-base runs first.\n2. **PR output diff, informational.**\n   - It posts a summary of what changed against the PR's base.\n   - It fails only on a `no-output-change` label.\n   - The allow-list, its validator and the `allow-list-empty` workflow are deleted.\n3. **Weekly accuracy and speed record.**\n   - It runs caliper, RDT and react-docgen on pinned corpora and records recall, time, memory and per-story latency.\n   - It compares each run to the last green record on `main`, with no baseline file.\n   - It opens an issue if recall drops by more than 2 points.\n\n**Why delete most of it:**\n- **Scorecard:** it caught one real regression, and that was in the weekly run. Its PR job never blocked anything.\n- **Equivalence:** it caught one real class, the 95 `X & X` intersections in #235. Its job is `continue-on-error`, so 55 of 60 runs show success whatever the diff, and the allow-list silenced it anyway.\n- **Parity:** it found two real regressions among about ten flagged rows, and six of seven runs on 10-26 failed.\n- **Oracle:** it found real extraction bugs, but its committed baseline is stale.\n- **Size:** Python goes from about 2,360 lines to about 1,000, baselines and allow-lists from about 650 lines to 0.\n\n**Order:** wait for the open stack to merge, since it edits the same scripts. Then calibrate noise and land three mostly-deletion PRs: speed gate, output diff, weekly record. Making the new speed job required in branch protection is a step for you.\n\n**Open items:** `apps/validate` is about 1,990 lines and needs its own audit. antd's install has no lockfile, so its weekly numbers drift.\n\nThis doubles as the hard numbers on react-docgen we never had. Should I start the calibration run now, or wait until the stack merges?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1897,"cache_read_input_tokens":140935,"output_tokens":859,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1897,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":859,"cache_read_input_tokens":140935,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1897,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1897},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"310ba460-f33c-4a27-ae06-17b96d5cfb1c","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgRRpAH9V2t5DuejZEnWJ","requestRef":"1fc7303e-9919-43e2-a152-7d73f6694b76","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"a2d7bfba-0bdd-40d3-9347-8d18d8cb89a2","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:49:40.572Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"docs/cleanup-stale-docs-adrs","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
