{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:58:16.864Z","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a024b5be31ee9cf6f</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01W4eGcHefriaUaRYghwDkZN</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/a024b5be31ee9cf6f.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Cleanup docs, ADRs, confidence script\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>PR #240 is open against `main`: https://github.com/orin-dx/caliper/pull/240. It deletes about 14,500 lines and retires three ADRs. `just lint`, `just doc-check` and `just typos` pass. I haven't seen its CI run yet, and there is no changeset because nothing is consumer-visible.\n\n**Deleted (all stays in git history):**\n- **`docs/archive/`:** 19 files, about 540 KB.\n- **`docs/root-cause-analysis.md`:** the audit it analysed has fully landed.\n- **`docs/projects/architecture-roadmap.md`:** its own header says to delete it when the work ships.\n- **`scripts/confidence.py` and `docs/confidence-experiment.md`:** the finding is now a short paragraph in `docs/STATUS.md`. `scripts/precision-sample.py` stays, since `docs/precision.md` uses it.\n- **`docs/edge-cases.md`:** cut from 47 KB to about 20 lines, one entry per gap still open. I rechecked the four items I kept against the code, and dropped one that turned out to be fixed.\n\n**ADRs retired, with tombstones in the README:**\n- **0004:** already superseded by 0006.\n- **0015:** a resolver lookup rule. I moved it, with its measurements, into `resolver-type-resolution.md`.\n- **0020:** a tuning of 0016's design. `pipeline-orchestration.md` already described it, and 0016 now points there.\n\nI kept 0011, 0012, 0013 and 0014 for now. Between them they have many code references, and retiring them means editing resolver comments that open PRs also touch. 0021 is a release procedure and the clearest next retirement. I left it because #232, #233 and #235 each add README lines right after it.\n\nThe README's \"Not ADR material\" list now rules out defaults, thresholds and lookup orders that one module reads, release procedures, and tunings of an earlier decision.\n\n**Recommendations for the open-PR ADRs (also in the PR body, judged from each PR's title and file list; I haven't read the ADR texts in them):**\n- **0022 (#232):** keep. It routes the backend through NAPI, which ADR 0006 says not to do.\n- **0023 (#233):** retire. It's a contract extension already covered by the schema version bump.\n- **0024 (#235):** retire, along with 0013, after #235 merges.\n\n**Stale claims I fixed while checking references:**\n- **`docs/STATUS.md`:** said the semantic backend isn't implemented, and gave a test count of 745 against more than 900 now.\n- **`pipeline-orchestration.md`:** said dependency loading is off by default, and listed fixed `watch --out` write failures as open.\n- **`resolver-type-resolution.md`:** said `resolve_named` has no cycle detection.\n- **`extractor-ast-visiting.md`:** listed four component shapes as unrecognized that are detected now.\n- **Other docs:** `serialization-formats.md` pointed at a \"proposed ADR-0006\", and `benchmarks.md` now says its quality half is a 2026-07-25 snapshot.\n\n**Two things to know:**\n- **Conflicts:** other open PRs edit the same files, so whichever lands second may need a one-line resolution in `docs/STATUS.md` or the ADR README. #235 touches STATUS, #232, #233 and #235 all touch the ADR README, and #233 touches two architecture pages.\n- **Worktree:** the sandbox only allows writes in this worktree, so I branched here from `origin/main`. It had three uncommitted files (generated napi bindings and `storybook-parity.mjs`); I saved them as `release-0.2.0-leftover.patch` in `$CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp`. The tap notifier branch (#236) is already pushed.\n\nNot touched: `scripts/equivalence*`, `parity*`, `scorecard*` and the workflows, since the measurement redesign and open PRs edit them.\n\nresult: PR #240 deletes about 14,500 lines of finished audits, plans and the confidence script, and retires ADRs 0004, 0015 and 0020, with lint, doc-check and typos passing and CI not yet seen.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>334127</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>155</tool_uses><duration_ms>629240</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
