{"parentUuid":"6068d11f-d2d8-40b4-9197-bc58173b5bde","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRSUsc88cNifFru5fR4Z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"PR #240, the cleanup, is open against `main`. It deletes about 14,500 lines and retires three ADRs. `just lint`, `just doc-check` and `just typos` pass, but its CI hasn't run yet.\n\n- **Deleted:** `docs/archive/` (19 files), `root-cause-analysis.md`, the architecture roadmap, `scripts/confidence.py` and its experiment doc. The confidence finding is now a short paragraph in `docs/STATUS.md`. `edge-cases.md` went from 47 KB to about 20 lines, one per gap still open.\n- **ADRs retired:** 0004, 0015 and 0020, with tombstones in the README. The README now has a \"Not ADR material\" list that rules out defaults, thresholds, lookup orders, release procedures and tunings of an earlier decision.\n- **Stale claims fixed:** `STATUS.md` said the semantic backend isn't implemented. `pipeline-orchestration.md` said dependency loading is off by default. A few resolver and extractor docs listed gaps that are fixed.\n- **Kept for now:** ADRs 0011–0014, since retiring them means editing resolver comments that open PRs also touch. 0021 is the next retirement candidate.\n\n**Open-PR ADRs:** the fork judged these from PR titles and file lists, not the ADR texts.\n- **0022 (#232):** keep, since it routes the backend through NAPI, which ADR 0006 says not to do.\n- **0023 (#233):** retire, since the schema version bump already covers it.\n- **0024 (#235):** retire it and 0013 after #235 merges.\n\n**Conflicts:** #232, #233 and #235 all edit the ADR README, and #235 and #233 also touch `STATUS.md` or architecture pages. Whichever lands second needs a one-line resolution. I can retire 0023 and 0024 on those branches. That edits #233 and #235, so say if you want it.\n\n**Measurement redesign:** my question above, whether to start calibration now or wait for the stack, is still open.\n\n**Still running:** the fork measuring `full` and the shared attribute layer."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1928,"cache_read_input_tokens":143693,"output_tokens":712,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1928,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":712,"cache_read_input_tokens":143693,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1928,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1928},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"3d0edfc9-a65a-44b9-b4d6-01e82a6d4de2","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgRSUsJ2irVkxktNKvCNz","requestRef":"3ced3a10-c5fd-4788-9669-b512517b9415","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"60993c09-a2a0-49b2-badc-7d03dd082b89","timestamp":"2026-10-26T19:58:26.549Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"docs/cleanup-stale-docs-adrs","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
