{"parentUuid":"70cdf681-49cb-4113-9443-b2f3ecfedf6f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRUK9PN6RTPz3zJ97fuo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The `full` fork hit its 200-turn limit mid-prototype with only partial output, so I resumed it.\n\nIt will write the measurement tables first, with gaps marked, to `$CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp/full-measurements.md`. The tables cover old default, `full`, `full` with the shared layer, react-docgen and RDT. Then it finishes or drops the shared-layer prototype. It keeps the prototype only if output is identical and it cuts time, memory or JSON size, and it opens a PR on #235's branch only if it's worth keeping.\n\nI'll report the numbers and a recommendation on `full` as default when it finishes. Two questions of mine are still open:\n- Start the measurement calibration now, or wait until the stack merges?\n- Retire ADRs 0023 and 0024 on #233 and #235?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1406,"cache_read_input_tokens":146969,"output_tokens":277,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1406,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":277,"cache_read_input_tokens":146969,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1406,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1406},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"3bacd4f9-00da-4870-a856-711eadf22a39","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgRUK8yJZQWVkSkS95rqo","requestRef":"13f5ffdb-db29-4374-a5e7-bb90b82d41b0","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"3cc523