{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","prNumber":241,"prUrl":"https://github.com/orin-dx/caliper/pull/241","prRepository":"orin-dx/caliper","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:23:42.041Z"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:24:15.749Z","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a1a953946ad6090dc</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_014S3MWop4KLgJrYH5fMNHwe</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/a1a953946ad6090dc.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Measure Storybook full cost, share element layer\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Task: measure `full`'s cost, make it cheaper, and open a stacked PR. The cost is mostly a lookup bug, not the attribute layer, and PR #241 fixes it.\n\n**PR #241** (`perf/component-lookups-by-name`, base `fix/react-props-never-omitted`) indexes component lookups by name. Output is byte-identical to #235 on all five corpora in `full`, `curated` and `none`, apart from `durationMs`. Nextest passes (929 tests), clippy and `cargo fmt --check` are clean, and I added one test for the lookup. CI on #241 has not run yet.\n\n**Finding:** `ComponentProps&lt;typeof X&gt;` compared the path of every project and dependency component on each reference. That scan was the largest part of `full`'s cost on shadcn. The fix also speeds up `none`.\n\nMeasured with deps installed, `extract --json --no-cache`, wall ms / peak RSS MiB:\n\n| corpus | old default | #235 full | #241 full | #241 none | RDT | react-docgen |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| shadcn | 124 / 200 | 153 / 257 | 127 / 260 | 92 / 196 | 3,166 / 1,195 | 3,206 / 666 |\n| antd | 44 / 95 | 48 / 108 | 48 / 108 | 42 / 92 | 1,833 / 1,027 | 1,840 / 399 |\n| mantine | 54 / 111 | 67 / 143 | 68 / 143 | 52 / 107 | 1,463 / 548 | 1,151 / 393 |\n| chakra | 233 / 321 | 254 / 367 | 248 / 369 | 213 / 314 | 16,601 / 1,605 | 882 / 205 |\n| spectrum | 80 / 148 | 85 / 160 | 82 / 160 | 76 / 143 | 2,537 / 944 | 3,541 / 528 |\n\n- **Cost of `full` over the old default now:** shadcn +2%, antd +9%, mantine +26% (14 ms), chakra +6%, spectrum +3%. Memory is +8% to +30% (shadcn 200 → 260, mantine 111 → 143).\n- **Lead over RDT:** 22–67× in time and 3.8–9.5× in memory.\n- **Lead over react-docgen:** 17–43× on shadcn, antd, mantine and spectrum. Chakra is only 4×, and its run hit 56 errors on 126 files, so treat that as unreliable. Chakra's memory is 0.6×, so react-docgen uses less.\n- **JSON size, canonical (MB), old → full:** shadcn 3.8 → 7.7, antd 1.9 → 3.5, mantine 2.6 → 5.8, chakra 5.0 → 8.4, spectrum 4.2 → 6.3.\n- **Prop recall against RDT (components both report):**\n\n  | corpus | react-docgen | old default | curated | full |\n  |---|---|---|---|---|\n  | `@types/react` props: shadcn | 0% | 0.2% | 55% | 97% |\n  | `@types/react` props: antd | 0% | 0.3% | 52% | 92% |\n  | `@types/react` props: mantine | 0% | 0% | 53% | 99% |\n  | `@types/react` props: chakra | 0% | 0% | 55% | 99% |\n  | `@types/react` props: spectrum | 0% | 0% | 23% | 96% |\n  | own props: all five | 0.1–52% | 49–100% | 49–100% | 49–100% |\n\n  The old default lists effectively none of the `@types/react` props. Curated is a partial fix. Only `full` gets them. Own-prop recall is the same across the three caliper modes; shadcn is the lowest at 49%.\n- **Storybook path** (first story / median later story, ms):\n\n  | set | old default | #241 full |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | shadcn | 112 / 5 | 96 / 4 |\n  | chakra sampled | 222 / 12 | 119 / 11 |\n  | spectrum real | 189 / 8 | 176 / 5 |\n\n  RSS is +2% to +10% (shadcn 315 → 346 MB). First story is no slower with `full` than with `none`. react-docgen's in-process median per file is 0.75–4.2 ms, comparable per story.\n\n**Shared element layer: prototyped and dropped.** Caching each element's resolved attributes across components gave no gain (shadcn full 125 → 122 ms, within noise; the layer cache makes `curated` about 5% faster only). A one-walk attribute table gave no time gain and raised RSS 4–8%. Most components get their attributes through the interface chain, so the layer was never the cost. Not built: a representation shared end to end through `ComponentEntry` and the JSON output.\n\n**Recommendation:** keep `full` as the default. After #241 it costs 2–9% in time on four of five corpora, about 26% on mantine (14 ms), 8–30% in memory, and nothing measurable on the Storybook path. It is the only mode that returns the `@types/react` props (92–99% recall, against 0–55% for the others). If memory matters more, `curated` is the fallback, but it recovers only about half of those props. Merge #241 before or with #235.\n\n**Not done / gaps:**\n- **Measurements:** the per-story numbers are one run each (millisecond granularity). The RDT timings are earlier runs on the same machine, not re-run today.\n- **Open items (unchanged):** #235's Scorecard speed gate still needs re-checking now that the baseline is lower, and the 41-test oracle matched-rate baseline is stale.\n- **Git workaround:** the shared worktree was switched to another branch by another actor, so I committed via git plumbing from my session's directory and pushed that commit as the new branch. I did not touch that worktree's index or working tree. I restored its three files that I had edited. I removed my two temporary worktrees, and the local `perf/shared-element-layer` branch is left behind for you to delete.\n- **Changeset:** `cargo/caliper-docgen-core: patch`.\n\nFull tables, with gaps marked, are in `$CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp/full-measurements.md`.\n\nresult: #241 is open (stacked on #235): indexing component lookups cuts `full` on shadcn from 153 to 127 ms with identical output. The shared element layer gave no gain and was dropped. Recommendation: keep `full` as the default.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>466519</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>232</tool_uses><duration_ms>3182160</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
