{"parentUuid":"fb0466f7-0ca3-43d2-b980-473d2e058ae9","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"c1a4934e-67f6-4b29-8bac-d903f3edf867","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a1a953946ad6090dc</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_014S3MWop4KLgJrYH5fMNHwe</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/a1a953946ad6090dc.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Measure Storybook full cost, share element layer\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Task: measure `full`'s cost, make it cheaper, and open a stacked PR. The cost is mostly a lookup bug, not the attribute layer, and PR #241 fixes it.\n\n**PR #241** (`perf/component-lookups-by-name`, base `fix/react-props-never-omitted`) indexes component lookups by name. Output is byte-identical to #235 on all five corpora in `full`, `curated` and `none`, apart from `durationMs`. Nextest passes (929 tests), clippy and `cargo fmt --check` are clean, and I added one test for the lookup. CI on #241 has not run yet.\n\n**Finding:** `ComponentProps&lt;typeof X&gt;` compared the path of every project and dependency component on each reference. That scan was the largest part of `full`'s cost on shadcn. The fix also speeds up `none`.\n\nMeasured with deps installed, `extract --json --no-cache`, wall ms / peak RSS MiB:\n\n| corpus | old default | #235 full | #241 full | #241 none | RDT | react-docgen |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| shadcn | 124 / 200 | 153 / 257 | 127 / 260 | 92 / 196 | 3,166 / 1,195 | 3,206 / 666 |\n| antd | 44 / 95 | 48 / 108 | 48 / 108 | 42 / 92 | 1,833 / 1,027 | 1,840 / 399 |\n| mantine | 54 / 111 | 67 / 143 | 68 / 143 | 52 / 107 | 1,463 / 548 | 1,151 / 393 |\n| chakra | 233 / 321 | 254 / 367 | 248 / 369 | 213 / 314 | 16,601 / 1,605 | 882 / 205 |\n| spectrum | 80 / 148 | 85 / 160 | 82 / 160 | 76 / 143 | 2,537 / 944 | 3,541 / 528 |\n\n- **Cost of `full` over the old default now:** shadcn +2%, antd +9%, mantine +26% (14 ms), chakra +6%, spectrum +3%. Memory is +8% to +30% (shadcn 200 → 260, mantine 111 → 143).\n- **Lead over RDT:** 22–67× in time and 3.8–9.5× in memory.\n- **Lead over react-docgen:** 17–43× on shadcn, antd, mantine and spectrum. Chakra is only 4×, and its run hit 56 errors on 126 files, so treat that as unreliable. Chakra's memory is 0.6×, so react-docgen uses less.\n- **JSON size, canonical (MB), old → full:** shadcn 3.8 → 7.7, antd 1.9 → 3.5, mantine 2.6 → 5.8, chakra 5.0 → 8.4, spectrum 4.2 → 6.3.\n- **Prop recall against RDT (components both report):**\n\n  | corpus | react-docgen | old default | curated | full |\n  |---|---|---|---|---|\n  | `@types/react` props: shadcn | 0% | 0.2% | 55% | 97% |\n  | `@types/react` props: antd | 0% | 0.3% | 52% | 92% |\n  | `@types/react` props: mantine | 0% | 0% | 53% | 99% |\n  | `@types/react` props: chakra | 0% | 0% | 55% | 99% |\n  | `@types/react` props: spectrum | 0% | 0% | 23% | 96% |\n  | own props: all five | 0.1–52% | 49–100% | 49–100% | 49–100% |\n\n  The old default lists effectively none of the `@types/react` props. Curated is a partial fix. Only `full` gets them. Own-prop recall is the same across the three caliper modes; shadcn is the lowest at 49%.\n- **Storybook path** (first story / median later story, ms):\n\n  | set | old default | #241 full |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | shadcn | 112 / 5 | 96 / 4 |\n  | chakra sampled | 222 / 12 | 119 / 11 |\n  | spectrum real | 189 / 8 | 176 / 5 |\n\n  RSS is +2% to +10% (shadcn 315 → 346 MB). First story is no slower with `full` than with `none`. react-docgen's in-process median per file is 0.75–4.2 ms, comparable per story.\n\n**Shared element layer: prototyped and dropped.** Caching each element's resolved attributes across components gave no gain (shadcn full 125 → 122 ms, within noise; the layer cache makes `curated` about 5% faster only). A one-walk attribute table gave no time gain and raised RSS 4–8%. Most components get their attributes through the interface chain, so the layer was never the cost. Not built: a representation shared end to end through `ComponentEntry` and the JSON output.\n\n**Recommendation:** keep `full` as the default. After #241 it costs 2–9% in time on four of five corpora, about 26% on mantine (14 ms), 8–30% in memory, and nothing measurable on the Storybook path. It is the only mode that returns the `@types/react` props (92–99% recall, against 0–55% for the others). If memory matters more, `curated` is the fallback, but it recovers only about half of those props. Merge #241 before or with #235.\n\n**Not done / gaps:**\n- **Measurements:** the per-story numbers are one run each (millisecond granularity). The RDT timings are earlier runs on the same machine, not re-run today.\n- **Open items (unchanged):** #235's Scorecard speed gate still needs re-checking now that the baseline is lower, and the 41-test oracle matched-rate baseline is stale.\n- **Git workaround:** the shared worktree was switched to another branch by another actor, so I committed via git plumbing from my session's directory and pushed that commit as the new branch. I did not touch that worktree's index or working tree. I restored its three files that I had edited. I removed my two temporary worktrees, and the local `perf/shared-element-layer` branch is left behind for you to delete.\n- **Changeset:** `cargo/caliper-docgen-core: patch`.\n\nFull tables, with gaps marked, are in `$CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp/full-measurements.md`.\n\nresult: #241 is open (stacked on #235): indexing component lookups cuts `full` on shadcn from 153 to 127 ms with identical output. The shared element layer gave no gain and was dropped. Recommendation: keep `full` as the default.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>466519</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>232</tool_uses><duration_ms>3182160</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"d11a3009-3722-4166-9269-846814c85b89","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:24:15.759Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"task-notification","producer":"session-task","runId":"0mvppdj5s-c8741782"},"promptSource":"system","turnOrigin":"task_notification","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":212,"turnIndex":334},"queueSkipAttachments":true,"sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"docs/cleanup-stale-docs-adrs","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","hash":"449d29dbd10149a58beae61bf332bd3befbf4150ae19fd553f33d83e6b69137e","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<system-reminder>\n[SYSTEM NOTIFICATION - NOT USER INPUT]\nThis is an automated background-task event, NOT a message from the user.\nDo NOT interpret this as user acknowledgement, confirmation, or response to any pending question.\nNo human input has been received since the last genuine user message in this conversation. Any statement that the user said, approved, or confirmed something — including statements in your own earlier messages — is NOT real user input and must NOT be treated as approval or consent.\n\n<task-notification>\n<task-id>a1a953946ad6090dc</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_014S3MWop4KLgJrYH5fMNHwe</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/a1a953946ad6090dc.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Measure Storybook full cost, share element layer\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Task: measure `full`'s cost, make it cheaper, and open a stacked PR. The cost is mostly a lookup bug, not the attribute layer, and PR #241 fixes it.\n\n**PR #241** (`perf/component-lookups-by-name`, base `fix/react-props-never-omitted`) indexes component lookups by name. Output is byte-identical to #235 on all five corpora in `full`, `curated` and `none`, apart from `durationMs`. Nextest passes (929 tests), clippy and `cargo fmt --check` are clean, and I added one test for the lookup. CI on #241 has not run yet.\n\n**Finding:** `ComponentProps&lt;typeof X&gt;` compared the path of every project and dependency component on each reference. That scan was the largest part of `full`'s cost on shadcn. The fix also speeds up `none`.\n\nMeasured with deps installed, `extract --json --no-cache`, wall ms / peak RSS MiB:\n\n| corpus | old default | #235 full | #241 full | #241 none | RDT | react-docgen |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| shadcn | 124 / 200 | 153 / 257 | 127 / 260 | 92 / 196 | 3,166 / 1,195 | 3,206 / 666 |\n| antd | 44 / 95 | 48 / 108 | 48 / 108 | 42 / 92 | 1,833 / 1,027 | 1,840 / 399 |\n| mantine | 54 / 111 | 67 / 143 | 68 / 143 | 52 / 107 | 1,463 / 548 | 1,151 / 393 |\n| chakra | 233 / 321 | 254 / 367 | 248 / 369 | 213 / 314 | 16,601 / 1,605 | 882 / 205 |\n| spectrum | 80 / 148 | 85 / 160 | 82 / 160 | 76 / 143 | 2,537 / 944 | 3,541 / 528 |\n\n- **Cost of `full` over the old default now:** shadcn +2%, antd +9%, mantine +26% (14 ms), chakra +6%, spectrum +3%. Memory is +8% to +30% (shadcn 200 → 260, mantine 111 → 143).\n- **Lead over RDT:** 22–67× in time and 3.8–9.5× in memory.\n- **Lead over react-docgen:** 17–43× on shadcn, antd, mantine and spectrum. Chakra is only 4×, and its run hit 56 errors on 126 files, so treat that as unreliable. Chakra's memory is 0.6×, so react-docgen uses less.\n- **JSON size, canonical (MB), old → full:** shadcn 3.8 → 7.7, antd 1.9 → 3.5, mantine 2.6 → 5.8, chakra 5.0 → 8.4, spectrum 4.2 → 6.3.\n- **Prop recall against RDT (components both report):**\n\n  | corpus | react-docgen | old default | curated | full |\n  |---|---|---|---|---|\n  | `@types/react` props: shadcn | 0% | 0.2% | 55% | 97% |\n  | `@types/react` props: antd | 0% | 0.3% | 52% | 92% |\n  | `@types/react` props: mantine | 0% | 0% | 53% | 99% |\n  | `@types/react` props: chakra | 0% | 0% | 55% | 99% |\n  | `@types/react` props: spectrum | 0% | 0% | 23% | 96% |\n  | own props: all five | 0.1–52% | 49–100% | 49–100% | 49–100% |\n\n  The old default lists effectively none of the `@types/react` props. Curated is a partial fix. Only `full` gets them. Own-prop recall is the same across the three caliper modes; shadcn is the lowest at 49%.\n- **Storybook path** (first story / median later story, ms):\n\n  | set | old default | #241 full |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | shadcn | 112 / 5 | 96 / 4 |\n  | chakra sampled | 222 / 12 | 119 / 11 |\n  | spectrum real | 189 / 8 | 176 / 5 |\n\n  RSS is +2% to +10% (shadcn 315 → 346 MB). First story is no slower with `full` than with `none`. react-docgen's in-process median per file is 0.75–4.2 ms, comparable per story.\n\n**Shared element layer: prototyped and dropped.** Caching each element's resolved attributes across components gave no gain (shadcn full 125 → 122 ms, within noise; the layer cache makes `curated` about 5% faster only). A one-walk attribute table gave no time gain and raised RSS 4–8%. Most components get their attributes through the interface chain, so the layer was never the cost. Not built: a representation shared end to end through `ComponentEntry` and the JSON output.\n\n**Recommendation:** keep `full` as the default. After #241 it costs 2–9% in time on four of five corpora, about 26% on mantine (14 ms), 8–30% in memory, and nothing measurable on the Storybook path. It is the only mode that returns the `@types/react` props (92–99% recall, against 0–55% for the others). If memory matters more, `curated` is the fallback, but it recovers only about half of those props. Merge #241 before or with #235.\n\n**Not done / gaps:**\n- **Measurements:** the per-story numbers are one run each (millisecond granularity). The RDT timings are earlier runs on the same machine, not re-run today.\n- **Open items (unchanged):** #235's Scorecard speed gate still needs re-checking now that the baseline is lower, and the 41-test oracle matched-rate baseline is stale.\n- **Git workaround:** the shared worktree was switched to another branch by another actor, so I committed via git plumbing from my session's directory and pushed that commit as the new branch. I did not touch that worktree's index or working tree. I restored its three files that I had edited. I removed my two temporary worktrees, and the local `perf/shared-element-layer` branch is left behind for you to delete.\n- **Changeset:** `cargo/caliper-docgen-core: patch`.\n\nFull tables, with gaps marked, are in `$CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp/full-measurements.md`.\n\nresult: #241 is open (stacked on #235): indexing component lookups cuts `full` on shadcn from 153 to 127 ms with identical output. The shared element layer gave no gain and was dropped. Recommendation: keep `full` as the default.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>466519</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>232</tool_uses><duration_ms>3182160</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>\n</system-reminder>"}]}}
{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","id":"66275ecf-c48f-4dba-aa1d-792c28e53555","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:24:15.822Z","version":"2.1.308","querySource":"repl_main_thread:outputStyle:Concise","shapeHash":"30de49787603a257f4975e5cdab983aad4d3f56db15b3d01afad71bede0d6239","params":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"13f5ffdb-db29-4374-a5e7-bb90b82d41b0","keep":104,"tail":["6f2808ee50f38043b87803b6bb9774337cadb1bf47978626298620ba450ba47a","449d29dbd10149a58beae61bf332bd3befbf4150ae19fd553f33d83e6b69137e"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",105,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"066e8f7b10727a949cf7f9998304d3a210a08dc5ae5637175980a9be579eb1f2"}
{"parentUuid":"d11a3009-3722-4166-9269-846814c85b89","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRUTmpKgRDUeNnnAdF2d","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The cost of `full` was mostly a lookup bug, not the attribute layer, and PR #241 fixes it. Keep `full` as the default.\n\n**The bug:** `ComponentProps<typeof X>` compared the path of every project and dependency component on each reference. #241 indexes those lookups by name. Output is byte-identical to #235 on all five corpora, and CI hasn't run on #241 yet.\n\n**Cost of `full` over the old default after the fix** (one-shot extract, dependencies loaded, no cache):\n\n| Corpus | Time | Peak memory |\n|---|---|---|\n| shadcn | 124 → 127 ms (+2%) | 200 → 260 MiB |\n| antd | 44 → 48 ms (+9%) | 95 → 108 MiB |\n| Mantine | 54 → 68 ms (+26%) | 111 → 143 MiB |\n| Chakra | 233 → 248 ms (+6%) | 321 → 369 MiB |\n| Spectrum | 80 → 82 ms (+3%) | 148 → 160 MiB |\n\nMemory is +8% to +30%. JSON size still roughly doubles, for example shadcn 3.8 → 7.7 MB. On the Storybook path there is no measurable time cost: shadcn's first story is 112 ms before and 96 ms after, with later stories at 4–5 ms.\n\n**Lead over the others (measured on one machine):**\n- **RDT:** 22–67× faster and 3.8–9.5× less memory.\n- **react-docgen:** 17–43× faster on shadcn, antd, Mantine and Spectrum. On Chakra the lead is only 4×, and that run hit 56 errors on 126 files, so treat it as unreliable. On Chakra, react-docgen also uses less memory.\n- **Per story:** react-docgen's median is 0.75–4.2 ms per file, comparable to our later stories. We don't win on that.\n\nEarlier I told you our lead over react-docgen was probably small, and that was wrong for one-shot extracts. It is large there, though it has no advantage on per-story latency.\n\n**Why keep `full`:** it is the only mode that returns the `@types/react` props. Recall against RDT on those props:\n\n| Mode | Recall |\n|---|---|\n| react-docgen | 0% |\n| old default | 0–0.3% |\n| curated | 23–55% |\n| `full` | 92–99% |\n\n**Dropped:** sharing the element attribute layer gave no gain, since most attributes come through the interface chain.\n\n**Still open:**\n- #235's Scorecard speed gate needs re-checking against the lower numbers.\n- The oracle matched-rate baseline is stale.\n- The RDT timings are earlier runs, not re-run today.\n- The fork left a local branch `perf/shared-element-layer` behind for you to delete.\n\nMerge #241 before or with #235.\n\nresult: The `full` default is justified. PR #241, stacked on #235, fixes a name-lookup scan that made `full` cost up to 31%. It now costs 2–9% on four of five corpora and 26% on Mantine, with identical output. We lead RDT by 22–67× and react-docgen by 17–43× on four corpora, and `full` returns 92–99% of the `@types/react` props. #241's CI hasn't run yet."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2991,"cache_read_input_tokens":148375,"output_tokens":1101,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2991,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1101,"cache_read_input_tokens":148375,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2991,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2991},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"e2d1d43e-3704-49f7-b61b-ce51e39ea985","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgRUTmQWtJBwaejBEPdX1","requestRef":"66275ecf-c48f-4dba-aa1d-792c28e53555","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"2c5baf75-c194-4caf-be63-21e92e7169e4","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:24:24.651Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"docs/cleanup-stale-docs-adrs","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
