h 0% false positives at 1.05 and 1.10 on every corpus. On CI, N=5 only slipped on chakra (5% at 1.05). Locally, antd needs N≥9. N=3 is too noisy (antd 20% at 1.05).\n\n**Runner differences:**\n- **CI:** AMD EPYC 7763 and AMD EPYC 9V74 (4 vCPU, 16 GB). Per-run wall time is 86–179 ms with dependency loading off. Wall noise is as small as locally.\n- **Local:** Apple machine (`Valinor-2`). I couldn't read the CPU model because `sysctl` is blocked in the sandbox. Per-run wall time is 38–241 ms.\n- **RSS:** much noisier on CI, with run-to-run swings up to 12%, against 2% locally. I haven't tested the cause. My guess is allocator and thread timing, so a single-thread RSS measurement might be quieter.\n\n**Scope notes:**\n- **Configuration:** the local runs used the installed corpora. The CI runs used the scorecard's sparse source-only corpora with `--no-load-dependencies`, which is the configuration the proposal's gate would use.\n- **Heavy path:** I didn't run CI with dependencies loaded. That would need the multi-GB parity installs.\n\n**Recommended gate:**\n- Wall time at **1.10×** (the 1.05 line sits inside observed noise locally).\n- RSS at **1.20×**, since 1.15 left only 0.03 of headroom over the worst CI sample.\n- Median of **9** interleaved runs per side, alternating which side goes first.\n- Re-run the failing corpus once before failing the job.\n- This also cuts the timed runs by about 40% against 15.\n\nA real regression is well clear of the gate: the ones we merged unseen were +38% and +47%. A gate this tight would also catch a +10% regression like `full`'s.\n\n**Scratch artifacts and cleanup:**\n- **Scratch branch:** `scratch/gate-calibration` (commits `9fc15694`, `d121d902`) holds `.github/workflows/gate-calibration.yml` and `scripts/aa.py`. It has no PR and I merged nothing.\n- **Delete the remote branch:** `git push origin --delete scratch/gate-calibration`\n- **Local worktree:** it's nested under this worktree at `.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0/.claude/worktrees/gate-calibration`. Remove it with `git worktree remove` and delete the local branch.\n- **Result files:** in `$CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp`: `aa-local.json`, `aa-local-nodeps.json`, `ci1/aa-ci.json`, `ci2/aa-ci.json`, plus `aa.py` and `aa_report.py`.\n\nresult: Base-against-base noise on the speed gate is low. Wall-time ratios stay within 1.037 at p95 on all five corpora on both CI runs and locally, so a 1.10× threshold gave no false failures on CI. Peak RSS is noisier on CI (up to 1.12×), so gate it at 1.20×. N=9 interleaved runs per side is enough, with a re-run-once rule as insurance.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>206361</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>50</tool_uses><duration_ms>1762974</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>\n</system-reminder>"}]}}
