{"parentUuid":"414a0324-bdb1-48e8-a76a-b6f31acc49ef","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRZCG8JVhTbBanVK78Mb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The speed gate is quiet enough to be reliable: base against base, wall time stayed within 1.037× at p95 on every corpus, on both CI runs and locally. Nothing is built from this yet.\n\n**Recommended gate:**\n- Wall time at **1.10×**.\n- Peak memory at **1.20×**, not 1.15×.\n- Median of **9** interleaved runs per side, alternating which side goes first. That is 9 instead of 15, about 40% fewer timed runs, and still 0% false positives on CI at 1.05 and 1.10.\n- Re-run the failing corpus once before failing. That removes every false positive at 1.10, including one local shadcn outlier of 1.22. I was pushing and downloading in parallel when it happened, so the local deps-on numbers are slightly pessimistic.\n\n**What it shows:**\n- **Wall time:** across 200 CI trials, nothing crossed 1.05.\n- **Memory on CI:** noisier, with swings up to 12% run to run, against 2% locally. At 1.15 the worst CI sample left only 0.03 of headroom, which is why the memory line goes to 1.20. The fork hasn't found the cause. Its guess is allocator and thread timing.\n- **Detection:** the regressions we merged unseen were +38% and +47%. A gate this tight would also have caught a +10% regression like `full`'s.\n\n**Caveats:**\n- The CI runs used the scorecard's source-only corpora with dependency loading off, which is the configuration the proposed gate would use. I haven't tested the heavy dependencies-loaded path on CI, since that needs the multi-GB parity installs.\n- The fork was still running background work when it reported, so this may be an interim result.\n\n**Cleanup:** delete the remote scratch branch with `git push origin --delete scratch/gate-calibration`. The fork's nested worktree needs `git worktree remove` and a local branch delete.\n\nWith the thresholds settled, the implementation waits only on the open stack merging. I can start the three deletion PRs once it lands: speed gate, output diff, weekly record. The result files are in `$CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp`.\n\nresult: Gate calibration is done. Wall-time noise is low enough for a blocking gate at 1.10× with a median of 9 interleaved runs per side and a re-run-once rule. Memory needs 1.20×, because CI swings up to 12%. The gate itself is not built yet and waits on the open stack merging."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3351,"cache_read_input_tokens":153599,"output_tokens":822,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3351,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":822,"cache_read_input_tokens":153599,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3351,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3351},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"eabbfbb6-88bb-4500-bad6-4ccbb0d98a65","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgRZCFpCJwBvnxFKauRAA","requestRef":"e4fdca53-17f9-4211-85df-11aec579ab09","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"6598c2bc-9738-4152-94d6-41426dfa67cd","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:26:30.310Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308",