{"parentUuid":"e5695877-84e0-4bae-b0ac-9242901b0402","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRjbHn5YWLPpfsZXbnJV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Two follow-ups are running, both chosen to avoid colliding with the open stack. Nothing has merged yet, so everything is still on the merge order I gave you.\n\n- **`validate-audit`** is read-only.\n  - It goes through `apps/validate` (about 1,990 lines) and decides keep, fold or delete for each part.\n  - It judges each part against the measurement proposal and `parity.py`/`scorecard.py`, using git history and actual usage.\n  - It writes `$CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp/validate-audit.md`.\n- **`forwardref-detection`** opens a PR against `main`.\n  - It finds out why `ref` is missing on antd `Breadcrumb` and Spectrum `TreeView`, and fixes it by shape with no library names.\n  - It adds tests that assert the exact prop set, and checks the five corpora so only the intended `ref` additions differ.\n\n**Held back:**\n- **Readonly, index signatures, `RefObject` (task #42):** these would conflict with #233's function-flag changes. They go after the stack lands.\n- **Gate implementation:** the three deletion PRs wait for the stack to merge, because they edit the scripts it touches.\n- **Allow-list cleanup and the ADR 0013/0023/0024 retirement:** both follow the merges.\n\nI'll report as each finishes. I haven't merged anything, and the merge order from my last message stands. Do you want to start merging so the held-back items can proceed?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2288,"cache_read_input_tokens":160279,"output_tokens":491,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2288,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":