{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"remove","timestamp":"2026-10-26T23:44:32.031Z","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>acca5785196919f20</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01WC6gGkcCMrmipNoDviC7X4</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/acca5785196919f20.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Audit apps/validate\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Audit of `apps/validate` against the measurement proposal is written to `/Users/gabe/.claude/jobs/ba6a68d6/tmp/validate-audit.md`. No code changed and no PRs were opened.\n\n`apps/validate` is two things stuck together:\n\n- **Keep the TS 7.1 oracle (760 lines with its test).** `scripts/parity.py oracle` runs it weekly, and it found real extraction bugs on 10-23 and 10-24. The package's dependencies also stay, since `scripts/parity-rdt.mjs` and `scripts/scorecard-rdt.mjs` resolve RDT and typescript from it, and CI's `tsx` comes from it.\n- **Delete the July fixtures harness (about 1,250 lines).** That covers `compare`, `analyze`, `parity.ts`, `baseline`, `run-ours`, `run-react-docgen-typescript`, `run-semantic`, `fixtures`, `types`, `bench-cold.sh` and `moon.yml`.\n  - Nothing in CI, the justfile or `scripts/` runs it. The only trigger is the `validate:compare` moon task, which no workflow invokes.\n  - Its baselines are gitignored, and its last substantive change was 2026-07-25.\n  - `parity.py` and `scorecard.py` took over its job, and the proposal's weekly record replaces `bench-cold.sh`.\n- **Fold `run-react-docgen.ts` first.** It is the only place react-docgen runs. Port it (about 60 lines) to `scripts/parity-rdg.mjs` next to `parity-rdt.mjs`, as the third tool of the weekly record, then delete it.\n- **Net result:** about 1,990 lines becomes about 800, with no committed baselines.\n- **Docs to update:** `docs/benchmarks.md` is already slated for collapse. In `docs/type-checker-integration.md`, keep the evidence table with a note that the harness was removed.\n- **Decision for the TS 7.1 backend owner:** deleting `run-semantic.ts` loses the ability to re-run \"does the tsc-api algorithm still reproduce RDT\" on a new TS beta. I judged the backend's own tests sufficient.\n- **Caveat:** \"unused\" comes from grep and git history. I ran none of the harness, so a local script outside the repo could still use it.\n- **Out of scope:** `fixtures/` stays, because `parity.py` and `equivalence.py --lazy fixtures` use it. I didn't audit it.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>194270</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>19</tool_uses><duration_ms>99874</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>","reason":"absorbed_mid_turn","commandUuid":"45e3d9a7-9a71-41d6-a1b2-26c09965600e","deliveryId":"67a0fca3-f373-4a10-8096-97f39102c365"}
