{"parentUuid":"5d5855b1-c32a-4576-b62b-d8584a4714bc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRjp8CyJpaYGoyZnecE4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YCD5EZrwGE9jbhsSZtHSdR","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Fix stack conflicts permanently","subagent_type":"fork","name":"fix-stacking","prompt":"Make the open PR set merge in sequence with zero conflicts, proven by simulation. Tool: python3 -I $CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp/sim_merge.py (chained git merge-tree in sequence, order 228,234,230,231,236,229,233,232,235,241,240; optionally pass PR numbers); it showed conflicts: (1) scripts/equivalence-allow.json — every PR with entries edits the one shared file (#230,#229,#233,#235,#241,#234); (2) crates/core/src/extractor/tests.rs between #228 and #229 (#233 stacked on #229 also). Fix, without force-pushing: (A) New small PR off main (base main): change scripts/equivalence.py + the allow-list-empty workflow + docs/tests so the allow-list is a directory scripts/equivalence-allow.d/<pr-or-topic>.json (same validator rules, no bare wildcards), main must hold no entry files, test updated; keep behaviour otherwise identical (the indexed allowed() from #235 must carry over — check scripts/equivalence.py on #235 and port that into this PR so #235 merges cleanly, or coordinate so no conflict). (B) For each PR carrying entries (#234,#230,#229,#233,#235,#241): merge A's branch into it (stack on A until A merges: if a PR must wait for A, set its base appropriately only if it truly depends; prefer merging A's branch in and noting 'merge A first') and move its entries from the shared file into its own allow.d file; the shared file should end empty/deleted on every branch. (C) Stack #229 on #228's branch (gh pr edit --base, merge #228's branch into #229, then #233 remains on #229) so tests.rs ordering is resolved, or otherwise resolve so the simulation passes. Also account for the forwardref-detection fork's new PR (check gh pr list). After each change rerun CI watch on affected PRs. Success criterion: sim_merge.py prints ok for every PR in the stated order AND each PR still has green CI. Note the simulation treats retargeted/stacked branches as merged in order, so also verify the chain bases are right (gh pr view). Rules: never force-push or merge, commits end `Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/REDACTED`, PR body for A ends with the session URL, sandbox off for git/gh, one plain git command per call, read exit codes directly, do not hard-wrap prose. Final report: table of PR, base, merge order position, sim result, CI, and the exact merge order the user should follow."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":781,"cache_read_input_tokens":168394,"output_tokens":1717,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":709},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":781,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1717,"cache_read_input_tokens":168394,"cache_creation_input_tokens":781,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":781},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01YCD5EZrwGE9jbhsSZtHSdR":{"description":"Fix stack conflicts permanently","subagent_type":"fork","name":"fix-stacking","prompt":"Make the open PR set merge in sequence with zero conflicts, proven by simulation. Tool: python3 -I $CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp/sim_merge.py (chained git merge-tree in sequence, order 228,234,230,231,236,229,233,232,235,241,240; optionally pass PR numbers); it showed conflicts: (1) scripts/equivalence-allow.json — every PR with entries edits the one shared file (#230,#