{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","id":"3b23a830-be95-459b-8556-63deb0b71437","timestamp":"2026-10-26T23:45:50.484Z","version":"2.1.308","querySource":"repl_main_thread:outputStyle:Concise","shapeHash":"30de49787603a257f4975e5cdab983aad4d3f56db15b3d01afad71bede0d6239","params":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"52012d49-5e57-40c8-9f20-cdfa8f33e61b","keep":147,"tail":["313cac905dff665746f899571ed7b1aca8554dc470d7455cd29a5442ff95b97d","43d54e4ed16c635143aa9be32ebcb74a84be6555cf8b019ac99fe66fce050be7","b25b302f3ff97946e632db140d94a6e9085d169af6be45c732e1e71ece61eb46"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",149,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"8160bf26790be812a8b59683386d089bd372fc37ae9ab1a5708da93784e7e10d"}
{"parentUuid":"97e20073-25d8-4626-95b4-186fda4d49a8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRjqKYPV3kZG4pgQxHUE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A fork is fixing the stacking, and it has to prove the fix with a simulation before reporting. Without that, my earlier \"mergeable\" checks only tested each PR against `main`, not against each other, which is why conflicts appeared once merging started.\n\n**What the simulation showed:** it merged the open PRs in sequence in a scratch run, with no branches changed. It found two conflict sources.\n- **The shared allow-list:** every PR with entries edits `scripts/equivalence-allow.json`, so #230, #229, #233, #235 and #241 all collide.\n- **`extractor/tests.rs`:** both #228 and #229 append to it. #233 sits on #229, so it inherits the collision.\n\n**The fix, in the fork:**\n1. A small new PR off `main` turns the allow-list into a directory with one file per PR. The validator rules stay the same and `main` must hold none, so a PR's entries no longer touch anyone else's.\n2. Each PR that carries entries merges that branch and moves its entries into its own file.\n3. #229 gets stacked on #228's branch, which resolves the `tests.rs` collision. #233 stays on #229.\n4. The forwardRef PR gets stacked on whatever it overlaps, as I instructed earlier.\n\nIt succeeds only when the simulation prints OK for every PR in merge order and CI is green on each. It will report a table with the exact merge order. Please hold off merging until then, so you don't hit conflicts again."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2183,"cache_read_input_tokens":169175,"output_tokens":479,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2183,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":479,"cache_read_input_tokens":169175,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2183,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2183},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"88c4f094-c13f-401f-9f4e-e94741acb8b3","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgRjqKEn97XvieP8fSLZ6","requestRef":"3b23a830-be95-459b-8556-63deb0b71437","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c410c854-8a4a-42a7-a616-9bacd4644a6a","timestamp":"2026-10-26T23:45:54.433Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"fix/forwardref-shape","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
