t `c3ff7e46` before the rebase; the pushed hash differs):\n- One helper, `is_forward_ref_call`, in `crates/core/src/extractor/component.rs`.\n- It sets the existing `DetectionRule::ForwardRef`, so there's no schema bump and no library names.\n- New test file `crates/core/tests/forward_ref_shapes.rs` asserts exact prop sets, and I confirmed it fails without the fix.\n- Changeset: `.changeset/forward-ref-by-shape.md`.\n\n**Before and after** (deps on, `full`, five corpora):\n\n| Corpus | Gained `ref` | Lost any prop |\n|---|---|---|\n| Mantine | 0 | 0 |\n| Chakra | 1 (`Group`) | 0 |\n| shadcn | 0 | 0 |\n| antd | 9 | 0 |\n| Spectrum | 353 | 0 |\n\nEvery difference is the `ref` prop and nothing else. Storybook parity, props Storybook lists that the addon lacks: antd 34 → 33 (the remaining 33 are the `PurePanel` pairing mismatch), Spectrum 1 → 0.\n\n**Verification:** 735 core tests passed on my earlier base, and `cargo clippy -p caliper-docgen-core -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n**Stacking** (per the coordinator's message):\n- **Base:** I branched from the top of #235's chain and set the PR base to `perf/component-lookups-by-name` (#241). The `ref` rule only exists with #235.\n- **Rebase:** #241's head moved while I worked, so I rebased my one unpushed commit onto it. No force-push.\n- **Trial merges:** `git merge-tree` against `main` and every open PR head (#228–#236, #239–#241, #243) is clean.\n- **#239 exception:** the release PR conflicts in `crates/binding/Cargo.toml`. It conflicts the same way with bare #241, so my change doesn't cause it.\n- **New tests:** they're in a new file, not appended to `extractor/tests.rs`.\n- **Merge order:** #232, #235, #241, then #244.\n\n**Needs attention:** #241's head (`1bfa80df`) doesn't compile its tests. `crates/core/src/extractor/tests.rs` has an unclosed function near line 1277, where the tagged-factory test and the #228 test were merged together. I didn't touch that file, so #244's CI fails until it's repaired.\n\n**Limits:**\n- The check matches the name `forwardRef`, so another library's `forwardRef` would count too. Matching by import source is a follow-up.\n- `memo(forwardRef(function…))` without type arguments is still not detected, since `try_hoc_wrapped` returns early for it.\n- The Spectrum harness run used the prebuilt napi binding. Its post-step needed the sandbox off (`spawn EPERM`).\n\nLeft over: the branch `fix/forwardref-by-shape` and the PR body temp file is removed. Scratch scripts are in `$CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp` (`fr_diff.py`, `trial_merge.py`).\n\nresult: PR #244 makes `ref` appear on `forwardRef` components by call shape: antd gains 9, Spectrum 353, Chakra 1, nothing is lost, and Spectrum parity goes from 1 missing prop to 0. It is stacked on #241 and merges cleanly with every open PR, but its CI fails until #241's head, whose `tests.rs` doesn't compile, is repaired.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>267344</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>120</tool_uses><duration_ms>827527</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>\n</system-reminder>"}]}}
