{"parentUuid":"d279a588-e0f6-47dd-9099-5dc30713262c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRketjiR9mbZ7pQFqpsB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"PR #244 is open: `ref` now appears on `forwardRef` components by call shape. It isn't green yet, because a compile break is on the branch below it.\n\n**What #244 does:** antd gains 9 `ref` props, Spectrum 353 and Chakra 1. No other prop changed or was lost. Spectrum parity goes from 1 missing prop to 0.\n\n**Problem found:** #241's head (`1bfa80df`) doesn't compile its tests. `crates/core/src/extractor/tests.rs` has an unclosed function near line 1277, where the #229 and #228 tests were merged together. #244 can't pass CI until that's repaired.\n\n**Stacking:** #244 sits on #241 and trial-merges cleanly with `main` and every other open PR except the release PR #239, which already conflicts the same way with bare #241. The merge order for the chain is #232, #235, #241, #244.\n\n**What I did:** I sent the stacking fork the break. It must run `cargo test -p caliper-docgen-core --no-run` on each head it touches, repair the break on the branch where it started rather than only on #241, and add #244 to the simulation. It will also report which branch introduced the break. It had already added the allow-list directory PR, #243, to its order.\n\n**Limits of #244:** it matches the name `forwardRef`, so another library's `forwardRef` would count too, and `memo(forwardRef(function…))` without type arguments isn't detected yet.\n\nHold off merging until the stacking fork reports."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1408,"cache_read_input_tokens":173833,"output_tokens":495,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1408,