{"parentUuid":"8e80c61d-05a4-476b-9b5b-1ee3d303c59a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS9MzfcJ2qaKwp2smQT3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I checked every open PR against the latest `main`. None has a real conflict by my checks, but 11 of the 13 branches are 2 commits behind, and the fork `sync-main` is updating them. #230 and #231 are already current.\n\n**What's behind:** #229, #232, #233, #234, #235, #236, #240, #241, #243, #244, and the release PR #239. The two commits are #245 and the earlier merges.\n\n**Rebase:** I told the fork to merge `main` into each branch rather than rebase. A rebase rewrites history and needs a force-push, which your standing rule forbids. If you want true rebases, say so and I'll make an exception for these branches.\n\n**Order:**\n- **First:** the `main`-based PRs: #243, #234, #236, #240, #229 and #232.\n- **Then:** their children, each after merging its parent's updated head: #233 after #229, #235 after #232, #241 after #235, and #244 after #241.\n- **#239:** the release PR is generated by Callisto, so the fork leaves it alone if it conflicts.\n\n**Checks:** it runs `cargo test --no-run` before each push, re-runs the merge simulation at the end, and watches CI on every PR until green. It fixes failures on the branch where they start.\n\nIf you're seeing conflicts on GitHub that don't match this, tell me which PR and I'll look at it directly. I'll report with a table when the fork finishes."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1484,"cache_read_input_tokens":196430,"output_tokens":463,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1484,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens