{"parentUuid":"7786d104-1a07-48ab-9fa1-74d9893408c0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS9TkDNXwQoGwWFrkCqS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Right now no pair of open PRs conflicts. I merged every possible pair of the 12 heads (excluding the release PR #239), skipping pairs where one branch already contains the other, and found 0 conflicting pairs. That is a stronger test than my earlier one, which only checked a single merge order.\n\nI also tried to count which PRs touch the same files, but the numbers were wrong because the branches carry merged copies of `main`, so I discarded them. Textual conflicts are the only thing I can vouch for.\n\n**Why conflicts kept appearing:** I tested one merge order and called it clean, but conflicts depend on order and on what lands on `main` in between. The real causes were files edited by several PRs. They were the shared allow-list, `extractor/tests.rs`, and the ADR and docs files. The stack was also being rewritten while I tested it.\n\n**Tactical stacking I'd apply:**\n- **Chains stay:** #229 → #233 and #232 → #235 → #241 → #244. Each child contains its parent, so they merge in order.\n- **Independent PRs stay on `main`:** #230, #231, #234, #236, #243. They have no pair conflicts.\n- **#240 goes first, not last.** The docs cleanup edits files that #232, #233 and #235 also touch (the ADR README and `STATUS.md`). After it lands, the others only merge `main`, and the simulation says that resolves cleanly.\n- **Rule from now on:** any new PR that touches a file another open PR touches gets stacked on that PR, or waits. New tests go in new files, not appended to shared ones.\n- **Before each merge:** rerun `python3 -I $CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp/pairs.py`. It takes seconds. After a merge, `main` moves, so rerun it before the next one.\n\nThe `sync-main` fork is still pushing updates, so heads are moving. I'll rerun the pair test when it finishes and tell you if anything changed.\n\nShould I make the pair test a check in CI? It would catch this before merge, but it adds machinery, which you told me to avoid. I'd keep it as a local script."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1390,"cache_read_input_tokens":201054,"output_tokens":1245,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":547},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1390,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1245,"cache_read_input_tokens":201054,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1390,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1390},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"82cbcd25-6ad0-4c78-99e0-f53bce3fbf3c","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgS9TjuH367q59xhmxaiZ","requestRef":"5df794ad-8a8e-4c00-8c75-8bf4c7961cf6","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"3f8c8f66-a545-484a-a56c-cd3c237fcd8d","timestamp":"2026-10-27T04:55:53.048Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"fix/forwardref-by-shape","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
