{"parentUuid":"3d9acef8-d160-4efc-b0b2-ad518d63ff3c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS9cQgdRE48ysJ5gHMUo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019ZEKka2NYyDoUdgYrYsAfX","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Fix equivalence crash and scorecard flake","subagent_type":"fork","name":"fix-gate-crashes","prompt":"Two CI failures on open PRs. (1) #230 (fix/type-losses) Equivalence job crashes: scripts/equivalence.py line ~151 `for name, prop_id in sets[set_id].items()` -> KeyError: 'WebkitAppearance' (run 40451111648). Diagnose from the canonical JSON the binaries emit (interned prop sets / name lists, ADR 0018 + SCHEMA_VERSION on main) versus what canonical() expects; reproduce locally on chakra/shadcn with the base (origin/main) binary and #230's head binary; find whether main's script is wrong for current output or #230 genuinely emits a malformed set reference (the latter is a product bug — fix it in #230's branch). Add a regression test in scripts/test_equivalence.py. Because #243 (ci/allow-list-directory) also rewrites scripts/equivalence.py, stack any script fix on #243's branch (separate small PR with base ci/allow-list-directory, or push to #243 if it's the same concern) — do NOT create a conflict with #243; trial-merge against every open PR head with python3 -I $CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp/pairs.py and sim_merge.py before pushing. (2) #231 Scorecard failed 'chakra: 103.4 ms is more than 1.1x main's 71.7 ms' though #231 only touches storybook/export code: re-run the Scorecard job for #231 (gh run rerun --failed) up to twice and compare against the calibration in $CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp (gate-calibration results); decide noise vs real; if noise, report the numbers and recommend (e.g. median of several runs in the scorecard PR job per measurement-proposal.md) but don't build the redesign. Rules: never force-push or merge, no blanket allow-list entries, commits end `Claude-Session: https://claude.