{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","id":"a57d2a31-380a-45e5-8abf-81bdb8954cf5","timestamp":"2026-10-27T04:59:03.771Z","version":"2.1.308","querySource":"repl_main_thread:outputStyle:Concise","shapeHash":"30de49787603a257f4975e5cdab983aad4d3f56db15b3d01afad71bede0d6239","params":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"3342decf-7650-4fe0-987e-ea04c4e044a8","keep":261,"tail":["7bb2130fbfea0576c74bf01d1415b9492ca0d4796ac48ad5a23079b01262716a","8dd4f895f6dfd3bfad69cf7820648f41c1f5db9bb180dffe52bae81556d80e74","f5d2d0e3cafedd1578800bac6e9f69af29c6b9e95f4f73fc3885773e898cb3da"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",263,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"291d8f00011043d5979162992b4a865774cf3f61265f1f1cd2388662d52760e0"}
{"parentUuid":"92c8c3bc-5809-4cd4-8834-66a7cf93ea30","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS9if5UbZurbBREFdSdb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Today we use trails as a mirror of our PRs, and that adds almost nothing. I'd use them to plan, but only in a light way.\n\n**What they are, from the CLI:**\n- A trail captures intent across repositories and branches.\n- It holds changes (branches or PRs), comments, agent findings and approvals, and it can merge a change.\n- The \"Entire Gates\" check on our PRs links to a trail.\n\n**What we have:**\n- `entire trail list` shows 45 open trails.\n- Each is one auto-created trail per PR, such as #34 (the docs cleanup), which has exactly one change: `docs/cleanup-stale-docs-adrs`.\n- Trails #1–#33 belong to old PRs that merged long ago but still show as open.\n- Nothing is grouped by goal, so nothing tells us where the work stands.\n\n**How I'd use them:**\n1. **One trail per goal, not per PR.** For example:\n   - \"`full` as default\": #235, #241, #244 and the cost follow-ups.\n   - \"Measurement redesign\": the speed gate, output diff, weekly record and the `apps/validate` deletion.\n   - \"Homebrew auto-update\": #236 and the tap repo's side.\n   - \"Docs and ADR cleanup\".\n\n   A trail can link branches across repos, so work in the tap or in `monokl` can sit under the same intent.\n2. **Put the stack in the trail.** Link each PR's branch with `entire trail link`. The parent and child relationship of the chains then lives next to the intent, which is where we lose track today.\n3. **Use findings and approvals for review.** Agent findings go on the trail instead of in chat.\n4. **Close the stale ones.** The 30-odd trails for merged PRs should be closed with `entire trail update`.\n\n**What I'd skip:** per-PR trails, comment threads duplicating GitHub, and any ceremony beyond the above. You asked for simple, and this is useful only if it stays that way.\n\n**What I don't know:**\n- I don't know exactly what the Entire Gates check enforces. It failed earlier on #243, #240 and #241 and then went green, and the fork found it wanted branches up to date with `main`. I haven't read its rules.\n- Whether closing a trail affects the gate on its PR is untested.\n\nI can set up the four goal trails and link the current branches, and close the stale ones. Closing trails is outward-facing, so I'd list them first for your OK. Want that?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":748,"cache_read_input_tokens":218514,"output_tokens":803,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":748,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":803,"cache_read_input_tokens":218514,"cache_creation_input_tokens":748,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":748},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"b73abb4f-2d64-46bb-bef3-5e886d01ddf6","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgS9ieevvdNYuqMEp2ZAP","requestRef":"a57d2a31-380a-45e5-8abf-81bdb8954cf5","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"cff19ae1-b5a4-431a-bfb6-858fe2f88b46","timestamp":"2026-10-27T04:59:10.911Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"fix/forwardref-by-shape","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
