{"parentUuid":"c14024d6-e687-453d-8d3d-07b31f7450fb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS9jgue3Cyv4ernyrdT5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Your suspicion was right, and the cause wasn't how I stacked. `main` was moved backwards: it was force-pushed from `ab051882` to an old commit, and I confirmed it.\n\n- **What happened:** at 03:14 UTC on 10-27, the activity log shows a force-push by `castrog` from `ab051882` (the tip after #228 merged) back to `ef9136ed`. The merge queue then merged #245 on top. `ab051882` is no longer an ancestor of `origin/main`, and `scripts/equivalence.py` no longer exists on `main`.\n- **What was lost from `main`:** #127 through #228 — lazy resolution, the equivalence and parity scripts, the workflows and ADRs. The commits are still on GitHub and in the PR branches, but they aren't on `main`.\n- **Why CI and merges broke:**\n  - Every PR now compares against a `main` that lacks the work its branch builds on.\n  - #230's Equivalence crash and #231's Scorecard 1.44× are likely symptoms of that, not bugs in those PRs. The fork didn't reproduce the crash, so this is the likely cause rather than a verified one.\n  - The earlier conflicts and \"behind\" states are the same problem.\n- **Where the stack stands:** the fork had it clean before the rewind. Its last simulation ran against the broken `main`, so it proves nothing now. I pushed nothing to `main`, and I can't force-push there.\n\n**Fix, which only you can do.** Was the rewind deliberate? If not, restore `main` to the last good commit:\n\n```\ngit push --force-with-lease=main:b7fb9a2bce61f3346a163b9ebf011b84bcf6ed36 origin ab051882:main\n```\n\nBranch protection and the merge queue may block that, so it may need admin rights. #245 (`0f1b84df`, \"chore: fix entire and cleanup hooks\") then needs re-applying on top of the restored `main`. It deleted `.cursor` and `.opencode` hook files, so check it against the restored tree. The PR branches already contain #245's commits, because the fork merged the broken `main` into them, so they would bring it back when merged.\n\nIf the rewind was deliberate, tell me what it was meant to do. I'd then need to rework the merge order from the old state.\n\nOnce `main` is restored I'll rerun the pair test and simulation, bring each branch up to the restored `main`, and watch CI to green. I haven't started on the trails setup.\n\nneeds input: Was the force-push of `main` deliberate? If not, someone with admin rights needs to restore `main` to `ab051882` and re-apply #245."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2482,"cache_read_input_tokens":221536,"output_tokens":1179,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":308},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2482,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1179,"cache_read_input_tokens":221536,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2482,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2482},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"0b59cdb7-5a01-4ce6-a5d7-1fbc2f0c4aab","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgS9jgbnf3Nczo8SCPj9K","requestRef":"81ef95b9-9255-45d6-8cb5-19184effc4be","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"ed43cf5f-b91d-4dc5-a152-1b60a2e39c8a","timestamp":"2026-10-27T04:59:27.008Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2