{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","id":"895bf040-ec0a-4940-8a52-7d62d54fc3be","timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:01:56.036Z","version":"2.1.308","querySource":"repl_main_thread:outputStyle:Concise","shapeHash":"30de49787603a257f4975e5cdab983aad4d3f56db15b3d01afad71bede0d6239","params":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"ddfc21ed-71f1-415d-b232-06b872affc11","keep":272,"tail":["02a426884abb9b0b2c19130fccbb88c2acc5cb2aed47a0a069e1099c04ac9927","b180b8ffd5a1dbda59891b0b68b54fc143f0640349a55174ec76e234077201ec","4732d1ded8271694a1b12cc95df227f3596b7aa6f825207e3d947cf646fc1183"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",274,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"131bf488c426adc348777a013b10aa5fcc3ed40cb14ca47f647dc8440f1146cc"}
{"parentUuid":"fc8aff33-fb52-4d79-a7a8-eb3202326872","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS9wMRTByu8MLy5VgCkU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Many failures, and they are all from the base: `main` still points at the old commit, so every Equivalence and Scorecard run compares against the wrong build. Nothing in the PRs themselves has been shown broken.\n\n`origin/main` is still `b7fb9a2b`, the post-rewind tip (#245 on top of the old #125 commit). Until it is restored, CI on these PRs will keep failing.\n\n| PR | Failing |\n|---|---|\n| #230 | Equivalence |\n| #231 | Equivalence |\n| #234 | Equivalence, Scorecard |\n| #243 | Equivalence, Scorecard |\n| #232, #233, #236, #240 | Scorecard |\n| #229, #235, #241, #244 | none yet; 13–16 checks pending |\n| #239 | none |\n\nEverything that has finished failing is Equivalence or Scorecard, the two checks that build `main` and compare against it. That matches the cause the fork found. The Scorecard failures are the speed gate comparing against an old, faster build, so they're not trustworthy either way.\n\n**What fixes it:** restore `main` to `ab051882`, which only you can do:\n\n```\ngit push --force-with-lease=main:b7fb9a2bce61f3346a163b9ebf011b84bcf6ed36 origin ab051882:main\n```\n\nThen re-apply #245. Branch protection or the merge queue may block that push and need admin rights.\n\n**Not doing:** I'm not trying to make the PRs pass against the wrong base. Allow-listing differences or relaxing the gates to get green would hide the real state.\n\nOnce `main` is restored, I'll rerun the pair test and simulation, bring each branch up to date, and watch CI until it is green. Can you restore `main`, or tell me the rewind was intentional?\n\nneeds input: restore `main` to `ab051882` and re-apply #245, or tell me the rewind was deliberate."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1399,"cache_read_input_tokens":225270,"output_tokens":626,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1399,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":626,"cache_read_input_tokens":225270,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1399,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1399},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"013768fd-7153-40f4-9027-b059a714cbd9","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgS9wMAKeJq8x3RL2x9WW","requestRef":"895bf040-ec0a-4940-8a52-7d62d54fc3be","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c026bb5f-c0cb-48e3-8b18-884d7e863a22","timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:02:01.275Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"fix/forwardref-by-shape","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
