{"parentUuid":"8b1bedb4-1813-4eeb-a826-92bee5fba069","isSidechain":false,"type":"system","subtype":"turn_duration","durationMs":15309,"messageCount":3746,"timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:02:03.077Z","uuid":"40c1e0cb-cc09-405b-8abc-10d7af200f68","isMeta":false,"sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"fix/forwardref-by-shape","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"40c1e0cb-cc09-405b-8abc-10d7af200f68","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6c17e80f-2b7e-41c9-a155-a5afb9f7370d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"FYI from another session on understanding trails:\n\n\n\n<pasted_content id=\"d5b8\">\nI've read the trails overview and the gates page.\n\nWhat trails are:\n- A trail replaces the pull request in Entire's model. It holds the intent (title, description, type, priority), the linked branches (changes), the agent sessions, and the review evidence.\n- A change is one linked branch in one repo. Each change merges separately. The trail has open and closed status, and \"Planning\" is the phase before any branch is linked.\n- For GitHub mirrors, CI and merging still run through a linked PR. Entire review and GitHub review are separate and both must pass.\n\nGates: these are per-repo merge requirements, set under Settings → Gates:\n- Up to Date: the branch is current with its base.\n- Human Review: a minimum number of approvals, and whether a push resets them.\n- Agent Review: unresolved findings from the trail-review runner, blocking at a severity threshold you choose.\n- Checks: GitHub CI.\n\nWhat this means for your scoping question:\n- The recommended workflow starts by capturing the intent: problem, outcome, acceptance criteria. So a trail should be feature-sized with a done state, which confirms you were right about \"v1 hardening\".\n- A trail can link several branches, so the stack (#391, #393, #397, #398) could be one trail with four changes. I'd try that on the release-recovery group first. I'm inferring this from \"changes across repositories and branches\". The docs don't show several same-repo branches on one trail.\n- Acceptance criteria belong in the trail description. For the release-recovery trail that's: callisto release pending shows nothing after the 0.15.0 run.\n\nThe Entire Gates failure: the docs don't explain the check's output, so I still can't say which gate failed. The candidates are:\n- Up to Date, because I restacked branches by merging, so they may read as behind their new bases.\n- Human Review, if approvals are required.\n- Agent Review, if findings are open.\n</pasted_content id=\"d5b8\">\n"},"uuid":"1d9e2f77-0a91-4095-bf24-e2e38ae4a950","timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:03:24.775Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"human"},"promptSource":"typed","turnOrigin":"human","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":224,"turnIndex":354},"sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"fix/forwardref-by-shape","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
