{"parentUuid":"b94a547a-7798-4c01-943b-fd5f171d3e79","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgSA3uMFaUMv8razLwHFQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":720,"cache_read_input_tokens":227295,"output_tokens":1023,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":232},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":720,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1023,"cache_read_input_tokens":227295,"cache_creation_input_tokens":720,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":720},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":2007,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"d08ad3bf-4d37-407b-aaff-1d7673be81ed","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgSA3tux7gBRyF5TT6A9G","requestRef":"c2c3e24d-7b3f-49b5-afb1-8473b1e00053","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"8d88d85e-8a36-4717-9e83-4fefa52b9214","timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:03:27.662Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"fix/forwardref-by-shape","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
{"parentUuid":"8d88d85e-8a36-4717-9e83-4fefa52b9214","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgSA3uMFaUMv8razLwHFQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This fits what we've seen. The \"Entire Gates\" failures on #243, #240 and #241 were the Up to Date gate, which the stacking fork also found. The other three gates explain the BLOCKED status on PRs whose checks are all green: Human Review (approvals) or Agent Review (open findings) is the likely cause. I haven't confirmed which, because the check output doesn't say.\n\n**How I'd use trails, given that model:**\n- **One trail per goal, with a done state.** The description holds the problem, outcome and acceptance criteria. The PR is just a change inside it. Proposed trails:\n\n| Trail | Changes | Done when |\n|---|---|---|\n| `full` as default | #235, #241, #244 | Time and memory against the old default recorded; recall on `@types/react` props at 92% or better on all five corpora |\n| Measurement redesign | the speed gate, output diff and weekly record PRs, plus the `apps/validate` deletion | Speed gate at 1.10× wall and 1.20× memory; no allow-list or committed baselines on `main` |\n| Homebrew auto-update | #236 | A CLI release opens a formula PR in the tap |\n| Docs and ADR cleanup | #240 | Retired ADRs listed; stale docs removed |\n| Type-resolution gaps | #229, #230, #231, #233 | Each gap has a test asserting exact props |\n\n- **Stacks as one trail with several changes.** That is inferred from the docs. They don't show several branches from the same repo on one trail, so I'd try it on the `full` trail first. If it doesn't work, one trail per chain is the fallback.\n- **Planning phase:** anything not started yet (readonly, index signatures, `RefObject`) gets a trail with acceptance criteria and no branch. That makes it the backlog.\n- **Gates to set deliberately:** Up to Date is the one that keeps burning us. With merge commits it flips to \"behind\" after every merge. Turning it off, or using the merge queue, is your setting in Gates. Human Review and Agent Review need a decision on whether they should block at all, since you merge your own work.\n- **Cleanup:** close the stale trails for merged PRs.\n\nI haven't done any of this. Closing trails is outward-facing, so I'd list them for your OK first.\n\nThe blocker is unchanged: `main` still has to be restored to `ab051882` before CI means anything."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":720,"cache_read_input_tokens":227295,"output_tokens":1023,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":232},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":720,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1023,"cache_read_input_tokens":227295,"cache_creation_input_tokens":720,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":720},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"d08ad3bf-4d37-407b-aaff-1d7673be81ed","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgSA3tux7gBRyF5TT6A9G","requestRef":"c2c3e24d-7b3f-49b5-afb1-8473b1e00053","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"dd4a186c-423e-4442-aed6-dbad941ead47","timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:03:33.384Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"fix/forwardref-by-shape","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
