{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","id":"1777768b-ca2d-4ac6-9905-0230666ef711","timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:24:00.719Z","version":"2.1.308","querySource":"repl_main_thread:outputStyle:Concise","shapeHash":"30de49787603a257f4975e5cdab983aad4d3f56db15b3d01afad71bede0d6239","params":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"8f9e9ddd-9196-4aca-95da-7a29c3529d74","keep":302,"tail":["be53bed058819a0d482c389bc9285b41f33cabfb25bdffc0cc6bfd17a99f269d","7e77b938487c51148bf9ae3efbeb4d40f2e6dd2890f1d89067b633dcf11e737b","a69fea90ed060ad1083be6dca3d261a7e690f89879d4972b6d2a923d4b6f9d54"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",304,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"f094ffa71f22a9e64297d4cdd1d5364937cc3668efa2669135a3153bef020222"}
{"parentUuid":"b7b4d8da-fb4c-4587-92b5-3c7eb4040d62","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgSBd11rYGvmazxpiHanM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I opened PR #246, which brings back the lost history without a force-push, so you don't need admin rights.\n\n- **What it does:** it merges `ab051882` (`main` after #228) into the current `main` as a normal merge commit. A trial merge showed it is clean, since `ab051882` descends from the rewind point and #245 sits on top without conflicts.\n- **What comes back:** #127 to #228, including the lazy resolver, the equivalence, parity and scorecard scripts, the workflows, and ADRs 0013 to 0021.\n- **Why this should fix CI:** once it lands, Equivalence and Scorecard compare each PR against a `main` that has the code its branch builds on.\n\nMerge #246 first. Merging to `main` runs the release workflow, so check the `.callisto/release-decision.json` change before you merge. Its checks are just starting.\n\nAfterwards I'll merge the new `main` into each stacked branch, rerun the pair test and simulation, and watch CI to green. I'll do the same for #239.\n\nThe plain question remains whether the original force-push was intentional. If it was, #246 undoes it, and you shouldn't merge it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":610,"cache_read_input_tokens":241742,"output_tokens":377,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":610,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":377,"cache_read_input_tokens":241742,"cache_creation_input_tokens":610,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":610},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallb