{"parentUuid":"f718c84b-c1c1-4817-a3c8-580a82d2c7df","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgSBwPm5StGJXXJ546MBU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The entire fix wasn't reverted. #245 (\"chore: fix entire and cleanup hooks\") merged through a PR at 04:39 UTC and is on `main` now as `b7fb9a2b`. It changed 7 files: it deleted the `.cursor` and `.opencode` hooks and skills, and added `.entire/settings.json` and `.entire/.gitignore`.\n\n**What was reverted is everything before it.** At 03:14 UTC, someone force-pushed `main` from `ab051882` back to `ef9136ed`, the #125 version-packages merge from Oct 23. That dropped about 295 commits, #127 through #228, from `main`. #245 landed afterwards, on top of the old base.\n\n**Who did it:** the GitHub activity log attributes the force-push to `castrog`, which is your account name. I can't tell whether you ran it, or another session or tool acting as you. Nothing in this session did it.\n\n**Why it matters to #245:** #245 came out of the rewound `main`, so it is based on an Oct 23 tree. It merged cleanly onto the restored history in my trial merge, so nothing in it is lost or conflicted.\n\nPR #246 merges `ab051882` back in and keeps #245. If the force-push was meant to remove something specific, tell me what, and I'll check whether #246 would bring it back before you merge."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1237,"cache_read_input_tokens":242962,"output_tokens":654,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":209},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1237,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":654,"cache_read_input_tokens":242962,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1237,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral