{"parentUuid":"a664d288-ca4e-47d9-8421-d292416bc9f4","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"cba2c4da-b727-492a-8887-59222a5a76b3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a5e71d42220e1b7b4</task-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/a5e71d42220e1b7b4.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Update all PR branches with main\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Task: bring every open PR head up to date with `main`. The finding is bigger than that: `main` has lost its history, which explains the conflicts and the red CI.\n\n**Finding:** `main` is `ef9136ed` (10-23, the #125 release) plus #245. #245's branch started at `ef9136ed` and `main` was at that commit when it merged, so the merges from #203 to #228 are no longer in `main`'s history. I checked #222's and #228's merge commits; neither is an ancestor of `main`. GitHub still shows those PRs as merged. `main` now lacks:\n- `equivalence.py`, `parity.py` and the Equivalence, Parity and Allow-list workflows.\n- The interned output (`propSets`).\n- ADRs 0013–0021.\n\nThat is why every PR fails Equivalence with `KeyError: 'WebkitAppearance'`: `main`'s binary doesn't emit the format the script expects. I reproduced it by building `main` locally. Scorecard fails against the same stale base. The CI-only #236 fails both, with Scorecard at 1.43–1.51× on chakra, so a PR with no code change fails it.\n\n**Fix I prepared, not merged:** #247 (`fix/restore-main-history`, base `main`) merges the previous head `ab051882` (#228) back into `main`. The merge is conflict-free, keeps #245's changes, and needs no force-push. Merge it first, as a merge commit, not a squash. After it, the other PRs need one more `main` merge each.\n\n**What I did on the PRs:** before finding this, I merged `main` into every head except #239, using plain merge commits (no force-push), and pushed them. #243, #234, #236, #240, #229, #232, #233, #235, #241 and #244 are all up to date with `main`. #230 and #231 already were. The core tests compile (exit 0) at the top of the chain, and the merge simulation printed OK for all of them in order. Those merges are valid but need repeating after #247 lands.\n\n| PR | Base | Was behind main | Conflicts | CI now |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| #243, #234, #236, #240, #229, #232 | main | 2 | none | Equivalence and Scorecard fail on the stale `main` |\n| #233 | #229's branch | 2 | none | same |\n| #235 | #232's branch | 2 | none | same |\n| #241 | #235's branch | 2 | none | same |\n| #244 | #241's branch | 2 | none | passing |\n| #230, #231 | main | 0 | none | #230: Equivalence fails; #231: Equivalence and Scorecard fail |\n| #239 | main | 2 | not touched, Callisto-generated | no failures; its release may be stale after the rewind |\n\n**Left over:** a scratch worktree is removed. The scripts I used are in `$CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp` (`sync_main.py`, `sim_merge.py`, `behind.py`, `rerun_failed.sh`).\n\n**Still unknown:** who or what reset `main`. Likely an update-branch or hook action around #245, since its branch name is \"fix-entire\". Worth checking before the next merge.\n\nresult: `main` lost the merges from #203 to #228 when #245 merged on a stale base. That is why every PR conflicts or fails Equivalence. I prepared the conflict-free, no-force-push fix as PR #247, which you merge first as a merge commit. All other PR heads were merged up with `main`, and they need one more `main` merge after #247.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>253848</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>66</tool_uses><duration_ms>2399049</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"640078ee-e76e-494a-b0a4-3afd5223a30b","timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:34:24.873Z","permissionMode":"auto","origin":{"kind":"task-notification","producer":"session-task","runId":"0mvq8cay2-2c95efa0"},"promptSource":"system","turnOrigin":"task_notification","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":226,"turnIndex":360},"queueSkipAttachments":true,"sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"restore/main-history","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
