{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","id":"d2967c83-0cc3-4ec3-81b0-efb2a34dd9db","timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:34:31.790Z","version":"2.1.308","querySource":"repl_main_thread:outputStyle:Concise","shapeHash":"30de49787603a257f4975e5cdab983aad4d3f56db15b3d01afad71bede0d6239","params":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"0d41d594-73e1-44ad-8067-ba45bbc267a8","keep":313,"tail":["ccc690c06dc59472bf0be11c7cd60863b34e1215d555acbfb0ab8489a501bac3","6ebc1cb3dfc5add2f3b2dc578520bd8af3280d7350f3955c0e0885fc8de162fa","a51714b185cbf341060e935dd6700085abe00f4bacd28892a8284b1aca3209ef"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",315,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"ca948947d16745984e5d4e486594fc70f65006db44bd339367481d7fbee3a5cf"}
{"parentUuid":"12985b50-0a32-4f70-b474-c2f1d8d6738f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgSCRXAbrpFRwGNAvoXRr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Two PRs now do the same restore, #246 (mine) and #247 (the sync fork's), and their trees are identical: the diff between the branches is empty.\n\nMerge one and close the other. I'd keep #246, which already has the explanation in its body. Closing #247 is yours to confirm, since it's a PR the fork opened on your behalf.\n\n- **What the fork found:** it reproduced the CI failures by building `main` locally. `main`'s binary doesn't emit the interned output format that `scripts/equivalence.py` expects, which is the `KeyError: 'WebkitAppearance'` crash. Scorecard fails against the same stale base. It also failed on #236, a CI-only PR with no code change, which shows the failures come from the base, not the PRs.\n- **What it did to the PRs:** before finding this, it merged `main` into every head except the release PR #239, with plain merge commits and no force-push. #243, #234, #236, #240, #229, #232, #233, #235, #241 and #244 are up to date, and #230 and #231 already were. Core tests compile and the simulation was clean at the top of the chain. Those merges need repeating once the restore lands.\n- **How `main` got there:** the fork's account differs from mine. It thinks #245 merged on a stale base. The GitHub activity log shows a force-push by `castrog` at 03:14 UTC. Both agree on the result, and I haven't resolved who or what reset `main`. It's worth checking before the next merge.\n\n**Order from here:**\n1. Merge #246 as a merge commit, not a squash. Check the `.callisto/release-decision.json` change first, since merging to `main` runs the release workflow.\n2. I merge the new `main` into each stacked branch, rerun the pair test and simulation, and watch CI to green.\n3. Then the merge order I gave you earlier applies.\n\nClose #247 yourself, or tell me to."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":935,"cache_read_input_tokens":246486,"output_tokens":622,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":935,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":622,"cache_read_input_tokens":246486,"cache_creation_input_tokens":935,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":935},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"e6ae5d09-dc28-46e3-9178-c11207054da5","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgSCRWq1FySonbUsP5nvk","requestRef":"d2967c83-0cc3-4ec3-81b0-efb2a34dd9db","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"b5571a24-8654-4db8-b07b-a2a1b0e9cbfd","timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:34:36.685Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"restore/main-history","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
