{"parentUuid":"1050ae8e-2345-4735-a177-b0798297ecbd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgTH14UusnV2XbkmMHEb5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The other PRs have the same problem, and none of them is fixed. I tried to fix them, but the change was blocked, so I stopped.\n\n**What I tried:** retarget the eight PRs that are based on `main` onto the restore branch from #246, so CI compares each against a base that has the code. They are #229, #230, #231, #232, #234, #236, #240 and #243. This is the stacking rule I've been following: build on the unmerged parent. The permission check denied it, so I haven't changed any PR's base, and I won't try another route around the denial.\n\n**The other PRs:**\n- **#229, #230, #231, #232, #234, #236, #240, #243 (based on `main`):** same cause as #229. Equivalence and Scorecard compare against the rewound `main`, which doesn't emit the format `scripts/equivalence.py` expects. #236 is a CI-only change and fails the same way.\n- **#233, #235, #241, #244 (stacked on a parent branch):** these compare against their parent, so most checks are fine. They still sit on the same unrestored base, so they fail whenever a check compares against `main`.\n- **#239 (release PR):** no failures, but its release may be stale after the rewind. I haven't touched it.\n\n**Two ways to fix it. One needs you:**\n1. **Merge #246** as a merge commit, not a squash. It restores the history, so every `main`-based PR compares against the right code. I then merge the new `main` into each branch and watch CI to green. This is the cleanest and needs no base changes.\n2. **Allow me to retarget** the eight PRs to `restore/main-history` and re-trigger their CI now. CI would pass or fail on its merits before #246 merges, and GitHub retargets the PRs to `main` when #246 merges. This needs your approval to proceed.\n\nWhich do you want? Option 1 is the minimum.\n\nneeds input: merge #246, or tell me to retarget the eight `main`-based PRs onto `restore/main-history`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1746,"cache_read_input_tokens":248201,"output_tokens":761,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":115},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1746,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":761,"cache_read_input_tokens":248201,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1746,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1746},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"38dba31d-bc91-4c29-80b6-302b0514f5ec","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgTH1495AfYJgwWcC7tsp","requestRef":"237bd188-eb0d-48e7-85fd-0e0336e8ca0e","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"683f41d3-ac87-4880-b2bc-7382f7310431","timestamp":"2026-10-27T19:15:16.263Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"restore/main-history","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
