{"parentUuid":"59e75714-faf9-438f-8f95-7e88c14d6c91","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgTm67MgrLKtMKfgUwzEo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The red on #246 is built in, not a defect in the restore, and I should have said so before I told you to merge it.\n\n- **Equivalence** builds the PR's base and its head and compares them. #246's base is the rewound `main`, and #246's head is the restored code. The base binary emits the old output format, so the script crashes with `KeyError: 'WebkitAppearance'` at the same line as before.\n- **Scorecard** times the restored code against the rewound `main`. Chakra comes out 1.41× slower, because the rewound `main` lacks the Oct 24–26 work. The gate fails against a base that is older and faster. The log has chakra at 68 ms against main's 49 ms.\n- **Entire Gates** fails too. I haven't confirmed which of its gates; the likely one is Human Review.\n\nSo #246 can't pass these gates by construction. Every other PR that compares against `main` fails for the same reason. It's a bootstrap problem: once `main` has the code back, the base binary emits the new format and everything compares against the right thing.\n\n**What it needs from you:** merge #246 with an admin override of the two failing checks (Equivalence and Scorecard), and the Entire gate if it requires approval. This is a one-time exception, and it is safe because #246's tree is `ab051882` plus #245. `ab051882`'s own checks passed when #228 merged.\n\n**Then, without you:** I merge the new `main` into each stacked branch, rerun the pair test and simulation, and watch each PR to green. The red should clear, since their bases will emit the right format.\n\n**Alternative:** you restore `main` directly with the force-push command from earlier. That skips the gates entirely, but it needs admin rights too.\n\nI haven't been able to retarget the PRs myself, as the permission check blocked it. If you'd rather not override checks, allowing the retarget onto `restore/main-history` is the other route, and it lets CI judge each PR on its merits.\n\nneeds input: merge #246 with an override of Equivalence, Scorecard and the Entire gate, or allow me to retarget the `main`-based PRs onto `restore/main-history`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2308,"cache_read_input_tokens":259302,"output_tokens":1260,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":569},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2308,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1260,"cache_read_input_tokens":259302,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2308,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2308},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"48d527fc-c183-43f4-8482-2cde91d894c2","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgTm6736qN37Drrx4JACQ","requestRef":"06e5262d-1596-4c2d-9e91-c4b8965b08e4","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"d5f6700c-6a32-41e4-b342-6b3e45d1d0aa","timestamp":"2026-10-28T01:23:40.279Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"restore/main-history","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
