{"parentUuid":"238463ee-ca44-4bbf-936c-8217a1e4b24d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgTnTnxPoau8SNW6F9L4N","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"#246 no longer conflicts: GitHub shows it as MERGEABLE, though its checks are still running.\n\n**Cause:** dependabot PRs #249, #250 and #251 merged into the rewound `main` after I opened #246. They touched `pnpm-lock.yaml`, which the restore also changes, and that was the only conflict. I should have rechecked `main` before telling you the PR was ready.\n\n**Fix:** I merged the new `main` into #246's branch. For the lockfile I took the restore's version and regenerated it against the merged manifests. `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` passes, and `cargo metadata --locked` agrees with `Cargo.lock`. Pushed as a plain merge commit, with no force-push.\n\n**Checks:** the checks are rerunning now. Equivalence and Scorecard will still fail on #246, because they compare the restored code against the old `main`. That is the bootstrap problem from before, so merging #246 still needs an override of those two checks, or the retarget route.\n\n**More conflicts coming:** `main` keeps moving while it is rewound. Dependabot merged three PRs in a few hours, and each one makes #246 conflict again. The fewer hours between my fix and your merge, the better. Merging soon avoids another round.\n\nWhich way do you want to take the gates: override on #246, or let me retarget the `main`-based PRs onto the restore branch?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":238,"cache_read_input_tokens":267783,"output_tokens":460,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":238,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"inp