{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-28T01:49:06.577Z","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>af246074909220d5b</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01NaPVxfmGTtPiWctcM9R32a</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/af246074909220d5b.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Clear PR conflicts against restore branch\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>I merged `origin/restore/main-history` into every PR branch, resolved the conflicts and pushed, with no force-pushes and no merges. #246 had already merged into `main` as `3d524193` (01:48 UTC) before I finished, so all of these branches are now behind `main` by that one merge commit.\n\n- **Conflicts:** none. Every merge was clean, including #243, #240 and #232, which had been conflicting.\n- **Verification:** each branch passed `cargo metadata --locked`, `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile --lockfile-only`, `cargo fmt --check` and `cargo test -p caliper-docgen-core --no-run` before I pushed it. #240's first push hit a transient network timeout and succeeded on the retry.\n- **Simulations:** the pair test shows 0 conflicting pairs. The merge simulation prints OK for all 12 PRs in order, both with #246 first and against the real `main` after it merged.\n\n| PR | Base | Mergeable | Checks now |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| #243 | main | yes, BLOCKED | Scorecard and Entire Gates fail; 2 pending |\n| #240 | main | yes, BLOCKED | Scorecard and Entire Gates fail; 2 pending |\n| #234, #236, #232 | main | yes, BLOCKED | none failing; 14 pending |\n| #229, #231 | main | yes, BLOCKED | none failing; 17 pending |\n| #230 | main | not yet computed | none failing |\n| #233 | #229's branch | yes, BLOCKED | none failing; 17 pending |\n| #235 | #232's branch | yes, BLOCKED | none failing; 17 pending |\n| #241 | #235's branch | yes, BLOCKED | none failing; 17 pending |\n| #244 | #241's branch | yes, UNSTABLE | none failing; 17 pending |\n\n- **Failing checks on #243 and #240:** those two failed before my last push. Scorecard is the speed gate, and Entire Gates is most likely the Up to Date gate. I haven't read the logs, and both PRs have pending reruns. I didn't allow-list or relax anything.\n- **Behind `main`:** each branch is 1 commit behind, the #246 merge commit. The simulation shows no content conflict. Merging `main` into each would clear the Up to Date gate, and I didn't do it, so it's one more round for the parent to decide.\n- **Not touched, as instructed:**\n  - #239 (release PR) is 11 commits behind `main`.\n  - #247 duplicates #246 and still fails Equivalence, Scorecard and Entire Gates.\n  - #248 (dependabot) fails Lint, Test, Coverage, MSRV and others. Those failures were not investigated.\n\nI committed only merge commits, one per branch, with the session trailer. The branch heads I pushed:\n\n| PR | Head after push |\n|---|---|\n| #243 | `e76e98b8` |\n| #240 | `685a4c63` |\n| #232 | `f3a24208` |\n| #234 | `4940f4ed` |\n| #236 | `f3dfbb0d` |\n| #231 | `9e03b0d1` |\n| #230 | `19b34149` |\n| #229 | `1ca929d1` |\n| #233 | `503e6125` |\n| #235 | `3507d8eb` |\n| #241 | `38e9506a` |\n| #244 | `eb5c40e3` |\n\nLocal scratch branches `cc-229` to `cc-244` (eleven in all) remain in this worktree and can be deleted. The verification helper is `$CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp/verify.sh`, and `sim_merge.py` now lists #246 first.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>299778</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>70</tool_uses><duration_ms>395991</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
