{"parentUuid":"c11c7220-2c0e-4b7b-a23d-280ff3ef9dfb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgTo4dfGMDDnaYtikxR8m","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The conflicts are cleared. The fork merged the restore branch into every PR with no content conflicts, and #246 has since merged into `main` as `3d524193`. Equivalence and Scorecard now compare against a base that has the code, so their failures should reflect the PRs themselves for the first time.\n\nA new fork, `green-the-stack`, is driving every PR to green:\n1. It merges the new `main` into each branch, bottom-up, which clears the Up to Date gate.\n2. It reads every failing log. Real product failures are fixed on the branch where they start. Intended output changes go in the per-PR allow-list file with narrow entries and no wildcards. A speed failure is rerun once and compared against the calibration data.\n3. It identifies which Entire gate fails on each trail, so we know whether it's Up to Date or a review gate.\n4. It reports whether the release PR #239 needs regenerating, and why the dependabot bump #248 fails: the bump or the old base.\n\nIt leaves #247, the duplicate restore PR, alone. You can close it now that #246 is in.\n\nIt will report a table with every PR's checks and the exact merge order. I haven't merged anything, and I won't."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1491,"cache_read_input_tokens":276161,"output_tokens":384,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1491,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":384,"cache_read_input_tokens":276161,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1491,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ep