{"parentUuid":"c7c9c574-013d-4dad-aae6-fb17e1050e55","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgTq9RcM5KXE7xUtL8UdR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The re-sign was blocked as a destructive git action. I didn't force-push anything and I'm not trying another route around the block.\n\n**State:** I stopped the fork that was producing unsigned commits, so nothing new is being pushed unsigned. No branch has been rewritten, and all 12 PR heads are as they were.\n\n**What I was about to do:** re-sign the 12 PR branches by replacing each with one signed commit that has the identical tree, so the code doesn't change. The `--force-with-lease` push would be pinned to each branch's current SHA and run once per branch, and I'd back up the old heads first. Your \"Go ahead\" answered a question that listed three options, so I read it as the first. The permission check wants that authorization stated explicitly.\n\n**What each way costs:**\n- **Force-push re-sign (what I planned):** every PR gets signed commits. Each branch's history collapses to one commit, so the per-commit messages are lost, though the PR title and body stay. CI reruns on all 12 PRs. Entire may need to relink the trails to the rewritten branches.\n- **Merge as they are:** no rewrite, and GitHub signs its own merge commit. The unsigned commits stay in history underneath. This only works if the repo doesn't require signed commits, which I haven't checked.\n\n**What I need:** a clear yes if you want the force-push re-sign, in words like \"yes, force-push those 12 branches to re-sign\". The alternative is to tell me to merge as they are. If you grant it, I'd also check first whether branch protection requires signed commits, since that decides whether it matters at all.\n\nneeds input: confirm \"yes, force-push the 12 PR branches to re-sign them\", or tell me to merge them as they are."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2032,"cache_read_input_tokens":292607,"output_tokens":827,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":267},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2032,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":827,"cache_read_input_tokens":292607,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2032,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2032},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"9f5d0f9e-b537-49f3-b917-399541746fa4","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgTq9RKykqj1ncarzdYZU","requestRef":"55df5e4f-7431-4113-97d6-509b629cd1a9","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"3a48ae56-e396-4acb-a377-487dad4de1f5","timestamp":"2026-10-28T02:16:49.187Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"cc-244","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
