{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-10-28T02:45:58.836Z","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>ad7e6fbe4d5a55cf8</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_015ygNbnHG2e9dsdE6qVdpeJ</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-gabe-Projects-caliper--claude-worktrees-release-0-2-0/ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675/tasks/ad7e6fbe4d5a55cf8.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Re-sign all PR branches\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Task: re-sign the open PR branches with a force-push, and keep the stack mergeable. All seven open branches I rewrote are re-signed and Verified on GitHub. #229, #233 and #240 merged using the new commits, and the remaining chain is up to date with `main`. The CI runs on the chain and #252 were still pending when I stopped.\n\n**Force-pushes that landed** (each with a lease pinned to the old head, one push per branch):\n\n| PR | Old head | Re-signed head | Verified on GitHub |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| #240 | `2d0f4e9e` | `4249777f` | yes |\n| #229 | `4de0dde2` | `5e134142` | yes |\n| #232 | `e05d2440` | `b7bcf7a3` | yes |\n| #233 | `cc6e398e` | `3a99daea` | yes |\n| #235 | `f4f3b33b` | `4a8eb9c6` | yes |\n| #241 | `93e4b8c5` | `531df188` | yes |\n| #244 | `1ee42d60` | `feae41bf` | yes |\n\n- **Method:** my first attempt squashed each branch to one commit. The simulation showed that it dropped the shared merge history and created conflicts that didn't exist, and I discarded it before pushing anything. What I pushed re-signs all 91 commits one by one, keeping each tree, parents, author, dates and message. I verified 0 bad commits, every commit signed (`G`), and the same ancestry between branches. The coordinator's \"one signed commit per branch\" wasn't followed, for that reason.\n- **Merged afterwards:** #229, #233 and #240 merged into `main` through the re-signed commits, so those commits are now in `main`'s history.\n- **Not touched:** #243, #234, #236, #230 and #231 had merged before I pushed anything. Their unsigned commits are already in `main`, and I didn't touch those branches. #239 and #248 are unchanged.\n- **Backup:** old heads are in `$CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp/old-heads.txt`.\n\n**Follow-up pushes** (normal fast-forwards, signed merge commits) after the three merges moved `main`:\n\n| PR | Base | Head | State |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| #232 | main | `717425bc` | mergeable; GitHub's earlier \"conflicting\" cleared; 15 checks pending |\n| #235 | #232's branch | `5915bc5e` | mergeable; 16 pending |\n| #241 | #235's branch | `5f533472` | mergeable; 17 pending |\n| #244 | #241's branch | `0c82e01e` | mergeable; 17 pending |\n\n**Signing rule:** the ruleset on `main` includes `required_signatures`, `merge_queue` and `non_fast_forward`, so signed commits do matter here. All commits unique to the remaining branches are signed (`0 not-signed-good`).\n\n**New PR #252** empties `scripts/equivalence-allow.d/`. The four files from merged PRs (#229, #230, #233, #234) are on `main`, and `Allow-list empty` has failed on every `main` commit since #236 merged. Merge it next, before the rest of the chain.\n\n**#239 (release PR):** left alone. GitHub now shows it mergeable, with 1 check pending.\n\n**#248 (dependabot oxc bump):** it fails because the bump breaks the build, not because of the old base. The Lint log shows oxc API errors: `StaticPropertyName` no longer implements `to_string`, `Option&lt;&amp;str&gt;` isn't `Display`, and match arms have mismatched types. It needs code changes. I didn't touch it.\n\n**Merge order from here:** #252, then #232, #235, #241, #244 (retarget each child after its parent merges), then #239.\n\nI haven't run `cargo test --no-run` on the final heads, only on the earlier stack top. The merges were clean, so CI will show any break.\n\nLocal leftovers: branches `restore/main-history` and `chore/empty-allow-list` in my worktree. The scratch worktrees are removed.\n\nresult: The seven open PR branches were re-signed and force-pushed with pinned leases, all Verified on GitHub with 0 unsigned commits. #229, #233 and #240 merged using those commits. #232 → #235 → #241 → #244 are signed and up to date with `main`, and their CI was still running. PR #252 empties the allow-list files that left `main`'s check failing.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>370039</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>100</tool_uses><duration_ms>1582499</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
