{"parentUuid":"342224fc-0121-46d5-8116-e24834ef07d1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgTwdQgGGpopmeaMCbU3i","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JW68j2kLhBw7WMowYopS6e","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Adapt code to oxc 0.155","subagent_type":"fork","name":"oxc-155","prompt":"Fix the dependabot oxc bump (#248: oxc_allocator/parser/ast/ast_visit/span/syntax 0.154 -> 0.155, Cargo.toml workspace deps + Cargo.lock). The Lint log shows API breaks: `StaticPropertyName` no longer implements `to_string`, `Option<&str>` isn't `Display`, mismatched match arms; likely more (oxc_str now a dependency of oxc_ecmascript, Atom/Str types). Read the oxc 0.155 changelog/release notes (https://github.com/oxc-project/oxc/releases, crates changelogs) to adapt properly, not by guesswork. Work in a new worktree off origin/main on a new branch `deps/oxc-0.155`: apply the Cargo.toml/Cargo.lock bump, then fix every compile error in crates/core (and others) in the repo's style (no unwrap outside tests, FxHashMap, CompactString, no AST refs escaping parse_file, Diagnostic on degrade). Then run the real gates, reading exit codes directly: `cargo build --workspace --locked`, `cargo test -p caliper-docgen-core` (snapshots must not change; if oxc changes parse output, show why each snapshot diff is right), `cargo clippy -p caliper-docgen-core -- -D warnings`, `cargo fmt --check`, the MSRV check from ci.yml (look at how CI runs it; the bump may raise the MSRV — if so say so and bump rust-version deliberately), Coverage, Vite plugin native binding test as in ci.yml; and a before/after speed+RSS check on mantine and chakra with the release binary vs origin/main (use scripts/scorecard.py or the A/B method in $CLAUDE_JOB_DIR/tmp/measurement-proposal.md) so we don't ship a perf regression: report numbers. Open ONE non-draft PR (base main) titled like the commits, body: what broke in 0.155 and how each was adapted, pe