{"parentUuid":"b1cbecd9-9864-48c6-8fa6-f712bc97afdb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgTwtJNRzxwsx5RExpudt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do the remaining merges, then the gate rebuild, then the accuracy gaps that matter most to Storybook. Here it is in tiers.\n\n**1. Land what's in flight (days)**\n- **Merge order:** #252, #232, #235, #241, #244, then #239 (release). Retarget each child after its parent merges.\n- **#248 oxc bump:** the `oxc-155` fork is on it.\n- **First Homebrew run:** the next CLI release is the first real test of the tap notifier (#236, merged).\n- **Retire ADRs 0023 and 0024** and fold 0013 into 0024's successor, as recommended earlier.\n- **Branch hygiene:** delete the remote scratch branches (`scratch/gate-calibration`, `scratch/parity-allow-probe`, and the earlier list) and the local `rc-*`, `cc-*` and `perf/shared-element-layer` branches.\n\n**2. Hardening (this is what burned us)**\n- **Rebuild the gates** per the proposal:\n  - a blocking speed and memory gate at 1.10× wall and 1.20× memory, median of 9 interleaved runs;\n  - an output diff with no allow-list;\n  - a weekly accuracy and speed record against RDT and react-docgen.\n  \n  That deletes about 1,360 lines of Python and all committed baselines.\n- **`apps/validate`:** keep the TS 7.1 oracle, move `run-react-docgen.ts` to `scripts/parity-rdg.mjs`, delete the July harness.\n- **Protect `main`:** a force-push still rewound it and lost about 295 commits of history. Confirm the ruleset has no bypass for admins or tooling, and check how the merge queue and the Up to Date gate interact.\n- **Signing:** require signed commits for every actor. Unsigned commits from #243, #234 and #236 are already in `main`.\n- **Trails:** close the stale ones and make one trail per goal, with acceptance criteria.\n\n**3. Accuracy gaps (the product)**\n- **Dropped syntax** (task #42): `readonly`, index signatures, `RefObject`.\n- **Detection:** `memo(forwardRef(function…))` without type arguments, and matching React APIs by import source instead of name.\n- **Chakra:** `NonNullable<union>` isn't reduced.\n- **Recall by library:** shadcn is about 40% against RDT without the opt-in TS backend and antd about 80%. That is where on-demand TS pays off.\n- **Harness:** `PurePanel`'s 33 props look like a pairing mismatch. Confirm it's the harness and not us.\n- **Heuristics:** the `{Name}Props` naming rule in #229's tagged-factory detection should become a shape rule, with an ADR if it holds.\n\n**4. Features**\n- **TS 7.1 on-demand follow-ups:** disk cache, prefetch, a version range and self-check, a memory cap, and CI coverage of real `tsc`. Promoting it from experimental needs evidence from the oracle.\n- **Agents via `monokl`:** an in-process API, no shell-out. It needs a stable session surface in the NAPI binding.\n- **Storybook:** first and later story latency tracked against react-docgen in the weekly record.\n- **Performance:** PGO once the resolver settles, and chained dependency index follow-ups.\n- **Issue #1 (presets):** I recommend closing it.\n\n**Start with** the merges, then the gate rebuild (it stops the false reds that cost us most of today), then dropped syntax and the shadcn and antd recall gap. I'd hold new features until the gates are stable.\n\nShould I start the gate rebuild as soon as #232's chain merges, or do you want the accuracy gaps first?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":529,"cache_read_input_tokens":314152,"output_tokens":1947,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":691},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":529,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1947,"cache_read_input_tokens":314152,"cache_creation_input_tokens":529,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":529},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"9cc46720-d08a-4405-a53a-446d50105db1","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgTwtJ5KcEktFMmN39Frw","requestRef":"b6a2755d-ec1d-4259-8668-c8a39d5d228c","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"b25fa01f-ef4d-4816-89c3-f60ebd80e1c5","timestamp":"2026-10-28T03:45:18.872Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gabe/Projects/caliper/.claude/worktrees/release-0.2.0","sessionId":"ba6a68d6-c702-4382-ab2f-60cd0f6af675","version":"2.1.308","gitBranch":"deps/oxc-0.155","slug":"purring-snuggling-matsumoto"}
